{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.784840+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0d13c98a1fd11db5d57b3319c37535d7c74e2804a733d165b911e9f9d629efb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem coupling-annulus-away-from-minus of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] There exists $C(d)>0$ such that for every $\beta>\beta_0(d)$, $\ell \le r/100$, and $R\ge r$,  
    \begin{align*}
        \| \pi^{\pm}_{A_{r,R}}(\cdot \mathord{\upharpoonright}_{\Lambda_{r+\ell}^c}) - \pi^+_{\Lambda_R}(\cdot \mathord{\upharpoonright}_{\Lambda_{r+\ell}^c})\|_{{\textsc{tv}}} \le \begin{cases}
            C r^C e^{- \ell^2/Cr}+ C e^{ - \beta r} & d=2 \\ C r^{d-1} e^{ - \beta \ell} & d\ge 3
        \end{cases}\,.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.266094+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0e50ff7149687ddd0aa5cfc7b33c6b07f0c38d596abdb15f4f1bab455bbcbd0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma S32L of arXiv:2410.23899, 'Tightness for interlacing geometric random walk bridges'] Fix $p, M\in (0, \infty)$. There exists $N_2 \in \mathbb{N}$, depending on $p$ and $M$, such that the following holds. If $M_1, M_2 \in \mathbb{R}$ are such that $|M_1 - M_2| \leq M$, $n \geq N_2$, $x, y \in \mathbb{Z}$ are such that $x \leq y$ and $x \geq M_1 n^{1/2}$, $y \geq pn + M_2 n^{1/2}$, $g: \llbracket 0, n \rrbracket \rightarrow [-\infty, \infty)$ is arbitrary such that $\Omega_{\mathsf{Inter}}(0,n,x,y, \infty, g) \neq \emptyset$, and $s \in [0, n]$, then we have
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}_{\mathsf{Inter}, \operatorname{Geom}}^{0,n, x, y, \infty, g} \left( Q_1(s) \geq \frac{n - s}{n} \cdot M_1 n^{1/2} + \frac{s}{n} \cdot (pn + M_2 n^{1/2}) - 3n^{1/4} \right) \geq \frac{1}{3}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:52.674379+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0e9f1af8fe1ea0c7dea7320d1b5328357f60473dc2a0ff8f092349a370d3ea9","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 5 of arXiv:2609.03750, '\bf Pullback Measure Attractors, Zero-Noise Limits, and Moderate Deviations for 2D Stochas'] An $H$-valued $\mathscr{F}_t$-adapted c\`{a}dl\`{a}g  stochastic process  $v$ is called a solution of (\ref{PEeq-2.15}) if the following conditions hold: 
$$
v  \in \mathcal{D}([\tau,{\tau+T}];H)\cap  L^2(\tau,{\tau+T};V),~~ \mathbb{P}\text{-a.s.;}
$$
and, for every $t\in [\tau,{\tau+T}]$ and $\psi\in D(A)$, 
\begin{align*}
	&~\langle v(t),\psi\rangle+\int^{t}_{\tau}\Big(\langle v(s), A \psi\rangle+\langle B(v(s),v(s)), \psi\rangle \Big)ds\\
	&=\langle \zeta,\psi\rangle+\int^{t}_{\tau}\langle g(s),\psi\rangle ds+\sqrt{\epsilon}\int^{t}_{\tau}\langle \sigma(s,v(s)) dW(s),\psi\rangle+\epsilon\int^{t}_{\tau}\int_{E}\langle h(v(s-),\xi),\psi\rangle\widetilde{N}^{\epsilon^{-1}}(ds,d\xi), ~~ \mathbb{P}\text{-a.s.}
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

