{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:52:23.587546+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0fd907991a936bef33c86714cd2c3afc50acc268f6c88b6d76fabdfec0068d2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:poisson_summation_hyperfluctuating of arXiv:2602.19773, 'Regularization of a stationary point process by a stationary increments perturbation'] There exists a finite positive measure supported on $\mathbb{R}^{+}$ so that
		\begin{equation*}
			s_{\xi_B}(t)-\bar{s}_{\xi_B}(t) = \frac{\sqrt{2\pi}}{t^{1/h}}\int_{0}^{+\infty}\sum_{n \neq 0}\frac{e^{-\frac{1}{2u}(2\pi n+t)^{2}t^{-2/h}}}{\sqrt{u}} \, \mu(\mathrm{d}u).
		\end{equation*}

		Moreover, $\mu$ satisfies
		\begin{equation*}
			e^{-\frac{1}{2}|t|^{2h}} = \int_{0}^{+\infty}e^{-\frac{1}{2}t^{2}u} \,\mu(\mathrm{d}u), \quad t \in \mathbb{R}.  
		\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:07.255432+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0fecddff732b214df8ef5a561b0d5755c6ab1c07a65d1ccfd5f20c343c5967f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2604.19220, 'Split merge dynamics for expanding intervals and point processes on the real line.'] Fix a family of splitting proportions and boundary conditions $\bpn=(p_{n,k}:(n,k)\in I, a_{n,0}, a_{n,n+1}:n \in \mathbb{N})$ 
and consider the associated random process $(s_n)_{n\ge0}$ defined on $\O$ by \eqref{sn}.
    Suppose, $\exists \bar{p}\in[0,1]$ s.t. under $\PP^\bp$,
    \begin{equation}

        \frac{s_n}{n}\xrightarrow[n\to\infty]{P}\bar p
    \end{equation}
Then, as $n\to\infty$,
\[
g_n \xrightarrow[n\to\infty]{d} \begin{cases}
