{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:23.317253+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c1085b522d7a56333899904e29c7b137a6e770108737d5b733e0f990a7c1a263","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 22 of arXiv:2506.20411, 'Maximal Counts in the Stopped Occupancy Problem'] As \ntoo, for every fixed $j\in{\mathbb Z}_{>0}$,
