{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:35:10.790290+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c18c59defac176e15d8e512d5444d0acdf09aa64c0a513c4445959a47b66154c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defin 1 (Empirical measure) of arXiv:2604.00635, 'Large deviations of the periodic Toda chain'] Given a vector $\bs{x}_N \in \mathbb{R}^N$, the associated empirical measure corresponds to

\begin{align}

\op{L}_N^{(\bs{x}_N)} \overset{\mathrm{def}}{=} \frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^N \delta_{x_i} \, .

\end{align}

Note that the map $\iota : \mathbb{R}^N \to \mathcal{M}_1(\mathbb{R})$, $\iota(\bs{x}_N) := \op{L}_N^{(\bs{x}_N)}$ is continuous.
In particular this means that if $E \subset \mathcal{M}_1(\mathbb{R})$ is a Borel set then
$\iota^{-1}(E) = \big\{ \bs{x}_N \in \mathbb{R}^N \, : \, \op{L}_N^{(\bs{x}_N)} \in E \big\}$ is a Borel set.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:11.412440+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c18c653b776b0ecb6f5e494ccff7785b0ae850e8df56c97ffabf8e061f44920e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thmd 2 of arXiv:2606.08115, '2606.08115'] Let $\bol{Z_n} = \left(Z_n^{(1)}, Z_n^{(2)}\right)$ be a critical PBPJRE. Let the sequence of random vectors $\{\ov{S}_n\}$ be the associated random walk with increments $\ov{X}_i = \left(X_i^{(1)}, X_i^{(2)}\right)$, $i \in \mathbb{N}$. Let
