{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:15.350480+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c1a5726be0f7a5cffa69147f2df03b626670b06d0e0fcc896d21a235ae582508","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2506.15736, 'Coming down from infinity for coordinated particle systems'] Let $\Lambda(dz)$ be a finite measure on $[0,1]$ with density satisfying \emph{(}\ref{eq:density}\emph{)}. Now let $(X(t))_{t \geq 0}$ be a coordinated particle system with a single site, coalescence according to $\Lambda(dz)$, death according to a finite measure $D(dz)$ on $[0,1]$, no reproduction, and an infinite number of particles present at $t = 0$. Then

