{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:09:15.345100+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c1b5541e04917e6f13bd7e31fe1c2c76d40b6148ce9d34d164626ffce83053e2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2411.05534, 'Inverse problems for stochastic partial differential equations'] Let $ X = (X_{1}, \cdots, X_{n}) $ be a $ \mathbb{R}^{n} $-valued random variable. The function 
    \begin{align*}
        F(x) \equiv F\left(x_1, \cdots, x_n\right) \mathop{\buildrel\Delta\over=} \mathbb{P}\left\{X_1 \leq x_1, \cdots, X_n \leq x_n\right\}
    \end{align*}
    is called the distribution function of $ X $. 
    Furthermore, if there exists a nonnegative function $ f(\cdot) $ such that 
    \begin{align*}
        F(x) \equiv F\left(x_1, \cdots, x_n\right)=\int_{-\infty}^{x_1} \cdots \int_{-\infty}^{x_n} f\left(\xi_1, \cdots, \xi_n\right) d \xi_1 \cdots d \xi_n,
    \end{align*}
    then the function $ f(\cdot) $ is called the density of $ X $.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:37:20.358398+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c1bb12a36f1cd47f0e7db9b75c91fb1c962bc89d45ef19fd4196d86d51d16356","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma diff between homo and homoinj of arXiv:2411.13062, 'Graphon-Theoretic Approach to Central Limit Theorems for $\epsilon$-Independence'] For any simple graph $f$ and node-weighted graph $(g,\alpha)$ with $|V(g)|\ge |V(f)|$, we have
    \begin{align*}
        |\rho(f,(g,\alpha))-\rho_{\operatorname{inj}}(f,(g,\alpha))|\le \frac{C_f\alpha_{\max}}{\vert\alpha\vert},
    \end{align*}
    where $C_f$ is a constant that depends only on $f$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:11.705301+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c1cbcd2dcf6acb8557c921b8a942292635b11b194e1611cf2bc948dad0c9ae81","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem reduce of arXiv:2609.00672, 'Deciding superellipticity and computing the Weierstrass normal form'] Let $\tilde h$ be as in (eq:htilde of the paper) and put

