{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:23:03.041416+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c1ccde32612b41ab25b061762c818f65037438c1d2eb12dc39746563af204371","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 45 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] For any $\lambda\geq \rho_{b}^{-2} $, stopping 
time $\tau$, and $\rho\in(0,\infty)$ on 
