{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:42:47.761710+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c1ea6f7dc580ac15837f4d251fb53f6602c5ec83c6bb5376e0fdbd1bb7241314","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2604.12317, 'Weak solution for distribution dependent SDEs driven by L\'{e}vy noise'] (i) For \( f \in \mathbf{W}^{1,1} \), there exists a constant \( C_{d}>0 \) and a Lebesgue measure zero set \( E \) such that for all \( x, y \notin E \),
