{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.762465+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c2688f27f614f42d492fecb5df4899b5039f6450fab97d9a78bd8f975b01301e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:lbm-response-transversality of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] The measures $\eta_{n_1}^x,\ldots,\eta_{n_N}^x$ are linearly independent.
