{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.660838+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c2a9f90c3c514cdbde011aa4d8e57dbaad11aa245d5c08853d2752783c172e72","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop cos-TVS of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] Let $\alpha\in(0,1)$. For $a_c=a_c(\alpha)=\lambda/\alpha$, let $\mathds A_{-a_c, a_c}$ be the critical two-valued set in a valid domain $D$. For any continuous, bounded  function $f:\mathbb C\to\mathbb R$,
