where the limit is in probability. In particular, the left-hand side converges to $(\mu, f)$ where $\mu\equiv\mu(a_c)\equiv\mu(\alpha)$ is a random measure which is measurable with respect to $\mathds A_{-a_c, a_c}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.445620+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c2af58ab0b15531e1b51c37f5f9249d8dbfb80d0ec45d75757ca0473775a1c29","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm main of arXiv:2411.11676, 'Surface sums for lattice Yang--Mills in the large-$N$ limit'] There exists a number $\upbeta_0(d)>0$, depending only on the dimension $d$, such that the following is true. Let $\Lambda_1\subseteq\Lambda_2\subseteq\hdots$ be any sequence of finite subsets of the lattice $\mathbb{Z}^d$ such that $\mathbb{Z}^d = \cup_{N=1}^{\infty}\Lambda_N$. If $|\upbeta|\leq \upbeta_0(d)$, then for any string $s=\{\ell_1,\dots,\ell_n\}$,
\begin{align}
	\lim_{N\to\infty}\phi_{\Lambda_N,N,\upbeta}(s) =
	\prod_{i=1}^n\phi(\ell_i),
\end{align}
where
\begin{equation*}
	\phi(\ell)=\sum_{K:\mathcal{P}_{\mathbb{Z}^d}\to\mathbb{N}} \phi^K(\ell), \quad\text{with}\quad \phi^K(\ell)=\sum_{M\in\mathcal{N}\mathcal{P}\mathcal{M}(\ell,K)}\upbeta^{\area(M)}w_{\infty}(M).
\end{equation*}
Here $\mathcal{N}\mathcal{P}\mathcal{M}(\ell,K)$ is a finite set of connected planar maps with a single boundary component and embedded in the lattice $\mathbb Z^d$ (to be described in more detail in Sections (sec: Background of the paper) and (sec: Main Results of the paper))

and $w_{\infty}(M)$ is a simple product of signed Catalan numbers depending on the perimeter of certain faces of $M$. Moreover, the infinite sum $\phi(\ell)$ is absolutely convergent,\footnote{The sum $\phi^K(\ell)$ is a finite sum for all $K$ and $\ell$.} in the sense that
\[ \sum_{K : \mathcal{P}_{\mathbb{Z}^d} \rightarrow \mathbb{N}} |\phi^K(\ell)| < \infty. \]
Finally, we also establish in Theorem~(thm: fixed K 't Hooft master loop equation for surface sum of the paper) and Corollary~(cor: 't Hooft master loop equation surface sum of the paper) an important recursive relation for $\phi(\ell)$, that goes under the name of master loop equation. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:04.961809+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c2b63ef7e379b48ef5f67e037f085454efa2b56f0a9180409cf6dcecc6272ea0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 (Contraction control) of arXiv:2604.00642, 'Quantitative central limit theorem for an integrated periodogram via the fourth moment the'] Under Assumption~\eqref{ass:LM}, we have
