{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.679347+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c2cf23e9849ee0f6575504e8192b20e15a5f916aa5ce94cfd87f42a8dd13898f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem timehom of arXiv:2411.12149, 'Airy limit for $\beta$-additions through Dunkl operators'] For $H_{1}, H_{2}\in \mathbb{Z}_{\ge 0},\ L\in\mathbb{Z}_{\ge 1}$, sample the walk $W(t)$ from $\mathcal{W}(H_{1},H_{2},L,N)$, with i.i.d.. increments as in Eqn.~((eq_rvx of the paper)), where $$\frac{H_{1}}{\sqrt{L}}\rightarrow u,\ \frac{H_{2}}{\sqrt{L}}\rightarrow v$$ for some given $u,v\ge0$.
