{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.087027+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c2d46b75971cd4d137bf8ba8ed5e00c256a742c17c2f40b3001073719cbccf6f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:dual_strip of arXiv:2606.12143, 'Continuous stochastic flows driven by white noise and their duals'] Let both $(\sigma,b)$ and $(\sigma^*,b^*)$ satisfy Assumption~(assu:H of the paper) and conditions~(item:1a of the paper), (item:1b of the paper), (item:2c of the paper), and~(item:2d of the paper) on ${\mathbb R}$. Assume that for all $x\in I$ and $s,t\in{\mathbb R}$,
