{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.852372+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c31c6bd36a8b5ec410c680fbd1f6db28ed745c555c05f27b0edf3545d13fdf2b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary c:Climit of arXiv:2607.10708, 'A class of Markov processes with resetting and applications to cybersecurity'] Let $X=(N,\Lambda,C)$  be a self-exciting PDMP with resetting. Then, for each $x\in S$,
