{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:57.700967+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c38435757c1b65e1a6bbc87aa549808717df3621da98aac1a23a47fdf7152828","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma log bound for some integral: lemma of arXiv:2605.29095, 'Asymptotics of the number of components of random polynomial lemniscates'] Let $B \subset \mathbb{D} $ and $\alpha \in \mathbb{C}$. Then there exists an absolute constant $C>0$, such that 
