{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.303213+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c39cd4ebba4013b436d2460769b795f7af1b28613bdf086564944b1262568e4f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop prop5.4 of arXiv:2411.14766, 'Axis-Driven Random Walks on $\Z^2$ \\ (transient cases)'] Assume $0<\alpha<\nicefrac{1}{2}$, for any $z$ and large $i$
   \begin{align} 
