{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.473130+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c3b1f1cd27e1ee16e9a93bb5d2d692a2016bcb8a7affe935b9a938ea97cec0b1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:exp-moment-XY of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[lemma]{lem:one-coordinate-Lindeberg}
Fix \(m\ge2\).  Let \(X,Y\) be real random variables satisfying
\[
 \mathbb E X^r=\mathbb E Y^r,
 \qquad r=1,\ldots,m,
\]
and
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb E e^{\left\lvertX\right\rvert/K}+\mathbb E e^{\left\lvertY\right\rvert/K}\le4.
\end{equation}
Let \(F:\mathbb R\to(0,\infty)\) be \(C^{m+1}\), fix constants \(C_1,\ldots,C_{m+1}<\infty\), and set
\begin{equation}
 a_0=a_0(K,m,C_1):=\min\{1,(2KC_1)^{-1}\},
\end{equation}
with the convention \(a_0=1\) if \(C_1=0\).  Suppose that, for some \(0<a\le a_0\),
\begin{equation}
 \abs{F^{(r)}(t)}\le C_r a^rF(t),
 \qquad t\in\mathbb R,\quad r=1,\ldots,m+1.
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
 \left\lvert\log\mathbb E F(X)-\log\mathbb E F(Y)\right\rvert\le C a^{m+1},
\end{equation}
where \(C\) depends only on \(m,K,C_1,\ldots,C_{m+1}\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.232604+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c3d64869680d9a53d3e3126878267b2d2c2e6237cf91fa67dd9606ef780b7c8e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 39 ({\cite[Theorem 1.2 and Theorem 1.5) of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] {BLL:FixedPointGeneral}}]
Suppose that $\lambda_N \in \Lambda_{N,k}$ with $k=\lfloor \theta N\rfloor$ for some $\theta \in (0,1)$ is a family of TASEP initial conditions so that for some $\hfixp_0 \in \UCp$
\begin{equation}
  \frac{-\hpTASEP(\lambda_N;\alpha N,0) + \theta\alpha N}{-\sqrt{2\theta(1-\theta)}N^{1/2}}   \rightarrow \hfixp_0(\alpha)
\end{equation} as $N\to \infty$ where the convergence is as a process in $\alpha$ in the space $\UCp$. Then for all $M \in \N$, 
and all $\tau=(\tau_i)_{i \in \lbr M \rbr}$, $\alpha=(\alpha_i)_{i \in \lbr M \rbr}$ and $\beta=(\beta_i)_{i \in \lbr M \rbr}$, 
 \begin{equation}
 \lim_{N \rightarrow \infty} \P\left( \bigcap_{i=1}^{M} \left\{ \frac{-\hpTASEP(\lambda_N;y_i,t_i)+\theta y_i-\theta(1-\theta)t_i}{ -\sqrt{2\theta(1-\theta)}N^{1/2}}\leq \beta_i \right\} \right) = F_{\hfix_0}^M(\beta,\alpha,\tau) , 
 \end{equation}
 where we set
 \begin{equation}
     t_i := \frac{\tau_i N^{3/2}}{\sqrt{\theta(1-\theta)}}, \quad y_i := \alpha_i N + (1-2\theta)t_i , 
 \end{equation}
 and $(F_{\hfix_0}^M)$ has an explicit formula given in Definition~2.1 of \cite{BLL:FixedPointGeneral}. Moreover, the family $(F_{\hfix_0}^M)$ defines a random field $(\alpha,\tau) \mapsto \mathcal{H}^{\per}_1(\hfixp_0;\alpha,\tau)$, called the \textbf{periodic KPZ fixed point}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

