{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:54:18.302065+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c3e168f0fdd0931167110e566276787178bd8b1a6f8807e50e7c9356a03b8482","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop strongly-convex-coordinate-gradients of arXiv:2608.30382, 'Convergence rates for the RMSprop optimizer with full control of the hyperparameters'] Let $ m, d, M \in {\mathbb N} $, $ \mu, B, R \in (0,\infty) $, and let
$\mathcal V\subseteq{\mathbb R}^d$. Let $U$ be an ${\mathbb R}^m$-valued random variable with a
Lebesgue density $g$ satisfying
\bas{
  \|g\|_{L^\infty}\le B,
  \qquad
  \text{and}
  \qquad
  {\mathbb P}\bigl( | U | < R \bigr) = 1 .
}
Let $U_1,\dots,U_M$ be independent copies of $U$, and set
$\mathbf U=(U_1,\dots,U_M)$. Let
$\ell:{\mathbb R}^d\times{\mathbb R}^m\to{\mathbb R}$ be differentiable in its first argument. For
every $ \theta \in \mathcal V $, $ i \in \{ 1, \dots, d \} $, define
\bas{
  \varphi_{\theta,i} \colon {\mathbb R}^m \to {\mathbb R},
\qquad
  \varphi_{\theta,i}( u )
  =
  \frac{\partial\ell}{\partial\theta_i}(\theta,u),
}
and assume that $\varphi_{\theta,i}$ is $\mu$-strongly convex.
For every $ \theta \in \mathcal V $, $ i \in \{ 1, \dots, d \} $, define
\bas{
X_M^{(i)}(\theta,\mathbf U)
=-\frac1M\sum_{r=1}^M
\frac{\partial\ell}{\partial\theta_i}(\theta,U_r).
}
Let $\omega_m$ denote the Lebesgue volume of the Euclidean unit ball in
${\mathbb R}^m$, and set
\bas{
C_m=1+m3^{m-1}
}
and
\bas{
s_0
=\mu\min\left\{
\frac{R^2}{4},
\frac{1}{
16B^2\omega_m^2C_m^2R^{2m-2}}
\right\}.
}
Then the minibatch innovation $(X_M,\mathbf U)$ is $(c_M,q)$-regular on
$\mathcal V$ with
\bas{
c_M=\frac{(1-e^{-1})s_0^2}{2M^2}
\qquad
  \text{and}
\qquad
q=\frac{1-e^{-1}}2.
}
If, in addition, the coordinate derivatives of $\ell$ are uniformly bounded
on $ \mathcal V \times \{ u \in {\mathbb R}^m \colon | u | < R \} $,
then assumption~(equation eq:combined-main-boundedness of the paper) in
(thm:combined-early-late-numerical-time of the paper) is satisfied for $X_M$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.588917+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c3e2dd6e6f11b1e89181c1d3f778d3c4bd97081fa221895ad9ef8a89a59f478d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 605 of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] For each $p \geq 1$ and $\beta >0$,  there exists a constant $C>0$ such that for any $\zeta, t\geq 0$ and $0\leq t_1<t_2\leq t$,
