{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:47.651603+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c3f3cdc93b92506ff325d2b4815b3ef1066f5cb40226e51da4f7976efeab63cf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 7 of arXiv:2605.07050, 'Universality of the fluctuations of the free energy in generalized Sherrington--Kirkpatric'] Recall the definition of $F_N(\beta)$ in Definition \ref{defn:sub_Gaussian}. Suppose that $W$ is a Wigner matrix, $\sqrt{N} W_{ij}$ $(i<j)$ is symmetric, and one of the following is true:
