{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.196345+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c3fc46fa63c54d371bdd7fda01323e79258b4cd65c3722d59b7fd75d79564ea1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 28 of arXiv:2510.22783, 'Universality of Cutoff for Riffle Shuffling'] For any $y\in \al, z\in \ar$ and $x\in A_{y,z}$, there exists $\mathcal S'$ with $\mathbb P(\mathcal S')\geq 1-\exp(-N^{\delta})$ such that the following holds.
