{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.302103+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c400932edafba9c39f5f1cee6d6a8d2a019896ef3742e24714d7f453870807ae","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:berryesseen of arXiv:2602.11129, 'Information-Theoretic Thresholds for Bipartite Latent-Space Graphs Under Noisy Observation'] {Berry-Esseen theorem, [klenke2008probability]}
    Let $X_1, \ldots, X_d$ be i.i.d. random variables with $\mathbb{E}\left[ X_1 \right] = 0$, $\mathbb{E}\left[ X_1^2 \right] = \sigma^2$ and $\mathbb{E}\left[ X_1^3 \right] < \infty$. Let $X = \frac{1}{\sqrt{d\sigma^2}} \sum_{i = 1}^d X_i$ and let $\Phi$ denote the CDF of the standard Gaussian distribution. 
    Then, 
    \begin{align*}
        \sup_x | \mathbb{P}\left( X \le x \right) - \Phi(x) | \le \frac{0.8\mathbb{E}\left[ X_1^3 \right]}{\sigma^3 \sqrt{d}}.
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

