{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:03:59.434434+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c407934490c6fbc8833f56fe427f51a4cf24109ac9d852a20e9074d64ccc592b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:g406 of arXiv:2507.08757, 'Strong existence and uniqueness of the tilt-indexed Busemann process in the planar corner '] Consider a fixed   weight configuration $\omega\in\mathbb{R}^{\mathbb{Z}^2}$ and $k\in\mathbb{Z}$.  Suppose $\pi_{k:\infty}$ is a semi-infinite geodesic such that $\pi_n\cdote_i\to\infty$ for $i\in\{1,2\}$.   Then  for all $x\in\mathbb{Z}^2$ the  monotone nondecreasing  limit 
\begin{equation} 
 A(x,\pi_k) =  \lim_{n\to\infty}  ( L_{x,\pi_n} - L_{\pi_k, \pi_n} )    \end{equation}
exists in $(-\infty, \infty]$.  
On the  quadrant $\pi_k+\mathbb{Z}_+^2$ we have a finite  Busemann function 
\begin{equation}  
A(x,y) =  \lim_{n\to\infty}  ( L_{x,\pi_n} - L_{y, \pi_n} ) .    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.898726+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c40e7132102c91a3fdcd088bbd94fc3a6e1439b381ddea0d203cca74e6690c82","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 13 (Asymptotics of the free energy) of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Consider an off-critical ensemble \eqref{eq_Hahn_cut_2} with fixed filling fractions. For any $\eps > 0$ and $\N$ larger than some $\N_0(\eps)$, we have
 \begin{equation}
 \Big|\log\Z_\N - \big(\I[\mu_1,\mu_2]\,\N^2 + (\hat{n}_1+\hat{n}_2)\N\log \N + \mathbbm{Rest}_1\,\N\big)\Big| < \eps,
 \end{equation}
 where $(\mu_1,\mu_2)$ is the equilibrium measure and  $\I[\mu_1,\mu_2]$ is the maximum of \eqref{eq_I_intro}, while $\mathbbm{Rest}_1$ is a twice differentiable function of the rescaled parameters $\hat{A},\hat{B},\hat{C},\hat{D},\hat{\mathfrak{t}},\hat{\mathfrak{h}},\hat{n}_1,\hat{n}_2$, which is bounded with $\N$ and whose first and second-order partial derivatives are bounded. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

