{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.700458+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c42360bcd6bc4c8e68c4823154aea551a25aba79da6c7ffb2e47813677e272bf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem asympforl of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] If $\gamma > 0$ is small enough then, for any $0 < \eta' < \eta < \tfrac{1}{2}$ sufficiently small (depending only on $\gamma$)  we have that, for all $k$ sufficiently large and $T \in [2k,{\rm e}^{\tfrac{1}{2}k^\gamma}]$,
