{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.369328+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4526c8a98054c5834598720e55ff1ac5e6168863dda843cdbfbecd8ab757f5f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition kpoint of arXiv:2607.21443, 'The critical KPZ scale for the averaging process'] For $k\in \Bbb N$, define the \textit{$k$-point motion} to be the continuous-time Markov process $\mathbf R=(R^1,\ldots,R^k)$ on $\Bbb Z^k$ with transition probabilities  given, for every $t\ge0$ and $\mathbf x = (x_1,\ldots,x_k), \mathbf y=(y_1,\ldots,y_k)\in \mathbb{Z}^k$, by
    \begin{equation}\mathsf p^{(k)}_t(\mathbf x, \mathbf y)\coloneqq \Bbb E \bigg[ \prod_{j=1}^k K_t (x_j,y_j)\bigg]\; \text{.}
    \end{equation} 
     Let $\ensuremath{\mathcal L}^{(k)} (\mathbf x,\mathbf y):= \frac{{\rm d}}{{\rm d} t}\big|_{t=0}\, \mathsf p^{(k)}_t(\mathbf x,\mathbf y) $, $\mathbf x, \mathbf y \in \mathbb{Z}^k$, denote the corresponding generator, while
    $\mathbf P_\mathbf x^{(k)}$ and $\mathbf E_\mathbf x^{(k)}$ stand for the path law and corresponding expectation when starting from $\mathbf x\in \mathbb{Z}^k$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.695285+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c45521ebf11b2711abe78544e0f450160d87b6b38267bcbe7901810242564145","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:marginals of arXiv:2510.22778, 'Free denoising diffusion models'] The unique adapted solution of (equation eq:forward of the paper) is
\begin{equation}
  X_{t}=\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\,X_{0}
  +\int_{0}^{t}\sqrt{\tfrac{\alpha_{t}}{\alpha_{s}}}\,\sqrt{\beta(s)}\;\mathrm{d} S_{s},
\end{equation}
and its spectral law is
\begin{equation}
  \mu_{t}:=\mu_{X_{t}}=\big(D_{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\mu_{0}\big)\boxplus\gamma_{1-\alpha_{t}},
\end{equation}
where $D_{c}\mu$ denotes the pushforward of $\mu$ under $x\mapsto cx$. In particular
$\int x^{2}\mathrm{d}\mu_{t}=\alpha_{t}\int x^{2}\mathrm{d}\mu_{0}+(1-\alpha_{t})$ and
