{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:28:53.657239+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c45a434c9540218d1df233199d0735f7487a2f5cd16c64e6be4ce1169c16c38d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 (diffusion local time) of arXiv:2605.13648, 'Sticky CIR process with potential: invariant measure and exact sampling'] \label[definition]{diffusion-local-time}
  For a diffusion $X$ with speed measure $m$, the \emph{diffusion local time} $\ell_t^a$ at level $a$ is defined by
\[
\ell^a_t(X) = \lim_{\varepsilon \downarrow 0} \frac{1}{m((a-\varepsilon, a+\varepsilon))} \int_0^t \mathbf{1}_{\{|X_s - a| < \varepsilon\}}\,ds.
\]
The following occupation-time formula holds: 
for measurable $f \geq 0$,
\begin{equation}
\int_0^t f(X_s)\,ds = \int f(a)\,\ell^a_t(X)\,m(da).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:31:14.333557+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4625c44351cf88904e95feae4c222682a82ec91de6c781fcee8ac865bff65c4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2606.16609, 'On stability of outliers from the circular law'] Set $Q_N(z):=1+b_N^*\mathbf{R}_{N}(z)\mathbf{R}_{N}(z)^*b_N$ for $z \notin Sp (D_N)$ and denote by $\mu_1,\ldots,\mu_{N-1}$ the eigenvalues of $D_N$. Then 
   \begin{equation*}
       Q_N(z) \overset{}{=} \prod_{k=1}^{N-1}\left(1+\frac{\lvert X_k\lvert^2}{N\lvert z- \mu_k \lvert^2}\right)
   \end{equation*}
   where $X_1,\ldots,X_{N-1}$ are i.i.d. standard complex Gaussian random variables, independent of $\mu_1,\ldots,\mu_{N-1}.$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.300887+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c462c540cbcc4d1be1f8ec75d0b79949582e50d65fe5d3d40c3ad1e6766a2f67","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:exists_varphi of arXiv:2605.26048, 'Classification of the eternal solutions and multiple coalescing shocks in the KPZ fixed po'] For almost-every $\omega$, whenever $b \in \mathcal{B}_\omega$, the set $\pmb{\xi}^b$ is countable. Furthermore, there exists a function $\varphi:\mathfrak{X} \to [-\infty,\infty)$ with $\operatorname{supp}(\varphi) = \pmb{\xi}^{b}$  such that $b = W\star \varphi$. For this choice of $\varphi$, we have that
    \begin{equation} 
    b(x,t) = \varphi(\xi) + W^\xi(0,0;x,t),\quad \forall \xi \in \pmb{\xi}^{b},\text{ and } (x,t) \in \mathfrak{C}^b(\xi).
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.286650+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4645abc34a7d21a2f214f329e7a39d07666c8b835b4bbb8e3a75ebae9c638ea","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm thm 4.8 of arXiv:2411.01847, 'Well-Posedness of Stochastic Chemotaxis System'] Let $(u, v, \tau_m)$ be a local mild solution of system ((main of the paper)), with $\tau_m$ defined by
    \begin{align*}
        \tau_m = \inf \{ t > 0 \mid \|u\|_{\Upsilon^u_t} \geq m \}.
    \end{align*}
    Then, for $p\geq 2$, the following It\^{o} formula for $\|u(t)\|_{p}^{p}$ holds $\mathbb{P}$-a.s. for all $t \in [0, T]$,
    \begin{align*}
        &\|u(t \wedge \tau_m)\|_{p}^{p} - \|u_0\|_{p}^{p} +p(p - 1)  \int_0^{t\wedge\tau_m}\|\nabla u^{\frac{p}{2}}(s)\|_2^2 \, ds \nonumber \\
        &= p(p - 1) \chi \int_0^{t \wedge \tau_m} \int_\mathcal{O} u^{p - 1}(s) \nabla u(s) \cdot \nabla G * u(s) \, dx \, ds \nonumber \\
        &\quad + p \int_0^{t \wedge \tau_m} \int_\mathcal{O} u^{p - 1}(s) g(u(s)) \, dx \, ds \nonumber \\
        &\quad + p \sum_{k=1}^\infty \int_0^{t \wedge \tau_m} \int_\mathcal{O} \sigma_k(u(s)) u(s) |u(s)|^{p - 2} \, dx \, dW^k_s \nonumber \\
        &\quad + \frac{p(p - 1)}{2} \int_0^{t \wedge \tau_m} \int_\mathcal{O} \sum_{k=1}^\infty |\sigma_k(u(s))|^2 |u(s)|^{p - 2} \, dx \, ds.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

