{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:52.745171+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4787d1962662503bb62442cba25d45f7bd8f7e6d8dc5da9eaa84a376d1c9f6a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 23 ({\cite[Theorem~4.19) of arXiv:2506.10511, '2506.10511'] {Morters_Peres_2010}}]
Recall \eqref{hausdorff}. Suppose that $(E,\widehat{D})$ is a metric space and $\Delta\geq 0$. If there exists a mass distribution $\zeta$ on $E$ along with constants $C <\infty$ and $\delta > 0$ such that
