{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:48:49.895422+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c47f886fea176883e31219ac1fd00926c7c7d5c153f50c25735d82cc2e0f98a2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem Taylor1 of arXiv:2510.23430, 'On the Martin boundary for discrete TASEP'] (1) Assume that $\alpha\in \mathbb R_{>0}$. We have $h'_\alpha(u^{crt})=0$ where $u^{crt}=\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha}$.

