{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.923803+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c48e7d0cc5b23e6dd11ad8c6c0dd55609b73781836943426028f08b2d7ff8261","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm critical_weights_unique of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] {KenyonPohoata}}]
    Fix a finite graph $G = (V,E)$, a weight function $w: E \to \mathbb{R}_+$, $\alpha_v \in [0,1]$ feasible and a sequence of multiplicites ${\mathbf N}$ with $N_v/K\to \alpha_v$ as ${\mathbf N}\to \infty$ for all $v\in V$. Then there exist a \textit{critical weight function} $\mathbf x:V\to \mathbb{R}_+$ such that for each $v\in V$,
\begin{equation}
\sum_{u:(u,v)=e\in E} w_e x_u x_v  = \alpha_v P(\mathbf x).
\end{equation}
Further, the critical weights $\mathbf x$ are unique up to the operation of multiplying by a constant on all black vertices,
and the inverse of this constant on white vertices. In particular, the \textit{critical edge weights} $w_e x_u x_v$ for $(u,v)\in E$ are unique. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:52:08.671335+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c49318f6c319563ee734b109f003dd679deb5b9c49ce5eb6a638a09d3fea41dc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 30 (Scalar quotient recursion and convergence) of arXiv:2608.30027, 'Under Ricci flow, a 3-torus goes flat'] Fix \(C_0\geq0\), and let \(b_k\geq0\), \(k\geq0\), be a summable
