{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:39:41.409620+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4a5bf9acbf1c8b1ed601762ed311dbb5855dfe10c977d1f78545045953aa22f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2604.07207, 'Mixing times of step-reinforced random walks'] (i). Under Assumption \ref{mainassum}, if $\mu$ is a class function, then for any $\varepsilon \in (0,1)$ and $n\geq 1$,
