{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:40.964215+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4c724e90cfc70fda7e1321dd8ef2155bcae73b546ceb81b4b3f6ce334878720","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem T:InvMea of arXiv:2412.03521, 'On ergodic properties of stochastic PDEs'] Let $u(t,x)$ be the solution to~(equation E:SHE of the paper) starting from a rough initial
  condition $\mu$, namely, $\mu$ is a signed Borel measure on $\mathbb{R}^d$ such
  that~(equation A:icon of the paper) holds. Assume that
  \begin{enumerate}[wide, labelwidth=!, labelindent=0pt, label=\emph{(\roman*)}]
    \setlength\itemsep{.1in}

    \item  $b(x,u)=b(u)$ and it verifies condition~(equation E:Cond-b of the paper).

    \item  there are two admissible weight functions $\rho$
      and $\tilde{\rho}$ such that~(equation E:rhorho of the paper) holds and
      \begin{equation}
        \limsup_{t\to\infty}\: \mathcal{G}_{\tilde{\rho}}(t;|\mu|) < \infty;
      \end{equation}

    \item  the spectral measure $\widehat{f}$
      satisfies~(equation E:Upsilon_0 of the paper), i.e., $\Upsilon(0)<\infty$ and the
      Lipschitz constant $L_b$ is small enough such that $4 L_b^2 \Upsilon(0)
      <1$;

    \item  for some $\alpha \in
      \left(4L_b^2\Upsilon(0),1\right)$, the spectral measure $\widehat{f}$
