{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.825748+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4ef305727f96698d9e2af766b14953928844854259e42844b7404bf87a5a61e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:compression of arXiv:2609.01690, 'Iterated-sumset spectra: The complete exponent law and its rank geometry'] For every $h\geq2$,
\begin{equation}
 D_h^{\max}\leq\nu(h,4)\leq\max\{h^2,D_h^{\max}\}.
\end{equation}
Consequently
\[
 \nu(2,4)=6,\qquad \nu(3,4)=11,
\]
while for every $h\geq4$,
\[
 \binom{h+2}{2}+\mathbf 1_{\{2\nmid h\}}
 \leq\nu(h,4)\leq h^2.
\]
In particular, $\nu(h,4)=\Theta(h^2)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.590964+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4f1c57620c5304694d5b9bddecac982910920525c1925b795e77834004cfc84","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma WPD-NHS-AA of arXiv:2608.30582, 'The flexible part of intermittent Onsager theorem for the two-dimensional stochastic incom'] For any $N \in \left\{ {0,1, \cdots ,10} \right\}$ and $t \in \mathop  \cap \limits_{j = 0}^{q} \left[ {0,{\mathfrak{t}_j}} \right] \cap \left[ {{t_k},{t_{k + 1}}} \right)$, there exists a real number $\alpha \in \left( {\frac{\beta }{{b}},\beta } \right)$ such that the backward flow ${{\tilde \Phi }_k}\left( {t,x} \right)$ and the Lagrangian flow ${{\tilde X}_t}$ satisfy
\begin{equation}
{\left\| {\nabla {{\tilde \Phi }_k}} \right\|_N} + {\left\| {{{\left( {\nabla {{\tilde \Phi }_k}} \right)}^{ - 1}}} \right\|_N}  \lesssim \lambda _q^N \lambda _{q + 1}^{ - \alpha }   ,
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
{\left\| {D{{\tilde X}_k}} \right\|_N} \lesssim  \max \left\{ {1,\lambda _q^N \lambda _{q + 1}^{ - \alpha }} \right\}  ,
