where ${{\bar D}_{t,\Gamma }} \triangleq {\partial _t} + {{\bar v}_{q,\Gamma }} \cdot \nabla $ is the material derivative corresponding to ${{\bar v}_{q,\Gamma }}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.528677+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4f235472beaf69cb28b30b7c114832c3e9c25a17a909d90d4d29c5d3ff09fc7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 7 of arXiv:2604.01852, 'The on/off Brownian snake'] Let $(\mathcal{Z}^{(\rm d)}_r, \mathcal{Z}^{(\rm a)}_r)_{r \geq 0}$ be the process defined in Theorem \ref{theorem ooSBM ffd convergence} and let $s \geq s' \geq 0$. Firstly we have $\text{supp}(\mu_{\rm d}) \subseteq \text{supp}(\mathcal{Z}^{(\rm d)}_s)$ $\mathbb{P}_{(\mu_{\rm d}, \mu_{\rm a})}$-a.s. and secondly we have $\text{supp}(\mathcal{Z}^{(\rm d)}_{s'}) \subseteq \text{supp}(\mathcal{Z}^{(\rm d)}_s)$ $\mathbb{P}_{(\mu_{\rm d}, \mu_{\rm a})}$-a.s.
