{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:54:18.242831+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c559a38b0bdb3a82424e180d015bdb666e816fe2c54984dc0edb88b107729614","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm main2 of arXiv:2608.30048, 'Counterexamples for generalizations of the non-elliptic Schr\"{o}dinger maximal operator'] Let $n,k\geq 2$. Let $P\in \mathbb{R}[X_1,...,X_n]$ be a polynomial of degree $k$ with leading form satisfying the hypotheses of Theorem (thm:main_general of the paper).
