{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:36:23.137124+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c55fb6644fd4474d53a77264cbf599c6c09dd8cb04bb60efe7b0d23d087a58b0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eq:strassens of arXiv:2507.01236, 'Disintegration theorem for multifunctions, \\ with applications to empirical Wasserstein d'] Let $(\mathfrak{X}, \mathcal{A}, \mu)$ and $(\mathfrak{Y}, \mathcal{B}, \nu)$ be Polish probability spaces, and let $\omega$ be a nonempty, closed subset of $\mathfrak{X} \times \mathfrak{Y}$.  Then there exists a probability measure $\lambda$ on $\mathfrak{X}\times \mathfrak{Y}$ (with its Borel $\sigma$-algebra) with marginals $\mu$ and $\nu$ such that $\lambda(\omega) = 1$ if and only if
    \begin{equation}
    \mu\big(\pi_{\mathfrak{X}}(\omega\cap(\mathfrak{X}\times U))\big)\geq \nu(U)
    \end{equation}
    for all open sets $U\subseteq \mathfrak{Y}$, where $\pi_{\mathfrak{X}}:\mathfrak{X}\times \mathfrak{Y}\rightarrow \mathfrak{X}$ is the projection of $\mathfrak{X} \times \mathfrak{Y}$ onto $\mathfrak{X}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:20:07.940222+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c561b81ddd2e2815958298f7a804185cbba6da745997e1eb61ba51b331ba9c01","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:lines of arXiv:2608.30254, 'Exact Recovery Thresholds for Weighted Data Selection\\ in Vector-Valued Linear Regression'] Let the features span $\mathbb{R}^d$ and $\tau(D)=(m+1)d=k$. Then:
\begin{enumerate}
\item every data point with $x_i\ne0$ belongs to some positive circuit of
  dyads supported on a single feature line and of size exactly $m+1$;
\item there is no positive circuit of dyads whose features span a subspace of
  dimension $\ge2$, and no line circuit of size $\le m$; in particular no
  point has $x_i\ne0$ and $\rho_i=0$;
\item the nonzero features lie on exactly $d$ linearly independent lines.
\end{enumerate}
Consequently, any dataset whose nonzero features are \emph{not} of this
$d$-line form satisfies $\tau(D)\le(m+1)d-1$ and is recovered exactly within
budget $(m+1)d-1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.602962+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c561edd84b3190de994c555e0d02818e997432c48290e599257ad4f719ef4104","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 44 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] For $x\in C$, the first-entrance kernel into $D$ is

\begin{equation*}
g_D=\psi^C*q^{C,D}.
\end{equation*}

In particular,

\begin{equation*}
g_D(k)(x,D)=\Pp_x\left(\tau_D<\infty,\ S_{\tau_D}=k\right),
\qquad k\in\N^d.
\end{equation*}

Consequently, for an initial law $\nu$ on $C$, the distribution of the first entrance over the lower rectangle with upper corner $k$ is

\begin{equation*}
F_{\nu,D}(k)=\int_C\sum_{r\leqd k}g_D(r)(x,D)\nu(\dd x),
\end{equation*}

and the reliability surface is

\begin{equation*}
R_{\nu,D}(k)=1-F_{\nu,D}(k).
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.411300+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c566f8034e68545a6c9f400503089a7d89e2e2688b4cb59b577f1d35280174d6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Determinant lemma of arXiv:2608.27248, 'Optimal Transport and the ABP Method in Higher Codimension'] Set $Z=\nabla^\Sigma\log f+H\in\mathbb{R}^{n+4}$.  For every $(x,y)\in\mathcal{C}$,
\begin{equation}
 \operatorname{tr} Q_x(y)=nf(x)^{\frac{1}{n-1}}
 -\big(h_{\mathcal E}(Z(x))+\langle Z(x),\Phi(x,y)\rangle\big),
