{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:02.092593+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c571d648fe7f60cc8fa3366addda8b4b574aaf139f7eb2058f730fa2ae74656a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 3 of arXiv:2604.25964, 'Strong convergence rate of Euler-Maruyama approximations in temporal-spatial H\"older-norm'] (A Gronwall-Lyapunov inequality) 
Let $\tau $ be a stopping time,  $\widehat{\mu}, \widehat{\sigma}$ and $\widehat{\gamma}$ real-valued measurable functions such that 
\begin{equation} 
\int_0^{\tau} \left(|\widehat{\mu} (\xi_s)| + |\widehat{\sigma}(\xi_s)|^2 + | \widehat{\gamma}(\xi_s)|^2 \right) ds <\infty, 
 \quad \mathbb{P}\text{-a.s.},
 \end{equation} 
 where  $\xi$ is an adapted  c\`adl\`ag process satisfying for all $t\in [0, T]$,   
 $$\xi_{t \wedge \tau } = \xi_0 + \int_0^t {\bf 1}_{[0, \tau]}(s)\widehat{\mu}(\xi _s)ds+ \int_0^t {\bf 1}_{[0, \tau]}(s)\widehat{\sigma}(\xi _s)dW_s + \int_0^t {\bf 1}_{[0, \tau]}(s)\widehat{\gamma}(\xi _{s-}) dZ_s, \quad  \mathbb{P} \text{-a.s.}.$$   
Let  $\alpha, \beta: [0, T] \to [0, \infty )$  be measurable functions  satisfying  $\int_0^{T}|\alpha_r|dr <\infty$. Suppose that for some function  $V=(V(s, x))_{s\in [0, T], x\in \mathbb{R}} \in C^{1,2}([0, T] \times \mathbb{R}, [0, \infty))$ it holds for any $s\in [0, u]$ with $u\in [0, T]$    that
\begin{align}

& \dfrac{\partial V}{\partial s} (s, \xi_s) + \dfrac{\partial V}{\partial x} (s, \xi_s) \widehat{\mu}(\xi_s)+\dfrac{1}{2}\frac{\partial^2 V}{\partial x^2}(s, \xi_s)\widehat{\sigma}^2(\xi_s)  \notag \\
& \quad + \int_{\bR_0} \left[ V(s, \xi_s+ \widehat{\gamma}(\xi_{s})z)-V(s, \xi_s) - \dfrac{\partial V}{\partial x} (s, \xi_s) \widehat{\gamma}( \xi_{s})z \right] \nu (dz)  \notag \\
& \leq \alpha(s) V(s, \xi_s)+  \beta(s) \quad \mathbb{P} \text{-a.s.}.
\end{align}
Then, for all $t \in [0, T]$, 

\begin{align*}
\mathbb{E} \left[ \dfrac{V(\tau \wedge t, \xi_{\tau \wedge t})}{\exp \left( \int_0^{\tau \wedge t} \alpha(r)dr\right)}\right] \leq \mathbb{E}[V(0, \xi_0)]  + \mathbb{E} \left[ \int_0^{\tau \land t}  \dfrac{\beta(s)}{\exp \left( \int_0^{s} \alpha(r) dr \right)}ds \right]. 
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.971551+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c57cecd1e9b6a017e6a6f1d3c4ebae2eaa3880958803e5d830c7b11f57879f1f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:grafting of arXiv:2411.07157, 'Rough differential equations in the flow approach'] Given $\underline{\tau}_1, \underline{\tau}_2\in \boldsymbol{\mathfrak{T}}$, we define, for any $n \in N(\underline{\tau}_1)$ a new labelled tree $\underline{\tau}_2 \graft_{n} \underline{\tau}_1 \in \boldsymbol{\mathfrak{T}}$ which will be constructed by ``grafting the tree $\underline{\tau}_2$ onto $\underline{\tau}_1$ at the node $n$''. More precisely, we set 
\begin{equs}  
r(\underline{\tau}_2 \graft_{n} \underline{\tau}_1 )\eqdef r(\underline{\tau}_1)\,,\; 
\enskip 
N(\underline{\tau}_2 \graft_{n} \underline{\tau}_1 ) \eqdef N(\underline{\tau}_1) \cup {N}\big(\underline{\tau}_2+ \ell_{\underline{\tau}_1,\underline{\tau}_2} \big)\,,
\end{equs}
and
\begin{equs}   
{E}(\underline{\tau}_2 \graft_{n} \underline{\tau}_1) \eqdef E(\underline{\tau}_1) \cup E\big(\underline{\tau}_2+ \ell_{\underline{\tau}_1,\underline{\tau}_2} \big) \cup \big\{\{{r}\big(\underline{\tau}_2+ \ell_{\underline{\tau}_1,\underline{\tau}_2} 
 \big),n\}\big\}\,.
\end{equs}","status":"unverified"}

