{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:16:53.662696+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c582ea78d07519cf08bcbabe749933a1e8812f79bb22ae11b41980777a60081d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem5 of arXiv:2412.05521, 'Random attractors for the stochastic Nernst-Planck-Navier-Stokes system with multiplicativ'] Let $(v^\varepsilon,\sigma,\rho)$ be a solution of system (equation b2 of the paper). Let $v^\varepsilon(t_0)$ $\in$  $H^1$ and $c_i(t_0) \in {L}^{2}$. Then,
		\begin{align}
			\|\sigma\|_{L^2}^{2}\ + \|\rho\|_{L^2}^{2}\ \leq (\|\sigma(t_0)\|_{L^2}^{2}\ + \|\rho(t_0)\|_{L^2}^{2})e^{2D(t_0-t)},~t \geq t_0.
		\end{align}
		\begin{proof}
	We recall $\sigma$  and $\rho$ obey
			\begin{equation}
				\left\{
				\begin{aligned} 
					\partial_{t}\sigma+z^{-1}(v^\varepsilon\cdot\nabla \sigma)=D\Delta \sigma +D\nabla\cdot(\rho\nabla \Phi) \\
					\partial_{t}\rho+z^{-1}(v^\varepsilon\cdot\nabla \rho)=D\Delta \rho +D\nabla\cdot(\sigma\nabla \Phi) \\
				\end{aligned}
				\right.
			\end{equation}
			Taking the ${L}^{2}$ inner product of the first equation in (equation d2 of the paper) with $\sigma$ and of the second equation with $\rho$, we add them and have
			\begin{align*}
				\frac{1}{2}\frac{d}{dt}( \|\sigma\|_{L^2}^{2}\ + \|\rho\|_{L^2}^{2}\ ) =-D (\|\nabla\sigma\|_{L^2}^{2}\ + \|\nabla\rho\|_{L^2}^{2}\ )+ \int \rho\Delta \Phi\sigma.
			\end{align*}
			In view of the fourth equation in (equation b2 of the paper), we know that
			\begin{align*}
				\int \rho\Delta \Phi\sigma=-\frac{1}{\varepsilon_0} \int {\rho}^2\sigma,
			\end{align*}
			where $\sigma > 0$. Then, we get
			\begin{align}
				\frac{d}{dt}( \|\sigma\|_{L^2}^{2}\ + \|\rho\|_{L^2}^{2}\ ) +2D(\|\nabla\rho\|_{L^2}^{2} + \|\nabla\sigma\|_{L^2}^{2}) \leq 0.
			\end{align}
			Thanks to Lemma (lem1 of the paper), we obtain (equation d1 of the paper).
		\end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.256414+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c5846c641e88d105fad9c924b3b7fc3a6e744aba2d729db6389da9fea4f9445c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma rbound of arXiv:2507.10545, 'KPZ equation from a class of nonlinear SPDEs in infinite volume'] \fsp Fix any {\small$\mathrm{D}=\mathrm{O}(1)$} and {\small$\T>0$} independent of {\small$N$}. With high probability, we have 

