{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.898124+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c585ab01972563b705c9bfeb1bcd9fc13a583ae454834e8627d4089e1d8f3d3c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 7 of arXiv:2606.19925, 'Asymptotic properties for fully coupled delayed forward-backward stochastic differential e'] Suppose that assumptions $({\bf A1})$-$({\bf A3})$ hold. Let For $0< \varepsilon < \varepsilon' < 1$ and and assume that the constants $T$ and $K$ are sufficiently small so that
