{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:42:47.772505+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c5bfd127f17e60f465d656f654a58077fa11356f316cab8cc28716955cbf3324","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 (Controlling the commutators) of arXiv:2604.12797, 'A free boundary problem for the mean-field limit of diffusing particles with nonlinear bou'] Let $\phi(t,x) \in \{ b_A(t,x), \sigma_{A}(t, x)^2 \}$. Then, the commutator $c^{\phi,\varepsilon}_t(x)$ defined in \eqref{eq:commutator} satisfies
