{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:36:49.852104+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c5d91551adcfc4cdf8e83a1e0b99615f154e316799f9e8d8771ef828e8eafb48","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:dgt4-path-survival of arXiv:2609.02829, 'Quantitative explosion and percolation of the divisible sandpile'] Let $T>0$, $\kappa>0$, and $n_R\coloneqq\lfloor R^2T\rfloor$, and suppose that for every
