{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.081932+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c5f0437936ee20833e4643ec27eb93cce2fae9ddb7f207826aa3d942efd3899a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition CanoncialSpaceProperties of arXiv:2411.12522, 'Canonical insurance models: stochastic equations and comparison theorems'] For  $s \in [0,\infty)$ and $i \in \mathcal{Z}$, let $Y$ be  a $\mathbb{P}_s^i$-integrable random variable. Then
	\begin{itemize}
