{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:49:05.532754+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c60b5c94ec70d855db2f994cfa78bfc05b13ccaeee264107c7c3bb7eb7b74908","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Deff def:invasion-rates of arXiv:2601.19145, 'Stochastic Persistence in Infinite Dimensions'] Fix $\mu \in P_{inv}(\mathcal{M}_0)$ (see (inv-meas of the paper)), $k \in \{1,\dots,m\}$, and suppose $\mu(\{x_k = 0\}) = 1$ 
