{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.255453+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c6156117373f248e3119979566b0d7f5d5c77ad10dc9cb27d4cca87fa87ec3d9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 9 of arXiv:2609.01101, '2609.01101'] There exist constants $A_2\ge1$ and $\eta_0\ge1$, depending only on
the fixed fields and on $\mathbf a$, such that the following
holds.  Let $\eta\ge\eta_0$ be fixed, and suppose that $T$ is sufficiently
large in terms of $\eta$.  Set
\begin{equation}
N=T^{1/2},\qquad \gamma=\frac12+\frac{\eta}{\log T}.
\end{equation}
Then, uniformly for $|b_i|\le T/2$,
\begin{align}
\sum_{n\le N}\frac{|c_{\mathbf b}(n)|^2}{n^{2\gamma}}
&\gg \eta^{-A_2}B(T,\mathbf b,\mathbf a), \\
\sum_{n\le N}\frac{|c_{\mathbf b}(n)|^2}{n}
&\ll B(T,\mathbf b,\mathbf a).                 
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:58.358319+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c615cd3524aba00c19d9dc1b702f8da03894d39e380eb6b42159b81997b6b484","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 9 of arXiv:2506.18834, '\large\bf On the random-time and finite-time ruin probability for widely dependent claim s'] In a nonstandard renewal risk model, let $Y_i,i\ge1$ be WUOD random variables with dominating coefficients $g_{U,G}(n),n\ge1$,
