{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.354863+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c61de7d2ad7124b3482195d2104d98f43dc201daee9f0ff78357033f0fce46e4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:duality-regularized of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] Let $p\in[2,\infty]$ and $\delta\in[0,\infty)$. Let $q=p/(p-1)$ denote the conjugate exponent, with $q=1$ when $p=\infty$. We have
\begin{align*}
    V_{p,\delta}^{\infty} =
    \sup
    \bigg\{
        {\mathbb E}[YB(1)] - \int_0^1\varphi_\delta\big(\big\|{\mathbb E}[Y\,|\,{\mathcal F}(t)]\big\|_{2}\big)\,dt
        :
        \begin{array}{c}
            Y:\Omega\to {\mathbb R} \mathrm{\ s.t.\ } \|Y\|_{q} \leq 1,\\
            \,
            {\mathbb E}|Y|\sqrt{\log(1+|Y|)}<\infty
        \end{array}
    \bigg\}
    \eqqcolon P_{q,\delta}.
\end{align*}
Moreover, there exists $\alpha\in\mathbb{A}$ such that the minimization problem $V_{p,\delta}^{\infty}$ is attained. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

