{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:44.955875+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c62c24674aa5aea278bd618649a389e2850def053cf379eda3198fe80987a5c6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2606.25501, 'An RDT based approach to large deviations of Wishart and Wigner matrices spectral edges'] (\cite{Gordon85})
 Let $X_{ij}$ and $Y_{ij}$, $1\leq i\leq n$, $1\leq j\leq m$, be two centered Gaussian processes which satisfy the following inequalities for all choices of indices
\begin{enumerate}
\item $\mE(X_{ii}^2)=\mE(Y_{ii}^2)$
\item $\mE(X_{ij}X_{il})\geq \mE(Y_{ij}Y_{il})$
\item $\mE(X_{ij}X_{lk})\leq \mE(Y_{ij}Y_{lk})$, $i\neq l$.
\end{enumerate}
 Then
\begin{equation*}
\mE(\min_{i} \max_{j} X_{ij})\leq \mE(\min_i \max_{j} Y_{ij}) \quad  \Longleftrightarrow \quad \mE(\max_{i}\min_{j} X_{ij})\geq \mE(\max_i \min_{j} Y_{ij}).
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:51.770695+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c62c3780351a398e8124c6553f8efe1bdfed6ec800ecf00a2b6e1ac6d9366cb8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma upper bounds for degrees d =2 of arXiv:2605.03151, 'Giants through Higher-Order paths in Random Simplicial Complexes'] Let $\sigma_0$ be an arbitrary edge in $X_n \sim \MRSC_d(n; p_1, p_2)$ satisfying the conditions in Proposition~(prop: MRSC satisfies the side condition of the paper) (i). Let $(\mathcal{X}_k)_{k \geq 1}$ be the simplicial complexes obtained by the breadth-first exploration starting at $\sigma$. Then, for any fixed constant $T > 0$, as long as $k \leq T n^{1- \alpha_1/2}$, it holds that
\[  \tag{4.1.7}
