{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:54:18.292608+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c659f5f242c5849189fab0b54533b838cf9e9e0c6d0a9a85b418ec1a0ce1837e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:bounded of arXiv:2608.30166, 'Square Functions and Rectifiability\\ under Monotone Transformations of the Density'] Let $\mu$ be $n$-AD-regular with constant $c_0$ and $\mu(\mathbb{R}^d)<\infty$, and let
$F\colon(0,\infty)\to\mathbb{R}$ be a Borel function and bi-Lipschitz on
$J_1=[2^{-n}c_0^{-1},c_1]$ with constant $\lambda_1$, where $c_1=5^dc_0$.
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)] If (equation eq:carlesonF of the paper) holds for some constant $c$, then $\mu$ is uniformly
$n$-rectifiable. No hypothesis on $F$ near $0$ is required.
\item[(b)] Conversely, if $\mu$ is uniformly $n$-rectifiable and in addition
\begin{equation}
\sup_{0<\varepsilon\le c_1}\ \varepsilon\int_\varepsilon^{c_1}
\bigl|F(t)-F(2^{-n}t)\bigr|^2\,\frac{dt}{t}\;<\;\infty,
\end{equation}
then (equation eq:carlesonF of the paper) holds. Condition (equation eq:tail of the paper) is satisfied whenever
$t\mapsto F(t)-F(2^{-n}t)$ is bounded on $(0,c_1]$, and for $F$ continuous on
$(0,\infty)$ this is the same as being bounded near $0$; in particular (equation eq:tail of the paper)
holds for $F=\log$, for which $F(t)-F(2^{-n}t)\equiv n\log 2$.
\end{itemize}
Consequently, for $F=\log$ the full equivalence of Corollary~(cor:log of the paper) holds with no
restriction on the total mass, with $\lambda_1=5^dc_0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:35:10.791797+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c65a3ffa56da346f04dbe3b6384a9988fdd397d8ec82cc9fda8f0bb0564a6608","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 11 (Exponential tightness) of arXiv:2604.00635, 'Large deviations of the periodic Toda chain'] There exists a sequence of compact sets $K_L \subset \mathcal{M}_1(\mathbb{R})$ ($L > 0$) such that

\begin{align}

\limsup_{L \to +\infty} \limsup_{N \to +\infty} \frac{1}{N} \ln \overline{\Pi}_{N}[K_L^c] = - \infty \, .

\end{align}

Likewise, if we let $K_{L,\mathsf{c}} = K_L \cap \mathcal{M}_{1,\mathsf{c}}(\mathbb{R})$
then (we claim, according to our earlier choice of $K_L$) $K_{L,\mathsf{c}}$
is compact in the subspace topology of $\mathcal{M}_{1,\mathsf{c}}(\mathbb{R})$

\begin{align}

\limsup_{L \to +\infty} \limsup_{N \to +\infty} \frac{1}{N} \ln \overline{\Pi}_{N,\mathsf{c}}[K_{L,\mathsf{c}}^c] = - \infty \, .

\end{align}

where here the complement is taken in $\mathcal{M}_{1,\mathsf{c}}(\mathbb{R})$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:41:28.167629+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c65be0eae40f22853bba723fc9817915fc2bd36c2e04f56d70dbdd68d75b17ea","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Partial TWGs of arXiv:2510.26724, 'Sharp Fuss-Catalan thresholds in graph bootstrap percolation'] We call a subgraph $S$ a {\it partial TWG} 
