{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.225173+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c66cce8539334f0af5e519d62fd7caab9af79a1d8ee4e59478c4dca6eef0efdc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop RW/RI to independent RI coupling of arXiv:2411.16398, 'Large Deviations of Cover Time of Tori in Dimensions $d\geq 3$'] Let $\delta > 0$. Assume that $R \in [1, \frac{N}{1+\delta}]$ and $\boldsymbol{F} \subset \mathbb{T}_N$ (resp.\ $F \subset Q(0,N)$) is $(1+\delta)R$-well separated. Then for every $u>0$, $\rho \in (0,1)$, there exists a probability measure $\widetilde{\mathsf{P}}$ (resp.\ $\widetilde{\mathbb{P}}$) extending $\mathsf{P}$ (resp.\ $\mathbb{P}$) and carrying independent random interlacements $\left(\mathcal{I}^{(x),u(1\pm\rho)}\right)_{x\in F}$ with the same law as $\mathcal{I}^{u(1\pm\rho)}$, such that
