{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.669381+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c679fe44fc6b175f422ef66e678b5b8a1bafa14a2352faab6ce02c7cfcb901ab","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem finite-n-coming-generation of arXiv:2609.00110, 'Phase Transition and Fluctuation Results for First-Passage Percolation on Spread-Out Cycle'] For $r\geqslant0$, define the stopping line $\mathcal{I}_n(r)$ and its associated martingale value $\mathcal{W}_n(r)$ by
\begin{align*}
 \mathcal{I}_n(r):= \{u\ne\varnothing:\tau_{u^-}\leqslant r<\tau_u\}, \qquad 
 \mathcal{W}_n(r):= \sum_{u\in\mathcal{I}_n(r)}e^{-\alpha_n\tau_u},
\end{align*}
where $u^-$ denotes the parent of $u$. For $n_0$ sufficiently large, there exist constants $c,C>0$ such that uniformly for $n\geqslant n_0$ and $r\geqslant0$,
\begin{alignat*}{2}
 \E\mathcal{W}_n(r)&=1, 
 &\E\sum_{u\in\mathcal{I}_n(r)}e^{-2\alpha_n\tau_u} &\leqslant e^{-\alpha_nr},\\
 \E\abs{\mathcal{W}_{n,\infty}-\mathcal{W}_n(r)}^2 &\leqslant Ce^{-\alpha_nr},\qquad 
 &\E\sum_{u\in\mathcal{I}_n(r)} e^{-\alpha_n\tau_u}\mathds{1}\{\tau_u>2r\} 
 &\leqslant C(1+r)e^{-cr}.
\end{alignat*}","status":"unverified"}

