{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:32:18.863395+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c6c098652764bbb1b950266aaa4b419ea86f4a94be05e48bc48fd8f8b4fd590c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 49 of arXiv:2609.03875, 'Measure theory without infinities'] Let $\mathbb K$ be an algebraic ring and $\mf A$ be both an HCLM$_{\mathbb{K}}$ and a left $\mathbb K$-module.
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item[(i)]  Let $\mu$ be an $\mf A$-valued measure. If $k\in\mathbb K$ is invertible, then $k\boxdot \mu = k\cdot\mu$.
  \item[(ii)] If $k,l\in\mathbb K$ and $\mu$ is an $\mf A$-valued premeasure, then $(kl)\boxdot\mu=k\boxdot(l\boxdot\mu)$ and $(k+l)\boxdot\mu = (k\boxdot\mu)\boxplus(l\boxdot\mu)$.
  \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:30:14.227724+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c6c77fed2f529dff3367905078738b19103c0c6794b015cec42082ccb5969f1a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition Bramson-psi-estimate-for-one-sided-f of arXiv:2608.23202, 'Locally finite Fixed points of Branching Brownian Motion'] For a function $f$ of type (equation Form of f of the paper) and $\phi(x) = 1-e^{-f(-x)}$, let $u_{\phi}$ be the solution to the F-KPP equation with initial condition $\phi$. Define for $z\in \mathbb R$ and $t>r>0$,
\begin{equation}
\psi(r,t,z+\sqrt 2t):=\frac{e^{-\sqrt 2z}}{\sqrt{2\pi(t-r)}}\int_0^\infty u_{\phi}(r,y+\sqrt 2r)e^{\sqrt 2y}e^{-\frac{(y-z)^2}{2(t-r)}}\{1-e^{-2y\frac{z+\frac{3}{2\sqrt 2}\log t}{t-r}}\}dy.
\end{equation}
Then, for all $r$ large enough (depending only on the initial condition $\phi$), $t\geq 8r$ and $z \geq 8r-\frac{3}{2\sqrt 2}\log t$,
\begin{equation}
\gamma_r^{-1} \psi(r,t,z+\sqrt 2t) \le u_{\phi}(t,z+\sqrt 2 t) \le \gamma_r \psi(r,t,z+\sqrt 2t),
\end{equation}
where $\gamma_r \downarrow 1$ as $r\to \infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

