{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.573077+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c6d597ec8c6a1f7dfe39d0a8ba6890e8ab9f4c4a8af65a98f6b95c4f8701ca7b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 34 of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] Let $h$ be a real random variable with moments of all orders, and let $F:\R\to\C$ be a smooth function. For every fixed integer $\ell\geq1$,
