\item (Extremal fluctuations up to location scale $N/(\log N)^{\frac1{2p}}$ in $d=2$) If $N^{-1/2}\ll |   \varsigma_N| \ll  (\log N)^{-\frac1{2p}} \text{ as } N\to \infty$ and if $\frac{   \varsigma_N}{|  \varsigma_N|} \to   {\boldsymbol v}_{\mathrm{unit}}$ as $N\to\infty$, then the limit point is unique and coincides with the law of the solution of the additive-noise SPDE \begin{equation}\partial_t \mathcal U(t,   x) = \frac12\Delta \mathcal U(t,   x) + \sqrt{2\pi} \cdot \gamma_{\mathrm{ext}}(  {\boldsymbol v}_{\mathrm{unit}})\cdot   (\mathfrak H_0 *G_t)(x)\; \xi(t,   x),
