started from $\mathcal U(0,   x)=0.$ Here $ \xi$ is a standard space-time white noise defined on $\mathbb R_+\times \mathbb R^2.$

\end{itemize} Above $G_t(x)=G(t,   x) = (2\pi t)^{-1}e^{-|   x|^2/2t}$ is the standard deterministic heat kernel, and $*$ is spatial convolution. Furthermore $\pi^{\mathrm{inv}}$ is the invariant measure of the  (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:36:12.193683+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c6f9249383b3348160acf9c6434ffc3ab050b9483b5e28c13091701b4b937e4f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 (Generalized resolvent identity) of arXiv:2609.03924, 'Beyond normal fluctuations in local laws for Wigner matrices'] For $H=H^*\in\C^{N\times N}$ and $z_j\in\C\setminus\R$ denote $G_j:=(H-z_j)^{-1}$, $j=1,2$. For any $k,l\in\N$ it holds that
