{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:30.017085+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c70a806df861bfee411341272405751f80647f343f95c56ba4eff37f09e668c8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 18 of arXiv:2605.05864, 'Classification and Metrization of Classes of Smooth measures'] Assume that $\mu\in{\cal S}$ and its $\alpha$-potential $R_\alpha\mu$ belongs to $L^\infty(E;m)$ for  all $\alpha>0$. 
