{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.298948+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c7166304ef47c0a83de54676a97cde938343865777a1335188b3cc3c43da8a8b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Th:Particula_aleatoria of arXiv:2605.24671, 'Immigration Processes with Binomial Catastrophes and Random Survival Parameters'] The survival probability of the process $C_{\mathrm{ind}}(\lambda,\nu)$ is given by
\begin{equation}
\mathbb P(\mathcal A_{C_{\mathrm{ind}}})
=
\frac{1+\lambda}
{\lambda+\lambda\sum_{j\ge1}
\prod_{k=0}^{j-1}
