{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.188099+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c72b352f853d4fd91329de013e35452a76b0802ddde294cab0ca48c192a2124e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2604.18871, 'Quantitative approximation of the Vlasov(--Fokker--Planck)--Navier--Stokes system by stoch'] Let $f\in H^\gamma_{p}(\T^d)$ with $\gamma>\frac{d}{p}$ and $\mu$ a probability measure on $\T^d\times \R^d$. Then there exists $C = C(\gamma,d,p)>0$ such that for any $N\in \N$ and any $(x,v)\in \T^d\times \R^d$,
