{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.593187+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c72cc7f1f070955a0bf830bf8d9844b38bdc910432d16732f95e961bfb55bf96","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem colour_position_symmetry_step of arXiv:2412.03370, 'TASEP with a general initial condition and a deterministically moving wall'] Let $I \subseteq \mathbb{N}$, $\{Z_n\}_{n \in I} \subseteq \mathbb{Z}$ and let $(x^{\textup{step},Z_n}(t),t\geq 0), n \in I,$ be coupled by basic coupling. Then, for any $s \in \mathbb{R}$, it holds
