{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.582625+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c732cbefa964ffa85041a1233d49db7aff90ad9de33752f49ec5d0d6098ff6f1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition tightness condition of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] For a sequence of c\`adl\`ag stochastic processes $\{X^{(n)}\}_{n\geq 1}$ defined on a common probability space with $\sup_{n \geq 1}  \mathbf{E} \big[|X^{(n)}(0)|^q\big] < \infty$ for some $q>0$, it is $C$-tight if the following two conditions hold for any $T\geq 0$ and some constant $\beta>2$.
 \begin{enumerate}
  \item[(1)] 
  There exist some constants $C>0 $, $p\geq 1$ and $\rho,\alpha>0$ such that for any $\delta\in(0,1)$ and $n\geq 1$,
  \begin{eqnarray*}
   \sup_{t\in[0,T]} \mathbf{E}\Big[\big| X^{(n)}(t+\delta)-X^{(n)}(t)\big|^{p}\Big] 
   \leq C\cdot \Big(  \delta^{1+\rho}+ \frac{\delta}{n^\alpha}\Big).
  \end{eqnarray*}

  \item[(2)] 
  $\displaystyle\sup_{k=0,1,\cdots,[Tn^\beta]} \sup_{\delta\in[0,1/n^{\beta}]} \big|  X^{(n)}(k/n^\beta+\delta) -X^{(n)}(k/n^\beta)\big|  \overset{\rm p}\to 0$  as $n\to\infty$. 
 \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:52:08.647340+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c7372986ee3daadc85d7408cd1afc412ab376519be6afefd581860087efc4058","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2608.29878, 'Discontinuous phase transitions \\ in the one-dimensional \\ pair and triplet creation pro'] Let $x^k\in \RR$ and $x_\vep^k\in\vep\ZZ$, $\,k=1,\dots
