{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:23:05.284452+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c74a38bd81f35cbb9ea6180820d16ae2905b31e179b1fc85bf1442045c44a211","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 1 (Closed-form sparse loading update) of arXiv:2608.21551, '\bf Sparse Separable Factor Analysis in the Complex Domain with an Application to Local Fi'] Let $\Ab^{(t)}=(a_{rc}^{(t)})$ be the unpenalized reduced loading estimate in \eqref{eq:main-4}, and let $\psi_{rr}^{(t)}$ be the $r$th diagonal entry of $\Psib^{(t)}$. The unique minimizer of $\mathcal{L}_{\rho} \left(\Lambdab\mid\thetab^{(t)} \right)$ in \eqref{eq:penalized-reduced-loading-objective} over $\Lambdab\in\CC^{p\times k}$ is $\Lambdab^{(t+1)}$, with entries
\begin{align}
  \lambda_{rc}^{(t+1)}
  &=
  \mathcal{T}_{\rho\psi_{rr}^{(t)}/2}
  \left(
    a_{rc}^{(t)}
  \right),
  \qquad
  r=1,\ldots,p,
  \quad
  c=1,\ldots,k,

\end{align}
where the complex soft-thresholding operator is given by
\begin{align}
  \mathcal{T}_{\rho\psi_{rr}^{(t)}/2}
  \left(
    a_{rc}^{(t)}
  \right)
  &=
  \begin{cases}
    \displaystyle
    \left(
      1-
      \frac{\rho\psi_{rr}^{(t)}}
           {2|a_{rc}^{(t)}|}
    \right)
    a_{rc}^{(t)},
    &
    |a_{rc}^{(t)}|
    >
    \dfrac{\rho\psi_{rr}^{(t)}}{2},
    \\[3mm]
    0,
    &
    |a_{rc}^{(t)}|
    \leq
    \dfrac{\rho\psi_{rr}^{(t)}}{2}.
  \end{cases}

\end{align}
All entries of $\Lambdab^{(t+1)}$ can be updated simultaneously. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:12:19.519716+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c7571a266f85b589ccf766118c38d9203acb357b3b023c40c6228e18cd2d6ef3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 (Two-point decomposition) of arXiv:2608.18392, 'On Samuels' Conjecture'] For every $\nu\in \mathcal{M}(1)$, there exists a probability measure $\eta_\nu$ on $\Theta$ such that
