{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.729669+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c76a734d319a0d060bfefccb30eab5d495b93ea93b96af2af3e055f76840afcf","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2412.09290, 'Asymptotics of Harish-Chandra transform and infinitesimal freeness'] For a probability measure $\varrho$ on $\hat{U} (N)$, a \textbf{Schur generating function} $S_{\varrho}^{U (N)}$ is a symmetric Laurent
