{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-09-07T12:18:08.279390+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c782d691696bdd13f496ff4ff7b532ad11f07f1c2e3a4e30636f76ed1bfd7289","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 (Theorem 3.1.1 in \cite{de_la_Pena_Book}) of arXiv:2505.20799, 'A note on the improved sparse Hanson-Wright inequalities'] Let $F: \mathbb{R}^{+}\to \mathbb{R}^{+}$ be a convex function and $A=(a_{ij})_{n\times n}$ be a diagonal-free matrix. If $\{\xi_{i}, i\le n\}$ is a sequence of independent random variables and $\tilde{\xi}_{i}$ is an independent copy of $\xi_{i}$, then there exists a universal constant $C$ such that
