{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.248334+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c785463d40ee1a2549e2f7269665b8ad5f5fe6ba59fbeb383960a2f9b3fdd323","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma aprioricompact of arXiv:2507.10545, 'KPZ equation from a class of nonlinear SPDEs in infinite volume'] \fsp Fix {\small$\mathrm{L}>0$}. If {\small$\zeta,\zeta_{\mathrm{large}}=\mathrm{O}(1)$} are large enough, then with probability $1-\mathrm{o}(1)$, we have

