{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:01:01.835125+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c79d31a9918cc31e64768d588253327e7433da2d134235f5b737a82e069bbcf5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:scalar-powers-app of arXiv:2609.00556, 'Higgs--Demailly System and Positivity of Higgs Bundles'] Let \(x,y>0\) and \(0<\sigma\leq1\). Then
\begin{equation}
 (x-y)(x^\sigma-y^\sigma)\geq0.
\end{equation}
Moreover,
\begin{equation}
 \left(\frac yx-1\right)(y^\sigma-x^\sigma)
 \geq x^{-\sigma}|y^\sigma-x^\sigma|^2.
\end{equation}
Finally, if \(0<s\leq\sigma/2\) and \(0<x\leq1\), then
\begin{equation}
 0\leq
 \frac{s+\sigma/2}{s}(1-x^s)
 \leq x^{-\sigma/2}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.527367+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c7a1d16ba48b62cd9c280c73c9b67c00eb84886f550d6108fd1e3abe7ffb1c6b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 7 (Lemma 4.1.1 in \cite{exact}) of arXiv:2604.01748, 'Largest-loop-first loop-erased random walk on $\mathbb{Z}^{4}$'] Suppose that $\phi (n)$ satisfies the following two conditions (A1) and (A2).
