{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.055897+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c7a1e8d193ae9d2123eda62a612ac96b88bef2354ee99b7b9157843fa4c22944","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 17 (Regularity of $\psi_\circ$) of arXiv:2606.16636, 'Free energy of non-convex multi-species spin glasses with centered Ising spins'] The function $\psi_\circ$ given in~\eqref{e.psi_single=} can be extended to $\mcl Q_1$ and satisfies
\begin{align*}
    \Ll|\psi_\circ(q)-\psi_\circ(q')\Rr|\leq |q-q'|_{L^1},\quad\forall q,q'\in\mcl Q_1.
\end{align*}
The restriction $\psi_\circ:\mcl Q_2\to\R$ is Gateaux differentiable everywhere; we denote its Gateaux derivative by $\dr_q \psi_\circ(q) = \dr_q \psi_\circ(q, \cdot) \in L^2([0,1])$. We have, for every $q \in \mcl Q_2$,
\begin{equation}

\partial_q\psi_\circ(q) \in \mcl Q_{\infty,\leq 1},
\end{equation}
and, for every $q \in \mcl Q_\infty$ and $\pi \in L^2([0,1]; \R)$,  \begin{equation*}
\la \pi,\dr_q \psi_\circ(q)\ra_{L^2} = \E \la \pi \Ll(\alpha\wedge\alpha'\Rr)\tau\tau'\ra_{q}
\end{equation*}
where $\la\cdot\ra_q \propto  \exp\Ll(\sqrt{2}w^q(\alpha)\cdot \tau-q(1) \tau\tau\Rr)\d \fR(\alpha) \d P_{\{-1,1\}}(\tau)$, and $(\tau',\al')$ denotes an inpendent copy of the canonical random variable $(\tau,\al)$ under $\la \cdot \ra_q$.
Moreover, for every $r \in [1,+\infty]$ and $q, q' \in \mcl Q_2$ with $q-q' \in L^r$, we have
\begin{equation}

\Ll|\dr_q \psi_\circ(q) -\dr_q \psi_\circ(q')\Rr|_{L^r}\leq 16\Ll|q-q'\Rr|_{L^r}.
\end{equation}
In particular, the mapping $q \mapsto \dr_q \psi_\circ(q)$ can be extended to $\mcl Q_1$ by continuity, and the properties in \eqref{e.bound.der.psi} and \eqref{e.continuity.der.psi} remain valid with $q, q' \in \mcl Q_1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

