{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.667540+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c7daecf33fe5d4bd4a0a34b0de9f1db55bcdb59edb4d68f7cb6a12c0fc745c06","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 6 (Theorem 3.1 in \cite{MR0810975}) of arXiv:2604.24189, 'Malliavin calculus and densities for chaos-driven stochastic differential equations'] For $m\in \N^*$ and $1<p<\infty$, we have $\hat{\mathbb{D}}^{m,p}(\mathcal{U})=\mathbb{D}^{m,p}(\mathcal{U})$, and for any $F$ in this space, we have, for a.e. $\omega\in\Omega$, and for any $h\in \HHH$,
