then \((Y_n)\) is uniformly integrable, \(\mathbb{E} Y=1\), and \(\mathbb{P}(Y>0)>0\). If \(\mathbb{E}[W\log_2 W]\ge1\), then \(Y=0\) almost surely. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

