{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.829695+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c7fd8cccfcea648bb472500c456e1be920b625b2e3b4d868cbff2037848a273b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:affine-pgf of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] For the unaugmented scalar counting path $N$, the Marcus signature collapses to
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{Sig}^M(N)_{0,T}=\exp_{\otimes}(N_T e_1).
\end{equation}
Consequently, its expected signature is determined by the moment generating function
\begin{equation}
M(T,\theta)=\mathbb{E}[e^{\theta N_T}].
\end{equation}
For the exponential Hawkes model, $M$ has the affine representation
\begin{equation}
M(T,\theta)=\exp\{A(T,\theta)+B(T,\theta)\ell\},
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
\frac{\partial B}{\partial T}= -\beta B+e^{\theta+\alpha B}-1,
\qquad
\frac{\partial A}{\partial T}=\beta\mu B,
\qquad
A(0,\theta)=B(0,\theta)=0.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.290621+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c8028e6d82f4de4a295cb5e8813c8815181ea59751216a8a971a22d5c2a1b2d0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 26 of arXiv:2606.23099, 'Path-dependent Affine Processes'] Let $q\in\N$, and let $F:\ccC_T^d\to \R^q$
    be a continuous non-anticipative functional. Assume that there exists a constant
    $C>0$ such that
    \begin{equation*}
        \|F(t,x)\|
        \leq C \biggl(1+\sup_{s\in[0,t]}\|x(s)\|\biggr), \quad (t,x)\in\ccC_T^d .
    \end{equation*}
    Then there exist continuous non-anticipative functionals
    \begin{equation*}
        F^n:\ccC_T^d\to\R^q,\quad n\in\N,
    \end{equation*}
    such that the following properties hold.

    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $F^n\to F$ locally uniformly on $\ccC_T^d$.

        \item For each $n\in\N$, $F^n$ is Lipschitz continuous with respect
              to the metric $d_{\ccC_T}$.

        \item There exists a constant $C'>0$, independent of $n$, such that
              \begin{equation*}
                  \|F^n(t,x)\|
                  \leq C'\biggl(1+\sup_{s\in[0,t]}\|x(s)\|\biggr),
                  \quad (t,x)\in\ccC_T^d,\ n\in\N .
              \end{equation*}
    \end{enumerate}

    In particular, for each $n\in\N$ and each fixed $t\in[0,T]$, there
    exists a constant $L_n>0$ such that
    \begin{equation*}
        \|F^n(t,x)-F^n(t,y)\|
        \leq L_n \sup_{s\in[0,t]}\|x(s)-y(s)\|,
        \quad x,y\in C([0,t],\R^d).
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.887100+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c80cfd7fb362e4ee0757cce073323858f2b731819079bc1110d9b09ff8c08a34","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 10 (Intersection of cells at small intensities) of arXiv:2504.02435, 'Poisson-Voronoi percolation in higher rank'] Let $G$ be a connected higher rank semisimple real Lie group and $(X,d_X)$ be its symmetric space.
    Then for every $\eps>0$ and $R>0$ there is $\lambda_0\in (0,1]$ such that 
