        \inf_{0<\lambda\le \lambda_0} \mathbb{P} \Big( \text{all cells at intensity } \lambda, \text{ which intersect } \mathcal B_R(o), \text{pairwise share a boundary}  \Big)>1-\eps.
    \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:32:23.811474+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c80f0840a7df29341feca19216bd46d1a1726dfd531b444f793101c001574a64","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma prop_cons_of_energy of arXiv:2603.26307, '\LARGE The incompressible Navier--Stokes--Fourier system with thermal noise'] Let Assumption (Ass:noise of the paper) hold, $(\Omega,\mathfrak{A},\mathbb{P})$ be a probability space equipped with a filtration $\mathscr{F}$ satisfying the usual conditions and $3$-dimensional standard $\mathscr{F}$-Brownian motions $(W_n)_{n\in \mathbb{Z}^3}$ and $3\times 3$-matrix valued $\mathscr{F}$-Brownian motions $(B_n)_{n\in \mathbb{Z}^3}$ with covariance structure (equation Eq_noise_matrix_covariation of the paper) be independent. Then, any local strong solution $(U,\Psi)$ to (equation Eq_new_var of the paper), defined up to a stopping time $\tau>0$, satisfies 
	\begin{equation}
		\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{T}^3}   |U_t|^2 + |\Psi_t |^2\,\mathrm{d} x \,=\, 	\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{T}^3}   |U_0|^2 + |\Psi_0 |^2\,\mathrm{d} x,
	\end{equation}
	for all $t\in [0,\tau)$, $\mathbb{P}$-almost surely. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.963061+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c81176b746a1b7bed1ac8c010df0e2adf0a71fa1536799b3e9a048cb2d6513e0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 20 of arXiv:2608.12291, 'When should one stop the most exciting game?\\ {\tiny Sequential Inference for win-marting'] Let $T<\infty$. For every $t\in[0,T]$ the map $x\mapsto V_T(t,x)$ is $\llip{(0,1)}$. Specifically, for the optimal stopping time $\tau^* :=\tau^*_T(t,x)$, 
    \begin{equation}
        \partial_x V_T(t,x)=\mathbb{E}\left[g'(X^x_{\tau^*})\partial_x X^x_{\tau^*}\right],
    \end{equation}
    for almost every $x\in(0,1)$. In particular, for $x,y\in[a,b]\subset(0,1)$,
    \begin{equation}
        |V_T(t,x)-V_T(t,y)|\leq K_\text{space}|x-y|,
    \end{equation}
    where $K_\text{space}:=\|g'\|_\infty$ under Assumption \ref{asmp:bounded:g'}, and there exists an interval $[A,B]\subset(0,1)$ independent of $t$ and $T$ such that $K_\text{space}:=\|g'\|_{L^\infty([a,b]\cup[A,B])}<\infty$ if Assumption \ref{asmp:bounded:c} holds.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.762794+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c826e7a86d36db4d3ebf7985947e2f903e131842f092ad737916f73ed7bb468d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t1.1 of arXiv:2411.19255, 'Moderate, large and super large deviations principles for Poisson process with uniform cat'] Let the scaling $\varphi(T)$ satisfies the condition ((15.11.2024-1 of the paper)). 
