{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.615503+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c82b497e8b51669c691dd3412731b1d7f54a442ca3f5f6b5d1a60cda9853e1fc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2604.22644, '2604.22644'] For $0 < q < 1$,
\begin{align}
    E[q^{\theta_1} I(e_1 \text{ does not reach } N)] = \frac{q}{2} + \int_0^1 p q b(1;p) dp,
\end{align}
where $b(k;p)$ is the unique solution to the following linear boundary value problem:
\begin{align}
    b(k;p) = q r^k p b(k+1;p) + q (1 - r^k p) b(k-1;p), \quad k = 1, 2, \dots, N-1,
\end{align}
with boundary conditions $b(0;p) = 1$ and $b(N;p) = 0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.820311+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c82c66011f5232eb62b121bf013c913aeb92fc5520acc07023b6bf565d8a5f91","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def-frac-Gaus-field of arXiv:2411.09614, 'Moment estimates for the stochastic heat equation on Cartan-Hadamard manifolds'] Consider  $\alpha>0$ and the following Hilbert space of space-time functions:
\begin{align}
\mathcal{H}_\alpha=L^2(\mathbb{R}_+, \mathcal{W}^{-\alpha}(M)),  
\end{align}
    where $\mathcal{W}^{-\alpha}(M)$ is the Sobolev space introduced in Definition (sobo_def of the paper). On a complete probability space $(\Omega, \mathcal{G},\mathbf{P})$ we define a centered Gaussian family $\{W(\phi); \phi\in \mathcal{H}_\alpha\}$, whose covariance is given by 
\begin{align}
\mathbf E\left[ W(\varphi) W(\psi)\right]
=&
\int_{\mathbb{R}_+}\ \left\langle \varphi (t,\cdot) , \psi (t,\cdot)\right\rangle_{\mathcal{W}^{-\alpha}(M)}  dt \notag\\
=&
\int_{\mathbb{R}_+} \int_{M^2} \varphi (t,x)  \psi (t,y)G_{2\alpha}(x,y)dxdy dt
\, ,
\end{align}
for $\varphi$, $\psi$ in $\mathcal{H}_\alpha$. This family is called the fractional Gaussian fields on $M$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.244462+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c82c9f12432358c7e9b08a303814e263c05b86d0f4e9d527bf9a52437d150855","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: fixed point CLT_fixed m of arXiv:2604.23890, 'The Cutoff Profile for Random Transpositions on Repeated Cards in the Full Range of Parame'] Let $n=ml$, such that $m\ge 2$ is fixed and $l=\omega(1)$. Suppose $
