{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.360627+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c83d7dc8517aa86ee3af360dbcb3a201648afb51b6db8aa30d08f612a508d771","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:entropy:symmetry of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] Suppose $\nu \in \mathcal{M}_{2, d}$ is absolutely continuous with respect to Lebesgue measure. Let $\psi_\nu^n$ be defined as in (equation eq:entropy:2reconstruction of the paper). Then $\psi_\nu^n$ is a 2-MRF on $(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{V_n}$, and can be formulated equivalently in the following ways:
