{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:08.952537+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c8785e9fdd41da8f893ff372ab29970c9c333b97a437061b0dfa5e0d53465ec0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:pointwise_measure_chain of arXiv:2609.01576, '\normalfont Pointwise Majorization for sub-Weibull and Mixed Tail Processes with Applicati'] Let $K\subset T$ be finite and contain $t_0$, let
$d_K:=d|_{K\times K}$, and let $\nu$ be a probability measure on $K$
such that $\nu(\cbr{t_0})\ge\frac12$. For $t\in K$ and $n\ge0$, define
\begin{align*}
r_n(t)
:=
\min\cbr{
r\in\cbr{d_K(t,s):s\in K}:
\nu(B_{d_K}(t,r))\ge2^{-2^n}
}.
\end{align*}
Then, there exists an admissible sequence
$\cT=(T_n)_{n\ge0}$ of subsets of $K$ such that
$T_0=\cbr{t_0}$, $T_n=K$ for all sufficiently large $n$, and, for
every $t\in K$,
\begin{align*}
G_{\cT}(t):=
\sum_{n\ge0}2^{n/\alpha}d_K(t,T_n)\le
v(t)
+
\kappa_\alpha
\int_0^{r_0(t)}
\left(
\log\frac{1}{\nu(B_{d_K}(t,r))}
\right)^{1/\alpha}dr,
\end{align*}
where
\begin{align*}
\kappa_\alpha
:=
\frac{2^{1+1/\alpha}}
{(\log2)^{1/\alpha}(1-2^{-1/\alpha})}.
\end{align*}
Moreover, $r_0(t)\le v(t)$ for every $t\in K$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.067396+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c882f658010f38ca89190b0ebee93921283fe3ef36d3883ba39b7babd1c1781c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 14 ($a+b=1$, moments) of arXiv:2606.00781, '2606.00781'] If $a+b=1$ then the moments of the stationary distribution $\mu$ are given by
