{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:52.655323+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c8871ee8922284738cfa8a78287a585f63e13fca6d7ca8ba72287252aeed817e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 20 of arXiv:2609.03713, 'A Sharp Mass Threshold for Boundedness in a Critical Quasilinear Chemotaxis Model with Ind'] The potential $E_d*\zeta^{1/(m-1)}$ of $\zeta^{1/(m-1)}$ is given by
\begin{equation}
    \big(E_d*\zeta^{1/(m-1)}\big)(x) = \frac{m}{m-1} \zeta(x) + \frac{2-m}{m-1} \frac{I_\zeta}{M_c}\,, \quad x\in\mathbb{B}_1\,, 
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
   \big(E_d*\zeta^{1/(m-1)}\big)(x) = \frac{M_c}{(d-2)\sigma_d} \frac{1}{|x|^{d-2}}\,, \quad x\in\mathbb{R}^d\setminus\mathbb{B}_1\,,  
