{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.667631+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c88b2b6a01378e0f21905dfffda9743412fc825b780946ac018de9ec6649245f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 7 of arXiv:2604.24189, 'Malliavin calculus and densities for chaos-driven stochastic differential equations'] For every $g\in \mathfrak{H}$, there exist two events $\Omega_g^\prime \subseteq \Omega_g$ with $\mathbb{P}(\Omega_g^\prime)=\mathbb{P}(\Omega_g)=1$ and a random variable $\widetilde{X}_g$ such that
