{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:12:19.464584+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c8ab886b67252904793b1a718561031c27f532ebe02fa81dcdc169f93a0a3316","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 17 (First- and second-order Komatsu estimates) of arXiv:2608.17540, 'Pathwise stability for one-dimensional SDEs driven by Brownian motion and a symmetric stab'] There exists $C=C(\alpha,\varphi)>0$ such that, for all $x\in\R$, $\delta\ge2$, and $\eps\in(0,1)$,
\begin{align}
|u_{\delta,\eps}'(x)|
&\le C\left(|x|^{\alpha-2}\1_{\{|x|>2\eps\}}
+\frac{\delta}{\eps^{2-\alpha}\log\delta}\1_{\{|x|\le2\eps\}}\right), \\
|u_{\delta,\eps}'(x)|\,|x|
&\le C\left(|x|^{\alpha-1}+\frac{\delta}{\log\delta}\eps^{\alpha-1}\right), \\
|u_{\delta,\eps}''(x)|
&\le C\left(|x|^{\alpha-3}\1_{\{|x|>2\eps\}}
+\frac{\delta^2}{\eps^{3-\alpha}\log\delta}\1_{\{|x|\le2\eps\}}\right), \\
|u_{\delta,\eps}''(x)|x^2
&\le C\left(|x|^{\alpha-1}+\frac{\delta^2}{\log\delta}\eps^{\alpha-1}\right). 
\end{align}
In particular,
\begin{equation}
  \|u_{\delta,\eps}'\|_\infty\le C\frac{\delta}{\eps^{2-\alpha}\log\delta},
  \qquad
  \|u_{\delta,\eps}''\|_\infty\le C\frac{\delta^2}{\eps^{3-\alpha}\log\delta}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

