{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.369775+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c8bd0472bc41eb52dcc2a71764d3114a7d18f49ce80c974f22481db1c4120979","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition guessing strategy symmetry of arXiv:2507.10294, 'Guessing Strategies for Shelf-Shuffling Machines'] We have $I_j^*=I_{n-j+1}^*$ for all $1\leq j\leq n$, that is, the best guesses in position $j$ and in position $n-j+1$ are the same.
