{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:30:14.217177+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c8bf284d9c35c380e752e7e18baff6f6772faa49f590bf2b2f77471355f698b3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:dbar-gap of arXiv:2608.19358, 'An optimal Poincaré inequality\\for the complex Ginibre log-gas'] For all $n\geq1$ and $g\in\mathcal{C}^\infty_c(\mathbb{C}^n,\mathbb{C})$, 
