is called the $\mathbb{H}$-valued normal Gaussian variable associated
to $Z_{1}$ and $Z_{2}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.122835+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c8f33741cf01ca82154853a66e9d580e7f8ae452f977e78a81394ad6439461b2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:free-Poisson-moments of arXiv:2608.18293, 'Critical tensor covariance at the Marchenko--Pastur threshold'] The limiting measure $\mu_{c,\lambda,v}$ is the free compound-Poisson law with
rate $1/c$ and jump distribution $\operatorname{Law}(cR)$. For every $k\ge1$ it has the
finite moment
\begin{equation}
  M_k=\int t^k\,\mu_{c,\lambda,v}(\,\mathrm{d} t)
  =\sum_{\pi\in\mathrm{NC}(k)}c^{k-|\pi|}
  \prod_{V\in\pi}\mathbb{E} R^{|V|}.

\end{equation}
Equivalently, its free cumulants are
\begin{equation}
  \kappa_k=c^{k-1}\mathbb{E} R^k
  =c^{k-1}\exp\!\left(\frac{k(k-1)}2\lambda v\right).

\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.597638+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c8f4341fdd95a7e61c5a5dea9323aebc2a9ded8e9642b27020c545773c19528d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 18 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] Assume that Assumption~\ref{ass:joint-minorization} holds and that the multiplicative drift condition \eqref{eq:regenerative-drift} is satisfied. Then there exists $\theta_1>0$ such that, for the split chain started from the atom,

\begin{equation*}
\Ee_{\mathfrak a}\left[\exp\{\theta_1(L_1+|Y_1|_1)\}\right]<\infty.
\end{equation*}

Consequently all polynomial moment assumptions imposed on $L_1$ and $Y_1$ in this paper are satisfied. If a transition reward $g$ satisfies

\begin{equation*}
|g(x,y,k)|\leq c_g(1+|k|_1)
\end{equation*}

for some finite constant $c_g$, then

\begin{equation*}
\Ee_{\mathfrak a}\left[\exp\{\theta_2 R_1^*(g)\}\right]<\infty
\end{equation*}

for some $\theta_2>0$. In particular, the reward moment assumptions used in the functional inverse theorem hold, and the one-cycle reward measures used in the regenerative lattice proof are exponentially summable. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:25:44.973343+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c8fbd2c2b7fb940777bea1ec9841d3df24af4b2614226946540c4c3291398f40","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 25 (Dirichlet append step) of arXiv:2605.11451, '2605.11451'] Let $Y$ be a projection generated by a $d$-dimensional $p$-ball through the sign-Dirichlet representation. Appending one coordinate with coefficient $c\ge0$ gives
