 \widetilde Y=(1-T)^\alpha Y+cT^\alpha\eps,
\end{equation}
where $\eps$ is a Rademacher sign and
\[
 T\sim\operatorname{Beta}(\alpha,1+d\alpha)
\]
is independent of $Y$ and $\eps$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.120392+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c90386a20e016b4132303eff497b0ffa9c10aa0f06016ed23189699bd78ee873","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def: def of good external field configuration event for cle singularity of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] Recall the definitions of  $\mathsf{a}_i(\tau),\mathsf{b}_i(\tau),\mathsf{c}_i(\tau), \mathsf{d}_i(\tau), \mathcal{F}_i(\tau)$ from Proposition~(prop: adding external field fluctuation of the paper). Recall that we have chosen $\kappa=10^{-5}.$ We define the event $\mathcal{A}_i\subset\mathbb{R}^{\Lambda_N}\otimes\{0,1\}^n$ to be the collection of pairs $(h,\tau)$ such that $$|\mathsf{a}_i(\tau)-\mathsf{b}_i(\tau)-\mathsf{c}_i(\tau)-\mathsf{d}_i(\tau)|\le ({\epsilon} M^{\frac{7}{8}})^{2.7}\mbox{  and  }|\mathsf{a}_i(\tau)|\le ({\epsilon} M^{\frac{7}{8}})^{0.9}$$ and let $\mathcal{A}=\cap_{i=1}^n\mathcal{A}_i$.  In addition, we define the following events \begin{equation*}
    \begin{aligned}
        \mathcal{B}&=\{(h,\tau):\sum_{i=1}^{n}(\frac{\mathsf{b}_i^2}{2}-\mathsf{b}_i)\ge c_7{\epsilon}^2M^{\frac{7}{4}}|\tau| +\sum_{i=1}^n\frac{{\mathbb{E}}\big(\mathsf{b}_i^2\mid \mathcal{F}_{i-1}\big)}{4} \},\\
    \mathcal{A}^*&=\{(h,\tau):|\sum_{i=1}^{n}(\mathsf{a}_i^2-\mathsf{b}_i^2)|\le 1\},
    \\
    \mathcal{C}&=\{(h,\tau):|\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathsf{c}_i|\le 1\},~~~~
    \mathcal{D}=\Big\{(h,\tau):|\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathsf{d}_i|\le \sqrt{\iota^{-2\kappa}\cdot \sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_i^2}\Big\}.
    \end{aligned}
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:52.738525+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c9065a3f5774bb1ba28ae2f421ff0bd8da310033833ebb4f70044bf78b828410","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 22 of arXiv:2506.10476, 'Construction of ergodic \textsc{idla} forests in $\mathbb{Z}^d$'] There exist positive universal constants $b,\ K_0,\ c$ such that for all real numbers $r>0$ and all $z\in\mathcal{H}$ with $0\notin \mathbb{B}(z_{n+1},r)$,
	\begin{multline*}
		\mathbb{P}\left(Z=z,\ \Over^*_{\alpha}(M_{n+1},\varepsilon_{n+1})\cap\Over^*_{\alpha}(M_{n},\varepsilon_{n})^c,\ \#\left(A_{Z^*}\cap \mathbb{B}(z_{n+1},r)\right)\leq br^d\right)
		\leq K_0e^{-cr^2}.
	\end{multline*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:34:33.546233+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c91a33dd26e09647913750e6546827f782fc3bb7eb98c96a2c77f6129815e8c5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2603.29446, 'Law of large numbers for stochastic multiscale spatial gene networks'] Let $0\leq \alpha, \beta, \gamma\leq 1$, satisfying one of the following assumptions
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(i)] If $1/2<\alpha\vee\beta\leq 1$, and $\gamma< \alpha\wedge\beta$, 
\item[(ii)] If $\alpha\vee\beta\leq 1/2$, and $\gamma < \alpha+\beta-1/2$, 
\end{enumerate}
Then, there exists $C>0$ such that for all $u,v\in H_N$,
$\|uv\|_{H_N^\gamma} \leq C  \|u\|_{H_N^\alpha}\|v\|_{H_N^\beta}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:29:08.756412+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c922a63e72120ffdba4695ccb5ddec16b558dd2cc9540ccc4b7e89d173f92e11","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem ratesHaarU of arXiv:2412.00593, 'A new approach to strong convergence II.\\The classical ensembles'] There exists a linear functional $\mu_m$ on $\mathcal{P}$ for every $m\in\mathbb{Z}_+$ 
such that for every $q\in\mathbb{N}$ and $h\in \mathcal{P}_q$
\begin{equation}

	|\mu_m(h)| 
	\le 
	\bigg(
	(C\tilde q\tilde q_0)^m
	+\frac{(C\tilde q\tilde q_0)^{2m}}{m!} 
	\bigg)
	\sobnorm{h}{0}{[-K, K]},
\end{equation}
and such that for all $N\in\mathbb{N}$
\begin{equation}

	\left| \mathbf{E}[\mathop{\textnormal{tr}} h(X^N)]- \sum_{k=0}^{m-1} \frac{\mu_k(h)}{N^k} 
	\right| \leq 
	\frac{1}{N^m}
	\bigg(
	(C\tilde q\tilde q_0)^m
	+\frac{(C\tilde q\tilde q_0)^{2m}}{m!} 
	\bigg)
	\sobnorm{h}{0}{[-K, K]}.
\end{equation}
Here $C$ is a universal constant,
$\tilde q:=q(1+\log q)$, and $\tilde q_0:=q_0(1+\log q_0)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.375222+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c925b02c6daf9f00aa683c52c525a5f9a4a435d43ad097885e31851217b61925","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 8 of arXiv:2606.04636, 'A Thomson-type variational principle for diffusion coefficients'] Let $D$ be the diffusion coefficient of the Bertini-Toninelli
model, defined via the transition rates given in equation (\ref{eq:c_BT}).
Then the following lower bounds hold:
\begin{eqnarray*}
D & \ge & \frac{2q}{1+q},\\
D & \ge & \frac{9q^{2}}{7-4q+6q^{2}},\\
D & \ge & \frac{1}{5000}pq^{9}.
\end{eqnarray*}
In particular $D\neq0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.744831+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c93ec62aef0fbad9ce413a077146c7ff37c3352af5dc1977660769e88ea2ba55","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conj ConjHP of arXiv:2605.06429, '\large \bf $\mathsf{GL}_N(\mathbb{C})$ BROWNIAN MOTION AND STOCHASTIC PDE ON ENTIRE FUNCTI'] Let $\mathfrak{s} > -\tfrac{1}{2}$ and $\mathfrak{hp}_0\overset{\mathrm{d}}{=}\mathbb{HP}_\mathfrak{s}$. Then, the reciprocals $(\mathsf{y}_{i}(\bullet))_{i\in \mathbb{Z}\backslash\{0\}}$ of zeroes of $\mathfrak{hp}_{\bullet}$ satisfy the equation
\begin{equation*}
\mathrm{d}\mathsf{y}_i(t)
= \sqrt{2}\mathsf{y}_i(t)\mathrm{d}\mathsf{w}_i(t)
- 2\mathfrak{s}\mathsf{y}_i(t)\mathrm{d}t
+ 2 \lim_{\varepsilon\to 0}
\sum_{\substack{|\mathsf{y}_j(t)|>\varepsilon\\ j\in \mathbb{Z}\setminus\{0,i\}}}
\frac{\mathsf{y}_i(t)\mathsf{y}_j(t)}{\mathsf{y}_i(t)-\mathsf{y}_j(t)}\mathrm{d}t, \ \ \forall {i}\in \mathbb{Z}\backslash \{0\}.
\end{equation*} (Stated as a conjecture by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.748959+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c948e55116a8b2d1de5f9160d27d4c24297ef5406d5bb20841aa7ac36dc45769","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:well_posed of arXiv:2608.30493, '\bf McKean-Vlasov Differential Equations:\\ {An introduction and a focus on some kinetic m'] We say that MKV$({\bf b},{\boldsymbol\sigma})$ is:
\begin{itemize}
