{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.309480+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c97c73689d1f5c7634f54525f9a5b5ed55dad5a8c4432c446485ae89c7c9ae76","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 100 of arXiv:2510.22155, 'Random walks in space-time random media in all spatial dimensions: the full subcritical fl'] Consider any adapted sequence of random variables $(X_n)_{n\ge 0}$ defined on any filtered probability space $(\Omega, (\mathcal F_r)_{r\in \mathbb Z_{\ge 0}}, P),$ with $M_0=0$. Assume that we have $\mathcal E_{\lambda_0} (M;P):=\sup_{n\ge 1} \| E [e^{4\lambda_0|X_{n+1} -X_n|}|\mathcal F_n] \big\|_{L^\infty(\Omega,\mathcal F,P)}<\infty,$ for some $\lambda_0>0$. Then for $|\lambda|<\lambda_0$ we have that 
\begin{equation}E[ e^{\lambda X_r}] \leq E\bigg[ \prod_{s=0}^{r-1} E[e^{2\lambda (X_{s+1}-X_s)}|\mathcal F_s]\bigg]^{1/2}.
\end{equation}
If in particular $X$ is a martingale, then for $|\lambda|<\lambda_0$ we have that 
\begin{align}
     \notag E[ e^{\lambda X_r}] &\leq E\bigg[ \prod_{s=0}^{r-1} \big( 1+4 \lambda^2 \mathcal E_{\lambda_0}(M,P)^{1/2}  E[|X_{s+1}-X_s|^4|\mathcal F_s]^{1/2}\big)\bigg]^{1/2} \\& \leq E\bigg[e^{4 \lambda^2 \mathcal E_{\lambda_0}(M,P)^{1/2}\sum_{s=0}^{r-1}  E\big[|X_{s+1}-X_s|^4\big|\mathcal F_s\big]^{1/2}}\bigg]^{1/2}
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

