{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.489563+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c9de5b01e256b33e24755918d5e025e8d0de3fe65347c513f8bb70bfc2ca9e51","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 211 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Adopt the assumptions of Theorem~\ref{Theorem_Master_equation_12}, assume that $\boldsymbol{E}(z)/\sigma(z)$ is tame, and let $\boldsymbol{\kappa}$ vary in a fixed compact of $\amsmathbb{C}^H$.

