	\end{flalign*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.761506+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c9f6d87953882d6c66da81ffd45ae8a092c25460edb525680afd3cdacaf2966b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lmm DtC of arXiv:2609.02682, 'LDP for tensor forms'] Suppose $D_n$ is a zero-diagonal real-valued function on $[n]^v$. Then
\begin{align}
 &\sup_{\{{\tau_i}^\ell\in [0,1] :i\in [n], \ell \in [v]\}}\left| \sum_{(i_1,\ldots,i_v)\in [n]^v}D_n(i_1,\ldots,i_v)\prod_{r=1}^v \tau^r_{i_r}\right|=\sup_{\{{\beta_i}^\ell\in \{0,1\} :i\in [n], \ell \in [v]\}}\left|\sum_{(i_1,\ldots,i_v)\in [n]^v}D_n(i_1,\ldots,i_v) \prod_{r=1}^v\beta^r_{i_r} \right|,\\
