\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.735227+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c9f8d5a723787546be2885322758a4fd9315cc900b4d74334316495d24536dc5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem_loc of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] Under (main_assm of the paper), for any small constant $\tau>0$, the following local laws hold uniformly in $z=E+\mathrm{i}\eta $ with $|z|\le \tau^{-1}$ and $ \eta \ge N^{-1+\tau}$. 
\begin{itemize}
    \item  \textnormal{\textbf{Anisotropic local law:}} For any deterministic unit vectors $\mathbf{u}, \mathbf{v}\in \mathbb{C}^{DN}$, we have
\begin{equation}
 \left(G(z)-M(z)\right)_{\mathbf{u}\mathbf{v}}\prec \sqrt{\frac{\im m(z)}{N\eta}}+\frac{1}{N\eta}.
\end{equation}

\item  \textnormal{\textbf{Averaged local law:}} For any deterministic matrix $B \in \mathbb{C}^{DN\times DN}$ with $\|B\|\le 1$, we have 
\begin{equation}
 \left\langle \left(G-M\right) B\right\rangle \prec \frac{1}{ N\eta } .
\end{equation}

\end{itemize}
As a consequence of (equation eq:aver_local of the paper) when $B=I$, we have the rigidity of eigenvalues:
\begin{equation}
\lvert \lambda_k-\gamma_k \rvert \prec N^{-2/3}\mathfrak{r}\left({k}\right)^{-1/3},\quad \forall 1\le k\le DN. 
\end{equation}
In addition, all the above estimates remain valid even if we do not assume identical distributions for the diagonal and off-diagonal entries of $H$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:39:41.407094+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c9fb4a872cb17dd556a9d8e811c04cafd729bd09e4a7e9c5c2a72144afb76e1e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 7 of arXiv:2604.06532, 'Random permutations from $q$-Demazure products'] The shock curve $\mathcal{V}(v)$
