{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:20:07.902404+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca2761af149e504283f0062f0578891fd8564cebf3c88c668420b9c288a486d7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:p1:locallinearrate of arXiv:2608.23765, '\texorpdfstring{Tight Majorizations and Convergence Rates\\ of Nuclear Norm Minimization I'] Let $\mathbf{X}_\star \in \mathbb{R}^{d_1 \times d_2}$ have rank $r$.
	Assume that the measurement operator 
	$\mathcal{A}: \mathbb{R}^{d_1 \times d_2} \longrightarrow \R^m $ 
	satisfies the NSP of order $r$ with constant $0<\eta_r<3/5$
	and that 
	$ \mathbf{y} = \mathcal{A} \left(  \mathbf{X}_\star \right) $.
	Let the IRLS iterates  
	$\left\{   \mathbf{X}^{(k)} \right\}_k$ and $ \left\{ \varepsilon_{k} \right\}_k$ 
	be defined by (eq:IRLS:step_1 of the paper) and (eq:IRLS:step_2 of the paper) 
	with rank estimate $\widetilde r=r$ and with fixed $q$-power mean weight operators for some $q\in[-1,0)$, and assume that (alg:algo1 of the paper) does not return in iteration $k$, i.e., that $\varepsilon_k > 0$, so that the iterate $\mathbf{X}^{(k+1)}$ is defined.
	Assume that
	\begin{equation}
	    \nucnorm{\mathbf{X}^{(k)} - \mathbf{X}_\star}  
		\le  
		\frac{  \sigma_r ( \mathbf{X}_\star ) }{\max \left( \eta_1 \sqrt{d}, 2 \right)}. 
    \end{equation}
	where $0 < \eta_1 \leq \eta_r$ denotes again the order-one NSP constant of $\mathcal{A}$. Set
	\begin{equation*}
	K_{\eta_r,q}
	:=
	2+2^{-1/q}+
	\frac{(3+\eta_r)^2(1+\eta_r)\left(\frac{3}{2}+\eta_r\right)}{(1-\eta_r)^3}
	\end{equation*}
	and
	\begin{equation*}
	\widehat c_{\eta_r,q}
	:=
	\frac{(3-5\eta_r)^{2}}{16(1+\eta_r)^{2}(3+2\eta_r)K_{\eta_r,q}}.
	\end{equation*}
	Then it holds that
	\begin{equation}
		\mathcal{J}_{\varepsilon_{k+1}}( \mathbf{X}^{(k+1)} ) -  \nucnorm{\mathbf{X}_\star} 
	\le 
    \left(
	1-  \widehat c_{\eta_r,q} \right)
	\left(     \mathcal{J}_{\varepsilon_{k}} \left( \mathbf{X}^{(k)}  \right) -  \nucnorm{ \mathbf{X}_\star } \right).
	\end{equation}
	In particular, for the harmonic-mean weight operator, i.e., $q=-1$, this implies the same estimate with
	\begin{equation*}
	c_{\eta_r}
	=
	\frac{(3-5\eta_r)^{2}(1-\eta_r)^{3}}{8(1+\eta_r)^{2}(3+2\eta_r)\Bigl[8(1-\eta_r)^{3}+(3+\eta_r)^{2}(1+\eta_r)(3+2\eta_r)\Bigr]}
	\end{equation*}
	in place of $\widehat c_{\eta_r,-1}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:23:27.787739+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca28cf0646f9bb92376784727f0c0d62112f06dcbf6c09cd038a3831e6adddc9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm clt:Wiener of arXiv:2606.09228, 'On topological indices of random caterpillar graphs'] For all $n \in {\mathbb N}$ and $m \ge 2$ we have
    \begin{align}
