    \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:00:30.496472+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca29423cbe0ae0ff190a2642d26025633ba0026fb0c82d248d0dee16ec27dba8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 (Gaussian Correlation Inequality) of arXiv:2607.04193, 'Onsager--Machlup Functionals for Generalized Newtonian Equations of Motion with Time-Varyi'] Let $\mu$ be a centered Radon Gaussian measure on a separable Banach space $E$. For any two $\mu$-measurable, symmetric, and convex sets $C_1, C_2 \subseteq E$, the following inequality holds:
