\]
where the constant $C > 0$ only depends on $d$. Furthermore, conditional on $\mathcal{X}_{k-1}$, $F_k$ and $B_k$ are independent, and it holds that
\[  \tag{3.2.29}
F_k + B_k \geq_{\mathrm{st}} d  \mathsf{Bin} \left( n - C \sum_{\ell = 1}^{d-1} \max_{\rho \in S_{\ell - 1}(\mathcal{X}_{k-1})} \deg_{\ell - 1, d-1}^{\mathcal{X}_{k-1}}(\rho), \min\{p_k^F, p_k^B\} \right).
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.570022+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca4e431c25dcccd57777575e8958a6dce8521748d10748cd8f4ec906e6ad5fd5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:basic} and \ref{ass:rand_ent}, let $E_*$ be a regular right edge in the sense of Definition~\ref{def:reg_r_edge}. Then, for any sufficiently small $\tau>0$, uniformly for $z=E+\ii\eta\in\mb D_*^{\eps_*}(\tau)$,
