{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.713875+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cadc0fbc1c9215257acd2e6e15f4fde9e83f635a4e790aed966cc6d6a3b8e714","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem l:104.4 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] Let $W$ be a standard Gaussian, $Y, Y'$ be random variables taking values in some measurable space $\mathcal Y$ and independent of $W$, and 
