where $C_{j,l}>0$ is a constant depending only on $j$ and $l$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:43:45.379953+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cae3f5bd7858c51e3801690968300bfab495809c110480c41424348c8ff28149","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2609.04033, 'From configuration spaces to graph complexes via $\mathbf{FA}$-modules'] Consider $H_c^\ast(F(S^1\vee S^1),n)$ as a $S_n\times D_{12}$-module, by inclusion of the dihedral group of order 12 in $GL_2(\mathbb{Z})$.  There exist isomorphisms of graded symmetric sequences:
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item $H^{\ast+1}(\mathsf{gr}_2(\mathsf{FT}_\Gamma))\oplus \mathsf{W}_{\pm} 
		\cong H_c^{\ast}(F(S^1\vee S^1),-)\tensor_{D_{12}} V_{120}$	
		\item $H^{\ast+2}(\mathsf{gr}_1(\mathsf{FT}_\Gamma)) \cong  H_c^\ast(F(S^1\vee S^1),-)\tensor_{D_{12}} (\chi_s \oplus V_{120} ) \oplus \mathsf{W}_{\pm}$	
		\item  $H^{\ast+3}(\mathsf{gr}_0(\mathsf{FT}_\Gamma))\cong H_c^\ast(F(S^1\vee S^1),-)\tensor_{D_{12}} \chi_s$	
	\end{enumerate}
where $\chi_s$ is the 1-dimensional representation fixed by rotation generator $r$ and alternating on reflection generator $s$, $V_{120}$ is the 2-dimensional irreducible in which $r$ corresponds to $120^\circ$ rotation, and $\mathsf{W}_{\pm}$ is a $\mathbb{Z}_2$ graded sum of Whitehouse modules $\mathsf{W}_{n,\ast}$ concentrated in degrees $n$ and $n-1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.470080+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_caf0eec501e758f0003539a9db7f7b941aa9674adc11d93bc14c61ca0d39c618","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 84 (Deformation tensors) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] Let $Z$ be a spacetime vectorfield.
We define the \emph{deformation tensor} $\deform{Z}$  of $Z$ 
(with respect to $\gfour$)
to be the following symmetric type $\binom{0}{2}$ tensorfield:
\begin{align} 
\deformarg{Z}{\alpha}{\beta} 
& 
\eqdef \Lie_Z \gfour_{\alpha \beta} 
= 
\Dfour_\alpha Z_\beta + \Dfour_\alpha Z_\beta,
\end{align}
where the final equality in \eqref{E:DEFORMATIONTENSORDEF} follows from the torsion-free property of $\Dfour$. We define $\angdeform{Z} \eqdef \torusproject \deform{Z}$ as in Def.\,\ref{D:PROJECTIONTENSORFIELDSANDTANGENCYTOHYPERSURFACES}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:40:21.313517+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cafe6d4d1416e631ea5c3684a1f286f3c194fab8786e4ddeacf5489aa145e636","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 41 of arXiv:2604.08127, 'Asymptotics of Brownian occupation measures \\ with unusually large intersections'] Suppose $d \ge 1$, $q > 1$, and $0 < \gamma$ such that $d(q-1) < 2q$ and $\gamma \le \frac{2q}{d(q-1)}$. Then the variational problem
    \[
    \rho_{d, q, \gamma} = \sup \{ \| \xi \|_q^{\gamma} - \mathcal{I}(\xi) : \xi \in \widetilde{\mathcal{X}}_{\le 1}(\mathbb{R}^d) \} = \left(\frac{2q - \gamma d(q-1)}{2q} \right) \left( \frac{\gamma d(q-1)}{q} \right)^{\frac{\gamma d(q-1)}{2q - \gamma d(q-1)}} \kappa_{d, q}^{\frac{4\gamma q}{2q - \gamma d(q-1)}}
    \]
    has a unique solution, which is an element of $\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}_{1}(\mathbb{R}^d)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.860979+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cb03629e8c0f062b2477d9c27b40de3716eac28dcd6538f8bd25c3d999ca66c9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Atheo 1 of arXiv:2506.10817, 'On the Weak Error for Local Stochastic Volatility Models'] Let $f$, $\sigma$ be sufficiently smooth functions and $\xi$ satisfying Assumptions \ref{Ass:Half_Step} and \ref{Aspt_new}. Let $\delta,h$ be small. Then there is a constant $C>0$ such that
    \begin{align*}
         \Bigl|\E\bigl[ f(Y_T)\bigr]-\E\bigl[f\bigl(\tiX_T^{h,(1),N,\delta}\bigr)\bigr]\Bigr|
        \lesssim 
        h + \delta^{1-}
        + \frac1{\sqrt{N}} \exp\Bigl( Ch^{-1-}\delta^{0-}\Bigr).
    \end{align*}
    Here $\delta^{1-}$ means that this term decays faster than $\delta^{1-\gamma}$ as $\delta \rightarrow 0$ for all $\gamma >0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:02.100298+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cb119b34a4b2bec11ab837339db2c7ce2d7659293aee425b21eb8b590a7c33b4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 9 of arXiv:2604.26499, 'Spectrum of Random Matrices with Exploding Moments'] \cite[Theorem 9]{weaver1985centrosymmetric}
 \begin{enumerate}[label=(\alph*)]

