{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:23:58.622682+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cb48d6716e4000de3e9e34894ad7c55f5a3493632c639cc5f4b6a1c487d106fa","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 191 (Sharp decomposition of  $\rm{d} \tander^N \vortrenormalized$ and $\rm{d} \tander^N \GradEnt$) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] For a $\Sigma_t$-tangent vectorfield $\SigmatTan$, let $(\mathrm{d} \SigmatTan_\flat)_{\alpha\beta} = \partial_\alpha \SigmatTan_\beta - \partial_\beta \SigmatTan_\alpha$ denote its spacetime exterior derivative. Let $\upepsilon_{\alpha\beta\gamma\delta}$ denote the fully anti-symmetric spacetime tensor normalized by $\upepsilon_{0123} = 1$. Then, the following identities hold:
