{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:42:47.764107+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cb8738a3174db46b98f8cf03bb479b1863a06db5af316541dafb0bdd376261fc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 15 of arXiv:2604.12334, 'On additive averaging kernels for finite Markov chains'] For $P \in \mathcal{S}(\pi)$ and $G$ a Gibbs kernel defined on some partition $(\mathcal{O}_i)_{i=1}^k$, 
