{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:42:55.299468+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cb8bd367fdfadc09aac150595ce25b8b46e35e28ea445cb4a90461917b282f4b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 (Information identity, ceiling, and comparison invariance) of arXiv:2609.02362, '\textbf{Farthest-cell triplet entropy: high-dimensional shell limits and hyperbolic curvat'] For every metric probability space,
\begin{equation}
  \log 3-\Htri(P,\metric)
  =I\{L_V(X);V\},

\end{equation}
and hence
\begin{equation}
  0\le \Htri(P,\metric)\le\log 3.
