{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.985584+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cbc695278cdf16b510ad17dfa16a619101501e364ca448c76077b0a0150822f2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 (Graphical Cauchy--Schwarz) of arXiv:2608.12492, 'Weak Limits of Wiener Chaos: Primitive--Fock Classification and Hilbert--Stein Extraction'] Consider a finite loop-free tensor network whose vertices carry Hilbert tensors
$(z_v)_{v\in V}$ and whose edges contract pairs of Hilbert legs.  If all
legs are contracted, its scalar value satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \left|\operatorname{Contr}_G((z_v)_{v\in V})\right|
 \le\prod_{v\in V}\norm{z_v}.

\end{equation}
If exactly $r\ge1$ edges join two distinguished vertices carrying $x$
and $y$, one may first perform all these $r$ contractions and obtains the sharper
bound
\begin{equation}
 \left|\operatorname{Contr}_G((z_v)_{v\in V})\right|
 \le\norm{x\otimes_ry}
 \prod_{v\ne x,y}\norm{z_v}.

\end{equation}
No edge is allowed to join two legs of the same vertex.  The same
inequalities hold for a network with open output legs, with the
absolute value replaced by the Hilbert norm of the output tensor.","status":"unverified"}

