{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.501614+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cbe4c415fbe28a4efffb3ff7fb3b5d0265c37df6f1387ab8377baa27f0c44591","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary eq:diagonal-free-spike of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[corollary]{cor:diagonal-free-spike}
Consider the diagonal-free ordered model
\[
 h_{N,\mathrm{df}}^J(x)=N^{-1/2}
 \sum_{\substack{I\in[N]^p:\ i_1,\ldots,i_p\ \mathrm{distinct}}}J_Ix_I,
 \qquad x\in\mathbb S^{N-1}(1),
\]
with i.i.d. centered \(K\)-sub-Gaussian entries having common law
\(\mu\).  There is \(M=M(p,K)\) such that, for all sufficiently large
\(a\) and every \(\eta>0\),
\begin{align}
 &\liminf_{N\to\infty}\frac1N\log
 \mathbb E\operatorname{Crt}_{N,\max}^{J,\mathrm{df}}
 \left([ap^{-p/2}-M,(a+\eta)p^{-p/2}+M]\right)\notag\\
 &\hspace{45mm}\ge-\overline I_\mu(a,\eta).
\end{align}
Here \(\operatorname{Crt}_{N,\max}^{J,\mathrm{df}}\) denotes the local-maximum count for \(h_{N,\mathrm{df}}^J\).  Thus the localized one-spike lower-bound mechanism does not rely on repeated tensor indices; this corollary does not compare its exponent with Gaussian diagonal-free complexity.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.197647+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cbec5aa2b3dda60be0f4ce6571324e3e77a46de399de9cf5cdc663c7193cbad3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 43 of arXiv:2510.22783, 'Universality of Cutoff for Riffle Shuffling'] Consider events ${F}_i$, ${F}'_i$ (for each $i \in \{\iota(p),\ldots,\tau(p)-2\}$), ${F}_{\tau(p)-1}$, ${F}'_{\tau(p)-1}$ and ${F}^{(\p)}$ of the form above. Suppose that there exists $\gamma>0$ such that for each $i \in [\iota(p),\tau(p)-2]$, the conditional estimate 
