{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.873008+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cbec9526cc055537c5205e1835b5a54d0a4ad33e6f8b32d0f4bba61a2b9b1495","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:quasicont-conseq of arXiv:2510.13659, 'On the energy image density conjecture of Bouleau and Hirsch'] Let  $(X,d,\mu, \mathcal{E}_p, \mathcal{F}_p, \Gamma_p)$ be a regular $p$-Dirichlet space.
		If $f\in \mathcal{F}_p$ is quasicontinuous and let $A\subset X$ be Borel measurable, then the following hold: 
		\begin{enumerate}
			\item If $\cCap(A)=0$, then $\Gamma_p\langle f\rangle(A)=0$.
			\item If $g \in \Lip(\mathbb{R})$ with $g(0)=0$, then $g \circ f \in \mathcal{F}_p$ and 
			\[
			\Gamma_p\langle g\circ f\rangle  \le( \Lip_a[g] \circ f)^p \cdot \Gamma_p\langle f\rangle.
			\]
			\item If $g\in \Lip(\mathbb{R}^n)$ with $g(0)=0$, and $f=(f_1,\dots, f_n)$ with $f_i\in \mathcal{F}_p$ and $f_i$ are quasicontinuous, then
			\begin{equation} 
				\Gamma_p\langle g\circ f\rangle  \le \left(1 \vee n^{(p-2)/2}\right) (\Lip_a[g] \circ f)^p\cdot \sum_{i=1}^n \Gamma_p\langle f_i\rangle.
			\end{equation}
		\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.314397+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cbef953e03e0a0115f561b85d65b257f2230c0e9389700ee43da9fc659d579c1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma tricky of arXiv:2411.14921, 'A boundary Harnack principle and its application to analyticity of 3D Brownian intersectio'] Let $E,F\subseteq \mathbb R^3$ be non-empty Borel sets. Let $\mu$ be a finite measure on $F$, and $\nu(y,\cdot)$ be a finite measure on $E$ for each $y\in F$. 
    Suppose $p(x,y)$, $s(y)$ and $r(z)$ are non-negative bounded Borel functions on $E\times F,\,F,\,E$, respectively, such that the following equality holds for all $x\in E$,
    \begin{equation}
        r(x)=\int _F p(x,y)\left (\int _E r(z)\nu(y,dz)\right )\mu(dy)+\int _F p(x,y)s(y)\mu(dy).
    \end{equation}
    Moreover, suppose there exists a constant $0\le a <1$ such that for all $x\in E$,
