    \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:21:56.737045+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cbf037cb20048e0c65616168485d22ea3211951630ac0645525867f035ccd5d7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:4arm_good_fl of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] Fix $p \in (0,1)$. Let~$h$ be a GFF on~$\mathbf{D}$ with boundary values so that its flow line $\eta$ is an ${\rm SLE}_{\kappa}${} from $-i$ to $i$. Let $X^0_{0,1},X^0_{0,\epsilon}$ be as defined in~(equation eq:fl_annulus of the paper). Let $I_\epsilon$ be the event that there exist two strands $\eta_{w_1;\mathrm{in}}$, $\eta_{w_3;\mathrm{in}}$ of $X^0_{0,1}$ and a strand $\eta_{w_2;\mathrm{out}}$ of $X^0_{0,\epsilon}$ so that the following hold.
