Then
\[\mathbf{P}[I_\epsilon]=O(\epsilon^{\alpha_{4,\kappa}+o(1)}).\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:09:23.971890+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cbf06a9ced292d1cd311a965b7e9608b0f95fc275251a2123ce2d8339dcac07c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 14 of arXiv:2607.22438, 'A deterministic scalar reduction for the phase transition in two interacting urns'] Let $s_0\in(0,1)$ be the unique solution of
