{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.578194+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cccc7144b3e901b65f1c03bec0528d673fd4d0a0c8784047ec2e955dc22e0824","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2606.14876, 'High-Order Talagrand and Eldan--Gross Inequalities via Besov-Type Variance Functionals'] For all $k\in \Nbb_{\leq n}$, $f:\cube^n\to [-1,1]$, and $1\leq q\leq p\leq 2$,
