{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.063627+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ccd56412672e2b3609b381259ab3de6c6a1989ae4842e245d5a070f19a2cddfb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 12 of arXiv:2606.17452, 'Optional Stopping for Superhedging Supermartingales'] [Tower Property I] 
Let  $S$ be an arbitrary element of $\mathcal{S}$ and  $\rho \le \tau$ be two stopping times; also let $f \in Q$. Then, 
\begin{equation}  
\overline{\sigma}_{\rho}( \overline{\sigma}_{\tau}~f)(S) = \overline{\sigma}_{\rho}[{\bf 1}_{\{\tau = \infty\}}~f+{\bf 1}_{\{\tau < \infty\}}~\overline{\sigma}_{\tau} f](S)\le \overline{\sigma}_{\rho} f(S).
\end{equation}
and, consequently,
\begin{equation} \nonumber  
 \underline{\sigma}_{\rho} f(S) \leq \underline{\sigma}_{\rho}[{\bf 1}_{\{\tau = \infty\}}~f+{\bf 1}_{\{\tau < \infty\}}~\underline{\sigma}_{\tau} f](S) = \underline{\sigma}_{\rho}( \underline{\sigma}_{\tau}~f)(S).
