{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:52.238069+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ccebf156f221f79307550dea15206bdac44fddc8961d7cda9c726d8ffe985a12","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Question 15 of arXiv:2512.10686, 'Maximal rigidity of random measures and uniqueness pairs: stealthy processes, quasicrystal'] Let $ \varphi :\mathbb{R}_{ + }\to \mathbb{R}_{ + }$ such that $ \varphi  (x)\to \infty $ as $ x\to \infty $, with $ \varphi (x) = o(x).$ Is a random stationary measure with atomic spectrum always perfectly interpolable from 
