{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.121266+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ccf61e950326177d24dff3bf59c13c44146393647cf2ae18a01b259a748fc2d5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: BK for Ising weak four arm of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] For any integers $0<M_1<M_2$, let $\mathtt{Con_2}(M_1,M_2)$ be the event that there exist two plus crossings in the annulus $\Lambda_{M_2}\setminus\Lambda_{M_1}$ such that their plus spin clusters, restricted to $\Lambda_{M_2}\setminus\Lambda_{M_1}$, are disjoint. Then there exists a constant $c_8>0$ such that for any integers $M_2>M_1>0$ and any boundary conditions $\xi,\nu$ on $\partial\Lambda_{M_2}$ and $\partial\Lambda_{M_1+1}$, respectively, we have
