{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.751656+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd109099319789de88f331010a4571246605d452ded98f6b127e40f6d8203d0b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:exact-dimension-support-mass-witnesses of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] Assume the minimal Kahane--Peyri\`ere regime. Let \(\beta>A_{\mathrm{loc}}(W)\), let \(\Lambda\) be the block-count exponent in Lemma~(lem:biggins-chernoff-block-count-exponent of the paper), and let \(C\) be a nonnegative random variable with \(0<C<\infty\) almost surely on \(\mathcal S_\circ\). Then, almost surely on \(\mathcal S_\circ\),
\begin{equation*}
\dim_{\mathrm H} E_{\beta,C}(\mu_\circ)=\Lambda(1-\beta).
\end{equation*}
Equivalently,
\begin{equation*}
\dim_{\mathrm H} E_{\beta,C}(\mu_\circ)
=
\inf_{q\ge0}
\left\{
1+\log_2\mathbb E(W^q)-q(1-\beta)
\right\},
\end{equation*}
where \(W^0=\mathbf 1_{\{W>0\}}\), and the value inside the infimum is interpreted as \(+\infty\) whenever \(\mathbb E(W^q)=+\infty\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.067472+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd243fd41eeba1a6141a4d1eba8208e0ea821726f8193597c5c9fbef510dc5c3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 (Sampling duality for the Binomial distribution) of arXiv:2606.00781, '2606.00781'] For all $N\in\nz$, $p\in[0,1]$ and $n,m\in\{0,\ldots,N\}$,
