{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.332121+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd3ab78c52705ab89930dd41738e23d18bcec37c53253ce57f9b92548ebb4b11","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:form_core_2 of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] Let $\Omega$ be an open subset of $\mathbb G$. Then, $((\mathcal{E}^\phi)^\Omega, (\mathcal{F}^\phi)^\Omega)$ is a regular Dirichlet form on $L^2(\Omega,dx)$. Moreover, $C^\infty_c(\Omega)$ is a form core for $\mathcal{E}^{\phi,\Omega}$. As a result, the generator associated with $\mathcal{E}^{\phi,\Omega}$ is the Friedrichs extension of $(\mathcal{L}^\phi_\Omega, C^\infty_c(\Omega))$ in $L^2(\Omega, dx)$, where for any $f\in C^\infty_c(\Omega)$,
    \begin{align*}
        \mathcal{L}^\phi_\Omega f = \left.\Delta^\phi_\Omega f^0\right|_{\Omega},
    \end{align*}
    with 
    \begin{align*}
        f^0(x)=\begin{cases}
            f(x) & \mbox{if $x\in\Omega$} \\ 
            0 & \mbox{if $x\in\Omega^c$}.
        \end{cases}
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.317706+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd3d79e3f6a8d45d96ebb58d0cfc4b8a741f85e072340623cd95c9bec8877773","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary fpcomm-onlyh of arXiv:2411.06131, 'Non-Markovian dynamics: the memory-dependent probability density evolution equations'] Let $ X=(X_t)_{t\in[0,T]} $ be the solutions of ((SDEscomxh of the paper)), if $ h(x) $ is $ C^{\infty} $ bounded function. Then the memory-dependent PDEE for PDFs $ p(x,t) $ of the solutions $ X_t $, satisfies the following equation
		\begin{align}
		\frac{\partial }{\partial t}p(x,t)=-\frac{\partial }{\partial x}\big\{Ht^{2H-1}h'(x)h(x)p(x,t)\big\}
		+\frac{\partial^2 }{\partial x^2}\big\{Ht^{2H-1}h^2(x)p(x,t)\big\},
		\end{align}
		which has the exact solution
		\begin{align*}
		p(x,t)=C_1\frac{1}{\sqrt{\frac{1}{2}t^{2H}h^2(x)}}\exp\bigg\{-\frac{\hat{x}^2(x)}{2t^{2H}}\bigg\},
		\end{align*}
		where $ C_1 $ is the normalization constant, $ \hat{x}(x)=\int_{x_0}^{x}\frac{1}{h(x)}\mathrm{d}x $, and the initial condition is given by $p(x,0)=\delta(x-x_0)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:05:57.796253+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd40e5199cc5184ebac5f1556bf4973ec35ea8f42d188031ebe57542f5a95f19","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 62 of arXiv:2608.30549, '\vspace{-1cm}Maximally Spread Out Measures and Implications\\{} for Phase Transitions in A'] Let $U,V$ be quasi-Banach spaces and let $T\colon U\to V$ be a compact linear map and let $t\in(0,\infty)$.
