{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.251511+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd4351c50c02e79018ba4e981c4a15fc08d56f6886b0d025016bc86bf8eb54e9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 16 (Integrated Davies trick - normalized) of arXiv:2609.01098, 'Gaussian upper bounds for averaged heat semigroups on graphs'] For any $q\in[1,\infty]$, denote by $q'$ its H\"older conjugate and let $A,B\subset X$, and $I\subset \RR$. Then, for any $q$-norm with respect to any measure on $X$, we have 
