{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.591107+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd55ef36c9dba613e45667e588382ddbb16738252a1c38d526ee66c6b832a391","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma WPD-NHS-HUD-BB of arXiv:2608.30582, 'The flexible part of intermittent Onsager theorem for the two-dimensional stochastic incom'] For any $N \in \left\{ {0,1, \cdots ,10} \right\} $ and $t \in \mathop  \cap \limits_{j = 0}^{q} \left[ {0,{\mathfrak{t}_j}} \right] \cap \left[ {{t_k},{t_{k + 1}}} \right)$, the stream function ${\mathfrak{S}_\xi }\left( \cdot \right)$ defined by (equation IUHYU-DJ of the paper) admits
