{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.244922+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd5e947024fba18aca0caf70f490798ead5ce9e29bfa17939173bdb2d58a8f67","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop quotient L2 formula of arXiv:2604.23890, 'The Cutoff Profile for Random Transpositions on Repeated Cards in the Full Range of Parame'] Let \(G\) be a finite group and \(H\leq G\) be a subgroup. Let
\(\mu_1,\mu_2:G\to\mathbb{C}\) be two class functions which are probability measures on \(G\).
For each irreducible representation \(\rho\) of \(G\), let
\(a_\rho^{(1)},a_\rho^{(2)}\in\mathbb{C}\) be the scalars such that
\begin{equation}
\sum_{g\in G}\mu_i(g)\rho(g)=a_\rho^{(i)}I_{d_\rho},
\qquad i=1,2.
\end{equation}
Denote by \(\sim_H\backslash\mu_1,\sim_H\backslash\mu_2\) the probability measures on
the left coset space \(H\backslash G\) induced by \(\mu_1,\mu_2\), respectively. Then, we have
\begin{equation}
D_{L^2}(\sim_H\backslash\mu_1,\sim_H\backslash\mu_2)^2
=
\frac{|H|}{|G|}
\sum_{\rho}
d_\rho\,\dim(V_\rho^H)\,
\left|a_\rho^{(1)}-a_\rho^{(2)}\right|^2.
\end{equation}
Here, \(D_{L^2}\) denotes the \(L^2\)-distance between measures on the quotient space
\(H\backslash G\), while on the right-hand side, we sum over all nontrivial irreducible representations $\rho$ of $G$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.302822+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd60733c30389f7d3e532b5a8bab9be1ac589d99609dadfadf2f95c74eb83913","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:one_extension of arXiv:2605.26048, 'Classification of the eternal solutions and multiple coalescing shocks in the KPZ fixed po'] Let $\widetilde \varphi$ be any function $\mathfrak{X}\rightarrow [-\infty,\infty)$.   Define the function $ \varphi:\mathfrak{X} \to [-\infty,\infty]$ by 
    \begin{equation} 
