    \end{equation}
    where we have added the second equality to clarify that we allow $\eta = \xi$ in the supremum. 
    Then, $\varphi \in \operatorname{USC}(\mathfrak{X})$, and $W\star  \varphi = W\star \widetilde \varphi$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.722414+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd627817426677c25bd809a60a56db440a69f2aede69a8e518998462219cd2c2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm4.3 of arXiv:2606.01944, 'Propagation of Chaos for Mean-field Mean Reflected Backward Stochastic Differential Equati'] For any $1\leq i\leq N$, set 
