{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:52:08.659098+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd66c948cfef463623bd954a7dee2601827c4013a4f8803f7920060027743f47","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2608.29984, 'On Cauchy Problems for Parabolic Equations with Rough Coefficients'] For $(p,q)\in(2,\infty)\times[1,\infty]$ and a sequence $\{f_{k}\}_{k\geq 0}\in L^{p,q}$, the following estimate holds:
