{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:37:20.360232+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd7b7232e719881979232d422cefc7e58fbf7caa0a2d428727851e1fbb3cd414","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop pr.Topo of arXiv:2411.13099, 'Long time behavior of killed Feynman-Kac semigroups with singular Schr{ö}dinger potentials'] Let $(L_t,t\ge 0)$ be a purely jump Lévy process over $\mathscr R^d$ such that its  Lévy measure $\nu$ has full topological support over $\mathscr R_0^d$, i.e. for all $y\in \mathscr R^d_0$ and all $r\in (0,|y|)$, $\nu(B(y,r))>0$, and such that for some $\beta >0$, 
