{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.315354+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd7bf153fdaaeb3ff2101886b165be72c514ed0f033753d9163e75a7643c6059","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:1530 of arXiv:2411.14921, 'A boundary Harnack principle and its application to analyticity of 3D Brownian intersectio'] Consider the triples $(x_i,y_i,D_i)$ with $x_i\in D_i$ and $y_i\in \partial D_i$ that belong to one of the following three cases
