{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:38:17.790765+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd7e7cc534ba316d17b67a95ad78e07cbc9a1c793c96e8facc2e35600a5d68ed","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def: srbmgeneral of arXiv:2509.20779, 'Diffusive Scaling limit of stochastic Box-Ball systems and P\MakeLowercase{ush}TASEP'] Let $S$ be the convex polyhedron in (equation eq:def_polyhedron of the paper). Given a Borel probability measure $\nu$ on 
	$S$, an SRBM associated with the data $(S, \theta, \Gamma,R,\nu)$ is an $\{\mathcal{F}_t\}$-adapted, $d$-dimensional process $W$ defined on some filtered probability space $(\Omega, \mathcal{F}, \mathcal{F}_t, P)$ such that 
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item $W= X+RY$, $P$-a.s.,
		\item $P$-a.s., $W$ has continuous paths and $W(t) \in S$ for all $t \geq0,$
		\item under $P,$
		\begin{itemize}
			\item $X$ is a $d$-dimensional Brownian motion with drift vector $\theta,$ covariance matrix $\Gamma,$ and $X(0)$ has distribution $\nu,$
