{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-09T07:38:10+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd7f42fa6cce70728b6f738f882eb1c9265b6470f11903f06083059a131ed96a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 4.5 of arXiv:2507.06186, '2507.06186'] For any $\ka,\eps,t>0$, we let $\mc K_{\ka,\eps}(t)$ denote the integral operator on $L^2(D)$ with kernel
