{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:35:19.871022+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd836b7ebd7aa8393c5446c95110b6fb08d6f8dcbbdc274c4cc2090a3e9282ab","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary Constant alternating regret for polyhedral OLO of arXiv:2608.24731, 'Optimal Alternating Regret for Online Learning and Games\thanks{Authors are alphabetically'] \label[corollary]{cor:polytope}
Let $\mathcal X=\operatorname{conv}\{\boldsymbol{v}_1,\ldots,\boldsymbol{v}_N\}$ be a  polytope. Consider  linear losses $f_t(\boldsymbol{x})=\langle \boldsymbol{c}_t,\boldsymbol{x}\rangle$, with $f_t(\boldsymbol{x})\in[-1,1]$ for every $\boldsymbol{x}\in\+X$. Running (alg:main of the paper) with $\mu$ being the uniform distribution on $\{\boldsymbol{v}_1,\ldots,\boldsymbol{v}_N\}$ gives
