{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:45:32.094715+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cda2da76d6afb77896ecb86da348bbd61f8277939aeb0379b617bd487082c0ed","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn qcdens of arXiv:2411.14350, 'Randomized Geodesic Flow on Hyperbolic Groups'] [coornaert-pjm] 
For $(X,d)$ Gromov-hyperbolic, let $M(\partial_g X)$ denote the collection of positive finite Borel measures on $\partial_g X $. A $G$-equivariant map $X \to M(\partial_g X)$ sending $x \to \mu_x$ is said to be a $C$ {\bf quasi-conformal density} of dimension $v$ ($v\geq 0$), for some $C\geq 1$, if
\begin{equation}
	\frac{1}{C}\exp\big(-v\beta_\xi(y,x)\big)
	\leq
	\frac{{\rm{d}}\mu_{x}}{{\rm{d}}\mu_y} (\xi)
	\leq C \exp\big(-v\beta_\xi(y,x)\big)
\end{equation}
for all $x, y \in X$, $\xi\in \partial X$. If $C=1$, it is a {\bf conformal density}. Equivalently, we also call the family of measures $(\mu_x)_{x\in G}$ a (quasi)-conformal density.","status":"unverified"}

