{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:29:14.941906+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cdf5da948a0c20e9f4f876291b46b9bc8e3d2ec73a565ad54fb2383b3f889b2a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Invariant sets and ergodicity of arXiv:2606.13615, 'Data-Driven Subsampling Rates for Diffusion Parameter Estimation of SDEs'] Let $\mathbf{Z}=(\mathbf{Z}_n)_{n \in \mathbb{N}_0}$ be a stationary $\mathbb{R}^d$-valued process.
A set $A \in \mathcal{A}$ is called invariant w.r.t. $\mathbf{Z}$ if there exists some $B \in \mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R}^d)^{\mathbb{N}_0}$ such that
\begin{equation*}
A = \lbrace (\mathbf{Z}_j, \mathbf{Z}_{j+1}, \ldots) \in B \rbrace
\end{equation*}
is true for all $j \in \mathbb{N}_0$. Furthermore, $\mathbf{Z}$ is called ergodic if any invariant set $A \in \mathcal{A}$ satisfies $P(A) \in \lbrace 0,1 \rbrace$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.327698+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cdfe90f5ad2cf8011284e88ecbda83bb6dfd6cba69bd7fe897b2496ae545ccc8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:sub-Laplacian of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] Let $\{X_1,\ldots,X_{m}\}$ be an orthonormal frame for $\mathcal{D}$. Define the \emph{horizontal gradient} of $f$, denoted by
$\nabla_{\mathcal{H}}f$, as the horizontal section
\begin{equation*}
\nabla_{\mathcal{H}}f:=\sum_{i=1}^{m}(X_if)X_i,
\end{equation*}
for any function $f:{\mathbb G}\longrightarrow {\mathbb R}$ for which the partial derivatives
$X_if$ exist. The second-order differential operator 
\begin{equation}
\Delta_{\mathcal{H}}:=-\sum_{i=1}^{m} X_i^2
\end{equation}
defined on $C^{\infty}(\mathbb{G})$ is called a \emph{sub-Laplacian}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.468642+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce0c940cfe337ed561b9874947de078748fbaefe55535f6ef89cbb9d06501aa3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 67 (Level sets of $\newuL \upmu$ and the $\newuL \upmu$-adapted tori) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] Given a non-negative number $\ubar' \le 0$, we define:
