{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.300579+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce50f65f3977aa913e42b73677cfc3214f5da2ce3706d7f696a6eabe5db3459b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi The decoupling map of arXiv:2604.21663, 'Large deviations for non-irreducible Markov chains on Euclidean spaces'] Let $n\in \mathbb N$. Let $u\in \widetilde{\mathcal{W}}_n$ be such that $|u|_\gamma\leqslant (\lambda_\gamma+\varepsilon)n$ for $\gamma\in \{1,2\}$ and set $(u^1,\ldots ,u^r)=F_n(u)$.
