{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:57.719355+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce534b31d1b26abbe644f147108d313d0731fc1b69cb32e4bb08f9d83dd61367","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:tail_Holder of arXiv:2605.30999, 'Functional central limit theorems for $U$-statistics of $\beta$-mixing data'] Let $h\colon S^m\to \mathbb R$ be a measurable function and let $\left(X_i\right)_{i\in \mathbb Z}$ be a strictly stationary sequence. Suppose that 
