{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:52.666474+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cebf340f792774a5ce8d2289ea2fcfd78ad26a84edad7d081cbed961dd0e1ece","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 18 (Keyl--Werner) of arXiv:2609.03736, '2609.03736'] Let $\tau$ be a density matrix on $\CC^m$ with decreasing eigenvalue list
$s$, and let $\Pi_\lambda^{(N)}$ be the $\mathfrak S_N$-isotypic projection
of shape $\lambda$ in $(\CC^m)^{\otimes N}$.  The numbers
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb P_{\tau,N}(\lambda)
 =\tr\bigl(\tau^{\otimes N}\Pi_\lambda^{(N)}\bigr)

\end{equation}
form a probability measure on partitions of $N$ with at most $m$ parts.
View $\lambda/N$ as an $m$-vector by appending zero parts.  For every
