Equivalently, the normalized row-length vector $\lambda/N$ converges in
probability to the spectrum $s$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.636151+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cec1854404378bd94069776b446522d1405a05fad4e6d03975e61d3f62a83ca1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma terms_in_signature_third of arXiv:2411.13707, 'High-degree cubature on Wiener space \\ through unshuffle expansions'] \[
\sum_{1\leq i\leq d}(\epsilon_0,\epsilon_0,\epsilon_i^2)=\sum_{1\leq i\leq d}((\xi_{0},\xi_{0ii})+\frac{2}{3}(\xi_{0i},\xi_{0i})+(\xi_{0},\xi_{0},\xi_{i},\xi_{i})\Big ) .
\]
\begin{proof}
Representation (equation eq:expansion of the paper) combined with (cor:parity of the paper) gives,
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
3\sum_{1\leq i\leq d}(\epsilon_0,\epsilon_0,\epsilon_i^2)&=\mathrm{e}^{\star 2}\Big (3\sum_{1\leq i\leq d}(\epsilon_0,\epsilon_0,\epsilon_i^2)\Big )+\mathrm{e}^{\star 4}\Big (3\sum_{1\leq i\leq d}(\epsilon_0,\epsilon_0,\epsilon_i^2)\Big )\\
&=\mathrm{e}^{\star 2}\Big (\sum_{1\leq i\leq d}(\epsilon_0^2\epsilon_i^2+\epsilon_0\epsilon_i^2\epsilon_0+\epsilon_i^2\epsilon_0^2)\Big )+\mathrm{e}^{\star 4}\Big (\sum_{1\leq i\leq d}(\epsilon_0^2\epsilon_i^2+\epsilon_0\epsilon_i^2\epsilon_0+\epsilon_i^2\epsilon_0^2)\Big ) .
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
The first term simplifies by substituting \(\xi_{0i}=-\xi_{i0}\), and \(\xi_{0ii}=\xi_{ii0}\) (reversal property),
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\mathrm{e}^{\star 2}\Big (\sum_{1\leq i\leq d}(\epsilon_0^2\epsilon_i^2+\epsilon_0\epsilon_i^2\epsilon_0+\epsilon_i^2\epsilon_0^2)\Big )=\sum_{1\leq i\leq d}&\Big (3(\xi_{0},\xi_{0ii})+3(\xi_{0},\xi_{ii0})+2(\xi_{0i},\xi_{0i})\\
&+2(\xi_{0i},\xi_{i0})+2(\xi_{i0},\xi_{i0})\Big )\\
=\sum_{1\leq i\leq d}&\Big (6(\xi_{0},\xi_{0ii})+2(\xi_{0i},\xi_{0i})\Big ) .
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
The second term is evaluated as,
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{e}^{\star 4}\Big (\sum_{1\leq i\leq d}(\epsilon_0^2\epsilon_i^2+\epsilon_0\epsilon_i^2\epsilon_0+\epsilon_i^2\epsilon_0^2)\Big )=\sum_{1\leq i\leq d}3(\xi_{0},\xi_{0},\xi_{i},\xi_{i}).
\end{equation}
Substituting (equation eq:k2_0_0_ii of the paper) and (equation eq:k4_0_0_ii of the paper) into (equation eq:0_0_ii of the paper) we obtain the required result.
\end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

