{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.240312+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cf07902b530d4b032c4fca653f6f4b32384e36d069880cdf9ddc3d2f49d24122","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 59 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] Let $C>0$, $\theta \in \R$, $N\in \N$ and $\mathfrak{a}\in (0,1)$. Let $\rho \in [\mathfrak{a},1-\mathfrak{a}]$ and consider ASEPs $(\eta_t)_{t \geq 0}$ and $(\bar{\eta}^{\per}_t)_{t \geq 0}$ evolving according to the extended $(\rho,\theta,1,N)$-reference frame basic coupling. Consider (random) data $\eta^{N} \in \{0,1\}^{N}$ with 
\begin{equation}
 \textup{Ber}_{\rho+CN^{-1/2}}^{N} \succeq \P( \eta^{N} \in \, \cdot \, ) \succeq  \textup{Ber}_{\rho-CN^{-1/2}}^{N} ,  
\end{equation} where $\textup{Ber}_{\rho}^{N}$ denotes the Bernoulli-$\rho$-product measure on $\{0,1\}^{N}$. Define initial data $\eta_0\in \{0,1\}^{\mathbb{Z}}$
\begin{equation}
\eta_0(x):=\eta^N(x- \lfloor \theta N \rfloor )
