{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:45:02.090972+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cf4dce8ae19232de2897d01057e2f3751d4eaf36c62e7d178766197f29e99635","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem deter-lemma:no_bushes of arXiv:2601.00119, 'The largest common subtree of two random trees'] Assume that $2+4n^{1/2-2\alpha}<n^{1/2-\alpha}$. If $B_n^{(4)}$ occurs, then at least one of the two following situations happens.
