{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:52.675632+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cf6177837aa28c66c1cfd8e856e7024de8344cc1ada60b561692ed08e62e2bbc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2609.03750, '\bf Pullback Measure Attractors, Zero-Noise Limits, and Moderate Deviations for 2D Stochas'] Suppose Hypotheses \ref{PEeqAssum-2.2}, \ref{PEeqAssum-2.3} and \eqref{PETNs-3.01} hold. Then, for every $\tau \in \mathbb{R}$ and $D = \{D(t), t \in \mathbb{R}\} \in \mathfrak{D}$, there exist ${T} := {T}(\tau, D) > 1$ and  $\epsilon_{0}\in (0,1]$ such that for all $\epsilon\in (0,\epsilon_{0})$ and $t \geq {T}$, the solution $v$ of \eqref{PEeq-2.15} satisfies
