{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.777399+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cf64659940ac1a12c1472f7c726edb6058aefc991ec5393b8610bc499b5b4bd3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 17 of arXiv:2608.17493, 'Integrals of some compound processes'] Let $M$ be a homogeneous Skellam-type process defined above. Then, for $x>0$,
\begin{align}
	P\bigg\{&\int_0^t M(s)\dif s\in \dif x\bigg\} \nonumber\\
