{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.253666+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cfae0d3734c774b4a76786df83748411131a32c560a9c484cfbeeee795aa13d0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn 4 of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] Let $(X,d^X)$ be a metric space. For a function $f:X\to\R$, a non-empty subset
  $A\subseteq X$ and a real number $\kappa\in (0,1]$, we define $\|f\|_A,$ $\|f\|_{\Lip^{\kappa}(A)}\in [0,\infty],$ and $\|f\|_{\BL^{\kappa}(A)}\in [0,\infty]$ 
  as follows.
  \begin{equation*}
    \|f\|_A:=\sup_{a\in A}|f(a)|,\qquad \|f\|_{\Lip^{\kappa}(A)}:=\sup_{\substack{x,y\in A\\x\neq y}}\frac{|f(x)-f(y)|}{d^X(x,y)^{\kappa}},
  \end{equation*}
  and
  \begin{equation*}
    \|f\|_{\BL^{\kappa}(A)}:=\|f\|_A+\|f\|_{\Lip^{\kappa}(A)}.
  \end{equation*} 
  If $A$ is a singleton, we set $\|f\|_{\Lip^{\kappa}(A)}=0$. 
  The quantity $\|f\|_{\Lip^{\kappa}(A)}$ is the $\kappa$-H\"older constant of $f|_A$, 
  and we call $\|\cdot\|_{\BL^{\kappa}(A)}$ the $\BL^{\kappa}(A)$ norm 
  or simply the $\BL^{\kappa}$ norm if $A$ is clear from the context.
Also, we denote the set of functions with a finite $\BL^{\kappa}(A)$ norm by
$\BL^{\kappa}(A)$. Namely,
  \begin{equation*}
  \BL^{\kappa}(A):=\{f:X\to\R:\|f\|_{\BL^{\kappa}(A)}<\infty\}.
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:37:51.456724+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cfaea02a170bd5799c285f24fbe6f09c79547787d1c7dec261d5a35b9b974d6b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 20 of arXiv:2604.03777, 'Equilibrium fluctuations for a multi-species particle system with long jumps'] Let $\gamma >0$, $0 \leq s \leq t \leq T$, $n \in \mathbb{N}_+$ and $A_n$ be an arbitrary subset of $\mathbb{Z}^{2}$. Then
\begin{align*} 
	&	\mathbb{E}_{\nu_{\rho}} \Bigg[ \Bigg\{ \int_s^t \dd r \frac{ \Theta(n) K_n }{\sqrt{n}}    \sum_{(x,y) \in A_n} B_{r,v}^{H,n}(x,y) a(y-x)   \bar{\xi} _x^{\alpha}( \eta_r^n ) \bar{\xi} _y^{\beta}( \eta_r^n ) \Bigg\}^{2} \Bigg] \leq \widehat{C} (t-s)^{2} \frac{  \big[ \Theta(n) K_n \big]^{2}  }{ n^{4}  } \mathbbm{1}_{ \{ \gamma \geq 1 \} },
\end{align*}
where for every $z,w \in \mathbb{Z}^{2}$, $B_{r,v}^{H,n}(z,w):=[  H ( \tfrac{w - r v_n }{n}  ) - H ( \tfrac{z - r v_n }{n}  )  ] - [  H ( \tfrac{ \lfloor w - r v_n \rfloor }{n}  ) - H ( \tfrac{ \lfloor z - r v_n \rfloor }{n}  )  ]$. Furthermore, if $H \in C_c^2(\mathbb{R})$, the role of $\widehat{C}$ is fulfilled by some constant $C(H)$ satisfying \eqref{Cinvshift}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:41.019393+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cfb822192bb460a565994c1fa5aae9551cb4cd5ef5960c4e485bec08f791db67","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition l06-1 of arXiv:2412.04015, 'Linear fluctuation of interfaces in Glauber-Kawasaki dynamics'] For all $t\ge 0$,
\begin{equation}

\frac{d}{dt} H_N(h^N_t\,|\, \nu^N_{\varrho (\cdot)})
\;\leq\; -\,2\,  I_N(h_t^N; \nu^N_{\varrho (\cdot)})
\;+\;    \int  h^N_t \, L^*_{N} \, {\mathbf 1}   \; d \nu^N_{\varrho (\cdot)} \;,
\end{equation}
where $\color{blue} {\mathbf 1} \colon \Omega_N \to {\mathbb R}$ is the constant
function equal to $1$, and $\color{blue} L^*_{N}$ represents the
adjoint of $L_N$ in $L^2(\nu^N_{\varrho (\cdot)})$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:31.998805+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cfbd85a695350dec101e859ce45a48e1fe242a12f03c37c3a6009686cb566acb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2512.02661, 'Worst-case mixing estimates for Brownian motion with semipermeable barriers'] There exist absolute constants $\delta_0,c>0$ such that the following holds for every $\delta \leq \delta_0$.
