{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.679353+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cfdd1cf996eec26923b73512548188a90dca701431036277857c20ec7ac0171c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2607.25986, 'Asymptotics of a two-species particle system associated to the doubly parabolic Keller-Seg'] Suppose Assumption~\ref{mol} and that $\chi<\chi^*_\theta$. Fix $\sigma\in (0,\frac 12]$.

\vip

(i) Set
\begin{equation}
\Aa_\sigma=\{(N,M,\e) : N\geq 2, M>0, \e\in (0,1], N M\e^{3+\sigma}\geq 1, N M^{1+\sigma} \e^{2+\sigma} \geq 1\}.
\end{equation}
The family 
$((X^{1,N,M,\e}_t)_{t\geq 0} : (N,M,\e)\in \Aa_\sigma)$ is tight in $C(\R_+,\R^2)$.

\vip

(ii) Fix $N\geq 2$ and consider $(M_n)_{n\geq 1}$ valued in $(0,\infty)$ and $(\e_n)_{n\geq1}$ valued in 
$(0,1]$ such that 
\begin{equation}
