M_n\e_n^{3+\sigma}=\infty.
\end{equation}
Then the family $((X^{k,N,M_n,\e_n}_t)_{t\geq 0, k \in I_N} : n\geq 1)$ is tight in $C(\R_+,(\R^2)^N)$
and any limit point $((X^{k,N}_t)_{t\geq 0, k \in I_N}$ as $M\to \infty$ is a $(\rho_0,c_0,N)$-1SKS system.

