{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.745700+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d0042e970e3fdd677260b34d5ca57b5c60232682f3218fedaf5a6e46aa98e2ae","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn GibbsDefinition of arXiv:2605.06429, '\large \bf $\mathsf{GL}_N(\mathbb{C})$ BROWNIAN MOTION AND STOCHASTIC PDE ON ENTIRE FUNCTI'] Let $N \in \mathbb{N}\cup \{\infty\}$. We say that a line ensemble $\mathcal{L}\in \mathrm{C}(\llbracket 1, N \rrbracket)$ satisfies the Gibbs resampling property with respect to the law of the $\mathsf{A}$-bridge if for all $\llbracket \ell,\ell+k-1 \rrbracket \subset \llbracket 1, N \rrbracket$ with $\ell, k \ge 1$ and any $[a,b]\in \mathbb{R}_+$ we have
