{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:47:04.947671+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d008721586db54828070fdf217928ca21b86b1758eacef3e280e756a0405a250","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop solntobicausalmongeegs of arXiv:2412.02948, 'Causal transport on path space'] Let $\sigma \in \mathscr{A}^{d,d}$, $b \in \mathscr{A}^{d,1}$ be such that the SDE \begin{equation}

    dX_t = b\del{t,X} dt + \sigma\del{t,X} dB_t, \; X_0 = 0,    
    \end{equation}
has a unique weak solution $\eta := \mu^{\sigma,b}_0$, where  $\sigma\del{t,\omega}$ is invertible for all $\del{t,\omega}$. 

 Let $\overline{\sigma} \in \mathscr{A}^{d,d}$ be such that $\overline{\sigma}(t,\omega)=\kappa(t)u(t,\omega)$ with $u(t,\omega)\in {\cal O}^d$ and assume the SDE 
  \begin{equation}

dY_t = \overline{b}\del{t} dt + \overline{\sigma}\del{t,Y} dB_t, \; Y_0 = 0,        
    \end{equation}

 has a unique, strong solution with law $\nu := \mu^{\overline{\sigma}, \overline{b}}_0$. Denote the corresponding  It\^o  map   by $F^{\overline{\sigma}, \overline{b}}_0 : \mathcal{W}^d \rightarrow \mathcal{W}^d$. 

Then an optimal transport from $\eta$ to $\nu$ for a cost of the form (equation eq.separablecost of the paper)  is given by the bicausal Monge map 
    \[
    \mathcal{W}^d \ni \omega \mapsto T\del{\omega} := F^{ \sqrt{\overline{\sigma} \overline{\sigma}^*},\overline{b}}_0\del{\int_0^\cdot Q_s \sigma^{-1}\del{s,X} dM^\eta\del{s} }

    \] 
    where $Q : \sbr{0,1} \times \mathcal{W}^d \rightarrow \mathcal{O}^d$ is a $\deln{\mathcal{H}^\eta_t}_{t \in \sbr{0,1}}$-progressively measurable process given by $Q_t\del{\omega} = Q\del{t,\omega} := V\del{t,\omega} U^*\del{t,\omega}$ for $U\del{t,\omega}, V\del{t,\omega} \in \mathcal{O}^d$ appearing in the SVD of matrix $\sigma\del{s,\omega} \sqrt{\overline{\sigma} \overline{\sigma}^*\del{s}}$. In particular, \begin{multline*}
    K\del{\eta,\nu} = M\del{\eta,\nu} = \mathbb{E}^{\eta}\del{h\del{\int_0^\cdot b\del{s,X} ds - \int_0^\cdot \overline{b}\del{s} ds}} + \\
    \mathbb{E}^{\eta} \del{g\del{\int_0^1 \Tr\del{ \sigma\del{s,X} \sigma^*\del{s,X} + \overline{\sigma} \overline{\sigma}^*\del{s}} ds - 2 \int_0^1 \Tr\del{\sigma\del{s,X} \sqrt{\overline{\sigma} \overline{\sigma}^*\del{s}} Q\del{s,X}} ds}}.
    \end{multline*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

