{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.644380+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d00aae30716f2239392a3ef96e2aafe396549b61d153ba55c7089a42a9a7bbb0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:exp_mom_local_time of arXiv:2512.17747, 'On exponentially height-penalized random trees'] We denote by $B^{(n)}_{x,y}$ a uniform bridge of length $n$ from $x$ to $y$, that is a uniform element from $\mathcal B^{(n)}_{x,y}$.
