{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.187888+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d039fd3e6a334d6b91e37195a4b169f5ee4873e0ec51ba87e6c0e52fb4aba1da","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 14 of arXiv:2604.18871, 'Quantitative approximation of the Vlasov(--Fokker--Planck)--Navier--Stokes system by stoch'] Let Assumption~\ref{assump-particles} hold with $p>d$ and $\gamma\in (\frac{d}{p}, 1)$. If $d=3$, assume further that $\frac{\gamma}{2} + \frac{3}{2}(\frac{1}{2}-\frac{1}{p}) <1$.
