{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:55:18.924357+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d05d5904d61d17e52b3801b0691883bf0331e1f1243520f99aca605620963130","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:uniformboundFOU of arXiv:2601.21762, 'Navier-Stokes with a fractional transport noise as a limit of multi-scale dynamics'] Let $w$ be the stationary solution of $dw_t = -Mw_t dt + Q^{\frac 12}dB^H_t$. Then:
\begin{equ}
      \sup_{t>0} \mathbb{E}\left[\left\|w_t\right\|_{H^\sigma}^2\right] = C_H \tr{M^{-2H}Q}, \qquad 
       \sup_{t>0} \mathbb{E}\left[\norm{M^{-1}w_{t}}_{H^{\sigma}}^{2}\right] = C_H\tr{M^{-2-2H}Q}.
\end{equ}
Furthermore $w$ satisfies the bounds: 
$$\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|w_{s,t}\right\|_{H^\sigma}^2\right]  \lesssim  \left(\tr{M^{2-2H}Q} +\ensuremath\trace[Q] + \tr{M^{-2H}Q} \right) |t-s|^{2H},$$
$$\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|M^{-1} w_{s,t}\right\|_{H^\sigma}^2\right]  \lesssim  
\left(\tr{M^{-2H}Q} +\tr{M^{-2}Q} + \tr{M^{-2-2H}Q}\right) |t-s|^{2H},$$
where the constants indicated by $\lesssim$ depend only on $H$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:19:46.229090+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d0647717be9255299f49b4f1fe33aa35c3f6dc8c6eb745ee9ec421c00f4731de","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 19 of arXiv:2507.08909, 'Annealed almost periodic entropy'] Consider a $(k+\ell+m)$-by-$(k+\ell+m)$ self-adjoint matrix
	\begin{equation}
		Q := \left[\begin{array}{ccc} Q_{11} & Q_{12} & R\\ Q_{12}^\ast & Q_{22} & Q_{23} \\ R^\ast & Q_{23}^\ast & Q_{33}\end{array}\right].
	\end{equation}
	Assume that the submatrices
	\[Q_{(1\cup 2)} := \left[\begin{array}{cc} Q_{11} & Q_{12}\\ Q_{12}^\ast & Q_{22}\end{array}\right] \qquad \hbox{and} \qquad Q_{(2\cup 3)} := \left[\begin{array}{cc} Q_{22} & Q_{23}\\ Q_{23}^\ast & Q_{33}\end{array}\right]\]
	are both positive semidefinite.  Then $Q$ is positive semidefinite if and only if it has the form
	\begin{equation}
		\left[\begin{array}{ccc} Q_{12}Q^\dag_{22} Q_{12}^\ast & Q_{12} & Q_{12} Q^\dag_{22} Q_{23}\\ Q_{12}^\ast & Q_{22} & Q_{23} \\ Q_{23}^\ast Q^\dag_{22}Q_{12}^\ast  & Q_{23}^\ast & Q_{23}^\ast Q^\dag_{22} Q_{23}\end{array}\right] + \left[\begin{array}{ccc} S_{11} & 0 & S_{11}^{1/2}CS_{33}^{1/2}\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\ S_{33}^{1/2}C^\ast S_{11}^{1/2} & 0 & S_{33}\end{array}\right],
	\end{equation}
	where
	\begin{equation}
		S_{11} := Q_{11} - Q_{12}Q^\dag_{22}Q_{12}^\ast \quad \hbox{and} \quad S_{33} := Q_{33} - Q_{23}^\ast Q^\dag_{22}Q_{23}
	\end{equation}
	are generalized Schur complements and $C \in \Xi(m,k)$.

	If $Q_{(1\cup 2)}$ and $Q_{(2\cup 3)}$ are both nonsingular, then the contraction $C$ promised here is unique, and the whole of $Q$ is nonsingular if and only if $C$ is a strict contraction.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.694516+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d066e2c5650dd503dc8474e7146320a25262dbe20ba7c91adaa83a200b8281eb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 39 (Projection and gate decomposition) of arXiv:2607.26377, '\textbf{Entire Logarithmic Signatures\\ of Bounded-Variation Paths in Finite Dimensions}'] Let $(\mathscr{T},d)$ be a complete metric tree and let $C\subset\mathscr{T}$ be nonempty, closed, and convex. Every $x\in\mathscr{T}$ has a unique metric projection $p\in C$. Moreover, $p\in[x,c]$ for every $c\in C$. If $p$ and $q$ are the projections of $x$ and $y$, respectively, and $p\neq q$, then
\begin{equation}
[x,y]=[x,p]\cup[p,q]\cup[q,y],
\end{equation}
where consecutive pieces meet only at their common endpoint and $[x,p]\cap[q,y]=\varnothing$.","status":"unverified"}

