{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.285305+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d0b1cb882d887644f6aa624f2a7c2643e2a7c805b12e07e04fc9345c3406254d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem annealed of arXiv:2604.20660, 'The Legendre structure of the TAP complexity\\ for the Ising spin glass'] Let $f\in\mathbb{R}$, $u\in(0,1)$, $q\in(0,1)$, and
		$\zeta\in\mathrm{Prefix}_2(u,q)$.
