{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:25.272087+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d11a4f96e44f2da93a675f0f26b899f25e4c9ed9819496816443d4808f3cbeff","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2606.21111, 'On Elephant Random Walk with Delayed Amnesia'] Let $\{M_n, \mathcal{F}_n\}_{n\ge1}$ be a locally square-integrable martingale in
$\mathbb{R}^{d}$ with predictable quadratic variation $\{\langle M \rangle_n\}_{n\ge1}$.
Let $\{V_n\}_{n\ge1}$ be a sequence of non-random positive definite diagonal matrices of order $d$ such that its diagonal entries decrease to $0$ at polynomial rates. Assume that conditions \eqref{Touaticondi1} and \eqref{Lindecondi} hold a.s. Moreover, suppose that there exists $\eta\in(1,2]$ such that
\begin{equation}
\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\frac{1}{(\log (\det V_n^{-1})^2)^\eta}\mathbb{E}(\|V_n\Delta M_n\|^{2\eta}|\mathcal{F}_{n-1})<\infty\ \ \text{a.s.}
\end{equation}
Then, we have the following quadratic strong law:
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n\to \infty}\frac{1}{\log (\det V_n^{-1})^2}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\Big(\frac{(\det V_k)^2-(\det V_{k+1})^2}{(\det V_k)^2}\Big)V_kM_kM_k^tV_k^t=V\ \ \text{a.s.}	
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

