{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.191200+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d12bd17e03a8efdd5d5e39e7111994fedabea429145b39dde69afabd60ce89bc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 9 of arXiv:2606.31287, '\bf Heat kernel lower bound estimates for symmetric pure jump processes via averaged jump '] {\rm (\cite[Theorem 1.15]{CKW1})} 
  Suppose that the metric space $(\sX, d)$ is unbounded.  
  The following are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}
\item[\rm (i)]  ${\rm FK}(\phi)$, ${\rm J}_{\phi,\le}$ and ${\rm CSJ} (\phi)$ hold.  


 \item[\rm (ii)]    $(\sE, \sF)$ is conservative   and  ${\rm UHK}(\phi)$ holds 
 \end{enumerate} 
If one of them holds, then there is a constant $c\geq 1$ so that for all $x\in \sX$ and $r>0$, 
\begin{equation} 
c^{-1} \phi (r) \leq \bE_x [ \tau_{B(x, r)}] \leq c \phi (r),
\end{equation} 
where $\tau_{B(x, r)}:=\inf\{t>0: X_t\notin B(x, r)\}$ is the first exit time from the ball $B(x, r)$ by the process $X$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:33:21.479633+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d13868d5d37897bcab8c5c9374ef895636a3bf5c7d6170470f6e8c4162c7271e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Def Def_strongly_convex_2 of arXiv:2606.22183, 'Expected loss of quasi-arithmetic means of exchangeable random variables'] Let $I\subseteq \mathbb{R}$ be a nondegenerate interval, and $\alpha:(I-I)\to\mathbb{R}_+$ be an even function.
A function $L:I\to\mathbb{R}$ is said to be strongly convex with respect to the error function $\alpha$, briefly strongly $\alpha$-convex, if
 \begin{align}
  \begin{split}
  L(tx+(1-t)y)&\leqslant  tL(x)+(1-t)L(y)\\
              &\phantom{\leqslant\;}- t\alpha((1-t)(x-y))-(1-t)\alpha(t(y-x)),\qquad x,y\in I,\,t\in[0,1].
 \end{split}
 \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.781400+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d13dfdcc53d2454443eff10698725c326aa17bf67eb1b8f9eb83ca4ed7296275","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lm Concentration Bound of arXiv:2411.01633, 'On the Limit of the Tridiagonal Model \\for $\beta$-Dyson Brownian Motion'] Let $F:\mathbb{R}^{n^2+(k+1)n} \to \mathbb{R}$ be a function with bounded Lipschitz norm on compact sets (independently of $n$ or $k$) and $|F(x)| \leq C(1+||x||)^d$ for some constants $C,d>0$ (again independent of $n$ or $k$). Then
    \begin{equation*}
    \begin{split}
        &\mathbb{P}\left(\sup_{t \in [0,T]} |F(\Tilde{M}(t)/\sqrt{n},\theta_0(t),\dots,\theta_k(t))-\mathbb{E} F(\Tilde{M}(t)/\sqrt{n},\theta_0(t),\dots,\theta_k(t))| > u\right) \\
        &\hspace{7cm}\leq C e^{-c(T,k) \frac{n u^2}{\log(n)}}+e^{-c(T,k)\frac{n}{\log(n)}},
        \end{split}
    \end{equation*}
    where the constants $C$ and $c(T,k)$ do not depend on $n$. In particular, setting $u=\sqrt{w}\log(n)n^{-1/2}$, we have
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathbb{P}\left(\sup_{t \in [0,T]} |F(\Tilde{M}(t)/\sqrt{n},\theta_0(t),\dots,\theta_k(t))-\mathbb{E} F(\Tilde{M}(t)/\sqrt{n},\theta_0(t),\dots,\theta_k(t))| > \frac{\sqrt{w}\log(n)}{n^{1/2}}\right) \leq C n^{-c(T,k)w},
    \end{equation*}
    which is summable for $w>c(T,k)^{-1}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.289536+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d13f955f8c5f7ba9b32b2e52685354e368d19d6b40d7ad8adcd7034f71cfb8aa","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2606.23099, 'Path-dependent Affine Processes'] Let $d = 1$.
