{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:40.963868+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d13fa41545b8a5a1820608baeaa3f45c31e2ec2036ed584b7982c39238262baa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem T:MomBdd of arXiv:2412.03521, 'On ergodic properties of stochastic PDEs'] Let $u(t,x; \mu)$ be the solution to~(equation E:SHE of the paper) starting from a rough
  initial condition $\mu$ which satisfies~(equation A:icon of the paper). Assume that
  \begin{enumerate}[wide, labelwidth=!, labelindent=0pt, label=\emph{(\roman*)}]
    \setlength\itemsep{.1in}

    \item the diffusion coefficient $b$ satisfies the degenerate
      condition~(equation E:Cond-b of the paper);

    \item $\rho: \mathbb{R}^d \to \mathbb{R}_+$ is a nonnegative $L^1 (\mathbb{R}^d)$ function;

    \item for all $t > 0$, the initial condition $\mu$ satisfies the condition
      that $\mathcal{G}_{\rho}(t;|\mu|) < \infty$, where
      \begin{equation}
        \mathcal{G}_{\rho}(t;\mu)
        \coloneqq \int_{\mathbb{R}^d} \left[\left(p(t,\cdot) * \mu\right)(x) \right]^2 \rho(x)\: \ensuremath{\mathrm{d}} x;
      \end{equation}

    \item the spectral measure $\widehat{f}$ satisfies~(equation E:Upsilon_0 of the paper),
      i.e., $\Upsilon(0)<\infty$, and the Lipschitz constant $L_b$ is small
      enough so that $4 L_b^2\Upsilon(0) < 1$.

  \end{enumerate}
  Then there exists a unique $L^2 (\Omega)$-continuous solution $u(t,x)$ such
  that for some constant $C>0$, which does not depend on $t$, the following
  holds:
  \begin{equation}
    \mathbb{E}\left(\left\|  u(t,\cdot; \mu)   \right\|_{\rho}^2\right)
    \le C \mathcal{G}_{\rho}\left(t; |\mu|\right)
    < \infty, \quad \text{for any $t > 0$},
  \end{equation}
  where we recall that the norm $\left\|  \cdot   \right\|_\rho$ is given
  by~(equation E:WeightedNorm of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

