{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:06:07.089541+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d18a6a57cfefff10f9183724485f45f12847eecc3c3ece88f4516f7958e82e04","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 14 of arXiv:2608.28148, 'Flows and homotopies of Banach Lie algebroids'] Let  $ \left(A,\pi,M,\rho,\LB_{A} \right) $  an Banach almost Lie algebroid.
 The \emph{Jacobiator}\index{Jacobiator}  is the $\mathbb{R}$-trilinear
map $J_{A_U}:\Gamma(A_{U})^{3}\to\Gamma(A_{ U})$ defined, for any open set $U$ in $M$ and any $\left( \mathfrak{u}_{1}, \mathfrak{u}_{2}, \mathfrak{u}_{3} \right) \in \Gamma(A_{U})^3$ by
