{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.362356+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d19e1da8a09ff81e07d353b2cc462bc6d2283ca6b07e4eff5f6f745eb974e196","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 64 of arXiv:2511.09517, 'From Cannings model to Brownian motion conditioned on local time profile'] For any $\delta>0$, $k\ge1$, and sequences $(a_i^n)$, $(a_i)$, $(b_i^n)$, $(b_i)$ satisfying the above assumptions, we have uniformly for all $s\in (\delta,h(\ell)-\delta)\cap\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{Z}$,
\begin{align*}
        \mathbb{P}_n\left(Y^n(s-\tfrac{1}{n})=y^n(s-\tfrac{1}{n})\,|\,B_s\right)
        =\,\begin{cases}
            1+o_n(1),&\quad\text{if }s-\tfrac{1}{n}\in \{a^n_1,\ldots,a^n_k\},\\
            \dfrac{\binom{y^n(s)}{2}\sigma_n(s)^2}{q_n(s)}\big(1+o_n(1)\big),&\quad\text{if }s-\tfrac{1}{n}\in \{b^n_1,\ldots,b^n_m\},\\
            1-\dfrac{\binom{y^n(s)}{2}\sigma_n(s)^2}{q_n(s)} \big(1 + o_n(1)\big),&\quad\text{otherwise}.
        \end{cases}
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

