{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.115042+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d1e803634a5be96fc5070cfd575e9ea656b2aa431d0f7f01c276bd997aa1f992","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma-sum-prod-L-x-j-delta of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] Let $0 < \alpha < 1$. There exists a constant $C>0$ depending on $D$ only such that for any $k \in \mathbb{N}$,
