{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:37:51.456637+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d20878722d7ae5fc7fb41dd1d06e8b5f9f0edf98b7cfbe48a7d91651207345b7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 19 of arXiv:2604.03777, 'Equilibrium fluctuations for a multi-species particle system with long jumps'] Let $\gamma >0$, $0 \leq s \leq t \leq T$, $n \in \mathbb{N}_+$ and $A_n$ be an arbitrary subset of $\mathbb{Z}^{2}$. Let also $B_{r,v}^{H,n}: \mathbb{Z}^{2} \mapsto \mathbb{R}$ be a deterministic map depending only on $v,H,n$ and $r \in [0,T]$. Then
