{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:38:23.583580+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d2350ab7527d42fecaf3c643c16468ef7f40f8674cab99bd3bab971b9c3c44f9","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition defi:interface of arXiv:2511.01851, 'Percolation on graphs of polynomial growth is local:\\analyticity, supercritical sharpness'] Let $\mathscr{I}\subset V$ be a finite set of vertices. We say that $\mathscr{I}$ is an \textit{interface} if it is $t$-coarse connected and either $o\in \mathscr{I}$ or $o$ lies in a finite connected components of $\mathscr{G}\setminus \mathscr{I}$. Let $\overline{\mathscr{I}}$ denote the set of vertices $x$ such that $d_{\mathscr{G}}(x,\mathscr{I})\leqslant 10N$. We say that an interface $\mathscr{I}$ \textit{occurs in $\omega$ at scale $N$} if
\begin{enumerate}
    \item every $x\in \mathscr{I}$ is bad,
    \item every $x\in V\setminus \mathscr{I}$ such that $d_{\mathscr{G}}(x,\mathscr{I})\leqslant t$ is good,
    \item the closed edges of $\overline{\mathscr{I}}$ form a bond-cutset between $o$ and $\infty$.
\end{enumerate}
When clear from context, we simply write that $\mathscr{I}$ occurs.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:45:02.064779+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d240573f80621a8002f161ee703c9d6f99bc646096e6fccbb1b12104522e7967","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem cases_sb of arXiv:2601.00119, 'The largest common subtree of two random trees'] Let $h\geq 1$. If $\operatorname{LCS}^\bullet(\tau_*,\tau_*') > h+1$ then, for any $0<\alpha<1$, one of the following situations happens: 
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item[\emph{(i)}] There is $v\in \tau_*$ and $v'\in \tau_*'$ with $|v|=|v'|=1$ such that $\mathrm{Ht}(\theta_v\tau_*)\wedge \mathrm{Ht}(\theta_{v'}\tau_*')\le h$ and \[h^{-\alpha}\operatorname{LCS}^\bullet(\theta_v\tau_*,\theta_{v'}\tau_*')> \mathrm{Ht}(\theta_v\tau_*)\wedge \mathrm{Ht}(\theta_{v'}\tau_*') +1.\] 
        \item[\emph{(ii)}] It holds that 
        \[\left(\sum_{i=1}^{\mathrm{k}_\varnothing(\tau_*)}1+\mathrm{Ht}(\theta_i\tau_*)\right)\wedge \left(\sum_{i=1}^{\mathrm{k}_\varnothing(\tau_*')}1+\mathrm{Ht}(\theta_i\tau_*')\right)>h^{1-\alpha}.\]
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.069411+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d24231a462621ded414122fa4423639f4b6713adff3cc5b5ab83c08862738ac6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm CPPR-survival of arXiv:2507.00329, 'Oriented bond-site percolation in random environment and contact processes with periodic r'] Consider the generalised contact process on $\mathbb{Z}_{\geq0}$ with $\mathbb{X}\sim\mathrm{PPP}(\lambda)$ and either 
