{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.893211+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d26309afda398ea9b0ac626e62271ce6dfe64928c029ffa0cb0acc2ce4f6a9e8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 3 of arXiv:2606.18877, 'Ergodic Properties of Non-Linear Density-Dependent Perturbations of the Ornstein--Uhlenbec'] Under the same assumptions as in Lemma~\ref{lem:unifbound}, the weak solution \(p\) of~\eqref{eq:NFPE} belongs to the class \(C^{1+\beta/2,2+\beta}_{\mathrm{loc}}\bigl((0,T)\times\mathbb R^d\bigr)\) for some \(\beta\in(0,1)\) and any \(T>0\) fixed. In particular, it is a locally classical solution. Moreover, for any \(t\in(0,T)\) and \(x\in\R^d\) its gradient satisfies
