{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.368358+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d26863b9872bc8c4c8d97687caabfc3cfe991286e43f45647339208ca802d989","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition thm:LSI:wu of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] Let $\varphi \in C^2(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)$. Define the differential operator $\mathcal{L}_\varphi := \Delta - \nabla \varphi \cdot \nabla$. Let  $\mathcal{L}_\varphi^{-1}$ denote the Poisson operator, which is the inverse of $\mathcal{L}_\varphi$ on the Banach space of Lipschitz continuous functions $C_{\text{\normalfont Lip}, 0}(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)$. That is, for $f \in C_{\text{\normalfont Lip}, 0}(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)$, $h = \mathcal{L}_\varphi^{-1} f$ if $\mathcal{L}_{\varphi} h = f$. Recall the definition of $w(r, \varphi)$ in (equation eq:LSI:w of the paper). If
    \begin{align*}
        \hat{c}(\varphi) := \frac{1}{4} \int_0^\infty s \exp\bigg(\int_0^s \frac{1}{4}w(r, \phi) dr \bigg) ds < \infty,
    \end{align*}
    then $\mathcal{L}_\varphi^{-1}$ is a bounded operator on $C_{\text{\normalfont Lip}, 0}(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)$ and we have $\|\mathcal{L}_\varphi^{-1} \|_{\text{\normalfont Lip}} < \hat{c}(\varphi).$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

