{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:13:18.527581+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d26ca6f74131a42a2c004d7c05e197ce2a7445ed8b254910ef02354f438c87e1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 16 (\cite{namba74}, see also Section 2.1 in \cite{Streets-Ustinovskiy21}) of arXiv:2608.30638, 'On compact steady pluriclosed soliton surfaces'] Let $(M,J)$ be a primary Hopf surface of class $1$, and we work over the open subset $\{z_1z_2\neq 0\}$. Consider the logarithmic coordinates
