{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:07.258514+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d2a87b6881a34525ae0d3d8eee13629bd643a51e9314a844a145e631b5204dce","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 16 of arXiv:2604.19308, '\textbf{On McKean--Vlasov SDEs with polynomial drifts for SIS epidemic models}'] Let~\eqref{co:3},~\eqref{co:5} and~\eqref{co:7}--\eqref{co:9} hold. Then the unique strong solution $I$ to~\eqref{eq:SIS epidemic model} with $I_{0} = \xi_{0}$ a.s.~satisfies
\begin{align*}
u(t)\E\big[|\hat{I}_{t}^{(n)} &- I_{t}|^{p}\big] \leq 
u(t_{j,n})\E\big[|I_{t_{j,n}}^{(n)} - I_{t_{j,n}}|^{p}\big]\\
&\quad  + \int_{t_{j,n}}^{t}u(s)\big(\delta_{p,j,n}(s) + \hat{\lambda}_{k+1}(s,N(s))p\E\big[|\hat{I}_{s}^{(n)} - I_{s}|^{p-1}\mathcal{W}_{p}(\mathcal{L}(I_{s}),L_{j,n})\big]\big)\,\mathrm{d}s\\
&\quad + \int_{t_{j,n}}^{t}\big(\dot{u}(s) + u(s)\lambda_{p,j,n}(s)\big)\E\big[|\hat{I}_{s}^{(n)} - I_{s}|^{p}\big]\,\mathrm{d}s
\end{align*}
for all $n\in\N$, $j\in\{0,\dots,k_{n}-1\}$ and $t\in [t_{j,n},t_{j+1,n}]$ and each absolutely continuous function $u\colon [t_{j,n},t_{j+1,n}]\rightarrow\R_{+}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:23:58.628795+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d2ad4c1eec5925d4895598339911358711eaf42a8a953fdde9c54b90fa8297c4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 224 (Preliminary top-order $L^2$ estimates for $\upchi$) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] Let $N = \Ntop$, and let
