{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:29:08.612065+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d2fe388bc7a0ea0e59e2c2debaee1c9ecf9fe83a83e061213c6759134521d435","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-resample-infty-2.5 of arXiv:2411.19810, 'Radial conformal welding in Liouville quantum gravity'] For $(\phi, \eta) \sim M_W$, let $\tau$ be the time $\eta$ separates $i$ from $\infty$, let $\sigma< \tau$ be the first time at which $\eta (\sigma) = \eta(\tau)$, and let $\mathcal{QCP}_{\phi, \eta((0, \sigma))\cap \mathbb{R}}$ denote the quantum cut point measure of $\eta ((0, \sigma)) \cap \mathbb{R}$. More precisely, this is the quantum cut point measure of the thin quantum disk defining $(\phi, \eta)$ (Definition~(def-thin-wedge of the paper)) restricted to the set of cut points $\eta ((0, \sigma)) \cap \mathbb{R}$.
