{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:49:05.498768+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d37f121dcc17a2ddcab8c57da7bac64068edec1b5452a3b1a483b443805b419c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm bigthm of arXiv:2601.19145, 'Stochastic Persistence in Infinite Dimensions'] Let $r$ be large enough. Under (sass-A of the paper)-(SPDE-G-sass of the paper), for every $R \geq 0$, $\theta \in \Theta$, and initial condition $\tilde{x}_0 \in C(\overline D)_+$ there is a unique mild solution in $L^r$ (see (def:mild of the paper)), denoted by $\tilde{x}_t = (\tilde{u}_t, \tilde{z}_t)$, to
    \begin{equation}
        \tilde{x}_t =S(t) \tilde{x}_0 + (S * \tilde F(R,\tilde{x},\theta))_t + (S \diamond \tilde G(R, \tilde{x},\theta))_t
   \end{equation}
    Furthermore, the following properties hold:
    \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
        \item  $\tilde{x}_t \geq 0$.
        \item  $\tilde{u}_t = 0 \iff \tilde{u}_0 = 0$.
        \item  $t \mapsto \tilde{x}_t$ is almost surely a continuous map from $[0,\infty)$ to $B$.
        \item  If $(R_n,\tilde{x}_0^{(n)},\theta_n) \to (R,\tilde{x}_0,\theta)$ in $[0,\infty) \times C(\overline D)_+ \times \Theta$, then $\tilde{x}^{(n)}$, the solutions to (equation eq:mild-solution of the paper) with initial condition $\tilde{x}_0^{(n)}$ and $R = R_n$, $\theta = \theta_n$, converge to $\tilde{x}$ in $L^p(\Omega;C([0,T];B))$ for all $p,T > 0$.
        \item  If $\tilde{u}_0 \neq 0$ then $(r_t,v_t) \coloneqq (R\|\tilde{u}_t\|_{L^1}, \tilde{u}_t/\|\tilde{u}_t\|_{L^1})$ satisfies
        \begin{equation}
            \begin{aligned}
            dr &= r[\ip{v}{\tilde e_u} + \ip{\tilde F_u(r,v,\tilde{z})}{1_u}]dt + r\ip{\tilde G_u(r,v,\tilde{z})^*1_u}{dW_t} \\
            dv &= A_uvdt + v[-\ip{v}{\tilde e_u} - \ip{\tilde F_u(r,v,\tilde{z})}{1_u} + \|\tilde G_u(r,v,\tilde{z})^*1_u\|_\mathcal{U}^2]dt \\
            &+ \tilde F_u(r,v,\tilde{z})dt - \tilde G_u(r,v,\tilde{z})\tilde G_u(r,v,\tilde{z})^*1_udt \\
            &+ \tilde G_u(r,v,\tilde{z})dW_t- \ip{\tilde G_u(r,v,\tilde{z})^*1_u}{dW_t}v \,,
        \end{aligned}
    \end{equation}
    where the equation for $v$ holds in the mild sense of (def:mild of the paper). We omitted the dependence on $\theta$ for brevity.

    \item  Let $\bar{x}_t \coloneqq (R\tilde{u}_t, \tilde{z}_t) = (r_tv_t,\tilde{z}_t)$, where $(r_t, v_t)$ was defined in (v). Then
    \begin{equation}
        d\|\bar x_t\|_{\beta,2}^2 = [-2\|\bar x_t\|_{\beta+1/2,2}^2 +2\ip{\bar x_t}{F(\bar x_t)}_\beta + \|G(\bar x_t)\|_{\beta,2}^2]dt + 2\ip{\bar x_t}{G(\bar x_t)dW_t}_\beta \,,
    \end{equation}
    where $\beta$ is as in (SPDE-G-lem of the paper). 
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.313916+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d37fc60f77755dea72988016e87bfae2f0f87f74de5fb551eb9c9d783e3c2f6c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 41 of arXiv:2608.05931, 'Effective Lagrangian regularity and the uniqueness threshold for random H\"older velocity '] Suppose $U=\sum_{j=0}^\infty u^j$ satisfies Assumption~\ref{asmp:main for autonomous}. Additionally, suppose that for some $\alpha\in(0,1)$ and $p>1$, we have a constant $K\geq 1$ such that for $n\in\{0,1,2\}$ and all $j\in\N$,
\begin{equation}
\|\nabla^n u^j\|_{L^p_\omega \mathcal{C}^0_{x}}\leq K 2^{(n-\alpha)j}.
\end{equation}
    Then for all $\eps>\frac{d}{p}$ and $A\geq 1$ there exist vector fields $\{u^{j,A}\}_{j \geq 0}$ (on possibly a larger probability space, though coupled to the original $u^j$) also satisfying Assumption~\ref{asmp:main for autonomous} such that for all $j\geq 0$, $n\in\{0,1,2\}$,
\[\|\nabla^n u^{j,A}\|_{\mathcal{C}^0_{x}} \leq A K 2^{(n-\alpha+\eps)j},
\]
and, letting $U^A:=\sum_{j=0}^\infty u^{j,A}$, there exists $C(d,p,\eps)>0$ such that
\[\P(U^A\neq U)\leq C A^{1-p}.\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:41:28.169196+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d3855a06ae1b77810c9c2efa5a67e3e8cc9157d76d24ecb20a2871f85a1349ea","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L_strTWB of arXiv:2510.26724, 'Sharp Fuss-Catalan thresholds in graph bootstrap percolation'] Let $T$ be a TWG and $S\subsetneq T$ a partial TWG. Then, 
\begin{enumerate}
\item $\mathcal E(S)\geqslant 0$, with equality 
if and only $S$ is obtained from $T$ 
by removing one of its branches; 
\item $\mathcal D(S,T)\leqslant c\mathcal E(S)+2$; and 
\item $\mathcal T(S)\leqslant c\mathcal E(S)$, 
\end{enumerate}
for some constant $c$ depending only on $r$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:12:13.550791+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d386e72d9587dffc4fe37be27ff3d2240fd7943ebcdc042b172d775be680c1a7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 (Pointwise finite-particle convergence to the target in KSD) of arXiv:2608.28827, 'Quantitative Target Convergence and Uniform-in-Time\\ Propagation of Chaos for Langevin-Re'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:core-target} and \ref{ass:ksd-kernel},
