{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.775904+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d3900a7d21e77c9bd760e158aef5b49955a22c895284da575ae42c2f22191451","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop role-of-shifted-a of arXiv:2411.03065, 'Growing conditioned BGW trees with\\ log-concave offspring distributions'] Let $({\mathbf{a}},{\mathbf{b}})$ be a non-degenerate weight pair, with $r({\mathbf{a}})\geq2$ so that $({\mathbf{a}}^+,{\mathbf{b}})$ is also non-degenerate.
	Let $C_n$ be a $\PComp{{\mathbf{a}},{\mathbf{b}}}n$-distributed random composition  for some fixed $n\geq 1$.
	If we let $X_n=\mathrm{proj}_1(C_n)$ and $C'_n=\mathrm{proj}_{>1}(C_n)$, then $X_n$ has distribution given by
	\begin{align}
	\Prob{X_n=m}=\frac{b_m\cdot\PFComp{{\mathbf{a}}^+,{\mathbf{b}}}{n-m}}{\PFComp{{\mathbf{a}},{\mathbf{b}}}{n}},
	\qquad
	m=1,\dots,n,
	\end{align}
	and conditionally on $X_n$, the composition $C'_n$ has distribution $\PComp{{\mathbf{a}}^+,{\mathbf{b}}}{n-X_n}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.605869+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d393f412becd0ccd80fbb3f371eb09b1f026d9f0b9152199814af4889254e141","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition omega of arXiv:2606.03079, 'Mean Field Limits for Stochastic, Underdamped Reactive Langevin Dynamics Models'] Consider a fixed reaction $\mathcal{R}_{\ell}$, with $\nu$ a fixed particle distribution given by (equation ncen of the paper) with representation (equation eq:densitymeasdefmargrep of the paper). Using the notation of Definition (D:indexSpace of the paper), we define the allowable substrate index sampling space $\Omega^{(\ell)}(\nu) \subset \mathbb{I}^{(\ell)}$ as
$$
\Omega^{(\ell)}(\nu)= \begin{cases}\varnothing, & |\bm{\alpha}^{(\ell)}|=0, \\ \{\bm{i}=i_{1}^{(j)} \in \mathbb{I}^{(\ell)} | i_{1}^{(j)} \leq \langle 1, \nu^{j}\rangle\}, & |\bm{\alpha}^{(\ell)}|=\alpha_{\ell j}=1, \\ \{i=\bigl(i_{1}^{(j)}, i_{2}^{(j)}\bigr) \in \mathbb{I}^{(\ell)} | i_{1}^{(j)}<i_{2}^{(j)} \leq\langle 1, \nu^{j}\rangle\}, & |\bm{\alpha}^{(\ell)}|=\alpha_{\ell j}=2, \\ \{i=(i_{1}^{(j)}, i_{1}^{(k)}) \in \mathbb{I}^{(\ell)} | i_{1}^{(j)} \leq\langle 1, \nu^{j}\rangle, i_{1}^{(k)} \leq\langle 1, \nu^{k}\rangle\}, & |\bm{\alpha}^{(\ell)}|=2, \alpha_{\ell j}=\alpha_{\ell k}=1, j<k .\end{cases}
$$
Note that in the calculations that follow $\Omega^{(\ell)}(\nu)$ will change over time due to the fact that $\nu=\nu_{t}$ changes over time, but this will not be explicitly denoted for notational convenience.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.353665+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d397f37566e9333f9ffb872001adc7c5937c62dff46d5263ab7f77945574df08","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary of arXiv:2608.22945, 'A Momentum-Based Variance-Reduced Algorithm for Federated Multiobjective Optimization'] Under the conditions of
	Theorem~(T1 of the paper), FSMGDA-M-VR attains an $\epsilon$-Pareto stationary
	solution with communication complexity
