{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.646823+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d3b825ecc5069bf0c21d6d639a698f0c5a7c36bd14a5015fe5a796ee1899346f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:negligible W+ of arXiv:2512.17747, 'On exponentially height-penalized random trees'] {Recall $t_{\mu/n}=\argmin_{t \in (0,2)}\lambda_{\mu/n}(t)$, and} $X_{n,m}$ be as defined as in~(equation eq:def smt of the paper), and $\epsilon_n\ll1$ be such that $\epsilon_nt_n\gg1$ and $\epsilon_n^2(\mu^2n)^{1/3}\gg\log(\mu^2n)$.
