{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.594703+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d3bea0ab3a4fe45e4e38bbf86ef301854a63b05b02e7e0da64cb066460055105","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 of arXiv:2608.25706, 'Fast rates in Bayesian online learning with approximate posteriors'] Under \cref{ass:sequence_model}, there is an absolute constant $L_{\cM}>0$ such that
