    \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
        \item $f_n(x) \to f(x)$ for all continuity points $x$ of $f$;
        \item $G_{f_n} \to G_f$ for the Hausdorff distance;
        \item $\varphi_n \to \varphi$ for the uniform distance.
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.116695+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d3d3acd9226857205270b6bd620011d05ae0a860761cb2239cce762a005cabbd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2608.27433, 'Scalar curvature on K\"ahler blow-ups and systolic inequalities'] There are a real-valued function $\Gamma\in C^\infty(X\setminus S)$, a function $h_S\in\mathcal K^*$, and a nonzero constant $c_0$ depending only on the dimension such that, in the distributional sense,
\begin{equation}
  L_\omega\Gamma=h_S-c_0\delta_S
\end{equation}
Moreover, in a tubular neighbourhood of $S$,
\begin{equation}
  \Gamma=\log d^2+B+\Psi,
\end{equation}
where $B\in C^\infty(S)$, extended smoothly to the neighbourhood, and
\begin{equation}
  |\nabla^j\Psi|\le C_jd^{1-j}
  \qquad(j\ge0).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:51:44.766807+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d3d8e1f5cddb27c2bded273c742207a78e8a280748100017d02dcdcc3d3edcf4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 ({\cite[Theorem 4.6.1) of arXiv:2608.26803, 'On bubbling of Fueter maps'] {BarletMagnusson2019CyclesI}}]
  Let $X$ be a complex space and let $n \geq 0$. Then the set $\cC_n(X)$ of compact analytic $n$--cycles in $X$ admits a natural structure of a reduced complex space such that the tautological family of compact $n$--cycles in $X$, parameterized by $\cC_n(X)$, is a proper analytic family. Moreover, this family has the following universal property:

  If $S$ is a reduced complex space and $(Z_s)_{s \in S}$ is a proper analytic family of compact $n$--cycles in $X$, then the associated classifying map $f: S \rightarrow \cC_n(X),\, s \mapsto Z_s $ is holomorphic. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:00.763666+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d3de093f53c6c2b2605c7817fedfe7a2cd96b0799198d5d015135c1c00c3f708","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 (Convergence rate for L\'evy area) of arXiv:2512.04646, '\textbf{Canonical Rough Path over Tempered Fractional Brownian Motion: Existence, Construc'] Let $\mathbb{B}^{(N)}_{H,\lambda}$ be the piecewise linear
approximation of $\mathbb{B}_{H,\lambda}$ on a uniform partition of
$[0,T]$ with $N$ sub-intervals. For $H > 1/4$,
\begin{equation}

\mathbb{E}\bigl[|\mathbb{B}^{(N)}_{H,\lambda}(0,T)
  - \mathbb{B}_{H,\lambda}(0,T)|^2\bigr]^{1/2}
\le C(H,\lambda,T)\cdot N^{-2H},
\end{equation}
where
$C(H,\lambda,T) = \widetilde{C}(H)\cdot\max\{1,\lambda^{-2H}\}\cdot
T^{2H}$ with $\widetilde{C}(H)$ depending only on $H$. The rate
$N^{-2H}$ is optimal: no first-order piecewise linear scheme can
achieve a better rate.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.443419+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d3e2bf100cde1ba5fed4e93ddc3f8ddb46b14854022b4c4d88bf1e2170392d59","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:D_n=0 of arXiv:2508.17838, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices'] Let $n=n_1+\cdots+n_s$, 
