{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:28:33.871112+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d3f826832798fce003a64104e1511d173fba6201102d4d39af033cd8eb0292c9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-exp-mon-D-x of arXiv:2504.20963, 'Exponential moments of truncated branching random walk martingales'] Under the assumptions of Theorem~(thm-tail-D-x of the paper), there exists $\mkern 1mu\overline{\mkern-1mu \theta\mkern-1mu}\mkern 1mu>0$, such that for all  $n \in \mathbb{N} \cup \{\infty\}$ and $x\ge 0$,
