{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:52.655030+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d3fe4ef059c680eeb80800b6e026444cc224757bf03a9abd4fbc43425486bbad","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 15 of arXiv:2609.03713, 'A Sharp Mass Threshold for Boundedness in a Critical Quasilinear Chemotaxis Model with Ind'] Let $a>0$ and consider a sequence $(u_l)_{l\ge 1}$ in $\Sigma_a$ such that $\lambda_l^d:=\|u_l\|_\infty\to \infty$.
Then there exists a constant $\kappa>0$ depending on $d$, $a$, and $R$ such that
\begin{equation}
