{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:33:12.351579+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d440dd7aebc9bf80443a419d4947adca2dc039c3b52b1a85d57d3b4ccce9acd7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Ppn 188 of arXiv:2608.29416, 'Algorithmic threshold for high-dimensional projection pursuit I: general theory'] The following estimates hold for $N$ large enough. We have
	\beq
	\E Q^{\RomI}(1) \le L^{O(1)} \delta\,.
