{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.590613+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d44d566c184030ee8c3e50f3411b6ba389e0821b90d9cc7c448529312b086557","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma GLTNNRS-A of arXiv:2608.30582, 'The flexible part of intermittent Onsager theorem for the two-dimensional stochastic incom'] Let ${\mathbb{B}_{\frac{1}{2}}}\left( {\mathrm{Id}} \right)$ be the metric ball consisting of symmetric $2 \times 2$ matrices, where $\mathrm{Id}$ is the identity matrix. Then, there exist finite set $\Lambda  \subset {\mathbb{Z}^2}$ and smooth function ${\gamma _\xi }:\ {\mathbb{B}_{\frac{1}{2}}}\left( {\mathrm{Id}} \right) \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}$ for each $\xi \in \Lambda$ such that
