{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.662064+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d4534251b20aee9a0c9d9ba8e27b2f01985b8d3412e6fa75601b19602812fad6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:local-set-1 of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] Let $D$ and $\mathbb P_\delta$ be as in Lemma (lem:conv-fields-fractal of the paper). Let $\ell_\delta$ be an inner boundary of the boundary cluster of $\hat\mathbf{n}_\delta$ on $D_\delta$, with parity label $c_\delta$. Let $\mathcal O(\ell_\delta)$ be the induced subgraph of $D_\delta$ whose vertices are enclosed by $\ell_\delta$, and let $\mathcal{O}(\ell_\delta)^*$ be its \emph{strong} dual graph, where all vertices of $D_\delta^\dagger$ belonging to $\ell_\delta$ are identified. Then,
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item[$\bullet$]  the law of the restriction of $\tau_\delta$ to $\mathcal O(\ell_\delta)$ is that of $-c_\delta$ times a XOR-Ising model $\tau_\delta^{\ell_\delta}$ with free boundary conditions, 
        \item[$\bullet$]  the law of the restriction of $\tau_\delta^\dagger$ to $\mathcal O(\ell_\delta)^*$ is that of $c_\delta$ times a XOR-Ising model  $(\tau_\delta^{\ell_\delta})^\dagger$  with $+$ boundary conditions.
    \end{enumerate}
    Moreover, every subsequential limit as $\delta\to0$ of the joint law
    \begin{equation}
        \left( h_\delta,\ \ell_\delta,\ c_\delta,\ \tau_\delta,\ \tau_\delta^\dagger,\ \tau_\delta^{\ell_\delta},\ (\tau_\delta^{\ell_\delta})^\dagger \right) 
    \end{equation}
    is given by 
    \begin{equation}
        \left(\frac{1}{2\sqrt{2}\lambda}\ h,\ \ell,\ c,\ \field{\cos(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\phi)},\ \field{\sin(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\phi)},\ \field{\sin(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\phi^\ell)},\ \field{\cos(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\phi^\ell)} \right),
    \end{equation}
    where 
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item[$\bullet$] the loop $\ell$ is a loop of the two-valued set $\mathds A_{-\sqrt{2}\lambda, \sqrt{2}\lambda}$ of $h$,
        \item[$\bullet$] the label $c$ is the label of the above two-valued set,
        \item[$\bullet$] given $\ell$, the conditional law of $\phi^\ell$ is that of a GFF with zero boundary conditions in $\mathcal O(\ell)$,
        \item[$\bullet$] given $\ell$, the label $c$ and the pair $\big(\field{\cos(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\phi^\ell)}, \ \field{\sin(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\phi^\ell)} \big)$ are conditionally independent.
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:11.635920+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d45927ee621e3dcb2e9d2cd8f7fac7d5314a560a1c5f2b64cb66bff701da5b32","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2605.31300, 'Cone-Additive Functions for Random Walks on Free Products of Graphs'] Let be $\pi=[u_0,\ldots,u_m]\in\Pi$ and $v\in V$. Then:
