{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:50:30.565846+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d465523e1242924c1b7298ac1899417aaf0f2e6a9fa2395981d392dc78721aa5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 18 of arXiv:2605.30616, 'Brownian motion: the hyperbolic number setting'] A second-order $\mathbb{H}$-valued stochastic
process indexed by $\mathbb{H}$ is a map $p\mapsto X(p)$ from $\mathbb{H}$
into ${L}_{2}(\Omega,\mathcal{C},P_{\mathbb{H}})$. Its covariance
function is defined to be 
\begin{equation}
E_{\mathbb H}(X(p)X(q))=\int_{\Omega}X(p,\w)X(q,\w)dP_{\mathbb{H}}(\w).
\end{equation}
With 
\begin{equation}
X(p)=U\begin{pmatrix}X_{1}(p) & 0\\
0 & X_{2}(p)
\end{pmatrix}U,
\end{equation}
we have 
\begin{equation}
E_{\mathbb H}(X(p)X(q))=U\begin{pmatrix}E_{1}(X_{1}(p)X_{1}(q)) & 0\\
0 & E_{2}(X_{2}(p)X_{2}(q))
\end{pmatrix}U.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:23:05.283401+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d466df0547b56925445ced594ed6a4d770d366fa29c78ee26af2bbe3b491aa46","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 (Arbitrary selection equals simultaneous protection) of arXiv:2608.21496, '2608.21496'] A confidence system is valid at level $1-\alpha$ after \emph{every} measurable target-selection rule if and only if it covers all targets simultaneously:
