{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.548192+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d4a4ac00e5eb37b57177b2af6b53683b49a7efba020ab2d7cf75232eda76f863","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 35 (Expectation of total mass) of arXiv:2604.01852, 'The on/off Brownian snake'] Let $\mu_{\rm d}$, $\mu_{\rm a} \in \mathcal{M}_F(\mathbb{R}^d)$ be such that $\mu_{\rm d} + \mu_{\rm a}$ is a non-zero measure and let $\gamma$, $c$, $\Tilde{c}>0$. Let $\mathcal{Y}=(\mathcal{Y}^{(\rm d)}, \mathcal{Y}^{(\rm a)})$ be an $\text{ooSBM}(\gamma, c, \Tilde{c})$ with initial measure $(\mu_{\rm d}, \mu_{\rm a})$. Then, for any $s \geq 0$ we have
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathbb{E}(\norm{\mathcal{Y}^{(\rm d)}_s}) = \norm{\mu_{\rm d}} \frac{c+ \Tilde{c}e^{-s(c+\Tilde{c})}}{c+\Tilde{c}} + \norm{\mu_{\rm a}} \frac{c(1-e^{-s(c+\Tilde{c})})}{c+\Tilde{c}}; \hspace{0.1cm} \mathbb{E}(\norm{\mathcal{Y}^{(\rm a)}_s}) = \norm{\mu_{\rm d}} \frac{\Tilde{c}(1-e^{-s(c+\Tilde{c})})}{c+\Tilde{c}} + \norm{\mu_{\rm a}} \frac{ce^{-s(c+\Tilde{c})} + \Tilde{c}}{c+\Tilde{c}}.
    \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:07:56.653000+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d4a8c9daa7d11d24cd0740cd0ad8b8c56001095aea682e9732341cdc3e3e1f67","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:GRR of arXiv:2411.04590, 'Singular stochastic delay equations driven by fractional Brownian motion: Dynamics, longti'] Let $\gamma < \frac{1}{2}$, $p > 2$, and let $\xi \colon [-r,0] \rightarrow \mathbb{R}^n$ be an $\gamma$-H\"older path. Then, there exists a constant $A_p$ such that
				\begin{align}
					\| \xi \|_{\gamma} = \sup_{-1 \leq s < t \leq 0}\frac{\|\xi_{s,t}\|}{(t-s)^{\gamma}} \leq A_p \left( \iint_{[-r,0]^2} \frac{\|\xi_u - \xi_v\|^p}{|u-v|^{p\gamma + 2}} \, du \, dv \right)^{\frac{1}{p}}.
				\end{align}
				If $X$ is $\gamma$-H\"older and $(\xi, \xi') \in \mathscr{D}_{X}^{\gamma}([-r,0])$, then
				\begin{align}
					\sup_{-r \leq s < t \leq 0}\frac{\|\xi^{\#}_{s,t}\|}{(t-s)^{2\gamma}} \leq A_p \left[ \left( \iint_{-r \leq u < v \leq 0} \frac{\|\xi^{\#}_{u,v}\|^p}{|u-v|^{2\gamma p + 2}} \, du \, dv \right)^{\frac{1}{p}} + \|\xi'\|_{\gamma} \|X\|_{\gamma} \right].
				\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.361938+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d4b220eaf9bb5e9f07d9f6ca4c76717958596d535fe88eeabd091560bfc68d98","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 37 of arXiv:2606.17859, 'Full $\Gamma-$expansion for the level-two large deviation rate functionals of non-reversib'] Let $I$ be a subset of $\bb Z$ and consider a family $\mz F$ of
