{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:21:06.867303+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d4b4757d6b5ce0e4bbe126e745628650f1f9f4687ab71b4667fac04d126add9a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 1 of arXiv:2608.21255, 'Laws of the iterated logarithm for random Dirichlet series with general weights'] Let $\alpha>-1/2$. Assume that $\me[\eta]=0$ and $\sigma^2=\me[\eta^2]\in(0,\infty)$. Then
\begin{equation}
