{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:56:00.669202+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d4d4ab18248e62dd0b98913a0f25b73be4f33a779be4dcda9dfd730b410cf1de","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem_large_dev_up of arXiv:2604.14851, 'Pool model: a mass preserving multi particle aggregation process'] For all fixed $\lambda>0$ and any $\epsilon>0$, there is an event $E_{\epsilon}$ such that ${\bf P}(E_{\epsilon})=1$ and that for all $\omega\in E_{\epsilon}$ there is some $R_0(\omega)<\infty$ so that 
