{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:48:25.143328+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d4d7b483ce5825ecfb794897bc758799b7e4239ff49dfa75bf249af1a38266bc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:tail-rate of arXiv:2607.04620, 'The Exact Ville Identity\\ \large From the Absorbing Case to the General Law\\ with an App'] Let $S_n$ be a centered martingale with $\mathbb{E}[S_n^2]=n$, and let $T$ be a first-passage time with $L=\mathbb{E}[S_T\mathbf{1}(T<\infty)]$ finite as in (thm:conservation of the paper). Then, from the moment inequalities of [klass2026beyond], for every $p>1$,
\begin{equation}
  |L|^{p/(p-1)}
  \le
  \liminf_{n\to\infty}\mathbb{P}(T>n)
  \left(\mathbb{E}[|S_n|^p\mathbf{1}(T>n)]\right)^{1/(p-1)}.

\end{equation}
The case $p=2$, after dropping the indicator inside the moment, gives the cruder $\liminf_n n\mathbb{P}(T>n)\ge L^2$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:17:17.102395+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d4ddbe8d0217652f61ed0f8c64823aa68e8ed3cc9f099539d86629d6d9197399","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 (Relative Palm determinant comparison) of arXiv:2608.20101, '\bfseries Largest bulk gap of the complex Ginibre ensemble'] Fix \(s<1\) and \(C_0<\infty\). There are \(c,C>0\) such that, uniformly for
\(|a|\le s\) and \(0\le r\le C_0n^{-1/2}(\log n)^{1/4}\),
\begin{equation}
 0\le\log\frac{q_n(a,r)}{q(\sqrt n\,r)}\le Ce^{-cn+nr^2}.
\end{equation}
In particular, \(q_n(a,r)/q(\sqrt n\,r)=1+O(e^{-c'n})\) uniformly in this range.
Also
\begin{equation}
 K_n(a,a)=\frac n\pi\bigl(1+O(e^{-c'n})\bigr).
