{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:35:10.800198+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d51983c4f63a77f17372197f2523848359aad2a1cf50390086c1259face99d30","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemme 76 (Chernoff bound) of arXiv:2604.00635, 'Large deviations of the periodic Toda chain'] Let $\{X_i\}_{i=1}^{n-1}$ be a collection of $n-1$ random uniformly distributed iid variables on $\intff{0}{1}$. Then, for any  $\xi \geq 1$,
