{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:09:23.970104+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d51a291b1fe725be8d70ce2271b3261f952df92f7679fffc552cb42f4d82003d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 22 of arXiv:2607.22416, 'A multi-player optimal stopping game based on a spider Brownian bridge'] There exists a Nash equilibrium in the multi-player version of the optimal stopping game with linear payoffs, if for every $i\in\{1,...,N\}$ 
