{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:32:23.846183+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d51b9a0facced450fda634c23e49e0a40de97487f881bf8f571bbc8760e8c29a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma timeregularity-es of arXiv:2603.26307, '\LARGE The incompressible Navier--Stokes--Fourier system with thermal noise'] Let 
			$(u_{\epsilon} ,\psi_{\epsilon},q_\epsilon)$ be the weak martingale solutions to  (equation ep_approx of the paper)--(equation eqn354865865 of the paper) with initial data $(u_0,\psi_0)$ constructed in Proposition (prp-existence-ep of the paper). Then, for every $\alpha \in (0,1/2)$ and $l > 5/2$, there exists a constant \[C = C(\alpha,l, u_0,\psi_0, F_1,F_2, G_1,G_2,T) <\infty, \] such that
