{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:45:17.709637+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d52bf7f7904ac088ab3122347fddbe93aa1005290b3a86071a032f1ffd8d02c3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm occu mdp of arXiv:2604.10509, 'Nonequilibrium fluctuations and moderate deviations for the occupation time of the SSEP wi'] As $n \rightarrow \infty$, the sequence  $\{ \Gamma^n (t)/a_n, 0 \leq t \leq T\}$ satisfies the moderate deviation principles with decay rate $a_n^2$ and with rate function ${\mathcal I}_T$ in the space $C([0,T], \mathbb R)$. Precisely speaking,
	for any closed set $C$ and any open set $O$ in $C ([0,T], \mathbb R)$,
	\begin{align*}
		\limsup_{n \rightarrow \infty} \frac{1}{a_n^2} \log \mathbb P^n_{\rho_*} \Big( \{  \Gamma^n (t)/a_n , 0 \leq t \leq T\} \in C\Big) \leq - \inf_{\gamma \in C} \mathcal{I}_T (\gamma),\\
		\liminf_{n \rightarrow \infty} \frac{1}{a_n^2} \log \mathbb P^n_{\rho_*} \Big( \{ \Gamma^n (t)/a_n, 0 \leq t \leq T\} \in O\Big) \geq - \inf_{\gamma \in O} \mathcal{I}_T (\gamma).
	\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.121990+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d52e6289375e7a63e75272d8f8b8961d01873c973ebaf833b57dc0f68380af08","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conj desirables of arXiv:2601.20502, 'Optimal matching under size priority'] Under the setting and notation of Theorem~(maintheorem2 of the paper), let us write $\mathcal{M}_{\max}(G_n)$ the set of maximum size matchings in $G_n$, then:
        \begin{equation}
            \begin{aligned}
                \lim_{n \rightarrow +\infty} \mathbb{E}\left[ \frac{1}{|E(G_n)|} \sum_{e \in E(G_n)} \mathbbm{1}_{\forall M \in \mathcal{M}_{\max}(G_n), e \in M}\right] = \mathbb{P}_{((i,Z),(i',Z'))\sim \zeta'\otimes\zeta'}\left( i+i'<k \right), \\
                \lim_{n \rightarrow +\infty} \mathbb{E}\left[ \frac{1}{|E(G_n)|} \sum_{e \in E(G_n)} \mathbbm{1}_{\forall M \in \mathcal{M}_{\max}(G_n), e \notin M}\right] = \mathbb{P}_{((i,Z),(i',Z'))\sim \zeta'\otimes\zeta'}\left( i+i'>k \right).
            \end{aligned}
        \end{equation} (Stated as a conjecture by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:48:24.311477+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d53157fbfdf72f8df4ce23c641a1cc0ad25e8b631b0c7c34de43ad8723146513","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition rthm:ID rep of arXiv:2605.31356, 'P\'olya--Schur problems and free probability'] A probability measure $\mu$ on $\mathbb{R}$ is $\boxplus$-ID if and only if $R_{\mu}$ can be analytically extended to the lower half-plane and there exists a positive finite Borel measure $\Sigma$ on $\mathbb{R}$ and a real number $c$ such that 
	\begin{equation}
		R_{\mu}(u)=c+\int_{\mathbb{R}}\frac{u+x}{1-xu}\mathrm{d}\Sigma(x).
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:01:48.560798+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d531d2a49a7cf4abea0b7ce23b398f81f8008980b3dff4b678c266d266ee3f5d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:class_B of arXiv:2606.29622, 'Affine Structure of the Brownian Signature'] We say that $\bm{p} \in \mathcal{B} \subset T(\mathbb{C}^2)$ if there exist three complex numbers
    $$
    \alpha, \beta \in \{z \in \mathbb{C}\colon \, \mathfrak{Re}(z) > 0\} \cup \{ 0\}, \quad \gamma \in \mathbb{C},
    $$
    two natural numbers $m, n \in \mathbb{N}^*$, and three coefficients $\bm{q}, \bm{r}, \bm s \in T(\mathbb{C}^2)$ satisfying
    \begin{align}
        \deg_{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{1}}}}(\bm{q}) < 2n,  \quad \deg_{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{0}}}}(\bm{q}) = 0, \quad \deg_{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{1}}}}(\bm{r}) < 2m, \quad \deg_{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{1}}}}(\bm s) < 2m \land 2n,
