{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.742549+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d55074263fbdec3aed4858036ffac6ce75cc4063ec27ba23fdd410b1619a7702","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:ExpGSA of arXiv:2605.05193, 'Grokability in five inequalities'] Fix $n\ge 1$, $\rho>0$, and an integer $N\ge 1$.
Let $x_1,\dots,x_N$ be i.i.d.\ uniform on the unit sphere $S^n\subset\mathbb{R}^{n+1}$ and set
\[
Q:=\bigcap_{j=1}^N\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{n+1}:\ \langle x,x_j\rangle\le \rho\}.
\]
Then
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{E}\,\operatorname{GSA}(Q)
=
N\,\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}e^{-\rho^2/2}
\int_{\mathbb{R}^n}\varphi_n(y)\,\bigl(1-p(|y|)\bigr)^{N-1}\,dy,
\end{equation}
where $p(r)$ depends only on $r\ge 0$ and is given by
\begin{equation}
p(r)=
\Bigg(\int_{-\sqrt{r^2+\rho^2}}^{\sqrt{r^2+\rho^2}}
\Bigl(1-\frac{t^2}{r^2+\rho^2}\Bigr)^{\frac{n-2}{2}}\,dt\Bigg)^{-1}
\int_{\rho}^{\sqrt{r^2+\rho^2}}
\Bigl(1-\frac{t^2}{r^2+\rho^2}\Bigr)^{\frac{n-2}{2}}\,dt .
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

