{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:57:07.196566+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d57fc308d9764eec61a144ac0cb4ea71f7841ff960b37abf55b7363ee34b080f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:cigar-shape of arXiv:2509.04333, 'The limiting law of the Discrete Gaussian level lines'] Fix $A, B$ with angle denoted $\theta_{A, B}$ and $B_1 - A_1 = M_{A, B}$. Define the curves $\ensuremath{\mathcal C}^\pm_{A, B}$ by
