{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.303690+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d591c0437aafcd816c836b31a482f8d3f74fda52b3a8c68e0a55b10d9cb8b051","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 43 (Anti-concentration/heat kernel estimates) of arXiv:2510.22155, 'Random walks in space-time random media in all spatial dimensions: the full subcritical fl'] Fix $\sigma>0$, $M>0$, $K > 0$. Let $F:[0,\infty)\to[0,\infty)$ be decreasing and of exponential decay at infinity. Let $\br_0 \in \Ekk$ be centered and $\delta$-repulsive. Then
    \begin{itemize} 
