       \item $d=1$. We have the weaker estimate just for the centered chain: $$\mathbf P_{\x}^{\br_0} ( |\mathbf R_r - \y|\le 1) \leq Cr^{-kd/2}  \big( 1+ r^{-1/2} |\x-\y|\big)^{-K}.$$ We also have the following time-averaged bound for non-centered chains when $q\ge 4$: there exists $\epsilon>0$ so that for all $\lambda>0$ one has 
