{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:41.036759+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d5c7fea9bfb739fd8a342e34e1a16bcf3a2d2a6cd49e4ef16e63b803b2c0608b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 2-l10 of arXiv:2412.04015, 'Linear fluctuation of interfaces in Glauber-Kawasaki dynamics'] Fix a function $G\colon {\mathbb R}_+ \times {\mathbb T}^{d}_N \to {\mathbb R}$ and a
cylinder function $f$. Then, there exists a finite constant
${\mathfrak c}({\boldsymbol u}^N)$, depending only on ${\boldsymbol u}^N$, $f$ and $d$, uniformly
bounded in $N$, such that
\begin{align*}
& {\mathbb E}_{\nu^N} \Big[\, \Big|\,
\int_0^t \, 
\sum_{x\in {\mathbb T}^d_N} G (s, x)\,
(\Xi^{\rm c}_{{\boldsymbol u}^N (\cdot), x}  f) (\eta (s))
\, ds \, \Big| \,\Big]
\\ 
&\quad \;\le \;
