{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.094666+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d5cc6c20a16ff13ff3b5809beff2ea30063a2d7449de43acbc3c1d4156bd17c3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop inside:L of arXiv:2411.12717, 'Excursion theory for Markov processes indexed by Lévy trees'] There exists
  sequences $(\delta_k)_{k \geq 0}$,  $(\upsilon_k)_{k \geq 0}$ and   $(\varepsilon_k^{\prime\prime})_{k \geq 0}$  of positive numbers  converging towards $0$  as $k \to \infty$ such that,  under $\mathbf{N}_{x,r}$, the following convergence  holds a.e.
