{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.529728+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d5de26d86aaaaa4d6538babd54db078a949855e6d2becdabd5b140b18657cddb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary eq:block-average-Chernoff of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[corollary]{cor:sharp-block-average}
In the ordered model, assume the stronger finite-\(N\) profile MGF
condition \(({\rm PSG})_p\).  Let
\(S\subset[N]\), \(\left\lvertS\right\rvert=k\), and set
\[
 \overline J_S=\frac1{k^p}\sum_{I\in S^p}J_I,
 \qquad
 u_S=k^{-1/2}\sum_{i\in S}e_i.
\]
For every \(b,a\ge0\),
\begin{align}
 \mathbb P\{\overline J_S\ge b\}
 &\le\exp\{-k^pb^2/2\},\\
 \mathbb P\{h_N^J(u_S)\ge a\}
 &\le e^{-Na^2/2}.
\end{align}
Moreover,
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb P\left\{\max_{\left\lvertS\right\rvert=k}h_N^J(u_S)\ge a\right\}
 \le\binom Nk e^{-Na^2/2}.
\end{equation}
Hence the right-hand side has exponential rate at most
\(-a^2/2\) whenever \(k=o(N)\).  If
\(k_N=N^{\gamma+o(1)}\), the coefficient level
\[
 b_{N,k_N}(a)=\frac{a\sqrt N}{k_N^{p/2}}
 =aN^{(1-p\gamma)/2+o(1)}
\]
interpolates, for \(0\le\gamma\le1/p\), between a quadratic-scale
spike (with endpoint \(k=1\)) and a fixed-amplitude mesoscopic coherent
block.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:09:23.953428+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d5e3093cc78a356a0dbd50d6bd370ebf37029ea3d8ba83fcf955fe260f87147f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 23 of arXiv:2607.21759, 'Marchenko--Pastur law for tensor powers of exchangeable unconditional vectors'] For each $n$, let $\nu = \nu^{(n)}$ be an exchangeable distribution on $\R^n$. There is an explicit sequence of probability distributions $\{w_n\}$ on $\mathcal P(\R)$ such that \begin{equation}
        \int_{\mathcal P(\R)} \Bigl(\int_{\R} x_1^2 \,d\theta\Bigr)^k \,dw_n = \frac{1}{n^k} \int \bigl(x_1^2 + \dotsm + x_n^2\bigr)^k\,d\nu.
    \end{equation}
    Therefore if for some $k \leq n$, we have \begin{equation}\int x_1^{2}\dotsm x_{k}^2\,d\nu - \frac{1}{n^k} \int \bigl(x_1^2 + \dotsm + x_n^2\bigr)^k\,d\nu \to 0, \end{equation}
    then \begin{equation}
        \int x_1^2\dotsm x_k^2 \,d\nu - \int_{\mathcal P(\R)} \Bigl(\int_{\R} x_1^2 \,d\theta\Bigr)^k \,dw_n \to 0. 
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:42:08.467850+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d5e445691def5ff364ba53d84819b4ad9fd25eb9251eb63f077c14942c44c333","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eq:decompLTn of arXiv:2511.15893, 'On a Class of Dynamical Poisson-Voronoi Tessellations'] Let $\rho\geq 0$. In the multi-speed case, the Laplace transform of $T$ under the Palm probability measure $\mathbb{P}^0_{{\mathcal V }}$ is given by:

