{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.292369+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d5f4744c4bbf8796c2849cc6ff890bc2f40c72e66ba76bddfcc021d020b766ae","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:uc of arXiv:2603.22652, 'A cohesive account on the ergodic behaviours and scaling limits of Random Walks in Cooling'] If the environment law $\mu$ is uniformly elliptic, $\lim_k z_k = z$, and $\lim_k n_k =\infty$ then, for $m_k = |[[n_k z]]_{n_k} - [[n_k z_{k}]]_{n_k}|$ 
