{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.617982+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d5f7394502e4a0beded6a61dc9091545d6cf3c28ae41d042e12db81e0a0f1f09","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 34 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] There exists~$\tilde c>0$ such that for all $n\ge1$, all $\gamma\colon\{0,\dots,n\}\to[0,\infty)$ and all $s\ge u\ge0$,
\begin{equation}

