$$
is an element of $\Lc$. 
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:16:53.569352+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d63d4291ea8597346592def490a7da0027d5603f7c4450c801f8a773843ba018","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:diff_char of arXiv:2412.04589, 'Inverting the Markovian projection for pure jump processes'] Let $X$ be an $\mathbb{R}^d$-valued It\^o semimartingale. The \emph{differential characteristics} of $X$ associated with a truncation function $h: \mathbb{R}^d \to \mathbb{R}^d$ is the triplet $(\beta, \alpha, \kappa)$ consisting in:\footnote{By truncation function, we mean that $h$ is measurable, bounded and $h(x) = x$ in a neighborhood of $0$.}
	\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*), nosep]
		\item $\beta$ is an $\mathbb{R}^d$-valued predictable process such that $\int_0^\cdot \beta_s \,ds$ is the predictable finite variation part of the special semimartingale $X^h \coloneqq X - \sum_{s \leq \cdot} (\Delta X_s - h(\Delta X_s))$.

		\item $\alpha$ is an $\mathbb{S}_+^d$-valued predictable process such that $\int_0^\cdot \alpha_s \,ds = \langle X^c, X^c \rangle \coloneqq (\langle X^{i, c}, X^{j, c} \rangle)_{1 \leq i, j \leq d}$, where $X^c = (X^{i, c})_{1 \leq i \leq d}$ is the continuous local martingale part of $X$.

		\item $\kappa$ is a predictable L\'evy transition kernel from $\Omega \times \mathbb{R}_+$ to $\mathbb{R}^d$ such that $\kappa_t(d\xi) dt$ is the compensator of the jump measure $\mu^X$ of $X$, where $\mu^X(dt, d\xi) \coloneqq \sum_{s > 0} \bm{1}_{\{\Delta X_s \neq 0\}} \delta_{(s, \Delta X_s)}(dt, d\xi)$ is an integer-valued random measure on $\mathbb{R}_+ \times \mathbb{R}^d$.\footnote{By L\'evy transition kernel, we mean that $\kappa_{\omega, t}(d\xi)$ is a L\'evy measure on $\mathbb{R}^d$ for each $(\omega, t) \in \Omega \times \mathbb{R}_+$, i.e.\ $\kappa_{\omega, t}(\{0\}) = 0$ and $\int_{\mathbb{R}^d} 1 \land |\xi|^2 \,\kappa_{\omega, t}(d\xi) < \infty$.}
	\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.257562+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d645d93ed36a8452c9bde011aa698f5dc28755b4757e9a73fd478444a5d31138","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 65 of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] Suppose that \cref{ncptas} is satisfied. 
  We regard $F$ and $F_n$ as subsets of a common $\bcm$ space $(M,d)$.
  Let $x\in F$ and $x_n\in F_n$. Take $r_{\infty}\ge r_0$ satisfying 
  $x\in B(\rho,r_{\infty})$ and $x_n\in B(\rho_n,r_{\infty})$.
  Then, for any $f\in\BL^{\kappa}(M),\kappa\in [1/2,1]$ and $t>0$
  \begin{align*}
    |P_{t}f(x)-P^n_tf(x_n)|
    \lesssim\|f\|_{\BL^{\kappa}}
    \inf\Bigl\{  \Psi_1(n,r)+C_n(r)\Psi_2(n,r)^E : r\in [r_{\infty},\infty), \Psi_2(n,r)\le \frac{1}{2}\Bigr\},
  \end{align*}
  where
  \begin{equation*}
    \Psi_1(n,r)=P_{x}^n(\sigma_{B(\rho,r)^c}\le t)\vee P_{x_n}^n(\sigma^n_{B(\rho_n,r)^c}\le t),
  \end{equation*}
  \begin{equation*}
    \Psi_2(n,r)=d_{\rm{H}}(F^{(r)},F_n^{(r)})^{\kappa}+d_{\BL^{\kappa}}(\mu^{(r)},\mu^{(r)}_n)+d(x,x_n),
  \end{equation*}
  \begin{equation*}
    \begin{aligned}
      C_n(r)=&(D_n^{(r)})^{4+2(1+\frac{s}{2(1+s)\theta})(2\kappa-1)}\\
    &\quad\times \left[(\diam K_n^{(r)}+\mu_n(F_n^{(r)}))\diam K_n^{(r)}\mu_n(F_n^{(r)})\mu(F^{(r)})^{3/2}\diam F^{(r)}(\mu(F^{(r)})^{1/2}+\mu_n(F_n^{(r)}))\right]\\
    \lesssim& r^{6+\frac{3}{2}s+2(1+\frac{s}{2(1+s)\theta})(2\kappa-1)}(r+\mu_n(F^{(r)}))(r^{s/2}+\mu_n(F^{(r)}))(r^s+\mu_n(F^{(r)}))^{4+2(1+\frac{s}{2(1+s)\theta})(2\kappa-1)},
    \end{aligned}
  \end{equation*}
  \begin{equation*}
    K_n^{(r)}=F^{(r)}\cup F_n^{(r)},\qquad D_n^{(r)}=\mu(F^{(r)})\diam F^{(r)}\vee \mu_n(F^{(r)}_n)\diam F^{(r)}_n,
  \end{equation*}
  and
  \begin{equation*}
    E=\frac{\kappa}{\kappa+(1+s)(2+\kappa)(\kappa+\theta)}.
  \end{equation*}
  Moreover, the time-dependence of the constant in $\lesssim$ is $t^{[\kappa-\frac{s}{2(1+s)\theta}(2\kappa-1)]},\;t\in (0,1]$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.559499+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d64b1664943796006ef345e365b04aa9f1e6dd75ba81d44da17606c576f80212","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:discrete-binary of arXiv:2604.04882, 'On a Problem of M. Kac on Laplace Distributions'] Let $L$ be as in Lemma~(lem:discrete-L of the paper), and let $\eta\in\cB$ be indecomposable. Suppose
