{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:06.326356+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d64b34fc9eebf7bd07ea424fe4d98253e7d9498cc4feb944b0ac096fb9935f1b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 13 of arXiv:2607.06242, 'Exponential mixing and Freidlin--Wentzell large deviation principle for Markov cocycles'] The family $\{\Phi_{0,\cdot,\sigma}^{\eps}u_0\}_{\eps\in(0,1]}$ of solutions of \eqref{e.080302} with time symbol $\sigma$ satisfies the Freidlin--Wentzell uniform LDP on $C([0,T];H)$ with rate function $I_{u_0,T}^{\sigma}$ if the following two conditions hold for the law $\nu_{u_0,\sigma}^{\eps}$ of the solution $\Phi_{0,\cdot,\sigma}^{\eps}u_0$:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item[(1)] For every $R>0$, $M\geq0$, and $\d,\d'>0$, there exists $\eps_0>0$ such that
        \begin{align*}
          \inf_{\|u_0\|\leq R}\inf_{\xi\in\{I_{u_0,T}^{\sigma}\leq M\}}
          \left(
          \nu_{u_0,\sigma}^{\eps}\bigl(\Nc_{\d'}(\xi)\bigr)
          -e^{-(I_{u_0,T}^{\sigma}(\xi)+\d)/\eps}
          \right)\geq0,
          \qquad \forall \eps\in(0,\eps_0],
        \end{align*}
        where $\Nc_{\d'}(\xi)$ is the $\d'$-neighborhood of $\xi$ in $C([0,T];H)$.

        \item[(2)] For every $R>0$, $M\geq0$, and $\d,\d'>0$, there exists $\eps_0>0$ such that
        \begin{align*}
          \sup_{\|u_0\|\leq R}
          \nu_{u_0,\sigma}^{\eps}
          \left(C([0,T];H)\setminus\Nc_{\d'}(I_{u_0,T}^{\sigma},M)\right)
          \leq e^{-(M-\d)/\eps},
          \qquad \forall \eps\in(0,\eps_0],
        \end{align*}
        where $\Nc_{\d'}(I_{u_0,T}^{\sigma},M)$ is the $\d'$-neighborhood of the level set $\{I_{u_0,T}^{\sigma}\leq M\}$.
    \end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.821651+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d651b85122f3fba33de8fba20ff367fe7688432916f45235b214a7f0c6290ddc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 5 of arXiv:2604.10142, 'H\MakeLowercase{arnack inequality for} $p$\MakeLowercase{-harmonic functions: \\ improved '] Let $u$ be a positive $p$-harmonic function on $B_5(0)$. Then $u$ satisfies the Harnack inequality:
