{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.331619+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d66921aac787488b60c92a471f036e8896fa05f7fe07d2c79e9c7cdc9dd344c6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Th:Chen-Strichartz of arXiv:2411.06827, 'The Exponential Lie Series and a Chen--Strichartz Formula for L{\'e}vy Processes'] The logarithm of  the flowmap has the following series representation
\begin{enumerate}
\begin{align*}
	\log\varphi_t 
& \,= \log\biggl(\sum\limits_{w\in{\mathbb A}^\ast} J_w(t) V_w\biggr)
\\
 &\,   = \sum\limits_{w\in{\mathbb A}^\ast}J_w(t)\biggl(\sum_{\sigma\in{\mathbb S}(|w|)}
\frac{1}{|\sigma|} c_\sigma 
V_{[\sigma (w)]_{\mathrm L}}\biggr),
\end{align*} 
\end{enumerate}
where 
$$
	c_\sigma:=\frac{(-1)^{d(\sigma)}}{|\sigma|}
	\biggl(\begin{array}{c}
	|\sigma|-1\\
	d(\sigma)
		\end{array}
	\biggr),
$$
and where $d(\sigma)$ denotes the number of descents in the permutation $\sigma \in {\mathbb S}_{|w|}$ and $|\sigma|:=|w|$. In particular, it can be represented as
$$\log\varphi_t = \sum\limits_{w\in{\mathbb A}^\ast} J_w(t) V_{\psi(w)},$$
where
$\psi(w):=\sum\limits_{\sigma\in{\mathbb S}(|w|)} 
\frac{1}{|\sigma|}c_\sigma [\sigma (w)]_{\mathrm L}$ is a Lie series.
Here $[w]_{\mathrm L}$ denotes the left-to-right Lie-bracketing of its letters, i.e., we have 
$
	[a_1\cdots a_n]_{\mathrm L}
	=[a_1, [a_2, \ldots [a_{n-1}, a_n]_{\mathrm L}]_{\mathrm L}\ldots ]_{\mathrm L}.
$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.528165+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d66a76c7cfd9f86c0fe0a1de01166ee42f94cd6658aa8ef37bf8c6859b72bed5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2604.01852, 'The on/off Brownian snake'] Recall the Poisson random measure from Definition \ref{definition oo snake} and its index set $I$. Let $i \in I$, let $\varepsilon>0$ and let $s>0$. Let $h = \varepsilon/2$ and recall $(\mathcal{Z}^{(\varepsilon, \rm d)}_{s,i}, \mathcal{Z}^{(\varepsilon, \rm a)}_{s,i})$ from Proposition \ref{proposition identification oobmm h erased tree}. Then we have
