{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.419977+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d671ba8e4a648ea07c32f6ac33cfc3a2b9fd513efdec06f019e1640152c59b10","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 125 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] In the setting of Theorem~\ref{proposition_FFF_conditioning}, let $\mu^X$ be the equilibrium measure of the ensemble $X$, $\mu^Y$ the equilibrium measure of $Y$. Let $h \in [H]$ and set $\amsmathbb{A}_h^{Y} = \amsmathbb{A}^Y \cap [\hat{a}_h',\hat{b}_h']$. For any $\delta > 0$, there exists constants $C_1,C_2 > 0$ depending only on $\delta$ and the constants in the assumptions such that, for any $z \in \amsmathbb{C}$ at distance at least $\delta$ from $\amsmathbb{A}_h^Y$, we have
\[
