{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.330194+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d6813cac745447caab46edf0e0ebef5b254223fb29db26d2b9dae2542a1b44a2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:results:uniqueRegime of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] Suppose $(U, W)$ satisfy Assumption (as:results:fixedPoint of the paper) and Assumption (as:results:LSI of the paper). Then there exists a unique Cayley fixed point $\pi \in \tilde{\mathcal{M}}_{2, d}$ and we have $\mathbb H_2^* = \mathbb H_2(\pi)$. In other words, for $\mathcal{Z}^n$ as in (equation eq:results:gibbsPFN of the paper), we have
