{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:39:41.440090+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d6b3f1d375d802676d96b8cfffedbdd9f820796b0903876e780933c1d9cccdef","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 27 of arXiv:2604.07370, 'Probabilistic Weyl law for twisted Toeplitz matrices with rough symbols'] Let $\widetilde{m}$ be  an order function satisfying \eqref{Hypothèse fonction d'ordre Mildred} with $\alpha$ replaced by $t$. Let $\psi\in \mathscr{C}^\infty_c(\R)$ and consider $0<h^{1-2\eta}\ll\alpha\leq t\leq \beta$ with notations \eqref{Scaling en fonction de t}, \eqref{Scaling de q atchek en fonction de t}, \eqref{Scaling de q_0 atchek en fonction de t} and \eqref{Fonction d'ordre théorème central - version en t}. Then, under the assumptions of Theorem \ref{Théorème central}, for $a\in \{0,1\}$ the following decomposition holds:
        \begin{equation}
        \mathrm{tr}\pr{\frac{1}{t^a}\psi\pr{\frac{\atc{q}_{N,t_1,t_2}}{t}}}=N^d\Bigl(I^a_t+II^a_t+III^a_t+IV^a_t\Bigl)

    \end{equation}
    where for $k\geq 1$,
    \begin{equation}
        \begin{split}
            I^a_t &:=\frac{(h^\eta t)^d}{t^a}\int_{\mc{T}_{t_1,t_2}}\psi\pr{\frac{\atc{q}_0(\widetilde{\rho})}{t}}d\widetilde{\rho}\\
            II^a_t &:=\mc{O}_M(1)\frac{(h^\eta t)^d}{t^a}\Tilde{h}\int_{\mc{T}_{t_1,t_2}}\widetilde{\chi}\pr{\frac{\atc{q}_0(\widetilde{\rho})}{t}}d\widetilde{\rho}\\
            III^a_t &:= \mc{O}_M(1)\frac{(h^\eta t)^d}{t^a}\Tilde{h}^M\int_{\mc{T}_{t_1,t_2}}\widetilde{m}(\widetilde{\rho})d\widetilde{\rho}\\
            IV^a_t &:= \mc{O}_k(1)\frac{(h^\eta t)^d}{t^a}\pr{Nh^\eta t^{1/2}}^{-k}\int_{\mc{T}_{t_1,t_2}}\widetilde{m}(\widetilde{\rho})d\widetilde{\rho}.
        \end{split}

    \end{equation}
    and where $\widetilde{\chi}\in \mathscr{C}^{\infty}_c(\R;[0,1])$ is such that $\widetilde{\chi}\equiv 1$ on a neighborhood of $[0,\sup\mathrm{supp}(\psi)]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:23:05.283288+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d6b63ec2909ef55ed620c1110feab24e79557bf00b99558159ed253b72b3361a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 (Span theorem and sharp ambiguity) of arXiv:2608.21496, '2608.21496'] For $\cF=\{f\in L^\infty(\mu):0\le f\le1\}$ and validation operator $Kf=(\langle v_j,f\rangle)_{j=1}^p$:
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
\item $R_k(f)$ is identified by $Kf$ for every $f\in\cF$ if and only if $k\in S_V$.
\item The largest separation between two validation-equivalent worlds is
\begin{equation}
\sup_{\substack{f,g\in\cF\\Kf=Kg}}
|R_k(f)-R_k(g)|=b(k;V).

\end{equation}
\item If all kernels integrate to one, the evidence $Kf=(1/2,\ldots,1/2)$ has an exact identified interval of width $b(k;V)$, centered at $1/2$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:49:05.412011+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d6b74af2ef407688f46f5a3d26208b864f5bb21f626e43d0fbfaa13e2a296ddd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Uniform bounds on long edges of arXiv:2601.07808, 'Supercritical long-range percolation on graphs of polynomial growth: the truncated one-arm'] \label[lemma]{lem:unif_bounds_long_edges}
    Let $G$ be a transitive graph of polynomial growth with $d \geq 2$, and suppose that $J : V \times V \to \mathbf{R}_+$ is a transitive kernel with $J(x,y) = O(d_G(x,y)^{-d \alpha})$ with $\alpha > 1$.    

    For $r \in \mathbf{N}$, $b \geq 2$, and $\mathbf{m} \in \mathcal{M}(b)$, there exists $c = c(G,J) > 0$ such that for all $r$ sufficiently large,

    \begin{equation}
        \sum_{\mathbf{r} \in \mathcal{R}(b,\mathbf{m},r)}
        \prod_{i = 0}^{b-2}
        \expdegrad{o}{r_i}
        \leq 
        c
        r^{d(1-\alpha)}
        (b-2)^{d\alpha - d + 1}
        \mathbf{E}_{\beta}\left[\deg(o)\right]^{b-1}
        .
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:26:02.534352+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d6b86abe56d6307263aff23c756e51987a517e71352eda1bc5678ed8d44234af","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] $\mathcal{Z}_{\mathrm{fine}}(\Phi) \subseteq \mathscr{S}^n$ is the set of fine boundary multislopes achieved by $\Phi$-horizontal foliations. $\mathcal{Z}_{\aleph, \mathrm{fine}} \subseteq \mathscr{S}^n$ where the following wildcard substitutions are permitted to eliminate $\aleph$ components:
