{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.700007+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d6f6d448ec4785036853409b12fe72b06d22d4935dbbcdc112040577db907a14","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem l:4.10 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] If $\gamma$ is small enough, then, given any $0 < \eta' < \eta < \tfrac{1}{2}$ small enough (depending only on $\gamma$), for each $u \geq 0$, $\varepsilon \in (0,1)$ and $k \geq 1$ there exists a probability measure ${\rm O}^{k,\epsilon}_u$ on $\mathbb{R}^{{\rm Q}(k)}$  such that 
