{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.275493+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d75a02d426ae723ef8fca098b7d1e0d7dd3c89259f016d90197bf603dba56bc9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma3.7 of arXiv:2412.06246, 'The smallest singular value for rectangular random matrices with Lévy entries'] [[tikhomirov2015limit], Lemma 12] We can find a universal constant $C_{(equation lemma3.7 of the paper)}>0$ so the following holds. Given $n,m\in\mathbb{N},n\geq m$, $\epsilon\in(0,1]$, a subset $S\subset\mathbb{S}^{n-1}$, and let $T\subset\mathbb{B}_2^n$ (the unit ball in $\ell_2^n$) be a subset of $m$-sparse vectors that satisfy 
