{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:04:07.031582+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d75bcedcf100fadf276c68109aadfa93218f757370e3261682a06d1f64a0e14e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:cole-hopf-plateau of arXiv:2607.29330, 'Large deviations for the maximum of\\ the generalized TAP free energy'] Let $0\le s<t\le1$, assume $\zeta((s,t))=0$, and set $\alpha:=\zeta([0,s])$.  Then
		\[
		U(r,x):=\exp\{\alpha\Phi_\zeta(r,x)\}
		\]
		solves the backward heat equation on $[s,t]$,
		\[
		\partial_r U(r,x)+\frac12\xi''(r)\partial_{xx}U(r,x)=0 .
		\]
		Hence, with
		\[
		p^{\mathrm{BM}}_{s,t}(x,y)
		:=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi(\xi'(t)-\xi'(s))}}
		\exp\left\{-\frac{(y-x)^2}{2(\xi'(t)-\xi'(s))}\right\},
		\]
		we have
		\begin{equation}
			e^{\alpha\Phi_\zeta(s,x)}
			=\int_\mathbb{R} e^{\alpha\Phi_\zeta(t,y)}p^{\mathrm{BM}}_{s,t}(x,y)\,\mathrm{d} y .
		\end{equation}
		Equivalently, conditionally on $X_s=x$, the transition density of the Auffinger--Chen process on the plateau is
		\begin{equation}
			p_{s,t}(x,y)
			=\frac{e^{\alpha\Phi_\zeta(t,y)}}{e^{\alpha\Phi_\zeta(s,x)}}
			p^{\mathrm{BM}}_{s,t}(x,y).
		\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.142224+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d76129fa8633655ddac1f246958a502d696202e44d86afde8a63ec73d9b91edb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2608.27630, 'Oriented planar maps and \\ annular mating of trees'] Let $k\in\bN$ and let $\cG_k$ be the set of  maps in $\cG$ with $k$ edges on the outer boundary.  Then 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item For each $k\geq 1$, there exists a   bijection between $\mathcal G_k$ and $\mathcal H_k$ which sends an oriented annular map to the associated pair of height functions and preserves the weights~\eqref{eq: planar map weight} and~\eqref{eq: lattice path weight}.
    \item Fix $b>0$. Let $G$ be sampled from $\mathcal G_{\lfloor b\sqrt{N}\rfloor} $ according to the weights~\eqref{eq: planar map weight} with associated height function $(\sfZ_j)_{0\leq j\leq n}$. Then as $N\to \infty$, the law of $(\frac{1}{\sqrt N}\sfZ_{\lfloor Nt \rfloor })_{0\leq \lfloor Nt \rfloor\leq n}$ converges in distribution to $\int_0^\infty \d a B^{\gamma, \bH}_{0, -a+ib}$ with respect to the metric~\eqref{eq:curve-metric}. The   parameter $\gamma$ is given by
    \begin{equation}

        \cos \ab(\frac{\pi\gamma^2}{4}) = \frac{2b_e + 2\sum_{i,j \in \bZ_{\ge 0}} ijb_{i,j}}{2b_e + \sum_{i,j\in \bZ_{\ge 0}}(i^2+j^2) b_{i,j}}
    \end{equation}
    and by choosing  numbers $\{b_e,b_{i,j}:i,j\in\bZ_{\geq0}\}$ properly, $\gamma$ may take every value in $(0,\sqrt{2})$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:21:06.877221+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d764991e8b15e3575deba6bdb2578a218bf247cda82bc712d8332e8e22195bbb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2608.21255, 'Laws of the iterated logarithm for random Dirichlet series with general weights'] Fix any $\gamma>0$ and put $\ms_n:=\exp(-n^{1+\gamma})$ for integer $n\geq 2$. Let $N_1$ and $N_2$ be integer-valued, possibly dependent on $\gamma$, functions defined on some (not necessarily the same) right vicinities of $0$ and satisfying $\lim_{s\to 0+}(N_1(s))^s=1$ and $\lim_{s\to 0+}(N_2(s))^s=+\infty$. Then
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n\to\infty} g(\ms_n)\sum_{k=1}^{N_1(\ms_n)}\frac {a_k}{k^{1/2+\ms_n}} \tilde{\eta}_{k,1}(\ms_n)=0\quad\text{{\rm a.s.}}
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n\to\infty} g(\ms_n)\sum_{k>N_2(\ms_n)}\frac {a_k}{k^{1/2+\ms_n}} \tilde{\eta}_{k,1}(\ms_n)=0\quad\text{{\rm a.s.}}
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:25:49.869315+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d774d545272020ba0099d41ed7c65fabecd0ea042efe2a9947a0dffd5a22e5ad","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 3 ({\cite[Proposition 1) of arXiv:2609.02050, '2609.02050'] {Magyar-1998-2}}]

