{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:51:11.953054+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d79911ee4adbcff49784688022dca3c8242fc82f6512bda1e30735db1ac085e8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2608.07365, 'A pathwise Ito formula \\for weakly differentiable functions'] Let $(\Omega, B, \mathbb{P}_x)$ be the canonical Wiener space defined as in Section \ref{sec:Bessel}
  and $\pi=(\pi_n)_{n\geq1}$ be a sequence of partitions of $[0,T]$ satisfying Assumptions \eqref{ass:partitioncond}, \eqref{ass:partitioncond2}.  Let $(h_m)_{m\geq1}\subset L^1(\mathbb{R}^d)$ be a sequence of nonnegative finite-valued Borel functions  such that:
\begin{enumerate}
