{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.644648+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d7cd38af6762a15db3f7e2d64546482f8c435965481f5d7a34c9c68d418520c6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:disc_loc_times of arXiv:2512.17747, 'On exponentially height-penalized random trees'] For any path $(p(t);0\leq t\leq n)$ of length $n$, define the local time at a particular level and the maximum local time as follows. For an integer $k\in [-n,n]$,
