{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.726554+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d7ce7f4806348caa00263b030fad3daf4855b77cd09b17d6264b5b9fb8f15b3b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop thm:polynomial of arXiv:2606.08325, 'Digit Mixing under Polynomial Maps'] Let \(P\in\mathbb R[x]\) have degree \(d\ge2\).  Then there is a constant \(c_P>0\), depending only on \(P\), with the following property.  If
