{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:17:17.060604+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d7dcf96a96a15fe8508e9665f9e6a5167f4e6ab2f07d8691e96a9d42c6311c0c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2608.19744, 'Conditioned Brownian motion and local equivalence of path ensembles'] There exist $\varepsilon,\gamma,C>0$, an analytic eigenvalue
$u\mapsto\lambda_u =\lambda(\beta-iu)$, and analytic rank-one Riesz
projections $u\mapsto P_u$, defined on an open neighborhood of $|u|\le\varepsilon$, such that
\begin{equation}
 S_u(t)=e^{-t\lambda_u}P_u+R_u(t),
 \qquad
 \norm{R_u(t)}_{2\to2}
 \leq Ce^{-(\lambda (\beta)+\gamma)t}

\end{equation}
for $|u|\leq\varepsilon$ and $t\geq1$.  Moreover,
\begin{equation}
 \lambda(\beta-iu)
 =\lambda (\beta)-iu \lambda'(\beta)
  -\frac12 \lambda''(\beta) u^2+O(|u|^3).

\end{equation}
After decreasing $\varepsilon$ if necessary,
\begin{equation}
 \Re\bigl(\lambda(\beta-iu)-\lambda(\beta)+iu \lambda'(\beta)\bigr)
 \geq c_0u^2,
 \qquad |u|\leq\varepsilon,

\end{equation}
for some $c_0>0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.589534+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d7dd84a2f096d3de070cd61c0c84f09551f8a7164a5ad9437296a9e60efab9d2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Theorem 1 of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] Let $\mathsf{P}_i\in \mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$ with $\mathcal F^{elec}_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_i)<\infty$, $i=0,1$. Then there exists a coupling $ \mathsf{Q}\in  \mathsf{Cpl}_{s,m}(\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1)$ such that for $0\leq t\leq 1$ \begin{align}
        \mathcal F^{elec}_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_{t})&\leq  (1-t) \mathcal F^{elec}_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_{0})+t\mathcal F^{elec}_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_{1})\\
        &-\frac{(\mathbbm{1}_0(s)+s(s+1))(1-t)t\beta}{4}\int \sum_{(0,0)\neq (x,y)\in \bar\xi} (x-y)^2\inf_{z\in [x,y]}\left\lvertz\right\rvert^{-s-2} \mathsf{Q}^0(d\bar\xi),\nonumber
    \end{align}
    where  $\mathsf U:=\iota( \mathsf{Q})$ and  $\mathsf{P}_t:= \mathsf{gap}^{-1}\left((T_t)_{\#}\mathsf U\right)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:05:57.775262+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d7ed3fb8d09af9496c7e6cbb38007dd224585dc394b334ec178f23e1242401f8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 17 ({cf.\ \cite[Section~2.2) of arXiv:2608.30549, '\vspace{-1cm}Maximally Spread Out Measures and Implications\\{} for Phase Transitions in A'] {GrohsCartoonApproximation}
  and \cite[Definition~6.1]{VoigtlaenderPeinAnalysisVSSynthesisSparsityAlphaShearlets}}]

  Let $\nu \geq 1$ and fix ${0 < \varrho_0 \leq \frac{1}{4} < \frac{1}{2} \leq \varrho_1 < 1}$.
  Then the family of \emph{star-shaped subsets of $\R^2$ with $C^{2}$ smooth boundary}
  is defined as
  \[
    \mathrm{STAR}^{2} (\nu; \varrho_0, \varrho_1)
    := \biggl\{
         x_0 + S_{\varrho}
         \,\,:\,\,
         \begin{array}{l}
           x_0 \in \R^2 \text{ and } \varrho \in C^{2}_{2 \pi}(\R)
           \text{ with } \| \varrho'' \|_{L^\infty} \leq \nu , \\
           \varrho_0 \leq \varrho \leq \varrho_1 ,
           \text{ and } x_0 + S_{\varrho} \subset [0,1]^2
         \end{array}
       \biggr\}
    ,
  \]
  where $C_{2\pi}^{2}(\R)$ denotes the set of all $2 \pi$-periodic $C^2$ functions
  $\varrho : \R \to \R$, and where
  \begin{equation}
    S_{\varrho}
    := \biggl\{
         r \cdot \begin{pmatrix} \cos(\phi) \\ \sin(\phi) \end{pmatrix}
         \,\,:\,\,
         \phi \in [0,2\pi] \text{ and } 0 \leq r \leq \varrho(\phi)
       \biggr\}
    \subset \R^2
    .

  \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:09:59.191057+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d7ee2e4f0fa6557aeb2c273a4ba5600c54a4d64b44ef762c0964cb2fc9d137e5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn leftconv of arXiv:2608.06500, 'Free energy of Ising models under a spectral condition'] Let $G=(\text{\boldmath $A$},\text{\boldmath $h$}_1,\ldots,\text{\boldmath $h$}_k)$ be a weighted graph on vertex set
    $[N]$ and $X=(\text{\boldmath $W$},\text{\boldmath $d$}_1,\ldots,\text{\boldmath $d$}_k)$ be a test graph on vertex
    set $[n]$. We define the \emph{weighted homomorphism density}
    $t(X,G)$ as the quantity

    \begin{align}
    t(X,G):=\frac1{N^{c(X)}} \sum_{f:[n]\rightarrow[N]} \left(
    \prod_{i\in[n]} \prod_{\ell=1}^k h_{\ell,f(i)}^{d_{\ell,i}}
    \right) \left( \prod_{i\le j\in[n]} a_{f(i)f(j)}^{w_{ij}}
    \right)\, .
    \end{align}

    We say that a sequence $G_1,G_2,\ldots$ of weighted graphs is
    \emph{left-convergent} if for all test graphs $X$, the sequence
    $t(X,G_1),t(X,G_2),\ldots$ converges to a finite value.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:51:11.954628+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d7f33f30bc399f3ab16e08f5a94a1b5008b4d65fa99757d3952b1d4ed68f23be","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 21 (Spike-profile bounded analytic LSS input) of arXiv:2608.07820, 'Linear Spectral Statistics for Entrywise-Transformed Spiked Wigner Matrices under Shifted '] Assume W3--W5 and the spike assumption \eqref{eq:spike-package}.  Let
\(H_N=H_N^{(4)}\) be the centered atomic array
\eqref{eq:R3-centered-array}, put
\(S_{ij}:=\E H_N(i,j)^2\), and let \(S_N^0\) be
\eqref{eq:R3-flat-S}.  Then
\begin{align}
 |\sqrt N H_N(i,j)|&\le C,\\
 \max_{i\ne j}|NS_{ij}-1|&\to0,\\
 \max_i\left|\sum_jS_{ij}-1\right|&=o(N^{-1/2}),
 \\
 \max_i\sum_j|S_{ij}-S_{ij}^0|&\to0,\\
 \norm{S_N-S_N^0}_{\HS}&\to0.
\end{align}
Let \(m_{i,N}(z)\) be the vector Dyson-equation solution
\begin{equation}
 -\frac1{m_{i,N}(z)}
 =z+\sum_jS_{ij}m_{j,N}(z),
 \qquad
 \overline m_N(z):=\frac1N\sum_i m_{i,N}(z),
\end{equation}
and let \(\overline m_N^0\) denote the corresponding scalar solution for
\(S_N^0\).  Moreover,
\begin{equation}
 \max_{i<j}\left|
 \cum_4(\sqrt N H_N(i,j))-\kappa_4^{f,\nu}
 \right|\to0.
\end{equation}
For a function \(\varphi\) analytic near \(\Gamma\), define the
zero-diagonal Dyson-density correction
\begin{equation}
 d_{\varphi,\Gamma,N}^{0,\rm Dyson}
 :=-\frac{N}{2\pi\ii}\oint_\Gamma
 \varphi(z)\bigl(\overline m_N^0(z)-m(z)\bigr)\,\dd z.
\end{equation}
Then, for every finite family of such functions, there are deterministic
bounded-endpoint biases \(m_{\varphi,\Gamma,N}^{\rm fluc}\) such that
\begin{equation}
 \left(
 \Tr\varphi_\ell(H_N)
 +\frac{N}{2\pi\ii}\oint_\Gamma
       \varphi_\ell(z)\overline m_N(z)\,\dd z
 -m_{\varphi_\ell,\Gamma,N}^{\rm fluc}
 \right)_\ell
 \Longrightarrow (G_{\varphi_\ell})_\ell .
\end{equation}
The bias not contained in the exact Dyson density satisfies
\begin{equation}
 m_{\varphi,\Gamma,N}^{\rm fluc}
 +d_{\varphi,\Gamma,N}^{0,\rm Dyson}
 \longrightarrow m_{\varphi,\Gamma}^{\rm base}(\kappa_4^{f,\nu}),
\end{equation}
and the limiting covariance is
\(\mathcal V_{\kappa_4^{f,\nu}}^\Gamma\).  No convergence or homogeneity of
the edgewise third cumulants is assumed.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:52.662002+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d7fba3647dec14b31bdadb5ac9408d0abbbd863e68de1a344e8fa45ebcf5e685","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 14 (generalized moving-subspace bound) of arXiv:2609.03736, '2609.03736'] Let $(\rho,\Lambda)$ be a positive survival datum for
