{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:48:30.907103+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d7ff276f7e12869917ba71ec861279c645221e5230f2d5242ee1d5206020753b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2609.00936, 'Extended Abstract of Counting Divisorial Contractions with Centre a $cA_n$-Singularity'] Let $\varphi$ be a three-dimensional divisorial contraction which contracts a prime divisor to a point $P$ such that one of the following holds:
