{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.366281+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d817ef57d1839fec6f5c9bd598c0e993652c1d19ba241993a98b25429ace158d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem geo of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] Let $d=d^{{\mathrm {geo}}}$. For each $V\in\mathfrak{C}$, the metric $(\mathcal{X}\cap\overline{V},\mathfrak{d}_{V})$ is a geodesic metric space, i.e., for all $x,y\in\mathcal{X}\cap\overline{V}$,
