{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.632570+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d819a7218482796e23515dea1e5ed0a5d94917aa82288e4fc0969674e923d432","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:capacity-R3 of arXiv:2411.13505, 'Capacity of loop-erased random walk'] Let $A\subset\mathbb{R}^3$. Let $M$ be a standard Brownian motion and denote by $\mathbb{P}^M_y$ the law of $M$ with $M(0)=y$. The \emph{capacity} of $A$ is defined\footnote{As in the discrete case, there are several different equivalent definitions of capacity, but for our purposes we only need the one stated here. We refer to [morters2010brownian] for more background.} as
\begin{equation}
    \Ca_{\mathbb{R}^3}(A):=\lim_{\|y\|\rightarrow\infty}\frac{\mathbb{P}_y^M(M[0,\infty)\cap A\neq\varnothing)}{G_{\mathbb{R}^3}(0,y)},
\end{equation}
with $G_{\mathbb{R}^3}$ the Green's function of Brownian motion on $\mathbb{R}^3$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.774943+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d819fd0b52a90718fdbfe42de458d949ababdcb53fd2a68194ddacd59b9002a5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:recursion-fnk of arXiv:2411.03065, 'Growing conditioned BGW trees with\\ log-concave offspring distributions'] The array $(\PFforests{{\mathbf{w}}}{n,k})_{n,k\geq 1}$ satisfies the recursion
