{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.067167+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d81b55ed51743bebd193de0f44b2ade2210debaeae011cf132b77359b4d7a1f2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2606.00781, '2606.00781'] {(Stationary distribution of the beta-mutation model).} 
   Let $\Lambda=\beta(a,b)$ with $a,b>0$. Then the following two statements hold.
