{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.772494+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d827eeeaea88772b69d51e194cc19a0645c183723318c12508e1a99e976b2d87","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 56 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] Fix $q \in (0,1), c \in (1, q^{-1})$ and set $\hat{\kappa}_0 = \left( \frac{1-qc}{c-q} \right)^2 \in (0,1)$. For $\hat{\kappa} \in (\hat{\kappa}_0, 1]$ and $z \in \mathbb{C} \setminus \{0,q,q^{-1}\}$, we define
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
&\hat{S}_1(z; \hat{\kappa}) = \log(1 - q/z) - \hat{\kappa} \log (1 -q z) - \frac{q(q+ 2\hat{\kappa}^{1/2} + q \hat{\kappa})}{1 - q^2} \cdot \log(z), \\
&\hat{S}_2(z;\hat{\kappa}) = \log(1-q/z) - \hat{\kappa} \log(1-qz) - \frac{qc\hat{\kappa} (c-q) + q(1-qc)}{(1-qc)(c-q)} \cdot \log(z).
\end{split}
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:42:57.238382+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d82ef1caa713399c29a1d453f5bffcd7d85bb53e4dba2c6c64dfb0d12de0f663","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:bound_on_number_of_iterations of arXiv:2609.04140, 'The conformally invariant metric on $\CLE_4$ III:\\ uniqueness'] Suppose that we have the setup described above.  Then,  for all $\rho$ and $\zeta$ as above,  there exists $\varepsilon_0 \in (0,1)$ depending only on $a,\delta,N,\rho$,  and $\zeta$ such that the following holds for all $\varepsilon \in (0,\varepsilon_0)$.  Let $F_{\varepsilon}$ denote the event that for all $1\leq m \leq n_{\varepsilon}$
