no matter what $\{a(i,k)\}_{i,k\in[N]}$ is. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.469181+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d8597d56713995b98fa7880b4643c2fc91b681d0ea8bdc8acf11f22d589b711c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 74 (Decomposition of $\gfour$ and $\gfour^{-1}$) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] The spacetime metric $\gfour$ and the inverse spacetime metric $\gfour^{-1}$ can be expressed as follows relative to the vectorfields $\newL$ and $\newuL$ from \eqref{E:DOUBLENULLEIKONALFUNCTIONNORMALIZEDNULLVECTORFIELDS} and the first fundamental forms $\gnulltori$ and $\gnulltori^{-1}$ from Def.\,\ref{D:FIRSTFUNDAMENTALFORMSOFDOUBLENULLTORI}: 
