{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:57:20.583720+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d87117a7e6f88750f78af73dfbbfcc7ce7ad00c89673a1739abe37ca1caee9ed","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm1 of arXiv:2411.09716, 'Stable Tables'] The probability $f(n)$ that a given person is unmatched at a table with $n$ people is
