{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.775977+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d879c976fbae9187e492cc39afbe26abb1fdfa9460b4582c26959cc56ab6a172","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop admissibility-vs-shift of arXiv:2411.03065, 'Growing conditioned BGW trees with\\ log-concave offspring distributions'] Let $({\mathbf{a}},{\mathbf{b}})$ be a non-degenerate weight pair.
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item If ${\mathbf{a}}=(a_0,a_1,0,0\dots)$ with $a_0,a_1>0$ then $({\mathbf{a}},{\mathbf{b}})$ is admissible.
		\item If $({\mathbf{a}}^+,{\mathbf{b}})$ is admissible and if the inequalities
		\begin{align}
		\frac{\PFComp{{\mathbf{a}}^+,{\mathbf{b}}}{n+1-m}}{\PFComp{{\mathbf{a}}^+,{\mathbf{b}}}{n-m}}
