{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:10:43.951674+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d881a707c4c2b6ea4ea3911e6d2b10421e0ef4e633e7e76974aeebf3007eee5e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:2 of arXiv:2412.04539, 'Counting minimal cutsets and $p_c<1$'] Let $u\in V$, let $\Pi$ be a minimal cutset from $u$ to $\infty$. Let $A$ be the connected component of $u$  in $(V,E\setminus \Pi)$ and $B=\{e\cap A,\, e\in \Pi\}$  be the set of inner vertices of $\Pi$. For every set $S$ of vertices, we have
