{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.717705+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d8821a11e1ffa6ccbf266295a8c0a454ea8cf980a0044f4a1cae67a1f0ec87f7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm.IIC of arXiv:2411.19145, 'On the intersection of critical percolation clusters and other tree-like random graphs'] Let $\mathcal C_\infty$ be the IIC of Bernoulli percolation on $\mathbb Z^d$, either with $d>6$ and sufficiently spread-out lattice,  or $d>10$ in the nearest neighbor model. There exist positive constants $C$ and $\kappa$, such that for any $\varphi : \mathbb Z^d \to [0,\infty)$,  satisfying  $\|g_{d-4} * \varphi\|_\infty \le 1$,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb E\left[\exp\left(\kappa \cdot \sum_{x\in \mathcal C_\infty} \varphi(x)\right)\right] \le 1+C \, \|\varphi\|_1.
\end{equation}
Furthermore, if $d\ge 9$ and $\widetilde {\mathcal C}_\infty$ denotes an independent copy of $\mathcal C_\infty$, then
\begin{equation} 
\mathbb E\left[\exp\left(\kappa \cdot|\mathcal C_\infty \cap \widetilde {\mathcal C}_\infty|^{1-\frac 4d}\right)\right] <\infty.  
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:29:14.927320+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d885df4ec5cbced0935a53cd5b62f706d666204f5714a85873218032f9ac167c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm.main_next of arXiv:2606.13442, 'Scaling limit of additive functionals for reversible non-gradient exclusion process: criti'] Under Hypothesis~(hyp of the paper) and under the stationary measure $\mathbb{P}_{\rho}$, for every centered local function $f$, the additive functional has a scaling limit in $C(\mathbb{R}_+, \mathbb{R})$ for the following cases. 
		\begin{itemize}
			\item $d = 1$, $\deg(f) = 2$, then 
			\begin{align}
				\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{N \log N}} \int_0^{Nt} f(\eta_s) \, {\mathrm{d}} s\right)_{t \geqslant 0} \Longrightarrow (B_t)_{t \geqslant 0}, 
			\end{align}
			has the scaling limit as a Brownian motion of covariance
			\begin{align}
				\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}[B_t, B_s] = \frac{\chi(\rho)^2}{4\pi\mathbf{D}(\rho)}\vert \overline{f}''(\rho)  \vert^2 (t \wedge s).
			\end{align}
			\item If $d_{\operatorname{eff}}(f) > 2$, i.e. $\deg(f)  > 2/d$, then 
			\begin{align}
				\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}} \int_0^{Nt} f(\eta_s) \, {\mathrm{d}} s\right)_{t \geqslant 0} \Longrightarrow (B_t)_{t \geqslant 0}, 
			\end{align}
			has the scaling limit as a Brownian motion of covariance
			\begin{align}
				\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}[B_t, B_s] = 2 \left\Vert{f}\right\Vert^2_{-1} (t \wedge s).
			\end{align}
		\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.734602+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d887f2e774f7391e2002f25f89a4ba5f50abf2d60e298ec3fb0decaa17a04409","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2609.02755, 'The Sharp Rate of Probabilistically Strong Convergence to the KPZ Equation'] Let $\tau \in \{\<bs(2)0>, \<ps(2)0>\}$. Then for all $\kappa > 0$ and each compact set $\mfK$,
