{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:17:13.072472+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d88f24fb328613b903a23780f041e51679fd9d3809045059518c888c85c9457f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo thm:random-SLE of arXiv:2509.08928, 'The near critical random bond Ising model via embedding deformation'] Fix $\alpha>0$. In the previous setup, for $t^{(\alpha)}_n= n^{-(\alpha+\frac{1}{3})}$, one has $\mathbf{P}$-almost surely
