{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.429745+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d8a085cdca2092f34fb2aa2f75015b7ced99b1972648c820ca5f144bf82cbbdb","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 199 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] The master problem asks to find an $H$-tuple of functions $\boldsymbol{F}(z)=(F_h(z))_{h=1}^H$ with the following properties for any $h \in [H]$.
\begin{enumerate}
\item $F_h(z)$ is a holomorphic function of $z \in \amsmathbb C\setminus \amsmathbb{A}_h^{\mathfrak{m}}$.
\item There exists a holomorphic function $A_h(z)$ of $z \in \amsmathbb{M}_h$ such that
\begin{equation}

 A_h(z) = \sqrt{(z-\alpha_h) (z-\beta_h)} \,\big\langle \bth_h \cdot \boldsymbol{F}(z)\big\rangle + E_h(z).
 \end{equation}
 \item $F_h(z) = \frac{\kappa_h}{z}+O\big(\frac{1}{z^2}\big)$ as $z \rightarrow \infty$. This can be equivalently restated as
\[
F_h(z)\,\, \mathop{=}_{z \rightarrow \infty} \,\, O\bigg(\frac{1}{z}\bigg) \qquad \textnormal{and} \qquad \oint_{\gamma_h} \frac{\dd z}{2\ii\pi}\,F_h(z) = \kappa_h.
\]
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:28.995936+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d8aab7b116e90fc022a71731b42a611d69219f2e21422ac46860d2993859a222","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm P th gau of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] There exist a deterministic constant $c_1\in(0,\infty)$
