{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.821947+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d91d53cd737f3b8b699b6d55d6beb242eca1a8ddb161694be9e3b926765b7665","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary lower phase transition of arXiv:2411.09614, 'Moment estimates for the stochastic heat equation on Cartan-Hadamard manifolds'] Suppose $\alpha>\frac{n-2}{4}$, $x\in M$, $R>0$ and $u_0\in L^\infty(M)$  satisfies $u_0\geq \varepsilon>0$ in some $B(x,R)$. If $u(t,x)$ solves (equation eq:PAM-mild form of the paper) starting from $u_0$, then for any $p\geq 2$, there exists $\beta_c(p)>0$ depending on $K_2$ such that $\beta>\beta_c(p)$ implies \begin{equation}
    \lim_{t\to+\infty}\frac{\ln\mathbb{E}[\abs{u(t,x)}^p]}{t}>0.
    \end{equation}
    Similarly for any fixed $\beta>0$, $\exists p_c(\beta)>0$ depending on $K_2$ such that $p>p_c$ implies (equation positive lyap exp of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.588398+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d920bb14eb853a35a191743da594f4ce763da68635ec56be67fdd363038b02f6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2412.03366, 'Regularity of Weighted Tensorized Fractional Brownian Fields and associated function space'] For $1 \leq p, \, q \leq \infty$ and $s \in \mathbb{R}$, the  Besov space with dominating mixed smoothness is defined by
\begin{equation}
 S^{s}_{p,q}B(\mathbb{R}^2)  :  = \Big\{ f \in \mathcal{S}'(\mathbb{R}^2)~:~ \,   \sum_{\bar{j} \in \mathbb{N}^2 }  2^{(j_1+j_2)sq} \Vert \Delta_{\bar{j}} f \Vert_p^q < \infty \Big\}
\end{equation}
with the norm
$$
\Vert f \Vert_{S^{s}_{p,q}B(\mathbb{R}^2)} = \left( \sum_{\bar{j} \in \mathbb{N}^2 }  2^{(j_1+j_2)sq} \Vert \Delta_{\bar{j}} f \Vert_p^q \right)^{1/q},
$$
with the usual modification if $q= \infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.932511+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d92127e10cd05169fa26517e5f736fee164357f04c7899943a1f4fb2b9a850f0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:wasserstein_bound_from_global of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] {3Ddimers}}]
       Suppose that $B\subset R$ is a connected region with piecewise smooth boundary. If $\mu,\nu$ are component measures supported in $R$ and $\mathbb{W}_1^{1,1}(\mu,\nu)<\delta$, then there is a constant $C(B)$ such that 
       \begin{align}
           \mathbb{W}_1^{1,1}(\mu\mid_{B},\nu\mid_{B}) < \delta + (C(B)+1)\delta^{1/2}.
       \end{align}
       Further, the constant $C(B)$ is bounded by the relation that $C(B)\delta^{1/2}\leq 2 \text{Vol}(\partial B, \delta^{1/2})$, the volume of the width $\delta^{1/2}$ annulus with inner boundary $\partial B$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

