{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:30:14.221876+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d932ab3a23195fddfb278ed09b69506c169371c0811d6868b28cc4b8cd348a26","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-26apr2002 of arXiv:2608.20537, 'Persistent anisotropy in multi-dimensional\\ branching Brownian motion'] Suppose there exists $C>0$ so that 
