{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.597761+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d94cacbc3e4e940a5126ff6b993e8864712b6b12d440ddd54354daac47b92e65","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main_mmpp_cm of arXiv:2606.10257, 'Downward conditional monotonicity gives survival and extinction for contact processes in r'] Consider an MMPP with monotone, irreducible generator matrix $T$ and increasing vector of arrival rates $\alpha$. If $k\geq3$, then the model is DCM if and only if, for all triples $\ell<i<j$, 
