{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.829410+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d953dfca55359a89b4900a5dc7e3a9ba4de935fa2e3ccde9588e7e996847d892","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop R2 of arXiv:2606.24385, 'Gradient Mean-Field Dynamics with Measure-Valued States: Well-Posedness, Chaos, and Long-T'] Assume that (equation hyp1 of the paper) holds true. Then for each $\lambda\in {\mathscr{F}}(U)$ the stochastic integral $\int_{0}^{t}\Pi_{\lambda}{\rm d} W^{Q}(s)$ is well defined as an ${\mathscr{F}}(U)$--valued process, and
