{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:57:51.740850+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d95cd25cb4f0946226a60630d75ce24a19f97df1be6f03974cc151f6ddaeaecd","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 14 of arXiv:2608.30120, 'Graphs of operators as points in the Grassmann manifold'] Let $P$ be an orthogonal projection in $\j=\j_+\oplus\j_-$. Denote $P_+=P_{\j_+}$ and $P_-=P_{\j_-}$. Then $P$ belongs to the restricted Grassmannian $\p_{res}(\j_+)$  (induced by this decomposition) if and only if
