{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:30:14.228095+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d999d23df699c9e9c24f9cbaa189b5c94f9d8ff7d4096368214efd1e8d857380","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lemma upper and lower of u of arXiv:2608.23202, 'Locally finite Fixed points of Branching Brownian Motion'] There exists a constant $C_1>0$ such that for all $t$ large enough and  $z\geq -\frac{1}{2} \log t $, 
