{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:58:40.815995+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d9bf7a2650a1ccf0876af4a6f07081f995969f5627ad295ba9056d180fd16a18","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi sol1 of arXiv:2605.10309, 'Exponential Decay of $L^2$-Solutions to Stochastic Nonlinear Schr\"odinger Equations Drive'] Let $\alpha\in(1,1+\frac{4}{d})$ and $T>0$. 
A $L^2$-solution of (equation SNLS of the paper) is a pair $(X,\tau)$, where $\tau(\le T)$ is an $(\mathcal{F}_t)$-stopping time, and $X=(X(t))_{t\in[0,\tau]}$ is a $L^2(dt)\cap L^2(d\langle M\rangle(t))$-valued continuous $(\mathcal{F}_t)$-adapted process, such that $|X|^{\alpha}\in L^1([0,T],H^{-2}(\mathbb{R}^d)), {
