as equation in $H^{-2}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.834243+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d9c1cb85a8b8f09185277f7f9f6c5d8ed809a2141b3e0dcb5500d646b8fe265a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition proo-09 of arXiv:2606.25336, '\bfseries Invariant Measures of L\'evy-driven Stochastic Differential Equations'] Let $d=1$. Assume \textup{(A1)}--\textup{(A3)}.   
	Then the  inverse  Fourier transform of $\frac 1{2\pi} \widetilde{\psi}(\xi)|\xi|^{-2}$ is given by
