{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:51:12.728733+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d9e57795d21caa38d9d413ebe45cc6fa644dd3a4b18cbc146e20bdf9481a82e7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 24 of arXiv:2605.02002, 'Glauber dynamics for random field Ising models on bounded degree graphs and MLSI'] Let $(u,v)\in E$ be any edge of the graph $G=(V,E)$ of maximal degree $\Delta$. Assume that Assumption \ref{thiasssumptionnew} holds for the given $p_0\in(0,1)$, then we have, for any $m\geq 1$,
