{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.223961+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da3f7285a763920914dc2275100b57531f30e06c1cf6e6d933f04d56577e965f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Benamou Brenier for W-p of arXiv:2603.14163, '\LARGE \bf Tail Bounds for Queues with Abandonment: Constant, Moderate, Large Deviations, '] \textnormal{Benamou-Brenier for Wasserstein-$p$ distance [ambrosio2005gradient][ledoux2015stein]} 
    Suppose $X, Z$ are two random variables in $\mathbb{R}^d$ with probability measures $\mathcal{L}(X), \mathcal{L}(Z) \in \mathcal{P}_p(\mathbb{R}^d)$ respectively. 
    For a weakly continuous curve of probability measures $\mu_t : I \to \mathcal{P}_p(\mathbb{R}^d)$ with open interval $I \subset \mathbb{R}$. If it  satisfies the continuity equation for some Borel vector field $v_t$ with $\int_I \int_{\mathbb{R}^d} \|v_t(x)\|_2^p d\mu_t(x) dt < \infty$ and
        $\partial_t \mu_t + \text{div}(\mu_t v_t) = 0, \; \forall (x,t) \in \mathbb{R}^d\times I$. Then curve $\mu_t: I\to \mathcal{P}_p(\mathbb{R}^d)$ is absolutely continuous and for Lebesgue-almost everywhere $t \in I$, we have
        \begin{align*}
            \lim_{ s\to t} \frac{W_p(\mu_s, \mu_t)}{|s-t|} \leq \left\{\int_{\mathbb{R}^d} \|v_t(x)\|_2^p d\mu_t(x) \right\}^{1/p} 
        \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:19:42.577785+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da3fd7f6d38655ca80b7e77007b67206e2c18b5bfecae2b00113409f9ab8f076","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2609.03512, ''] Let $G$ be a connected graph with $g(G)\neq 3$, $\gamma(G)=2.$ 
