{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.286363+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da9e824d4a19e7e69c885cea755f9ed3e1c62a15bb0f2ca9f59840d29373b513","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma opt2prefix of arXiv:2604.20660, 'The Legendre structure of the TAP complexity\\ for the Ising spin glass'] Let $f\in \mathbb{R}$, $q\in (0,1)$ and $u\in (0,1)$. Let $\zeta\in \mathrm{Prefix}_2(u,q)$ satisfy the assumptions of Proposition (prop:annealed 0 of the paper). Let $(X_t)_{t\in [0,1]}$ be the Auffinger--Chen process
		\begin{equation*}
