{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:05:37.777722+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dad72bfba6bb742f34e7fda492d98195772859844fb05793de1a5c03cf5c35e1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 3.2 of arXiv:2608.00420, '{Weighted $L^p$ solutions of scalar BSDEs with general unbounded stochastic coefficients}\'] Let the generator $g$ satisfy assumption (A:H1 of the paper). Assume further that either $\mu_\cdot\in {\mathbb R}_+$ or (A:H1 of the paper)(iii) is replaced with the following stronger condition: $g$ has a general growth in $y$ and a stochastic linear growth in $z$, i.e., there exists a function $\phi_t(\omega,x)\in\mathbf{S}$ such that for each $(t,y,z)\in[0,\tau]\times{\mathbb R}\times{\mathbb R}^d$,
