{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.669253+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dae997f79937e73a8ef183122eeb8d0cce547406ec78fd90536dfe5adc2d6aec","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem finite-n-characteristic-moments of arXiv:2609.00110, 'Phase Transition and Fluctuation Results for First-Passage Percolation on Spread-Out Cycle'] Let $\phi:[0,\infty)\to\mathds{R}$ satisfy $|\phi(a)|\leqslant Ce^{\eta a}$ for some $\eta<1$. Define $h_{n,\phi}(t) := e^{-\alpha_nt}\E Z_n^\phi(t)$ and $\mathcal{Z}_{n,\phi}(t) := e^{-\alpha_nt}\bigl(Z_n^\phi(t)-\E Z_n^\phi(t)\bigr)$ for $t\geqslant0$ (and zero otherwise). Then
\begin{align}
 \sup_{n\geqslant n_0}\sup_{t\geqslant0} \left( \abs{h_{n,\phi}(t)} + \E\abs{\mathcal{Z}_{n,\phi}(t)}^2 \right) <\infty.
\end{align}
If, moreover, $\sup_{n\geqslant n_0} \bigl( \sup_{a\geqslant0}e^{-\alpha_na}\left\vert\phi(a)\right\vert + \operatorname{TV}_{[0,\infty)} \bigl(e^{-\alpha_n\cdot}\phi\bigr) \bigr) <\infty$, there exists $C_\phi<\infty$ such that, for any interval $I$ of length at most one,
\begin{align}
 \E\sup_{t\in I} \abs{ \sum_{j=1}^m a_j\mathcal{Z}_{n,\phi}^{(j)}(t-b_j) }^2 \leqslant C_\phi\sum_{j=1}^m a_j^2
\end{align}
for all $a_j\in\mathds{R}$, $b_j\geqslant0$, and independent copies $\mathcal{Z}_{n,\phi}^{(j)}$, uniformly in $n\geqslant n_0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:08.852713+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_daec8f54cbf0c7710dc64bbd37f217b292265c3c3b4a5349a5b17c0bf0cae5a2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 16 (Eigenvalue master equation — Wishart case) of arXiv:2511.12623, 'The eigenvector bead process'] Fix integers $N, T \ge 1$, and let $\{\lambda_i\}_{i=1}^{N}$ denote the (positive) eigenvalues of $X_{N}^{\!\top} X_{N}$.
Consider the rank-one extension
\[
X_{N+1} \;=\; \big( X_N \;\; g \big),
\qquad g \in \mathbb{R}^{T},
\]
that is, $X_{N+1}$ is obtained by appending the column vector $g$ to $X_N$.
Then the eigenvalues $z$ of $X_{N+1}^{\!\top} X_{N+1}$ are the zeros of the \emph{secular equation}
\begin{equation}
F_N(z)
\;=\;
1
+ \sum_{i=1}^{N}
\frac{|\langle v_i, g \rangle|^2}{\lambda_i - z}
- \frac{\Gamma}{z}
\;=\;0,
\end{equation}
where ${v_i}$ are the eigenvectors associated with the nonzero eigenvalues of $X_N X_N^{\top}$, and
\(
\Gamma
:= \sum_{j=1}^{T-N} |\langle w_j, g \rangle|^2,
\)
with $\{w_j\}$ forming an orthonormal basis of the null space of $X_{N} X_{N}^{\!\top}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.290981+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dafba4e2d03a022eb24ea31ced5c3d5ef20f3e17bb9ecebd0c6efc3e1dcd581c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 30 of arXiv:2606.23099, 'Path-dependent Affine Processes'] Let $T \in \R_{\geq 0}$.
    Assume that $\mu \in \ccM([0,T], \C^d)$, and
    $P_T \in L^1([0,T],\R_{\geq 0})$ such that
    \begin{equation}
