{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:49:05.413817+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_db53db4422dce3d77ac73648ea8cb79ae8c015c23bc9515f02d669cd7c9ca996","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:one_arm_isolation of arXiv:2601.07808, 'Supercritical long-range percolation on graphs of polynomial growth: the truncated one-arm'] \label[lemma]{lem:one_arm_isolation}
    Let $G$ be a transitive graph of polynomial growth with $d \geq 2$, and suppose that $J : V \times V \to \mathbf{R}_+$ is a transitive kernel with $J(x,y) = \Omega(d_G(x,y)^{-d \alpha})$ with $\alpha > 1$.

