{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:17:13.075265+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_db6c399f67033815a334e9bdad56c7f724ee96edf885e7d67f428986fe1a4d5e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:SDE-embedding of arXiv:2509.08928, 'The near critical random bond Ising model via embedding deformation'] Assume that the collection of variances $(\sigma_e^2)_{e\in E(\mathbb{Z}^2)}$ vanishes outside of some finite box $\Lambda$. Consider the stochastic differential system defined on corners of $ \Upsilon^{\times} \cap  \Lambda  $, whose initial condition is given by $\mathcal{Y}^{(0)}$ and whose dynamic is given for any $\frak{p} \in \Lambda $ by $ \mathcal{Y}^{(s)}_{\omega}(\frak{p}):=\mathcal{Y}(\frak{p},\omega,s)$
\begin{align}
		d \mathcal{Y}^{(s)}_{\omega} (\frak{p})=& \frac{1}{2} \sum\limits_{z_k \in \Lambda} \sigma_k\Bigg[ \mathcal{Y}^{(s)}_{\omega}(c^+_k) \langle \chi_{\frak{p}}\chi_{a^+_k} \rangle_{S_{\omega}(s)} -  \mathcal{Y}^{(s)}_{\omega}(a^+_k) \langle \chi_{\frak{p}}\chi_{c^+_k} \rangle_{S_{\omega}(s)} \Bigg] dB^{(e_k)}_s \nonumber \\
