{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.775605+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dbb892c63d1716d37df3ca32bad4e7bdd79efdfe1a2383f8fc4e744f62335b65","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:delta of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] Under any coupling between $\mathbf{X}$ and $\mathbf{Y}$, we have
\begin{align}
    \mleft|
        \operatorname{Cov}[X^i(0), X^j(t)]
    \mright|
    &\leqslant
    2 \sqrt{
        \mathbb{E} \mleft[ X^i(0) (X^i(0) - Y^i(0)) \mright] \cdot
        \mathbb{E} \mleft[ X^j(t) (X^j(t) - Y^j(t)) \mright]
    } \\

    &\qquad + \mathbb{E} \mleft[ Y^i(0) (X^j(t) - Y^j(t)) \mright]
