Moreover, both factors appearing under the square root in (equation decom4631 of the paper) are nonnegative.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:04:59.427389+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dbbafe4c184a48dd9963dba60defade867be3bc1b7c8b013fb40f24d2a321583","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:two-point-decompose of arXiv:2605.19419, 'Tail exponents of the three-dimensional uniform spanning tree and Abelian sandpile'] Suppose $4r<R$ and $x\in\partial B_R$, $y\in\partial B_r$. Suppose that $\gamma$ is an ILERW started from $0$. $S_{1}$ and $S_{2}$ are two independent SRWs started from $x$ and $y$. Write $P_{x,y}$ for their joint law. Let $E$ denote the intersection of the following events:
\begin{itemize}
\item[1.]\ $S_{1}$ hits $0$ and, writing $\tau_{1}$ for the first hitting time of $0$, $S_{1}[0,\tau_{1}]\cap\gamma=\{0\}$.
