where $\binom{k}{d}=0,$ if $k<d$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:14:37.646785+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dbcbbbca9dc4dd629c49bfb63cd52bd97a82c901ed4253834be648295ea7a3b8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2608.19560, '\textbf{Computing transient probabilities in Markovian queues with balking conditional on '] The PGF $\pi_{k,\ell,s}^*(z,t \mid K)$ conditional on exactly $K$ customers
