{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.562580+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dbd0a335f497bfe1f08ef21b67c8e1bbc5b0d3bd98fbbccec3ede27dacc1f9ea","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Generic Morse property of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[lemma]{lem:Morse}
For fixed \(N,p\), the set of coefficient tensors for which the restriction of \(H_N\) to \(\mathbb S_N\) is not Morse is contained in a proper real algebraic subset of \(\mathbb R^{N^p}\).  Consequently, if the joint coefficient law is absolutely continuous, the field is almost surely Morse.
