where $\Theta^I$ is defined in \eqref{eq:theta_I_def}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:07:35.029105+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc1f9f40fc81090618d8c36dc9f4dacd49bb7c8985b03cc14600ff2a56b9237f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 14 of arXiv:2609.02879, 'On the cut locus of Hamilton--Jacobi equations I: structure and propagation via the touchi'] Let $x\in\R^n$, $r>0$ and $\phi\in\text{\rm SCL}\,(B(x,r))$ with linear modulus $C_1>0$, and let $\psi:B(x,r)\to\R$ be a semiconvex function with linear modulus $C_2>0$. If $\psi$ touches $\phi$ from below at $x$ in $B(x,r)$, then we have the following properties:
	\begin{enumerate}[\rm (1)]
		\item both $\phi$ and $\psi$ are differentiable at $x$ and $D\psi(x)=D\phi(x)$.
		\item for $C=\max\{C_1,C_2\}$ we have that
		\begin{align*}
			|p-D\phi(x)|\leqslant 3C|y-x|,\qquad \forall y\in B(x,\frac r2), p\in D^+\phi(y);\\
			|p-D\psi(x)|\leqslant 3C|y-x|,\qquad \forall y\in B(x,\frac r2), p\in D^-\psi(y).
		\end{align*}
	\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

