{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:42:16.246760+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc3b5b41bae3238705b06fbbd09991b598c2d6f2783cf19aad8a255f07dc3035","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:j fixed of arXiv:2607.01946, 'Second-order fluctuations for a phase transition in random partitions'] Under the notations above,
\begin{multline}
\pp{\frac{C_{j}(\floor{nt})-{\mathbb E}\pp{C_j(\floor{nt})\;\middle\vert\;{\mathcal P}}}{n^{\alpha/2}}, \frac{{\mathbb E}\pp{C_j(\floor{nt})\;\middle\vert\;{\mathcal P}} - \floor{nt}^\alpha p_j\topp\alpha S_\alpha}{n^{\alpha/2}}}_{t\in[0,1],j\in{\mathbb N}}\\
\Rightarrow\pp{\pp{\frac {S_\alpha}{\Gamma(1-\alpha)}}^{1/2}\zeta_{\alpha,j}\topp1(t),
\pp{\frac {S_\alpha}{\Gamma(1-\alpha)}}^{1/2}\zeta_{\alpha,j}\topp2(t)}_{t\in[0,1],j\in{\mathbb N}},
