where $M_\alpha$ is a Gaussian random measure on $(0,\infty)\times\Omega'$ with control measure $\alpha r^{-\alpha-1}{\rm d} r{\rm d}\mathbb P'$ and $N'$ on $(\Omega',\mathbb P')$ is a standard Poisson process, and $M_\alpha$ is independent of $S_\alpha$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.591918+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc45e50d9deb88ddc2fba582be4e90e76d2f902640f451c6d0f0cbc3fbd5991d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma TSP-E-L-A-1 of arXiv:2608.30582, 'The flexible part of intermittent Onsager theorem for the two-dimensional stochastic incom'] Suppose $\left| {t - {t_0}} \right|{\left\| u \right\|_1} \lesssim 1$. Let $w{\left( t ,x \right)}$ be the solution of the transport equation
