{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:33:01.741120+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc60cbe82590b45fa9314d31102779adb332fd5c392e874eeccb36097564f0d2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 3 of arXiv:2605.14206, 'The clumsy coupon collector's problem'] Suppose words in $L_1.L_2$ have a \emph{unique factorisation}
