for all $N\ge 1$, $x \in {\mathbb{T}}_N^d$, and smooth
$G\colon \sqrt{K} {\mathbb T} \times {\mathbb T}^{d-1}\to {\mathbb{R}}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.284224+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc8a296331be3a53b19c6c04ef3a25bf7cb770d6c39f10abb2d1674c60c94202","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma nonexplosition of arXiv:2411.01731, '$L^2$-Wasserstein contraction of modified Euler schemes for SDEs with high diffusivity and'] Under $({\bf H}_0)$  and $({\bf A}_1)$, it holds that for any $\delta\in(0,1]$, $x\in\mathds R^d,$ and $n\ge0,$
