{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.120205+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dd0978da371b31b3e2bfa967dc83e1eb47b4d3113d9e19b70d6edf17ad83baed","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop ilocal of arXiv:2601.20502, 'Optimal matching under size priority'] Under condition~(eq:uniquefixedpoint of the paper), for any edge weight distribution, the macroscopic marginal $i$ in $\left(\mathbb{T},o,w,(i,Z)(u,v)_{(u,v)\in \overset{\rightarrow}{\mathbb{T}}}\right)$ from Proposition~(prop:Zconstruction of the paper) is measurable in the weightless tree $(\mathbb{T},o)$.  In addition, $(\mathbb{T},o)$-\emph{a.e.}, there exists a unique family $(i(u,v))_{(u,v)\in\overset{\rightarrow}{E}(\mathbb{T})}$ verifying
