{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:59:45.564653+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dd22138f3b058702f2ab7ebfc90c54cc3307ec47309e13f3044ff5ad3320fb6d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition of arXiv:2411.17109, 'On the maximal correlation of some stochastic processes'] Let $X$ and $Z$ be independent copies of $\alpha$-stable random variables with $0<\alpha<2$. Then the L\'{e}vy measure $\nu_{X}(x)\mathrm{d}x$ of $X$ has the following form:
