\end{equation*}
and set $e_k=x_k-p_k$. Suppose that $x_k$ and $p_k$ lie in the same
interval of (equation eq:Upieces of the paper) for every $0\le k\le n-1$. Then, for
$0\le k\le n-1$,
\begin{equation}
 e_{k+1}=-\frac43e_k-\frac49e_{k-1}+\varepsilon_{k+1},
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
 \max_{0\le k\le n}\lvert e_k\rvert
 \le9\max_{1\le j\le n}\lvert \varepsilon_j\rvert.
\end{equation}
In particular, if
$\max_{1\le j\le n}\lvert \varepsilon_j\rvert\le1/180$, then
$\lvert e_k\rvert\le1/20$ for every $0\le k\le n$, and $x_k$ and $p_k$
lie in the same interval of (equation eq:Upieces of the paper) at every such step.","status":"unverified"}

