{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:48:27.282565+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de1e1a78f1d06dcd0d86776781b7fdd0536548ea6f1059f2384b8cdca6efbb7f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2604.25336, 'Central limit theorem for slow-fast system under mixed fractional Brownian motion'] Let \((\mathcal{V}, \mathcal{W})\) be Banach spaces and suppose \(K \in L_p(C^\alpha([0, T], \mathcal{V}))\), \(B \in C^\beta([0, T], U)\) for some 
\((\beta \in (\frac{1}{2}, 1])\), \((0 < \alpha \le \gamma < 1)\) and \((\alpha + \beta > 1)\). Also suppose that $f$ is of $BC^2$ and $G$ are Lipschitz continuous with respect to \(x\) and globally bounded over \(r\in[0,t]\).
Then, if \(X : [0, T] \to \mathcal{V}\)
satisfies the controlled Young differential equation
\begin{equation}
X_t = X_0 + \int_0^t f(s,X_s) \dd B_s + \int_0^t G(s) X_s\dd s + K_t.
\end{equation}
Then, 
\begin{equation}
\|X\|_{\infty,p,[0,T]} \le C_2 e^{(2|f|^{p}_{-\kappa,p})^{\frac{1}{(\bar \eta-\alpha)p }}}(\|X_0\|^p+\mathbb{E}[\|K\|_\alpha^p]+\|f\|_{\infty}+1)
\end{equation}
and 
\begin{equation}
\|X\|_{\alpha,p} \le C_1(\mathbb{E}[\|K\|_\alpha^p]+\mathbb{E}[\|X\|^p_{\infty}]+1).
\end{equation}
for some constants \(C_1, C_2 > 0\) depending on \(\alpha, \beta, H, T\) and \(\|f\|_{BC^2}, \|G\|_{Lip}\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

