{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.473220+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de41c01806f593df2211a9fff37b1bc1932fa27018ee8a9ced7f6901d840714c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:liftdiffusion of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] Let $P_t = \exp(tL)$ and $\hat{P}_t = \exp(t \hat{L})$ be the Markov diffusion processes defined as above. We say that $\hat{P}_t$ is a lift of $P_t$ if
    it holds that $\dom(L) \subset \dom(\hat{L})$, and 
        \begin{align} 
            \langle f \circ \pi, \hat{L} (g \circ \pi)  \rangle_{L^2(\hat{\mu})} = 0\,,\quad \forall f \in L^2(\mathcal{S},\mu)\,,\ g \circ \pi \in \dom(\hat{L})\,,
        \end{align}
    and for a positive bounded operator $\mathsf{S}: L^2(\mathcal{S}, \mu)^\perp \to L^2(\mathcal{S}, \mu)^\perp$, 
    \begin{align} 
        \langle \hat{L}(f \circ \pi), \mathsf{S}\, \hat{L} (g \circ \pi)  \rangle_{L^2(\hat{\mu})} = - \langle f, L g  \rangle_{L^2(\mu)}\,, \quad \forall f \circ \pi \in \dom(\hat{L})\,,\ g \in \dom (L)\,.
    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

