{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:30:14.221712+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de61b3aa28d5b287b679eeec002cc8f3a6a95ba1f3606a4b856a12d714871162","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:exp-lower of arXiv:2608.20537, 'Persistent anisotropy in multi-dimensional\\ branching Brownian motion'] There exists a constant $\mathring{c} \in (0, 1]$ such that for each $\mathfrak{t} \leq -1$, there exists a function $\mathring{u}(t,x; \mathfrak{t}) \geq 0$ satisfying the following properties:
