{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:38.633376+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de68ebc324cc9124da9e5a1ff1f6667fee5c17897a180f319e9c76aa0f2464f0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2506.17061, 'Non-uniform bounds for non-normal approximation via Stein's method with applications to th'] Let $p\ge 3$. Consider the critical Curie--Weiss model and let $W:=W_n=S_n/n^{3/4}$, where
