{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.329947+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de6ec7325cdc9be15196f2312207668ef1db250cf79c49ea1dcfe5a60ca341c8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition qshprod of arXiv:2411.06827, 'The Exponential Lie Series and a Chen--Strichartz Formula for L{\'e}vy Processes'] The commutative quasi-shuffle product $\star$ on ${\mathbb R}{\langle}{\mathbb A}{\rangle}$  is  inductively defined by
