and the infimum for the problem $MBB(\mu_0,\mu_1)$ of~\eqref{MBB} is achieved whenever it is finite. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:39:41.405785+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de82231fe69e3b4d553f65efe9859ceb2ce5bf890051b7593d83f8ab4c71d9ad","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2604.06516, 'From stochastic individual-based models to free-boundary Hamilton-Jacobi equations'] For all $t>0$ and $x\in \R$, the family of laws $(\mu^K_{x,t})_{K\geq 1}$ satisfies a large deviation principle on $\mathbb{D}[0,t]$ with rate $1/\log K$ and good rate function $I_{t,x}$: for any subset $A\subset \mathbb{D}[0,t]$,
\begin{multline}
    -\inf_{f\in \mathrm{int}(A)} I_{t,x}(f)\leq \liminf_{K\rightarrow +\infty} \frac{1}{\log K} \mathbb{P}_x\big((X^K_{s\log K})_{s\leq t} \in A\big)\\
    \leq \limsup_{K\rightarrow +\infty} \frac{1}{\log K} \mathbb{P}_x\big((X^K_{s\log K})_{s\leq t} \in A\big) \leq -\inf_{f\in \mathrm{cl}(A)} I_{t,x}(f),
\end{multline}where $\mathrm{int}(A)$ and $\mathrm{cl}(A)$ are the interior and closure of $A$ for the Skorohod topology. \\
    In addition, the family of measures $(\mu^K_{x,t})_{K\geq 1}$ satisfies the Laplace principle with rate $1/\log K$ and rate function $I_{t,x}$ uniformly on compact sets with respect to $x\in\R$, as recalled below. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

