{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:10.196943+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de8aacef1b64eeca6cdeb4f8c38a06b9115a4bf30cd75e84e79813b22655efab","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 29 of arXiv:2605.03851, 'The Relay Random Tree:\\A stochastic geometry approach of multihop relay in an urban visib'] \textbf{Stoppage Point.}

Let $\landsc$ be a given landscape.
Let $(x, y)\in\Half$ be a point. We define its stoppage point as the $x-coordinate$ starting from which line of sight from $(x, y)$ is cut off for all altitudes.
\[X_{stop}(x, y) := (\min\{a\in [x, +\infty[: \exists (a, b)\in \landsc, \forall (a, c)\in \mathrm{R}+(x, y), c<b\})\wedge (\max\{a : \exists (a, b)\in \mathrm{R}+(x, y)\}).\]
We can also consider the stoppage \textit{height} $X_{stop}(x, y)$ defined as either the height of the building inducing stoppage when it exists or $-\infty$ when it does not.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.188633+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de9226b4a6ed11ba992d176b9edb92865d5bb0c11159ad9b8135f2b4b170cde0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 22 of arXiv:2604.18871, 'Quantitative approximation of the Vlasov(--Fokker--Planck)--Navier--Stokes system by stoch'] Let Assumptions~\ref{assump-PDE} and \ref{assump-particles} hold, with $\sigma > 0$.
