{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.351294+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dedc697f6ff53f0f59b1269f02fe8c3adf1d0d0cd7c1ed4f8796ac67d3a990bb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 1 of arXiv:2606.17472, '2606.17472'] Assume that $X$ is recurrent and (\ref{ConditionA}) holds. We have that there is a unique probability measure $\mu_B$ with support in $B$ that arises as the weak limit
  \begin{align*}
