{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.537592+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df100e587754f62edbe4af1d740d3e403c4164a5cf9a500212b11640901d3062","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem dif:scm of arXiv:2411.11759, 'Milstein-type schemes for McKean--Vlasov SDEs driven by Brownian motion and Poisson random'] If Assumptions     \mbox{\normalfont  (asump:tame of the paper)} to \mbox{\normalfont  (asump:sig:gam:tame of the paper)}   are satisfied, then for any $p_0\geq 2$, $t\in[0,T]$ and $i\in\{1,\ldots,N\}$
