{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.252446+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df15c44bc8d589a21e25e571ead304cf7b713e566467ceedd317ffea185e5c38","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 75 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] Setting $\mathsf{t}' = \mathsf{t}/2$, we have w.o.p. that, for any $z \in \mathfrak{X}$ and $t \in [\mathsf{t}', N^5]$,
