{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:05:37.777869+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df2d3447e6f076d64e5ee9ca5ddb9de462ffeee324358f20f95dfd32fd086771","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 3.1 of arXiv:2608.00420, '{Weighted $L^p$ solutions of scalar BSDEs with general unbounded stochastic coefficients}\'] Let the generator $g$ satisfy assumption (A:H1 of the paper) plus $\mu_\cdot\in {\mathbb R}_+$ (or assumption (A:H1 of the paper)(i)-(ii) plus (equation eq:2.3* of the paper) or assumption (A:H1' of the paper)) with the nonnegative process $f_\cdot$ satisfying $\mathbb{E}\left[(\int_0^\tau f_t{\rm d}t)^{p}\right]<+\infty$ instead of (equation eq:2.2 of the paper). Assume further that for some constant $M>0$,
