{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.122679+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df33388b51db93395362b4652b66a32c41abe1886666b5421c5fc4b92f2dfe68","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:mainSPECTRUMgraph of arXiv:2510.00748, '\bf On irreducible central limit theorems'] Let $Z_n$ be as in (equation eq:bilformsubsec of the paper), and let $G_n=(V_n,\mathcal{E}_n)$ be its associated graph. Suppose that there exists $k\ge 2$ such that, as $n\to \infty$,
