{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.328758+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dfc98cf5a803ffa1ca89d2c565ad330dd892d20900823428720bfefbe2372c7a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:boundedness_p_extrapolated_spaces of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Let $B$ be a ball in ${\mathbb R}^d$. The Helmholtz projection $\mathbb{P}_{B}$ can be uniquely extended as a bounded linear operator $\mathbb{P}_{-1,B}$ from $\mathscr{X}_{-1}^{\mathrm{Dir}}(B;{\mathbb R}^d)$ into $\mathscr{X}^{\mathrm{Sto}}_{-1}(B)$. In particular,
