{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:53:10.161359+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e021c680fbc1f111b2a1fc11862fc1ef0372b2d381cf79f32a80f802e380abd4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition PropBivIntegral of arXiv:2608.28949, 'The information geometry of product-reference discrete diffusion: Interaction growth compl'] For any pair $0 < a < b < 1$, we can write the KL product-reference
error over the interval $[a,b]$ as
