{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:37:51.460594+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e030ce7a664b31b99dc4177f0b71e9e4201ceb6095b2a615792930b0fc8db485","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 52 of arXiv:2604.03777, 'Equilibrium fluctuations for a multi-species particle system with long jumps'] For any $\alpha \in \{ - 1, 0, 1 \}$, there exists a constant $C>0$ independent of $\varepsilon$ such that for all $F\in\mathcal{C}$, we have 
