{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.292564+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0a86e88caa079e8d8dc9cc48c21031b1fb599fa888bc627f88979ad2b4deac1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:Wick of arXiv:2605.21265, 'The non-Hermitian minor process'] Assume the set-up and conditions of Proposition~(prop:underline_comp of the paper) with the only differences that we additionally fix $n\in\mathbf{N}$, consider $j\in[n]$ instead of $j\in[2]$ and do not assume that $x_1\le x_2$. It holds that
\begin{equation}

\mathbf{E}\prod_{i=1}^n\langle G_i-\mathbf{E} G_i\rangle=\sum_{P\in \Pi_n}\prod_{\{i,j\}\in P}\!\!\mathcal{M}_{ij}+\mathcal{O}_\theta\left(\frac{N^{\xi}}{\sqrt{N\eta_*}}\prod_{i=1}^n \frac{1}{N\eta_i} \right),\quad\mathcal{M}_{ij}:=\mathcal{M}\big((x_i,\eta_i,z_i),(x_j,\eta_j,z_j)\big),
\end{equation}
uniformly in the same sense as explained below (equation eq:Cov_UV of the paper). Here $\Pi_n$ denotes the set of all pairings of $[n]$. We use the convention that $\Pi_n=\emptyset$ if $n$ is odd. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:48:49.896188+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0ac1c6b7d03b822f78307afc08559f8ae765747254cc1a109d37df56beb0de5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem Taylor2 of arXiv:2510.23430, 'On the Martin boundary for discrete TASEP'] (1) Assume that $\beta\in (0,1)$. We have $h'_\beta(u^{crt})=0$ where $u^{crt}=\frac{p-\beta}{1-\beta}=p-\frac{(1-p)\beta}{1-\beta}$.

(2)  Assume that $\beta\in (0,1)$. Then $h_\beta(\frac{p-\beta}{1-\beta})$ is the unique minimum of $h_\beta(x)$ on $(-\infty,p)$.

(3) Let $D$ be a convex compact set avoiding $p,1$. Then there exists a constant $K>0$ such that for any $z\in D$ and $\beta\in (0,1)$ satisfying $u^{crt}=\frac{p-\beta}{1-\beta}\in D$ we have
\begin{equation}

\left|h_\beta(u)-h_\beta(u^{crt})-\frac{(1-\beta)^3}{2\beta(1-p)^2}(u-u^{crt})^2\right|<K(u-u^{crt})^3.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

