{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:36:31.222763+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0ade8129b5b8f3a4395dd48ad1dc9c17872f0bb5956bcf39a6ed319997c897b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 (Umbilic event versus uniform nonumbilicity) of arXiv:2609.00501, 'Uniqueness of Finite-Time Varifold Limits for the M\"obius-Invariant Willmore Flow'] Let $F\colon[0,T)\times\Sigma\to\Sph^3$ be a smooth MIWF with
$T<\infty$.  Then exactly one of the following alternatives holds:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\roman*)}]
 \item there are $t_j\nearrow T$ and $x_j\in\Sigma$ such that
 \begin{equation}

  |A^0_{F_{t_j}}(x_j)|^2\longrightarrow0;
 \end{equation}
