{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:16:46.131351+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0b2a3457948080452fc7e5007798a8d9bd23e747ff4803ad07d32148c49e623","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:Laplacian of arXiv:2605.01444, 'From second moments to pairwise negative correlation: \\applications to minimal and unifor'] Let $G=(V,E)$ be a finite graph with $|V|=n$.
	The adjacency matrix $A_G$, degree matrix $D_G$ and Laplacian matrix $L_G$ are $n\times n$ matrices indexed by $V$ defined as follows:
	\begin{itemize}
		\item $(A_G)_{u,v}$ is the number of edges between $u$ and $v$;
		\item $(D_G)_{u,u}=\deg(u;G)$ and $(D_G)_{u,v}=0$ for $u\neq v$; 
		\item $L_G=D_G-A_G$.
	\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:58.357128+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0b5dc7c49e88ff0edbb66bbf5d8936b8c158cfff5aab03725e7ee51326e074d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2506.18558, '2506.18558'] Suppose that Assumption {\rm\ref{A2}} holds.
