{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:38:08.414575+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e1482bd8abe8f617fd66b74a332380f6e9277d81962b84fee496e6ec2f358f76","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma convergence of s-periods of arXiv:2609.02073, 'Existence of closed non-planar $p$-elasticae'] Let $(\lambda_n,C^2_n) \to (\lambda, C^2) \in S^0 \cup \partial S_{1}^0$ such that $(\lambda,C^2) \neq (\frac{p-1}{2},0)$ and $\lambda<p-1$. 
