{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.756678+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e1a697ebe91332405d384f0908e0d49fbf798288612f277d9a8f49bad0b1adba","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:capped-martingale-estimate-paper of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] There exist constants \(C<\infty\), \(c>0\), and \(\eta>0\) such that, for every \(n\ge1\), every \(2^n\le\lvert\xi\rvert\le2^{n+1}\), and every \(d\in\mathfrak D_{\xi,n}^{\mathrm{osc}}\),
