{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.976759+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e2db6b1b3f4137953f1c0b03a29ca5f684ad95bf1df969d2128441c51c89a37a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2606.11271, '\LARGE The $K$-th nearest neighbor random walk on a Poisson point process gets trapped'] On $\cE_n$, there exist $m \in \{1,\dots,n-1\}$, $T \in \cT_m$ and an embedding $x$ of $T$ such that the following holds.
