		and set $\Theta(R_L ; \partial_1 , \partial_2) = \sup\{ f_1(z) : z \in R_L\}$, which we abbreviate to $\Theta(L)$.  Then $\Theta(L)$ is a continuous, strictly decreasing function of $L$ such that 
