{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:15.337047+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e36fcfb7cca803511e0a1339d2369131a5c05e0ad99699ec93f2cda509142b06","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2506.15037, '2BSDE with uncertain horizon and application to stochastic control in erratic environments'] Let Assumption \ref{assumption:L}  be satisfied. Let $\xi$ be an $\mathcal G_{T\wedge \tau}-$measurable random variable such that $\|\xi\|_{L_{0,\hat{\chi}}^2(\mathbb G)}<\infty$. The auxiliary 2BSDE \eqref{2BSDEb:eq} admits a unique solution $(Y^b,Z^b ,(M^{b,\mathbb P})_{\p\in \mathcal P_0},(K^{b,\mathbb P})_{\p\in \mathcal P_0})\in \mathbb S^2_{0,\hat\chi}(\mathbb F)\times \mathbb H^2_{0,\hat\chi}(\mathbb F) \times \mathbb M_{0,\hat\chi}((\mathbb F^{\mathbb P +})_{\p\in \mathcal P_0})\times \mathbb I^2_{0,\hat\chi}((\mathbb F^{\mathbb P +})_{\p\in \mathcal P_0})$ such that
