{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:04.989508+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e4264de3e91c860883cfdf9d1f85e44cca7dcf5a42c1d0aaf16f37d8c4ec573e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 (\cite{BS2024}) of arXiv:2604.00882, 'On some extensions of generalized counting processes'] The process ${M}^{\psi,f}$ has probability distribution function
   	 \begin{equation}
   	          \tilde{p}_n^{\psi,f}(t)=\sum_{\Omega(k,n)}^{}\prod_{j=1}^{k}\frac{\lambda_j ^{x_j}}{x_j!}\left(-\partial_{\Lambda}\right)^{z_k}\tilde{\ell}_f(t,\psi (\Lambda)), \, n\ge 0,
    	\end{equation}
