{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:20:55.532046+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e46d20250ab54eabc853e24637c8af13a76c9879f8f12b0e7cf698ef17d291da","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem Duality Lemma of arXiv:2411.07671, 'Long Time Behavior of General Markov Additive Processes'] Consider a MAP $( (\xi,\Theta),\mathbb{P})$ such that there exists a MAP $( (\xi,\Theta) ,  \tilde{\mathbb{P}})$ with weak reversibility property. Let $\hat{\mathbb{P}}_{0,\theta}$ be the law of $(-\xi,\Theta)$ under $\tilde{\mathbb{P}}_{0,\theta}$. Then, for every $t>0$, we have \begin{enumerate}
    \item for $x\in\mathbb{R}$, the process 
    $(\xi_{(t-s)-}-\xi_t,\Theta_{(t-s)-})_{0\leq s \leq t}$  under $\mathbb{P}_{x,m}$ has the same law as $(\xi_s,\Theta_s)_{0\leq s \leq t}$ under $\hat{\mathbb{P}}_{0,m}$.
\item $(\Theta_0, t-\Bar{g}_t, \Theta_t, \Bar{\xi}_t-\xi_t, \Bar{g}_t, \Bar{\Theta}_t, \Bar{\xi}_t)$ under $\hat{\mathbb{P}}_{0,m}$ is equal in distribution to\\ $(\Theta_t,\Bar{g}_t,\Theta_0,\Bar{\xi}_t,t-\Bar{g}_t,\Bar{\Theta}_t,\Bar{\xi}_t-\xi_t)$ under $\mathbb{P}_{0,m}.$
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.313685+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e470527c8759a2300b9a21f4434bd6f564165f903f992b494f28deff5551a6ed","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorema WPFLS of arXiv:2608.30777, 'Inhomogeneous nonlinear Schr\"odinger equation \\ in Fourier-Lebesgue and modulation space'] \
