{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.251214+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e491baf1d0fdc96f05e9cd8412d07ffdfd876623944589f58daf5f3a2e3d5520","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 15 (Integrated Davies trick) of arXiv:2609.01098, 'Gaussian upper bounds for averaged heat semigroups on graphs'] For any $q\in[1,\infty]$, denote by $q'$ its H\"older conjugate and let $0\leq V,W\in\ell^\infty(X),$ $I\subset \RR$. Then, for any $q$-norm with respect to any measure on $X$, we have 
