{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.641169+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e63da932a99b621c4277f38945b49a512aca6d959f90fc7cb1bc13e2118e31a7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm-LSI-3 of arXiv:2411.13788, '\bf Gradient bounds and Liouville property for a class of hypoelliptic diffusion via coupl'] Let $f$ be a   positive, globally Lipschitz and bounded $C^2\left(\mathbb{R}^{m_0}\times\cdots\times\mathbb{R}^{m_r}\right)$ function. Then for any fixed $t\ge0$, $x=(x^{(1)},\cdots,x^{(r+1)})\in \mathbb{R}^{m_0}\times\cdots\times\mathbb{R}^{m_r}$,  we have
\begin{align}
\hskip0ptP_t(f\ln f)-(P_tf)\ln P_tf&\le \frac12P_t\left(f\left\langle \int_0^tE(-(t-s))AE^*(-(t-s))ds\nabla \ln f,\nabla \ln f\right\rangle\right).
\end{align}
For $t>0$, the following reverse Logarithmic Sobolev inequality  holds for any positive bounded function $f$:
\begin{align}
P_t(f\ln f)-P_tf\ln P_tf&\ge \frac12P_tf\left\langle \mathcal{C}(t)\nabla\ln P_tf,\nabla \ln P_tf\right\rangle,
\end{align}
where $\mathcal{C}(t)$ defined in (equation C-M of the paper) is a positive matrix.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.616030+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e65470498bb50c5d4c74a6ff94fe0ef7ae40560554200432fb985a7690a3e9d0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 13 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] For any~$\lambda>0$,
