holds for every $(s,t)\in \Delta\llbracket 0,N \rrbracket$ satisfying $\omega_{s,t}<\delta$. Both constants $\delta$ and $L$ depend only on $\theta$, $m$, $\|f\|_2$, $\mathrm{supp}(f)$, $p$, $\omega(S,T)$, and $\|X\|$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:12:13.568055+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e6a52e1fc5ece61ce37b6d6f3458c49b4fbfe03ef05488c122d462005c31262d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 28 (Uniform-in-time fixed-marginal chaos in $W_2$) of arXiv:2608.28827, 'Quantitative Target Convergence and Uniform-in-Time\\ Propagation of Chaos for Langevin-Re'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:core-target}, \ref{ass:W2}, and \ref{ass:concentration}, for fixed \(k\) and \(N\ge2k\),
