{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.731711+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e6e222684db5e5aac679a86aab3060841923ea86706f2ab12ddb0ecece1658e8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 of arXiv:2609.02755, 'The Sharp Rate of Probabilistically Strong Convergence to the KPZ Equation'] Fix $0<\kappa \le \kappa_0$ for $\kappa_0$ sufficiently\footnote{For example, $\kappa_0 = 1/100$ would do} small. We write $\mfT$ for the regularity structure generated by the noise types $\mathfrak{L}_- = \{\<b0>, \<p0>, \<0t>\}$ and kernel types $\mfL_+ = \{\<k>, \<bk>, \<pk>\}$ where the rule (in the sense of \cite[Definition 5.7]{BHZ}) is the one naturally associated to the system \eqref{eq:main_sys}. In particular, each $\mathcal{I}_{\diamond}$ for $\diamond \in \mfL_+$ is a degree $2$ integration operator and
