{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:22:59.740127+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e70ae8c5520e8d7c1baea6abfe9ee6d4938f0e6bb36e88b6bf023914f3cf56b0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem slconv of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] Suppose we have a sequence of $\Phi$-horizontal $C^0$-foliations $\mathcal{G}_k$, $k \geq 0$, on $\mathbb{T}^2$, converging to a $\Phi$-horizontal foliation $\mathcal{G}$ in the $C^0_\mathrm{Fol}$ topology. Furthermore, assume that each $\mathcal{G}_k$ is Reebless with slope $s_k \in \mathbb{R}$, and that $(s_k)_k$ converges to some slope $s_\infty \in \mathbb{R}$.
