{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:23:03.043393+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e76ffe607b5b404a5644d8057e35c9235475b84bd7f8aa4de9943b10c64ffab8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 71 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] There exist  $d_{0}\in(1,d)$ and    $N $, depending only
