{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.187508+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7b01e9b3101a61eb08a08e7dd243a453685566567a0c5c6ca6adf92b3fe1065","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 27 of arXiv:2510.20492, 'Heterochromatic two-arm probabilities for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For any $d\ge 3$, there exist $C,c>0$ such for any $T>0$, any distinct $v_1,v_2,w_1,w_2\in \widetilde{\mathbb{Z}}^d$ with $|v_1-w_1|\land |v_2-w_2|\ge d$, and any $z\in \{v_1,v_2,w_1,w_2\}$, 
 	 	\begin{equation}
 		\begin{split}
 			\mathbb{P}\big(  \widehat{\mathcal{L}}_{1/2}^{z} \ge T  \mid \{v_1\xleftrightarrow{} w_1\Vert v_2\xleftrightarrow{} w_2 \} \big)\le Ce^{-cT}. 
