{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:30:14.227648+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7b80c72887098ea5d2622e2578fef4edbce869a180ced32b631a4ce8d899095","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Bramson-converges-to-1 of arXiv:2608.23202, 'Locally finite Fixed points of Branching Brownian Motion'] \footnote{This claim can also be verified in the modern language of extremal point processes $\widetilde{\mathcal{E}}_\infty^\lambda$. Notably, the underlying reason for (equation other-main-input-from-Bramson of the paper) to hold is that the number of particles of $\widetilde{\mathcal{E}}_\infty^\lambda$ at a bounded distance from $x$ blows up as $x\to -\infty$: it grows like $ e^{-\mu x}$ for $\lambda >\sqrt{2}$ and $\approx (-x)e^{-\sqrt{2}x}$ for $\lambda = \sqrt{2}$.}
