{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:26:47.177933+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e83ce607c774ce79a213fbfbb661975d010b9f30505de52e1dbe9567196eefa1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Ppn 80 of arXiv:2608.29416, 'Algorithmic threshold for high-dimensional projection pursuit I: general theory'] On the time interval $[q_0,\gamma(1)]$,
for $\tilde{w}_t$ as defined by Lemma~\ref{l:time.change}, we have
    \[
        \int_{q_0}^{\gamma(1)}
        \Big(
            \bbE w_{\lambda(s)} - \bbE \tilde w_s
        \Big)_+ \,ds
        \le 2\epsilon^{1/4}
    \]
for all $\epsilon>0$ small enough.

\begin{proof} By Lemma~\ref{l:generalized.inverse.fn}, for bounding the integral we can ignore the measure-zero set of times $s$ for which $\gamma'(\lambda(s))=0$. Therefore, without loss, we restrict our attention to times $s$ for which
$\gamma'(\lambda(s))>0$. In this case, we have $\gamma'(\lambda(s)) \lambda'(s) = 1$, so the definition of $\tilde w_s$ for $s\in[q_0,\gamma(1)]$ 
can be written as $\tilde w_s = \lambda'(s)^{1/2} w_{\lambda(s)} \ind\{\lambda(s) \le \tau\}$. We therefore have
    \begin{align*}
        \int_{q_0}^{\gamma(1)}\lt(
            \bbE w_{\lambda(s)} - \bbE\tilde w_s
        \rt)_+ \,ds
        &\le
        \int_{q_0}^{\gamma(1)}
        \bbE\Big[
        w_{\lambda(s)} - \lambda'(s)^{1/2}
            w_{\lambda(s)} \ind\{ \lambda(s) \le \tau\}
    \Big]_+\,ds\\
        &\le
        \int_{q_0}^{\gamma(1)}
        \bbE\Big[ \lambda'(s)^{1/2} w_{\lambda(s)} \ind\{
        \lambda(s) > \tau\}\Big]\,ds\,,
    \end{align*}
    where the last inequality uses $\lambda' \ge 1$, as a consequence of \eqref{e:gamma.prime}. We then apply the Cauchy--Schwarz inequality to bound the above by
    \begin{align*}
      &  \bigg(
            \int_{q_0}^{\gamma(1)}
            \bbP(\lambda(s) > \tau)\,ds\bigg)^{1/2}
            \cdot\bigg(
            \int_{q_0}^{\gamma(1)}
            \lambda'(s)
            \bbE\Big[
            (w_{\lambda(s)})^2 \ind\{ \lambda(s) > \tau\}\Big]
            \,ds
        \bigg)^{1/2}\\
  &\quad      \le \bigg(
            \int_{q_0}^{\gamma(1)}
            \lambda'(s)
            \bbE\Big[
            (w_{\lambda(s)})^2 \ind\{
             \lambda(s) > \tau\}\Big]
            \,ds
        \bigg)^{1/2}.
    \end{align*}
Changing variables to $u = \lambda(s)$, we bound the last integral above by
    \begin{align*}
        \int_{q_0}^1
        \bbE[(w_u)^2 \ind\{u > \tau\}]\,du
        &= \bbE
            \int_\tau^1 (w_u)^2 \,du
       = \bbE[Y(1)^2 -\hat Y(1)^2]
        = 1 - \gamma(1)
        \le 4\epsilon^{1/2}\,,    \end{align*}
where the last step again uses
Proposition~\ref{p:gamma-1}. This proves the claim.
\end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.577790+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e842b726d5c7009d60d0bc476b7afe806eb0a804d181aa8f7f55b6c89f5ccc4f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2606.14812, 'Joint convergence in Wiener chaos via transport hierarchy and Malliavin covariances'] Let $p\geq 2$ and let $X_{N}= I_{p} (f_{N})$ with $ f_{N} \in H ^ {\odot p}$ for all $N\geq 1$. Assume that $(X_{N}, N\geq 1)$ satisfies (\ref{c1}). Let $Y_{N}= I_{q} (g_{N}) $ with $p<q<2p$ and $(Y_{N}, N\geq 1)$ bounded in $ L^ {2}(\Omega)$. Then
