{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:04:59.426153+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e8e60ea897a235de33c45da5f6bc53258d819f7281092f1c2029fffa6700b2ca","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop Lowerbound of arXiv:2605.18744, 'Lattice random-field Widom--Rowlinson models'] Let $d\le 2$ and $\Lambda_n=\{-n,\ldots, n\}^d$. If $\mathbb{E}[\tau_x(\eta)]>0$ for some $x\in \mathbb{Z}^d$, there is $c >0$ such that for all $t>0$
