{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:36:49.794284+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e91ea0628cb68696750e792021b441d6a7dbe021bbd15cc09fea796829263027","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:odometer-derivative of arXiv:2609.02829, 'Quantitative explosion and percolation of the divisible sandpile'] Suppose $(\zeta(x))_{x\in\mathbb{Z}^d}$ are independent and atomless. Then,
	$\mathbb{P}$-almost surely, for every $n\geq1$ and $x,z\in\mathbb{Z}^d$,
	\begin{equation}
		\partial_{\zeta(z)}u_n(x)
		=
		\mathbf E_x\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}
		\mathbf{1}_{\{X_j=z\}}
		\prod_{i=0}^j\mathbf{1}_{\{u_{n-i}(X_i)>0\}}
		=
		\mathbf E_x\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}
		\mathbf{1}_{\{X_j=z\}}\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau_n^*>j\}}\, .
	\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.831376+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e9226d15a188d3bf483d6eddd5ad5f910bd87c9f8d1ee5efbc0f0353c49a53ab","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:correlation of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] There are some $\lambda_0 > 1$ and $C, \gamma > 0$ such that for all $\lambda \geqslant \lambda_0$
    and all $i, j \in \mathbb{N}$,
    if $\mathbf{X}$ denotes the $\lambda$-tilted stationary line ensemble
    then for all $t > 0$, we have
    \begin{equation}

        0 \leqslant \operatorname{Cov}[X^i(0), X^j(t)] \leqslant C e^{-\gamma t} \lambda^{-(i+j-2)/3}.
    \end{equation}
    The same bound holds if $\mathbf{X}$ is replaced by the stationary
    $n$-line $\lambda$-tilted ensemble $\mathbf{X}_n \sim \mathcal{L}_n^\lambda$, for any $n$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.627973+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e92708e5d67dd0603e4c160c50c624df5156b7232300f4d3c605bb23136741f2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:normal_domain_comonotonic of arXiv:2411.03609, 'Asymptotically optimal Wasserstein couplings for the small-time stable domain of attractio'] Let $\bm{Z}$ be $\alpha$-stable with $\alpha \in (0,2)$ and $\bm{X}$ be in its domain of normal attraction. Let Assumption~(\nameref{asm:C}) (with constant $H\equiv G$ and $Q\equiv 1$) hold for some $p\in(0,\infty)\setminus\{\alpha-1\}$. Then, for any $q\in(0,1]\cap(0,\alpha)$ with $\mathds{E}[|\bm{X}_1|^q]<\infty$, we have, as $t \downarrow 0$, 
\[
\mathcal{W}_q\big(\bm{X}^t,\bm{Z}\big)
=\begin{dcases}
\mathcal{O}\big(t^{\min\{pq/\alpha,1-q/\alpha\}}\big),&\alpha\in(0,1),\\
\mathcal{O}\big(t^{q\min\{p/\alpha,1-1/\alpha\}}\big),&\alpha\in(1,2).
\end{dcases}
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

