{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.376816+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ea09964956835c20ab51032777369b399f5efd11849d4e2f0881a9f5d88f3707","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:two-point-discrepancy of arXiv:2607.21443, 'The critical KPZ scale for the averaging process'] Fix $\beta\in\mathbb{R}$ and set
	\begin{equation}
		\mathfrak c_\beta\coloneqq \cosh(\beta)\; \text{.}
	\end{equation}
	For $\mathbf x=(x_1,x_2)\in\mathbb{Z}^2$, the two-point discrepancy  $e^{-F_\beta}(\mathbf x)
		\ttonde{\ensuremath{\mathcal L}^{(2)}-\ensuremath{\mathcal L}^{\otimes2}}e^{F_\beta}(\mathbf x)$ in (equation eq:k-discrepancy of the paper) with $k=2$
	depends only on the gap
	$x\coloneqq x_1-x_2\in \mathbb{Z}$ and is given by
	\begin{equation}
    \begin{aligned}
		\left(\mathfrak c_\beta-1\right)
		\set{
			\mathfrak c_\beta \mathbf{1}_{\{x=0\}}
			-
			\frac12\mathbf{1}_{\{x=1\}}
			-
			\frac12\mathbf{1}_{\{x=-1\}}
		}= \left(\mathfrak c_\beta-1\right)\Phi_1(x)+\left(\mathfrak c_\beta-1\right)^2\Phi_2(x)\; \text{,}\;\;
        \end{aligned}
	\end{equation}
	where
	\begin{equation}
		\Phi_1(x)
		\coloneqq
			\mathbf{1}_{\{x=0\}}
			-
			\frac12\mathbf{1}_{\{x=1\}}
			-
			\frac12\mathbf{1}_{\{x=-1\}}\; \text{,}\;\;\qquad \Phi_2(x)=\mathbf{1}_{\{x=0\}}\; \text{.}
	\end{equation}
    Moreover, the terms $\Phi_1$ and $\Phi_2$ satisfy \begin{equation}
    \sum_{x\in \mathbb{Z}}\Phi_1(x)\,\pi(x)=0\qquad \text{and}\qquad \sum_{x\in \mathbb{Z}}\Phi_2(x)\,\pi(x)=1\; \text{.}
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:48:02.409879+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ea0d12e61ba93661491a0d7a9fe2f9325ef795b0d1624b26fa2583a01cd74ed7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:staggeredtraces of arXiv:2608.26564, 'Real ideal points, Conway spheres, and left-orderable Dehn fillings'] Suppose $\lambda=\ell_1\ell_2\ell_3\ell_4$ is in positive parabolic normal form along $B$. Then, as $t \to 0$,
