{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.244846+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb02856c08a965d5ea63d769e574910ea4104edac38bd8fa3804915580d9dbb5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm restate of pnkt and nu of arXiv:2604.23890, 'The Cutoff Profile for Random Transpositions on Repeated Cards in the Full Range of Parame'] Let $c\in\mathbb{R}$ be an absolute constant. Let $(n_N)_{N\ge 1},(m_N)_{N\ge 1}$ and $(l_N)_{N\ge 1}$ be sequences of positive integers, such that 
\begin{enumerate}
