{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.430806+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb1e6322acdfcadc1b293308f28d061633e6255276055410536409077d19d944","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:two.point.barycenter.filtered.gaussian of arXiv:2604.22453, 'Adapted Wasserstein Barycenters of Gaussian Processes'] One has
\begin{equation}

\inf_{\mathbb{Z}\in\mathcal{FG}}
\left\{(1-u)\mathcal{AW}_2^2(\mathbb{X}_0,\mathbb{Z})+u\mathcal{AW}_2^2(\mathbb{X}_1,\mathbb{Z})\right\}
=u(1-u)\mathcal{AW}_2^2(\mathbb{X}_0,\mathbb{X}_1),
\end{equation}
and $\mathbb{G}^{\hat a_u,\hat L_u}$ is a minimizer.  Conversely, if $\mathbb{Z}=\mathbb{G}^{b,M}$ is a minimizer, then $b=\hat a_u$ and there exist $Q\in\mathscr Q(L_0,L_1)$ and $R\in\mathscr O(T,d)$ such that
\begin{equation}

M=((1-u)L_0+uL_1Q)R.
\end{equation}
Thus, the set of two-point barycenters in $\mathrm{FG}$ is the collection of equivalence classes generated by (equation eq:two.point.interpolation of the paper) as $Q$ ranges over $\mathscr Q(L_0,L_1)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.588052+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb25294fa34ef3779d5cec6537fec64919811113ed6d8d401e7c24dce2eefddd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop lambda_conv of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] Let $1<p<2$. The space $(X^{a,b}_{p,p'},\mathscr W_p)$ is a complete geodesic metric space. Moreover,  the functional $\mathcal F_{\beta}$ is weakly $\lambda$-geodesically convex on  $(X^{a,b}_{p,p'},\mathscr W_p)$ with $\lambda=\beta a^{-\frac{2-p}{p}}$, i.e., for $\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1\in X^{a,b}_{p,p'}$ there exists a constant speed geodesic $(\mathsf{P}_t)_{0\leq t\leq 1}$ such that for any $0\leq t\leq 1$
    \begin{align*}
        \mathcal F_\beta(\mathsf{P}_t)\leq (1-t) \mathcal F_\beta(\mathsf{P}_0)+t \mathcal F_\beta(\mathsf{P}_1)-\lambda \frac{t(1-t)}{2} \mathscr W_p^2(\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1).
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:37:20.359043+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb256d99341edc5c2557e9e1879191bb6f1b842e5176f1f40b90375796145c39","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem le.finiteLcin of arXiv:2411.13099, 'Long time behavior of killed Feynman-Kac semigroups with singular Schr{ö}dinger potentials'] For all $\mathsf y\in \mathscr R^{2d}_0$,  
