 \]
 in $D({\mathbb R})$ as $n\to\infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:52:08.662758+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb51f39c1165d7df0e87106cfb95fefc92c62f97af491e225dc1513ffb09fa5a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 9 of arXiv:2608.29984, 'On Cauchy Problems for Parabolic Equations with Rough Coefficients'] Given $f\in L^{1}_{loc}(\R^{d})$, we say $f\in BMO(\R^{d})$ provided
\begin{equation}
[f]_{BMO}:=\sup_{Q}\frac{1}{|Q|}\int_{Q}|f-(f)_{Q}|dx,\ (f)_{Q}=\frac{1}{|Q|}\int_{Q}f(y)dy,
\end{equation}
the supermum is taken in all cubes in $\R^{d}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.673394+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb6068a1fe1e09bc6edce5b1d19954832d3631f38de7c68ba380f5750849ccdb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 6 of arXiv:2608.04853, 'Minimal-Norm Extensions of Stationary Kernels on Subgroups of Locally Compact Abelian Grou'] Given two bounded operators $T_0:\mathcal{N}(H) \to \mathcal{N}(G)$ and $T_1:L^2(H) \to L^2(G)$ such that $T_0 f =T_1f$ for all $f \in \mathcal{N}(H)$, where the equality is understood in $L^2(G)$, there exists a bounded operator $T_\theta:\mathcal{N}(H)_{\theta} \to \mathcal{N}(G)_\theta$, such that $T_0f=T_\theta f$ for all $f \in \mathcal{N}(H)$ and
\begin{align*}
\Vert T_\theta \Vert_{\mathcal{N}(H)_\theta \to \mathcal{N}(G)_\theta } \leq \Vert T_0 \Vert_{\mathcal{N}(H) \to \mathcal{N}(G)}^{1-\theta} \cdot \Vert T_1 \Vert_{L^2(H) \to L^2(G)}^{\theta}. 
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:53:54.854975+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb6ff359dad802ad751dacb0b47e1f0aa5cfe0ff5fe3bbb69ae938a92fec6658","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2607.16954, 'Repeated differentiation of deterministic polynomials with asymptotically radial root dist'] The coefficients of $\pp$ and $\qq$ as defined in Notation \ref{not:setting.derivatives} are related as follows.
\begin{equation}

\coef{k}{\qq}=\falling{mn-mk}{ml}\, \coef{k}{\pp},\qquad \text{for } 0\leq k\leq n.    
\end{equation}
Furthermore, the ratio of consecutive coefficients satisfies
\begin{equation}

\frac{\coef{k}{\qq}}{\coef{k-1}{\qq}}=\frac{\coef{k}{\pp}}{\coef{k-1}{\pp}} \prod_{i=1}^{m} \frac{ n-k-l+\frac{i}{m}}{n-k+\frac{i}{m}},\qquad \text{for } 1\leq k\leq n-c_\qq,
\end{equation}
where $c_\qq$ is the multiplicity of the root 0 of $\qq$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:35:04.211570+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb7392366f569741fe303aee40f61b09a501e2afa1e80edee15a220b91704eec","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 1 of arXiv:2608.03956, 'From Triangular Array Progression\\ to Near-Log-Concave State Transitions'] Define an infinite sub-triangular array $\tau$ by
\begin{align}
\tau_{n,j} \triangleq \T_{n + 3, j + 3} \notag
\end{align}
for every $n \geq 0$ and $1 \leq j \leq n +1$. Then, $\tau_{n,*}$ is a strictly-positive log-concave sequence for every $n\geq 2$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.243519+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb787a30f3c534d7d6517c9635a8c22a39ee6a8e6e6e63528a029e458b7a3f51","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:phi of arXiv:2604.23791, 'Finite-sample Borel--Cantelli inequalities under mixing conditions'] Let $N\ge1$ and let $(A_{k})_{1\le k\le N}$ be events, with
$\varphi(\cdot)$ fixed by one coefficient convention of
Section~(sec:prelim of the paper). For each integer $L\ge0$,
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb{P}\Bigl(\,\bigcup_{k=1}^{N}A_{k}\,\Bigr)
  \;\ge\; 1-\exp\!\Biggl(-\frac{1}{L+1}
  \sum_{k=1}^{N}\bigl(\mathbb{P}(A_{k})-\varphi(L+1)\bigr)_{+}\Biggr).
\end{equation}
In particular, if $\varphi(L+1)\le\min_{1\le k\le N}\mathbb{P}(A_{k})$,
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb{P}\Bigl(\,\bigcup_{k=1}^{N}A_{k}\,\Bigr)
  \;\ge\; 1-\exp\!\Bigl(-\tfrac{1}{L+1}\bigl(S_{N}-N\varphi(L+1)\bigr)\Bigr).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:31:49.906180+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb7e757be31dcad0095380976b91fb22ebba367f8b23441eeb0d3ec27f4d1897","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:flat-diagonal of arXiv:2608.26707, 'An Exponential Lower Bound for the Permanent\\of Random Bernoulli Matrix'] Let $Q$ be a real symmetric positive-semidefinite $N\times N$ matrix and set $T=\operatorname{tr} Q>0.$ Suppose that, for some $r\geq1$,
\begin{equation}
 \max_{1\leq i\leq N}q_{ii}\leq\frac{T}{r}.
\end{equation}
Let $\varepsilon\in\{-1,1\}^N$ be a uniform sign vector.
There exist absolute constants $C,c>0$ such that, for every $D\geq2$ and $H\geq1$,
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb{E}\min\!\left\{
   \log_{+}\frac{T}{\varepsilon^{\mathsf T}Q\varepsilon},H
 \right\}
 \leq
 C+CH\left(
   \frac{D^{7/4}}{\sqrt r}+e^{-cD}
 \right).
\end{equation}
The value inside the minimum is understood to be $H$ when $\varepsilon^{\mathsf T}Q\varepsilon=0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.511180+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb85357c821ce48d6e63bc96f943b8a1c6b06f7738413965c68927ae8a1ba328","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 (Spectral zero pattern) of arXiv:2609.02590, 'Directional Optimal Sub-Gamma Scales for Infinitely Divisible Laws'] The directional scales satisfy
\begin{equation}
 \cplus(X)=0\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\nu((0,\infty))=0,
 \qquad
 \cminus(X)=0\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\nu((-\infty,0))=0.

\end{equation}
Consequently, $\cplus(X)=\cminus(X)=0$ if and only if $X$ is Gaussian with
variance $V$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.300851+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb8c71cf9939f2ad4461beb0f81f828404ddf7406afca41582e80f928c971129","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem measurable density of arXiv:2604.21663, 'Large deviations for non-irreducible Markov chains on Euclidean spaces'] Let $p$ be a stochastic kernel on $\mathbb R^d$ such that $p(x,\cdot)$ is absolutely continuous with respect to $\mathrm {Leb} $ for all $x\in \mathbb R^d$. Then, $p$ has a jointly measurable density; in other words there exists a function $f:\mathbb R^d\times \mathbb R^d\to[0, \infty)$ that is $\mathcal B(\mathbb R^d\times \mathbb R^d)$-measurable\footnote{$\mathcal B(\mathbb R^d\times \mathbb R^d)$ denotes the Borel $\sigma$-algebra of $\mathbb R^d\times \mathbb R^d$.} and such that 
