{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:09:49.850042+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb8ca38fd584ee2e7ed87601e37b9f0ae8df8b1e764f5a0139760e6928da0e43","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 67 of arXiv:2609.03070, 'Variants of order semicontinuity in Banach lattices'] The following conditions are equivalent:
\item[(i)] $F$ is countably monotonically bounded;
\item[(ii)] $F$ is countably $r$-monotonically bounded, for some $r\ge 1$;
\item[(iii)] Every countable directed dominable subset of $\Ba_{F_{+}}$ is order bounded;
\item[(iv)] Every countable subset of $F$ which is order bounded in $F^{**}$ is also order bounded in $F$;
