{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:29:21.916113+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ebb121ee841d72e5b919ad7b7e0104855602c74f28c5ede1f9fa48204ac9a8bd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2608.01419, 'A model of opinion dynamics evolving via a preferential attachment mechanism involving mul'] Consider the stochastic approximation process $\{Z_{n}\}$, with $Z_{n}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}$, given by
\begin{equation}
Z_{n+1}=Z_{n}+a_{n+1}\left\{F(Z_{n})+\Delta M_{n+1}+\delta_{n}\right\} \text{ for }n\in\mathbb{N}_{0},
\end{equation}
with prescribed $Z_{0}$ and the following assumptions:
\begin{enumerate}[label=(B\arabic*), ref=B\arabic*]
\item  the map $F:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}$ is Lipschitz,
\item  the step-size sequence $\{a_{n}\}$, of positive scalars, satisfies $\sum_{n}a_{n}=\infty$ and $\sum_{n}a_{n}^{2}<\infty$,
\item  the sequence $\{\Delta M_{n+1}\}$ is a martingale difference sequence with respect to the filtration $\{\mathcal{F}_{n+1}\}$, where $\mathcal{F}_{n}$ is the $\sigma$-field consisting of all information about the process up to and including epoch $n$, and $\{\delta_{n}\}$ is a sequence of additional error terms adapted to $\{\mathcal{F}_{n}\}$, such that $\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}a_{i+1}(\Delta M_{i+1}+\delta_{i})$ converges almost surely as $n\rightarrow\infty$, 
\item  and $\sup\{||Z_{n}||:n\in\mathbb{N}_{0}\}<\infty$ almost surely, where $||\cdot||$ indicates the usual Euclidean norm in $\mathbb{R}^{d}$.
\end{enumerate}
Then, almost surely, $\{Z_{n}\}$ converges to a (possibly sample path dependent) compact connected internally chain transitive invariant set corresponding to the autonomous ODE $\dot{x}(t)=F(x(t))$ for $t\geqslant 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.261917+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ebbfba7185abffb5828a0a9764f0a1411d3ac124acb331472dba73fd187781d0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma stestimate-psi of arXiv:2507.10545, 'KPZ equation from a class of nonlinear SPDEs in infinite volume'] \fsp Take any {\small$\mathfrak{q}_{\n}$} from Lemma (lemma:stestimate-rep of the paper). Fix any {\small$N\gtrsim\ell\geq2\mathfrak{l}$}, where {\small$\mathfrak{l}$} is the support length from Lemma (lemma:stestimate-rep of the paper). We have the following second moment estimate:

