{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.051120+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ebc132869546e1289399efa916caeccab026f40cf7088913c4e93bc886acf5f1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 14 of arXiv:2606.16164, 'A Low-Regularity Semigroup Sewing Lemma via Quotient Structures'] Let $h\in Z\hat C(\Delta_T^3;B_\alpha)$. Then the map
\[
\mathcal T_h:\{R\in C(\Delta_T^2;B_\alpha) \mid \hat\delta R=h\}\to \{\text{compatible frozen increment families over }h\}
\]
defined by $\mathcal T_h(R):=(\Theta_\tau R)_{\tau\in[0,T]}$ is a bijection. Its inverse is given by
\begin{equation}

(r^\tau)_{\tau\in[0,T]}\mapsto R, \quad R_{ts}:=r^t_{ts}.
\end{equation}
In addition, if $\gamma\in(0,1)$ and $h\in Z\hat C^{\gamma}(\Delta_T^3;B_\alpha)$, then
$\mathcal T_h$ restricts to a bijection between $ \{R\in E^{\gamma}(\Delta_T^2; B_\alpha) \mid \hat\delta R=h\}$ and the compatible frozen increment families over $h$ satisfying
\begin{equation}

\sup_{\tau\in[0,T]}\|r^\tau\|_{\gamma-\varepsilon,\alpha+\varepsilon;\tau}<\infty, \quad \forall \varepsilon\in(0, \gamma).
\end{equation}
Likewise, if $h\in Z\hat C^{1}(\Delta_T^3;B_\alpha)$, then $\mathcal T_h$ restricts to a bijection between $\{R\in E_{\log}^{1}(\Delta_T^2; B_\alpha) \mid \hat\delta R=h\}$ and the compatible frozen increment families satisfying
