\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.580575+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ebd9b320c1571e1cf97241e4ba1bbd45ecc121d0bdf5fd614028be6ab64c78e9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 1 (Center accuracy after local calibration) of arXiv:2609.01319, 'Matched Queries for Curvature and Density at Branching Junctions'] Fix smooth localized score tests around a bounded reference offset. If the resulting exact tangent-model least-squares matrix has full column rank, then using the finite-noise score from \cref{thm:expansion} returns a physical center of the form
