{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:32:23.560950+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ebe064db40c26cfd4af0088d6bd811b9dc2fafa7f793c161e6f75fa17caf948f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 3.3 of arXiv:2603.13873, '{Solvability of BSDEs with possibly unbounded stochastic coefficients \\ on a general weig'] Let $\tau$ be a finite stopping time, i.e., $P(\tau<+\infty)=1$, and let $\rho,\mu\in{\mathbb R}$ and $\nu\in{\mathbb R}_+$ be three given constants satisfying $\rho> \mu+\frac{1}{2}\nu^2$. Assume that the generator $g$ satisfies
