and assumptions (A:H2 of the paper)-(A:H5 of the paper) with $\mu_\cdot\equiv \mu$ and $\nu_\cdot\equiv \nu$. Then, for each $\xi\in L_\tau^2(\rho;{\mathbb R}^k)$, BSDE (equation BSDE1.1 of the paper) admits a unique weighted $L^2$ solution $(y_t,z_t)_{t\in[0,\tau]}$ in the space of $H_\tau^2(\rho;{\mathbb R}^{k}\times{\mathbb R}^{k\times d})$. Moreover, we have
