{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.064431+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec051ac0341b3f52b8dc0bb8231c26cee519e999f127fa8fd19bc0d3017e97cf","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 21 (Dubins' inequality for finite time, $T < \infty$) of arXiv:2606.17452, 'Optional Stopping for Superhedging Supermartingales'] Let $f_0, f_1, \ldots, f_T,$ be a given real valued supermartingale sequence with $f_n \geq c $ where $c$ is a constant. Assume the definitions of $\rho_k, \tau_k$ given by Definition \ref{upcrossing_stopping_times}  with $T < \infty$ (i.e. the finite time case). Furthermore, assume
that $(L)-a.e.$ holds; then,
for any $k\ge 0$ and $c \leq a < b$:
\begin{equation} \nonumber 
\overline{\sigma}({\bf 1}_{\{\tau_{k+1} < T+1\}}) \leq \left(\frac{a-c}{b-c} \right)~~ \overline{\sigma}({\bf 1}_{\{\rho_{k}  < T+1\}}) \leq
\left(\frac{a-c}{b-c}\right)~~ \overline{\sigma}({\bf 1}_{\{\tau_{k}  < T+1\}}),
