and so
\begin{equation} 
\overline{\sigma}({\bf 1}_{\{\tau_{k+1}  < T+1\}}) \leq
\left(\frac{a-c}{b-c} \right)^{k+1} ~\overline{\sigma}({\bf 1}_{\{\rho_{0}  < T+1\}}) \leq
\left(\frac{a-c}{b-c}\right)^{k+1}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:23:03.044796+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec071ba98ea0bf443ed14bfff671ad0bf4e2eb1a4c5ee395adc3f1f6448f8739","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 89 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] We say that $X$ is a {\em regular
diffusion process 
\index{$D$@Processes!regular
diffusion process}
corresponding to
$\cL$ or to $a,b$\/} if



(i)  for any $(t,x)\in\bR^{d+1}$
