    \left(1+o(1)\right)\right) \qquad {\text{as}} \quad {t\to\infty},
\end{equation}
    where the function $\mathcal{N}(\cdot)\in{{\mathcal{SV}}_{\infty}}(\omega)$ and it has the property {(\ref{IIB3.2})}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:19:46.232526+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec23df2d8bbdcc6e06086d4420eb587aa72276ce56a0e71e3b504271d2b78427","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 49 of arXiv:2507.08909, 'Annealed almost periodic entropy'] For separable unital representations $\pi$ and $\rho$, the following are equivalent:
