{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.328151+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec4ec5e73fab836cf3297c65327b866596add7ba62f419edabf30d3e429dd63b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:spectral_heat1 of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] Let $\Omega$ be a bounded, open subset of $\mathbb{G}$. If $\Omega$ has $C^2$ boundary with no characteristic points, then
    \begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=*]
        \item  For $1<\alpha<2$, 
        \begin{align*}
            \lim_{t\to 0}\frac{\operatorname{Vol}(\Omega)-\widetilde{H}^{(\alpha)}_\Omega(t)}{t^{\frac{1}{\alpha}}}= \mathbb{E}\left[\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant 1} Y_t\right]\operatorname{Per}_{\mathcal H}(\Omega),
        \end{align*}
        where $(Y_t)_{t\geqslant 0}$ is a one-dimensional symmetric $\alpha$-stable L\'evy process such that $\mathbb{E}[e^{i \xi Y_t}]=e^{-t|\xi|^\alpha}$ for all $t\geqslant 0$ and $\xi\in\mathbb R$.
        \item  When $\alpha=1$, 
        \begin{align*}
            \lim_{t\to 0}\frac{\operatorname{Vol}(\Omega)-\widetilde{H}^{(1)}_\Omega(t)}{t\log(1/t)}= \frac{1}{\pi}\operatorname{Per}_{\mathcal H}(\Omega).
        \end{align*}
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

