{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.062205+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec516919e8911895b528ff33e7f670cc9aae2c6abaa5ad454ad8305c97405ab8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:3.1 of arXiv:2607.14993, 'Sharp phase transition for percolation with short-range dependencies'] Let $(f_n)_{n \geqslant 0}$ be a sequence of increasing differentiable functions from $[0, \beta_0]$ to $[0, M]$. Assume that this sequence converges to a function $f$ and that, for all $n \geqslant 1$, we have
  \begin{equation}
    f_n' \geqslant \frac n {\sum\limits_{k=0}^{n-1} f_k} f_n.

  \end{equation}
  Then there exists $\beta_1 \in [0, \beta_0]$ such that
  \begin{itemize}
      \item for $\beta < \beta_1$ there exists $c_\beta > 0$ such that for any $n$ large enough $f_n(\beta) \leqslant \exp(- c_\beta n)$,
