{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.249299+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec6f928455bf771d32ecf540a3e9bee0050b76d1610dc447dd497e2bfb8bfa6b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 39 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] The following holds for $\varepsilon > 0$ sufficiently small. Fix ${a}, {b}, {c} \in (1 - \varepsilon, 1 + \varepsilon)$, $q \in (-\varepsilon, \varepsilon)$ and a point $z_0=(x_0,y_0) \in {\mathfrak{L}}_{q; a,b,c}$,
