{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:48:49.883039+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ecb4540797feebb0a93f5eed111e15fa62bdbf005a2f3ecefb9f8202d9c3226e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defin coherency-eq of arXiv:2510.23430, 'On the Martin boundary for discrete TASEP'] A \emph{coherent system} on $\mathbb{G}^p$ is an element of the projective limit $\varprojlim \mathcal M(\mathbb{G}^p_n)$, that is, a family of measures $\{M_n\in\mathcal M(\mathbb{G}^p_n)\}_{n\geq 0}$ such that for every $\mu\in\mathbb{G}^p_n$ the following coherency relation holds
\begin{equation}

M_n(\mu)=\sum_{\lambda\in\mathbb{G}^p_{n+1}}p^{\downarrow}_{n+1,n}(\lambda,\mu) M_{n+1}(\lambda).
\end{equation}
Using the embedding $\varprojlim \mathcal M(\mathbb{G}^p_n)\to\prod_{n\geq 0}\mathcal M(\mathbb{G}^p_n)$ we define the Borel structure on the set of coherent systems $\varprojlim \mathcal M(\mathbb{G}^p_n)$.","status":"unverified"}

