{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.188351+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ecb6bc86c445bf1b7b9f2f767de1de7dc480a525200ae71074ee908ef76aa401","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def-condlim of arXiv:2603.01322, 'Gibbs conditioning, atypical consensus and splitting Gibbs measures on random regular grap'] Fix an edge potential $h$, and $c \in \R$, $c \neq \sref.$ Let $\Conset_n(h,c)$ and  $(c_\delta)_{\delta > 0}$ be  as in Definition (\oldref{def-rareevent}) and  (equation sdelta of the paper), respectively. 
