{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.317015+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ecbb67f34c0522aa961ea52e9038780844b6a2f2e30754d14fd180dcf8a2586d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma itolinax of arXiv:2411.06131, 'Non-Markovian dynamics: the memory-dependent probability density evolution equations'] Let $ X_t $ be the solution of ((mSDEline of the paper)). Suppose that $ F(t,x) $ is any twice differentiable function of two variables. If $ A_t, B_t $ and $ C_t $ satisfy the conditions of Lemma (Malianx of the paper), then
