{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.448012+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ed74d207c99c4ea0001d1061314a55639280bcb8fb36c522131b586f084eb365","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor mle-goal of arXiv:2411.11676, 'Surface sums for lattice Yang--Mills in the large-$N$ limit'] For all strings $s=\{\ell_1,\dots,\ell_n\}$ and all plaquette assignments  $K:\mathcal{P}_{\mathbb{Z}^d}\to\mathbb{N}$ the following master loop equation at every fixed edge $\mathbf{e}$ in $s$ holds:
