{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:29:14.939003+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ed9572f28d1ad2e7b0c0b2f41e59d72cf52c663132475ba7d01d348241920b42","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm1stResult of arXiv:2606.13615, 'Data-Driven Subsampling Rates for Diffusion Parameter Estimation of SDEs'] Suppose that Assumption (Assumptions of the paper) holds, let $\mathbf{X}_0$ be an initial random variable independent of $\mathbf{W}$, and let $\mathbf{X} = (\mathbf{X}_t)_{t \geq 0}$ be the corresponding solution to (equation eqGenSDEIntro of the paper) with $d$-th component $X = (X_t)_{t \geq 0}$. Then the probability distribution of the length of the first monotone run of the sampled process $(X_{n\delta})_{n \in \mathbb{N}_0}$ converges to the geometric distribution with parameter $1/2$ as $\delta \rightarrow 0$ , i.e., for all $\ell \in \mathbb{N} \cup \lbrace \infty \rbrace$ it holds that
