{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.648923+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ed988fd46492657f98a9a19a32fd4234122c2419379a563769fdec1683238d41","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm domination2GeneralOlD of arXiv:2411.13926, 'Random walks on random walks:\\ non-perturbative results in high dimensions'] The probability measure $\ensuremath{\mathbb{P}}^{(1)}_{I^{(1)}}( \cdot \;|\; \ensuremath{\mathcal{C}}^{(1)})$ is equal, in law, to  
\begin{equation}\sum_{\mathbf{y}} \ensuremath{\mathbb{P}}^{(1)}_{I^{(1)}}(\mathbf{y} \;|\; \ensuremath{\mathcal{C}}^{(1)}) \sum_{k=1}^{\kappa}\ensuremath{\mathcal{L}}(Y^{(k)}|\mathbf{y}), \quad \text{ where:}\end{equation}
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\mathbf{y} = (y_1,...,y_K)$ with $K\leq \kappa$, and $\ensuremath{\mathbb{P}}^{(1)}_{I^{(1)}}(\mathbf{y} \;|\; \ensuremath{\mathcal{C}}^{(1)})$ is the probability that the iteration of Lemma (lemma:decomposition of the paper) using Corollary (lemma:decompositionK of the paper) terminates after $K$ steps and $Y^{(k,k)}=y_k$, $k=1,...,K$;
    \item For $k=1,\dots,K$, $\ensuremath{\mathcal{L}}(Y^{(k)}|\mathbf{y}) =\ensuremath{\mathcal{L}}(Y^{(1,k)}|\mathbf{y})$ is the law of the random lifts $Y^{(1)}_k \in I^{(1)}$ of $Y^{(k,k)} = y_k$ given $\mathbf{y} = (y_1,...,y_K)$.
    \item For $k>K$, $\ensuremath{\mathcal{L}}(Y^{(k)}|\mathbf{y})$ is the law of the additional random lifts of points appearing from the iteration procedure.
    \item Given $\mathbf{y}$, the random variables $(Y^{(k)}|\mathbf{y})$ are independent.
\end{itemize}
Furthermore, there is an $n \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$ such that $\ensuremath{\mathbb{P}}^{(1)}_{I^{(1)}}( \cdot \;|\; \ensuremath{\mathcal{C}}^{(1)})$ is stochastically dominated by 
\begin{align}
\ensuremath{\mathbb{P}}^{(1)}_{I^{(1)}}  \bigoplus \sum_{\mathbf{y}} \ensuremath{\mathbb{P}}^{(1)}_{I^{(1)}}(\mathbf{y} \;|\; \ensuremath{\mathcal{C}}^{(1)}) \sum_{k=1}^{|\mathbf{y}|}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\ensuremath{\mathcal{L}}(Y_j^{(1,k)}|\mathbf{y}),
\end{align}
where, given $\mathbf{y} = (y_1,...,y_K)$, the $Y_j^{(1,k)}$ are independent random lifts  of $Y^{(k,k)} = y_k$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.376838+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ed98bc33ed0fcb9693f1b6fcc3030b553908eb807d47c69144f5d43a7e93a424","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:ybound of arXiv:2412.01995, 'Exciting games and Monge-Amp\`{e}re equations'] Denoting $\tilde C=C+\log(d+1)+10$, for any $y \in \tilde \Omega_C$ we have that $\tilde w(y) +h(y) \geq 0$, and 
