{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.366833+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_edbbec723ad0802bafdc20aaac4291dd980db4731d37c23d790932104625f69f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop char-mu-tilde of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] There exists a constant $c>0$ such that for all balls or boxes $B\subset[0,1]^2$,
