{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.041883+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eddab5a1682550d3801c374209f0f5ba440f2caedc545d03bc04889ea3db9cb8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2606.31596, 'The Invariant Measure of Multiscale Markov Chains via Fast Arborescence Factorization'] Fast edges of the reduced graph $(\hat V, \hat E\,)$ coincide with fast edges of the original graph $(V,E)$ with both endpoints in $\hat V$, namely $\hat E_F=E_F[\hat V]\,$.

