{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.618457+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ede3002ada7d41acb76468c342dd70bc19f2d20ca0b1d77e72790bc269fcd7ac","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 32 of arXiv:2608.25785, 'Proper Actions on Homogeneous Spaces of the Upper Triangular Matrix Group via Coarse Geome'] Fix $n\in \Z_{\geq 1}$ and a set $\Lambda$ with $\Lambda_0(n)\subset \Lambda\subset \Lambda_1(n)$. 
