{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.872402+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ee0cad380d5904f67bfc53868fae117738b69d8279b5d97167309582bbf294c1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:stima_utilde of arXiv:2605.07832, 'A Bismut -Elworthy formula for BSDEs with degenerate noise'] Assume that condition (equation condizione_traccia of the paper) are verified, let $T>0$ be fixed, let $\alpha\in\left(0,1\right)$ and let $\widetilde u_t$ be the function defined in (equation damped_def_ctrl of the paper). Hence, there exists a positive constant $C>0$ such that, for every $t\in(0,T]$ and every $a\in U$,
