{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.847328+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ee20b70eb635df92cbc0c94ae112a51d53d558c9e34d05a88730fde565ab340a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:WicksWigner of arXiv:2510.01021, '\Large Random Matrices, Intrinsic Freeness, and Sharp Non-Asymptotic Inequalities\relatedv'] Let $W_1,\dots,W_n$ be $N\times N$ independent standard Wigner matrices (recall Definition~(def:standardWignerMatrix of the paper)). Given a partition $\nu\in\mathbb{P}[2p]$ let $u_\nu$ be the $\nu$-assignment (see Definition~(def:pairpartition of the paper)). We have
    \begin{equation}
            \mathbb{E}\left[\tr W_{u_\nu(1)}\cdots W_{u_\nu(2p)}\right]  = 1,
    \end{equation}
    if $\nu\in \mathrm{NC}[2p]$ is non-crossing, and 
\begin{equation}
            \lim_{N\to\infty} \mathbb{E}\left[\tr W_{u_\nu(1)}\cdots W_{u_\nu(2p)}\right] = 0,
    \end{equation}
if $\nu\in \mathbb{P}[2p]\setminus \mathrm{NC}[2p]$ is crossing.

    Furthermore, $W_1,\dots,W_n$ enjoy (in the limit) a Wick's formula summing only over non-crossing partitions: For $u:[2p]\to[n]$ we have
    \begin{equation}
\lim_{N\to\infty}\mathbb{E}\left[\tr W_{u(1)}\cdots W_{u(2p)}\right] = \sum_{\nu\in \mathrm{NC}_2[2p]} 1_{u \sim \nu}.
    \end{equation}
The identities (equation eq:WignerNONcrossingpairings of the paper)--(equation eq:WicksforWigner of the paper) hold for a free semicircular family $s_1,\dots,s_n$ (without needing to take a limit). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:07.257085+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ee21a4008daf0e24e455a355d28ccbcbbcac2fea9e29dc9060666bcaa5348bf3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 1 of arXiv:2604.19308, '\textbf{On McKean--Vlasov SDEs with polynomial drifts for SIS epidemic models}'] Let $p=1$ and~\eqref{co:1} and~\eqref{co:2} be valid. Then pathwise uniqueness holds for~\eqref{eq:SIS epidemic model}, and any two solutions $I$ and $\tilde{I}$ to~\eqref{eq:SIS epidemic model} satisfy
\begin{equation}
\E\big[|I_{t} - \tilde{I}_{t}|\big] \leq e^{\int_{0}^{t}(\hat{b}_{k+1} + \hat{\lambda}_{k+1})(s,N(s))\,\mathrm{d}s}\E\big[|I_{0} - \tilde{I}_{0}|\big]
\end{equation}
for all $t\geq 0$. In particular, if $(\hat{b}_{k+1} + \hat{\lambda}_{k+1})^{+}(\cdot,N)$ is integrable, then $\sup_{t\geq 0} \E[|I_{t} -\tilde{I}_{t}|]$ is finite. If additionally
\begin{equation*}
\int_{0}^{\infty}(\hat{b}_{k+1}+\hat{\lambda}_{k+1})^{-}(s,N(s))\,\mathrm{d}s = \infty,\quad\text{then}\quad \lim_{t\uparrow\infty} \E\big[|I_{t}-\tilde{I}_{t}|\big] = 0.
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:11:57.342192+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ee21f82289586e31cf42ec401b367aca8656f6df94fc4f3aed4cfa2aad48600f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 29 of arXiv:2607.23791, 'Precise cover times for branching random walks on Hamming graphs: (iterated) logarithmic c'] For every fixed $a>0$, every $s\ge0$, and every integer $k\ge1$,
