 \end{equation}
 where the parity $(-1)^{\textnormal{par}(q_1,q_2)}$ is $(+1)$ if $\mathcal T_{q_1},\mathcal T_{q_2}$ are both left, or both right trapezoids, and $(-1)$ otherwise. In particular, \eqref{eq_Green_function_explicit} extends to a continuous function of $\Sigma^{\textnormal{half}} \times \Sigma^{\textnormal{half}}$ minus the diagonal. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:52.747106+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eeb96a03698f45f6274981ccc541218e58ea32b51b6f4644952327a58e8e11d8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 19 of arXiv:2506.10522, 'On the Law of the Iterated Logarithm for $m$-dependent stationary random variables under s'] Let $\{X_n;n=1,2,\cdots\}$ be a m-dependent stationary sequence in a sub-linear space $\sles$ satisfying following conditions :
