{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.685259+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eed454382ac64bc15dd515a339f6bbb6cb895c04688363e6c4c8e236d9e61c6c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 (Weighted-ratio expansion) of arXiv:2608.30916, 'Selection-Aware Stress Testing for Interactive Agents'] Let $a_g=P s_g>0$, $P^g h=P(s_gh)/a_g$, and $P_n^g h=P_n(s_gh)/P_ns_g$. Whenever $P_ns_g>0$,
