{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.075415+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eedf9099d8567733dbed6844453e7803a200b7b87407dcd4056743e6f94e6167","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 12 of arXiv:2606.02036, 'Self-intersection local times for Volterra Gaussian processes in stochastic flows with int'] Assume that the coefficients $a$ and $b$ of \eqref{eq:Eq_interaction} are continuously differentiable with respect to $v$ for all $\mu\in\cM_m$. Moreover, assume there exist constants $C, L>0$ such that for all $v_1,v_2\in\mbR^d,\ \mu^{(1)},\mu^{(2)}\in\cM_m, $
