{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.350925+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef50f19e9234cf5c81a06c7bd2409327ed12c583c4c8e58319bf045f10505db9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eq:Breg of arXiv:2412.06420, 'Accuracy, Estimates, and Representation Results'] If $\mathsf{acc}$ is proper, then $\varphi_\mathsf{acc}$ is convex and if it is differentiable, then:
		\begin{align}
		&\mathrm{Exp}_p\mathsf{acc}(p)-\mathrm{Exp}_p\mathsf{acc}(x)=\varphi_\mathsf{acc}(p)-\varphi_\mathsf{acc}(x)-(p-x)\varphi_\mathsf{acc}'(x)
		\end{align}
			If it is not differentiable, then we have the same form, but with $\varphi_\mathsf{acc}'$ as some sub-gradient. 

		Also for $v\in\set{0,1}$,
		\begin{align}
		&\mathsf{acc}_v(x)=\mathsf{acc}_v(v)-\br*{\varphi_\mathsf{acc}(v)-\varphi_\mathsf{acc}(x)-(v-x)\varphi_\mathsf{acc}'(x)}
		\end{align}
		And in fact
		\begin{align}
		&\mathsf{acc}_v(x)=\varphi_\mathsf{acc}(x)+(v-x)\varphi_\mathsf{acc}'(x)
		\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.041143+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef53f768b4129c7e523e6e7778bac52908bfe65c88c4ab523317230e0ffd7eac","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 12 of arXiv:2606.31596, 'The Invariant Measure of Multiscale Markov Chains via Fast Arborescence Factorization'] The weight of the set $\mathcal T_{x_1}$ of arborescences of $K_{n+1}$ and the reduced weight of the set $\hat{\mathcal T}_{x_1}$ of arborescences of $\hat K_{n}$ are related by:
