{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.598575+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef57b6bda39fb5b63f18ea1da10ba8cecf9bd051f224a9938b177ce268b85484","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L:basic-stationary-est of arXiv:2604.10020, 'The directed landscape in half-space'] Fix $\alpha_0 \in (0, 1/2)$. There is $c>0$ depending only on $\alpha_0$ such that the following is true. Take parameters $\alpha, \beta$ such that $\alpha > \alpha_0$, $\beta \in (2(1/2 - \alpha)\vee 0, 1/2 - \alpha_0)$. Set
$$
\bar Z^+(i) =\begin{cases}
	Z^+(i) - \frac{i}{1/2 - \beta}, \qquad i \ge 0 \\
	Z^+(i) - \frac{|i|}{1/2 + \beta}, \qquad i < 0.
\end{cases}
$$
 Then for any $i < j \in \mathbb{Z}$ and $m > 0$ we have that
\begin{equation}

\mathbb{P}\Big(\max_{r < s \in \llbracketi,j \rrbracket} |\bar Z^+(s) - \bar Z^+(r)| \ge m\Big) \le 2\exp \left(-\frac{cm^2}{m + (j - i)} \right).
\end{equation}
Moreover, for any $j_0 \in \mathbb{Z}, \delta > 0,$ and $m > 0$ we have that
\begin{equation}

	\mathbb{P}(|\bar Z^+(j_0 + i) - \bar Z^+(j_0)| \le m + \delta i^2 \text{ for all } i \in \mathbb{Z}) \ge 1 - 2\exp \left(-\frac{cm^2}{m + \sqrt{m/\delta}} \right).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.581169+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef5929b70a244e9b205a239364bd4d710be71de74f448177f681d24b1158d8e0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Fn of arXiv:2605.16963, 'Stochastic Euler Equations with Pseudo-differential Noise: Continuous and Discontinuous Pe'] Let $F(\cdot)$ be defined in (equation F-Euler of the paper). There exists a sequence of locally Lipschitz functions $\{F_n:\mathbb H^s\to \mathbb H^s\}_{n\ge1}$ with $s>\frac{d}{2}+1$ such that the following properties hold:
		\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=0.79cm]\setlength\itemsep{0.2em}
			\item If $s>\frac{d}{2}+1$ and $\theta\in(\frac{d}{2},s-1)$, $\{X_n,X\}_{n\ge1}\subset \mathbb H^s$ is bounded, and $\lim_{n\to\infty}X_n=X$ in $\mathbb H^\theta$, then
			$$\lim_{n\to\infty} F_n(X_n)=F(X)\quad \text{in}\quad \mathbb H^{\theta-1}.$$
			\item If (Constant Sound of the paper) holds, then 
			\begin{equation*}
				\sup_{n\ge1}\Abs{\left\langleF_n(X), X\right\rangle _{\mathbb H^s}}\lesssim  \big(\|\nabla u\|_{L^\infty}+\|\nabla \varrho\|_{L^\infty}\big)\|X\|_{\mathbb H^s}^2,\quad X=(\varrho,u)^T\in \mathbb H^{s},\quad s>\frac{d}{2}+1.
			\end{equation*}
			Moreover, if $s>\frac{d}{2}+2$ and $\theta\in(\frac{d}{2}+1,s-1)$, then 
			\begin{align*}
				\left\langleF_n(X)-F_m(Y),X-Y\right\rangle _{\mathbb H^\theta} 
				\lesssim \Big(1+\|X\|^4_{\mathbb H^s}+\|Y\|^4_{\mathbb H^s}\Big)
				\left((n\wedge m)^{-2(s-1-\theta)}+\|X-Y\|^2_{\mathbb H^\theta}\right), \quad X,Y\in\mathbb H^s.
			\end{align*}

			\item If (General Sound of the paper) holds, then 
			\begin{equation*}
				\sup_{n\ge1}\Abs{\left\langleF_n(X), X\right\rangle _{\mathbb H^s}}\lesssim \big(1+\Phi_\Lambda(\|\varrho\|_{L^\infty})\big)\big(\|\nabla u\|_{L^\infty}+\|\nabla \varrho\|_{L^\infty}\big)\|X\|_{\mathbb H^s}^2,\quad X=(\varrho,u)^T\in \mathbb H^{s}.
			\end{equation*}
			Additionally, if $s>\frac{d}{2}+2$ and $\theta\in\left(\frac{d}{2}+1,s-1\right)$, then for all $m,n\ge1$,
			\begin{align*}
				&\left\langleF_n(X)-F_m(Y),X-Y\right\rangle _{\mathbb H^\theta} \\
				\lesssim\ &  \Big(1+ \Phi^2_{\Lambda}\big(\|X\|_{\mathbb H^{s}}+\|Y\|_{\mathbb H^{s}}\big)+\|X\|^4_{\mathbb H^s}+\|Y\|^4_{\mathbb H^s}\Big)
				\left((n\wedge m)^{-2(s-1-\theta)}+\|X-Y\|^2_{\mathbb H^\theta}\right),\quad X,Y\in\mathbb H^s.
			\end{align*}

		\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

