{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.591982+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef5d6b8577d9524e0514e74b38d07a08cb34ac6247cbeb5871754f6eabd4c178","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem permutation_increases_number_of_holes of arXiv:2412.03370, 'TASEP with a general initial condition and a deterministically moving wall'] Let $\pi$ denote the swap operators corresponding to a permutation of $\mathbb{Z}$ that exchanges $a$ and $b$ for some $a < b \in \mathbb{Z}$ and maps all other integers to themselves. Let $\eta$ be a configuration of a single-species TASEP on $\mathbb{Z}$, and let $x \in \{a, \dots, b-1\}$. Suppose that in $\eta$, there are a hole at a site in $\{x+1, \dots, b \}$ and a particle at a site in $\{a, \dots, x \}$. Then, in $\pi(\eta)$, 
	\begin{itemize}
		\item[(i)] the number of holes at sites in $\{a, \dots, x \}$ increases by $1$; 
		\item[(ii)] a hole is moved to site $a$; 
