{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.786489+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef663d73b6bd864170368f401afa4f96ea502aa43e7af9a2beafe3c62c554dd4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop local-CLT-DKS of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] There exist absolute constants $C,\beta_0>0$ such that for all $N\geq 1, -N\leq k \leq N$ and $\beta>\beta_0$, if $NM_{N,H}=k$ then
