where $F(H) = \lim_{M} \frac{1}{M} \log \Xi(M,H)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.371763+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef67a1075007519ca5500391f506d9657dc24402d1fea21086069beb4a9a5b54","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2606.03973, 'A remark on the \\ majorizing measures theorem for general processes'] Suppose that $X \sim \mu$ is a centered random vector in $\R^n$ such that
  \begin{equation}

