{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.559077+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef82c57f4efff2e8e63af495bd8a312a51c548833e374ba0800cd435eb78cfb6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Question question-main-3 of arXiv:2604.04882, 'On a Problem of M. Kac on Laplace Distributions'] Let $D\subset\C$ and let $\Phi:D\times D\to\C$ be a map such that for every pair of characteristic functions $f_1,f_2$ on $\R$, the quantity $\Phi(f_1(\xi),f_2(\xi))$ is well defined for every $\xi\in\R$. Let $\cM$ be a subfamily of the set of all characteristic functions on $\R$. Suppose that
    \begin{align}
        \Phi(f_1(\xi),f_2(\xi))\in \cM
        \qquad\text{for all }\xi\in\R.
    \end{align}
