{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:07:48.568343+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef8701c50f6d97afb36c93a8bb9ded2a9df5e588ec0c647dad6a7501a034c9c6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 42 ($\mathrm{CD}(K, \infty)$ condition) of arXiv:2609.01460, 'On cost-induced Santal\'o-type inequalities \\ in Polish measure spaces'] Given $K \in \mathbb{R}$, we say that a Polish probability space $(X, d,\mu)$ is a $\operatorname{CD}(K, \infty)$-space if for any two measures $\nu_0, \nu_1 \in \operatorname{dom}_\mu\left(H\right)$ there exists a geodesic $\left(\nu_t\right) \in \operatorname{Geo}\left(\mathcal{P}_2(X)\right)$ which satisfies the convexity inequality
\begin{equation*}
H(\nu_t|\mu) \leq(1-t) H(\nu_0|\mu)+t H(\nu_1|\mu)-\frac{K}{2} t(1-t) W_2^2\left(\nu_0, \nu_1\right), \quad \text { for all } t \in[0,1] .
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:31.955409+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef8836ea6dff2a9f49db4ee277535d397cae7c573a1415c0e21661dd1f03fbaa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 3 of arXiv:2512.01483, 'Scaling Limits of Line Models in Degenerate Environment'] Assume $\varepsilon_1 \varepsilon_2 < 1$. Then, for almost all environments $\omega$, the random walk $X$ is conservative, i.e., for every $t < \infty$ 
