{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.355909+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f00f11fc7b845052912320fdb89f0452e8b273194f2639aa2b97d13cfa3bbe3f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t:scaling_limit_cutoff of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Let $M\geq 1$, $\mu>0$ and $R>0$. Suppose that $p,q\in (2,\infty)$ satisfy  (equation eq:condition_pq_subcritical_scaling_cutoff of the paper).

Then, for all $\varepsilon\in (0,1)$, 
\begin{equation}

\lim_{N \to \infty}\sup_{u_0\in \mathcal{B}_{p,q}(M)}{\mathbf P}\big(\|w_{{\rm cut}}^N - w_{{\rm cut,d}}\|_{L^{2p}({\mathbb R}_+;L^{2q}(\mathbb{T}^3;{\mathbb R}^3))}\geq \varepsilon\big)=0,
\end{equation}
where $w_{{\rm cut}}^N$ is the global $(p,q)$-solution to (equation eq:navier_stokes_cutoff of the paper) with initial data $u_0-\overline{u}_0$, and $w_{{\rm cut,d}}$ is the unique global $(p,q)$-solution to the following deterministic {{\normalfont{3D NSEs}}} with cutoff and \emph{increased viscosity} on $\mathbb{T}^3$:
\begin{equation}

\left\{
\begin{aligned}
\partial_t w_{{\rm cut,d}} 
&+(\overline{u}_0\cdot \nabla) w_{{\rm cut,d}} \\
&+\phi_{p,q}^R (\cdot,w_{{\rm cut,d}}) \,\mathbb{P}\big[ \nabla\cdot (w_{{\rm cut,d}} \otimes w_{{\rm cut,d}})\big] 
= \Big(1 + \frac{3\mu}{5}\Big)\Delta w_{{\rm cut,d}}, \\
w_{{\rm cut,d}}(0)&=u_0-\overline{u}_0.
\end{aligned}
\right.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:23:03.039607+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f013a1fbcf38cd347fabbaf1c9fed00b14da5de3cf17f16d9c62b00aa7031671","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 22 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] Let $0\in Q$. Then
