{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.357450+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f0206be30a331cd50a8c2073f8e38a84e50385f30cc19210855249b36f56202b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2511.09280, 'Random Walk conditioned to stay above a non-flat floor: curvature effects'] Let \(\beta>0, p\geq 1\). Then, there are \(c>0, n_0\geq 1, \lambda_0\geq 1\) such that for any \(n\geq n_0\), \(\lambda \geq \lambda_0\) with \(\lambda n^{\alpha_p}< n/2^p\),
