\end{equation*}
one has \(A_n\to\infty\) almost surely on \(\{\mu_\circ(\mathbb S^1)>0\}\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.780267+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f03ae4f67c6e9718027209e3ef5d0820b418757652873c11bb77c18ac6098ac4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Semicircular system asymptotics of arXiv:2411.01633, 'On the Limit of the Tridiagonal Model \\for $\beta$-Dyson Brownian Motion'] For each $n$, let $(M_1,\dots,M_k)$ be a jointly Gaussian family of GOE random matrices such that
    \begin{equation}
        \begin{split}
            \mathbb{E}\left[(M_i)_{\ell_1,\ell_2} (M_j)_{\ell_1',\ell_2'}\right]= \left(\delta_{(\ell_1,\ell_2),(\ell_1',\ell_2')}+\delta_{(\ell_1,\ell_2),(\ell_2',\ell_1')}\right) \varphi_{i,j}.
        \end{split}
    \end{equation}
    Then,
    \begin{equation}
        \begin{split}
            \frac{1}{n^{1+\ell/2}}\mathbb{E}\left[\mathrm{Tr}(M_{i_1}\dots M_{i_{\ell}})\right] = \sum_{\pi \in NC_2[\alpha]} \prod_{(j,j') \in \pi} \varphi_{i_j,i_{j'}}+O(n^{-1}),
        \end{split}
    \end{equation}
    as $n \to \infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:08.952776+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f040c9c9a7a28e277b9a5b2d8806d5161c0b2fd37d1abdab46d504cd520d7a6b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:mixed_tail_measurability of arXiv:2609.01576, '\normalfont Pointwise Majorization for sub-Weibull and Mixed Tail Processes with Applicati'] For every $j\in\cbr{1,2}$, the map
