{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:27:14.910992+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f10d98ec5558d652744a78b6a2d46a6f0cbd1c4173c66cdb14469ed54d5736df","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 (Lipschitz Continuity) of arXiv:2608.24146, 'Robust Data-Collection Policy Learning for Low-Variance Online Policy Evaluation'] The function $f: \mathcal{X}\to \mathbb{R}$ is $L-$Lipschitz if $\forall x_1,x_2\in \mathcal{X},$ 
