{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:33:06.540508+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f11077b64ecb16c3abf43156701db7a494576b98b35d9dd25bcb0bb7f83d1bca","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2608.25887, '\bf Efficient Estimation of High Information Projections using Nearest Neighbours'] Let $X_1, X_2, ...$ be i.i.d. random variables with density $f_X$ satisfying Conditions C1--C4. Let $0 < a \leq b$ and let $\{k(n)\}_{n\in \mathbb{N}}$ satisfy $\lim_{n \to \infty} k(n) = \infty$ and $\lim_{n\to\infty} k(n)/n = 0$. Then
