{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:38:17.792318+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f1196228c5947893f7c8048b549fb7522b615a51df07e8bf84759b3c27f9c5f4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:local_time_RW of arXiv:2509.20779, 'Diffusive Scaling limit of stochastic Box-Ball systems and P\MakeLowercase{ush}TASEP'] Let $S_{n}:=X_{1}+\dots+X_{n}$, $n\ge 0$, $S_{0}=0$ denote a random walk on $\mathbb{Z}$ where the increments $(X_{k})_{k\ge 1}$ are i.i.d., mean zero, finite variance, and integer-valued. Furthermore, assume   $\mathbb{P}(X_{1}\ge -1)=1$ (downward skip-free) and $\mathbb{P}(X_{1}=-1)>0$. Let $M_{n}:=\min_{0 \le k \le n} S_{k}$ 
