{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:13:18.503356+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f14fd9755ffa0d1df1a426197275b796d17fcd25649f78de116d975a3919c382","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 26 of arXiv:2608.30578, 'Compactly Supported Solutions near a Nehari Critical Value'] Let $D\subset\mathbb R^N$ be a bounded Lipschitz domain and let
$F:D\times(0,+\infty)\to\mathbb R$ be a Carath\'eodory function such that,
for a.e. $x\in D$, the map
\begin{equation}
	s\mapsto\frac{F(x,s)}{s}

\end{equation}
is strictly decreasing on $(0,+\infty)$. Let
$U,V\in H^1(D)\cap L^\infty(D)$, with $U>0$, $V>0$ a.e. in $D$, and assume
the one-sided trace condition
\begin{equation}
	(U-V)^+\in H_0^1(D).

\end{equation}
Suppose that $U$ is a weak subsolution and $V$ a weak supersolution of
\begin{equation}
	-\Delta w=F(x,w)
	\qquad\hbox{in }D,

\end{equation}
that is,
\begin{align}
	\int_D\nabla U\cdot\nabla\varphi\,dx
	&\leq
	\int_DF(x,U)\varphi\,dx,
	\\
	\int_D\nabla V\cdot\nabla\varphi\,dx
	&\geq
	\int_DF(x,V)\varphi\,dx

\end{align}
for every non-negative
$\varphi\in H_0^1(D)\cap L^\infty(D)$ for which the right-hand sides are
finite. Assume, moreover, that
\begin{equation}
	F(\cdot,U),F(\cdot,V)\in L^1_{\rm loc}(D)

\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
	\left(
	\frac{|F(x,U)|}{U}
	+
	\frac{|F(x,V)|}{V}
	\right)
	(U^2-V^2)^+
	\in L^1(D).

\end{equation}
Then
\[
U\leq V
\qquad\hbox{a.e. in }D.
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.656918+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f15184056d249ae22727065d8fcb3180dab375ccbaa9e5b539dee7d748bfc348","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:mainSmallMu of arXiv:2608.24830, 'Motion helps the contact process: survival below\\ the percolation threshold on Poisson Br'] Fix $\mathfrak{b}$ and $\mathfrak{o}$. There are $C,c>0$, depending only on $\mathfrak{o},\mathfrak{b},r,d,\lambda$, such that
