{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:03:59.406825+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f20e9d52eecf5296036079e21bf21ade2f27d79082eda0f5e32e0b0a649af89b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:xhat->Bhat of arXiv:2507.08757, 'Strong existence and uniqueness of the tilt-indexed Busemann process in the planar corner '] Take ${\widehat B}\in\widehat{\mathcal{K}}_c$. Then for $\widehat\mathbb{P}$-almost every ${\widehat\omega}$ and all $u,x,y\in\mathbb{Z}^2$
