{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.677752+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f21abba5a36136e31495ee541022bf57de3a0fa33207713874f2c42ecdc01186","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition GaussianandLaguerre of arXiv:2411.12149, 'Airy limit for $\beta$-additions through Dunkl operators'] For $\beta>0$, an $N\times N$ \emph{Gaussian $\beta$-ensemble} is a probability measure on $N$-tuple $(\lambda_{1}\ge \ldots\ge \lambda_{N})\in \mathbb{R}^{N}$ with density function 
    \begin{equation}    
   \frac{1}{Z_{N,\beta}}\prod_{1\le i<j\le N}(\lambda_{i}-\lambda_{j})^{\beta}\prod_{i=1}^{N}\exp\left(-\frac{\lambda_{i}^{2}}{2N}\right),
    \end{equation}
    and an $N\times L$ \emph{Laguerre $\beta$-ensemble} ($N\le L)$ is a probability measure on $N$-tuple $(\lambda_{1}\ge \ldots\ge \lambda_{N})\in \mathbb{R}^{N}$ with density function
    \begin{equation}
       \frac{1}{Z_{N,L,\beta}}\prod_{i=1}^{N}\left[\lambda_{i}^{\frac{\beta}{2}(L-N+1)-1}\exp\left(-\frac{\beta\lambda_{i}}{2} \right)\right]\prod_{1\le i\le j\le N}(\lambda_{i}-\lambda_{j})^{\beta}.
    \end{equation}
    $Z_{N,\beta}$ and $Z_{N,L,\beta}$ are certain normalizing constants.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":["X_1, \dots, X_n independent","\mathbb{E}[X_k] = 0","\text{Var}(X_k) < \infty"],"created_at":"2026-10-07T19:28:52+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f21eac128e32f15dff92291064ed99e1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"Let X_1, \dots, X_n be independent random variables with \mathbb{E}[X_k] = 0 and \text{Var}(X_k) = \sigma_k^2 < \infty. Let S_k = \sum_{j=1}^k X_j. Then for every \epsilon > 0, \mathbb{P}\left( \max_{1 \le k \le n} |S_k| \ge \epsilon \right) \le \frac{1}{\epsilon^2} \sum_{k=1}^n \sigma_k^2 = \frac{\text{Var}(S_n)}{\epsilon^2}.

Preserved duplicate statement and commentary:
Let X_1, ..., X_n be independent random variables with E[X_i] = 0 and Var(X_i) < infinity for each i, and let S_k = X_1 + ... + X_k. Then for every lambda > 0, P(max_{1 <= k <= n} |S_k| >= lambda) <= Var(S_n) / lambda^2 = (sum_{i=1}^n Var(X_i)) / lambda^2. This strengthens Chebyshev's inequality applied to S_n alone into a bound on the whole running maximum. [Durrett, Probability: Theory and Examples]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:07:35.030415+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f22327a41881418128ea1a1ba8f57b1c34418c681e5789ee2409bd6fa0c133f9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Pro 28 of arXiv:2609.02879, 'On the cut locus of Hamilton--Jacobi equations I: structure and propagation via the touchi'] Let $H$ be a Tonelli Hamiltonian on $\T^n$ and $u$ be a viscosity solution of \eqref{eq:HJe}. Then there holds
\begin{align*}
	\reg(u)=\bigcup_{t>0}\{t\}\times\reg(u(t,\cdot))=\reg(u,H)\cap\big((0,\infty)\times\T^n\big),\\
	\cut(u)=\bigcup_{t>0}\{t\}\times\cut(u(t,\cdot))=\cut(u,H)\cap\big((0,\infty)\times\T^n\big).
\end{align*}
In other words,
\begin{align*}
	\partial_P u(t,x)\neq\varnothing \Longleftrightarrow \partial_P u(t,\cdot)(x)\neq\varnothing,\qquad \forall (t,x)\in(0,+\infty)\times\T^n.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.751510+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f225714e3cac8a5a5c7e1c2f491db71e3a3ded24b64937fab3d076a5a79e7ba9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:support-mass-witness of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] Assume the minimal Kahane--Peyri\`ere regime. Let \(\beta>A_{\mathrm{loc}}(W)\), let \(\Lambda\) be the block-count exponent from Lemma~(lem:biggins-chernoff-block-count-exponent of the paper), and let \(C\ge0\) be finite almost surely on \(\mathcal S_\circ\). Define
\begin{equation*}
E_{\beta,C}(\mu_\circ)
:=
\left\{
x\in\operatorname{spt}\mu_\circ:
\mu_\circ(\mathcal I_{n_k}(x))
\ge C(\omega)2^{-\beta n_k}
\text{ for some }n_k\uparrow\infty
\right\}.
\end{equation*}
Then, almost surely on \(\mathcal S_\circ\),
\begin{equation*}
\dim_{\mathrm H} E_{\beta,C}(\mu_\circ)
\ge
\Lambda(1-\beta)
>
0.
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:09:49.861277+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f22631eb5f1d77af5775964f3473e066c380556ed9a15a19a8c032e6f6c426f0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2609.03084, 'Convergence rates to traveling waves for an FKPP model with nonlinear advection'] Let $u$ be a solution to \eqref{main_eq} with the assumption \eqref{initial_data_assumption}.
        There exists an $N > 0$ so that for all $x \geq N$,
