{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.328297+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f22dbc0ce595385aabfb0a3c626317c6d2c83bd5fdce821f55acea4000ebf969","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Coro 8 of arXiv:2608.30357, 'Mean convergence for Banach space-valued random elements indexed in measure spaces'] Let $\{K_n : n \ge 1\} \subseteq \cK(\cX)$ and $p \in [1, \infty)$. Let $\{u_n, v_n : n \ge 1\} \subseteq \bZ\cup\{\pm \infty\}$ with $u_n < v_n$ for all $n\ge 1$ and let $\{a_{n, k} : k \in [u_n, v_n]\cap \bZ, n \ge 1\} \subset \bR$ satisfy 
	$$\sup_{n \ge 1} \sum_{k \in [u_n, v_n] \cap \bZ} |a_{n, k}| <\infty.$$
Assume that $\{X^n_k : k\in S_n, n \ge 1\}$ is $(\nu_n)$-$\CUI(p)$ w.r.t. $\{K_n\}$, where $S_n: = [u_n, v_n] \cap \bZ$, $\cS_n : = \cP(S_n)$, and $\nu_n : = \sum_{k \in S_n} |a_{n, k}| \delta_{k}$. If 
	\begin{align}
		\lim_{n \to \infty} \lt\|K_n\rt\| \sum_{k \in S_n} |a_{n, k}| = 0,
	\end{align}
then
\begin{align*}
	\lim_{n \to \infty} \mathbb{E} \, \BB\| \sum_{k \in S_n} a_{n, k} X^n_k \BB\|^p  = 0.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:33:12.354144+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f22e234eb51e986078628efc45dc9c06fc2557c90a367f78f85deca9f35803b4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 210 (quenched first moment bounds on $\tilde{Q}$ and $\tilde{Q}^\frozen$) of arXiv:2608.29416, 'Algorithmic threshold for high-dimensional projection pursuit I: general theory'] With $\tilde{Q}$ the approximation of $Q$ given by Definition~\ref{d:tQ}, we have the quenched bounds
    \begin{align*}
    &\max\bigg\{
    \frac{\bE\Delta\tilde{Q}^{\RomI}(q_d)}{(\delta_d)^2 p'(q_d)},
    \frac{\bE\Delta\tilde{Q}^{\RomII}(q_d)}{\delta_d p(q_d)}
    =\bE \vvv^\trunc(q_d), \\
    &\qquad\qquad\qquad
    \frac{\bE|\Delta\tilde{Q}^{\RomII,\RomIII}|}
    {\delta_d [p(q_d) q_d p'(q_d)]^{1/2}}
    =\bE |\uuu^\trunc(q_d)|,
    \frac{\bE\Delta\tilde{Q}^{\Ising}(q_d)}{\delta_d}
    =\bE \www^\trunc(q_d)
    \bigg\}
