{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.788240+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f25b11114fe142d57f56904c84e1e962df033c413aeaa44fc36b43ab9e983664","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem Lem6.2-replacement of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] Let $R_l, R_r$ be left and right halves of $R$. There exist $c_5, c_6$ (independent of $\beta$) such that for all $\beta>\beta_0$ and $\ell \ge \beta e^{2\beta}$, and $\sqrt{C \log \ell} \le\bar \alpha \le (1/s)\sqrt{\ell}$ for $C$ large independent of $\beta$,
