{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.609530+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f280019897dd2869775df8ee4b10f94a067234b54453df666587ff3ffe814869","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 12 of arXiv:2608.25772, 'Propagation of Chaos and Gaussian Fluctuations for Mean-field Coupled Maps'] There exists a constant $\Delta_1>0$, depending only on $\|h\|_{C^1}$, such that when $\Delta<\Delta_1$, the mapping $\Phi$ becomes a diffeomorphism on $\T^N$ and $\phi_{\mu}$ also becomes a diffeomorphism on $\T$ for any $\mu\in\mathcal{P}(\T)$. In this case, for any $\rho\in L^1(\T^N)\cap\mathcal{P}(\T^N)$ and $\bar{\rho}\in L^1(\T)\cap\mathcal{P}(\T)$, we have
