{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.352763+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2f372e7977cff3a0bf35d57bbecb44e152a9b60ca6a573ab7e2a93df6e07887","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L:abstract-convergence of arXiv:2604.10020, 'The directed landscape in half-space'] Let $f_n:\mathbb{H}^{2+}_\uparrow \to \mathbb{R} \cup \{-\infty\}$ be a sequence of functions satisfying (equation E:MC-lambda of the paper) which converge uniformly on compact sets to continuous limit $f:\mathbb{H}^{2+}_\uparrow \to \mathbb{R}$ which also satisfies (equation E:MC-lambda of the paper). Suppose that additionally $f$ satisfies the following shape bound: 
	\begin{itemize}
		\item For all $c_0 > 0$, there exists a constant $C > 0$ such that for all $u = (x, a, t; y, b; t + s) \in \mathbb{H}^{2+}_\uparrow$ with $s < c_0$ we have that
		$$
		\left|f(u) + \frac{(x-y)^2}{s} \right|\le C s^{1/3} \log^2\left(\frac{{2\|u\|_2}}{s}\right).
