{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.912368+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2fc0d5fb87f60e53236b0527ada3e2466ed0d1898083c78e5287c8adee451f5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop prop2 of arXiv:2411.00663, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of invariant capacities and applications'] Let $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},P,T)$  be an ergodic measure preserving system, where $(\Omega,\mathcal{F})$ is a standard measurable space. Then the following two statements are equivalent:
	\begin{longlist}
		\item there exists $B\in\mathcal{F}$ with $P(B)>0$ such that for any $C\in\mathcal{F}$ with $C\subset B$,
		\begin{equation}
			\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}P^{1/2}(B\cap T^{-i}C)=P^{1/2}(B)P(C);
		\end{equation}
		\item $P$ is a periodic probability, i.e., there exist $r\in\mathbb{N}$ and distinct points $\omega_1,\ldots,\omega_r\in\Omega$ such that $P(\{\omega_i\})=\frac{1}{r}$, $i=1,2,\ldots,r$.
	\end{longlist}
	In this case, $r=\frac{1}{P(B)}\in\mathbb{N}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.474252+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2ff0cc57bef64bffb525ec609fe5dc7fd4f89a11febb3d60088b5674c783f26","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:optimalliftgns of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] Let $\mathcal{M}$ be a finite-dimensional von Neumann algebra. For a symmetric QMS generator $\mathcal{L}_O$ satisfying the $\kappa$-intertwining condition for $\kappa \in \mathbb{R}$, there exists a second-order lift $\mathcal{L}$ with convergence rate:
