{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:42:55.314252+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f31873ff621aaae7544780bb7b57b6bac70aedf18cd4751926e0093251010a9a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 13 (Variational identity) of arXiv:2609.02398, '\textbf{Convex Order Comparisons for Sub-Gamma Random Variables}'] Let $a > 0$ and $c > 0$. Then $X \lecx c\Lap$ holds for every $X \in \SE(1,a)$ if and only if
