{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.768380+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f330cff6742acd8d4756ae1b54965c36d2fb368f51969745ffced5391149d067","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] Fix $T_1 \in \mathbb{N}$, $\vec{y} \in \mathfrak{W}_2$, $q \in (0,1)$, $c \in [0, q^{-1})$. Then, $W(\mathfrak{B};q,c) \geq 0$ for all $\mathfrak{B} = (B_1, B_2) \in \Omega_{\ice}(T_1, \vec{y})$, and also 
