{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:29:08.611792+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3323ee80c8018c1185f9450ab3c770be1ff7fe0c112dcb4438f203d79ed9b59","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-resample-infty-1 of arXiv:2411.19810, 'Radial conformal welding in Liouville quantum gravity'] For $(\phi, \eta)\sim M_W$, let $\tau$ be the time $\eta$ separates $i$ from $\infty$. Let $\tilde \mathcal{D}$ be the ordered collection of two-pointed quantum surfaces disconnected from $i$ by $\eta$ strictly before time $\tau$; the two marked points on each quantum surface are the last and first points hit by $\eta$, and the ordering is the reverse of the ordering induced by the times that these quantum surfaces are disconnected from $i$. Let $\mathcal{D}_2$ be the three-pointed quantum surface disconnected from $i$ by $\eta$ at time $\tau$; its marked points are $\eta(\tau)$,  the rightmost point of  $\eta\cap \mathbb{R}$, and $\infty$. Let $\mathcal{D}_1$ be the ordered collection of two-pointed quantum surfaces disconnected from $i$ after time $\tau$; the two marked points on each quantum surface are the two boundary points visited twice by $\eta$. Then the  law of $(\mathcal{D}_1, \mathcal{D}_2, \tilde \mathcal{D})$ is 
	    \begin{equation} 
	    (1-\frac2{\gamma^2}W)^2\int 1_{r_1+r_2+\tilde r > \ell_2} {\mathcal{M}}^\mathrm{disk}_{0,2}(W; r_1+r_2+\tilde r - \ell_2, r_1)  \times {\mathcal{M}}^\mathrm{disk}_{0,2, \bullet}(\gamma^2-W; \ell_2, \cdot,  r_2) \times {\mathcal{M}}^\mathrm{disk}_{0,2}(W;\cdot, \tilde r) ,
	    \end{equation}
	    where the integral is taken over $(\ell_2, r_1, r_2, \tilde r)$ with respect to Lebesgue measure on $(0,\infty)^4$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.900330+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3333c565bdc5ebd89defb0248ccfed23acdecb6995a2ab4b1ef98c053ac2710","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 32 (Central limit theorem for fixed filling fractions) of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Suppose that Assumptions~\ref{Assumptions_Theta}--\ref{Assumptions_analyticity} hold. In addition, assume that for each $h \in [H]$, $\mu_h$ has exactly one band and the equations \eqref{eq_equations_eqs} deterministically fix the filling fraction $\hat{n}_h$. Then, if $f(z)$ is a $\N$-independent holomorphic function of $z$ in a neighborhood of $\amsmathbb{A}$, the linear statistics
\begin{equation}

