{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.635227+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f34da1a945732aa1d1ae9720e81ac97551e23d95a5ac267e6362a006ffdf2723","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition cubsigdef of arXiv:2411.13707, 'High-degree cubature on Wiener space \\ through unshuffle expansions'] We say a discrete probability measure $Q=\sum_{j=1}^{n}
