{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.062287+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3bb5cd67a355199c9b030d37bbb228b2abeeb82cbfefff99090211d7578f7bc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:lem-4.6 of arXiv:2607.14993, 'Sharp phase transition for percolation with short-range dependencies'] Let $G = (V, E)$ be a finite graph containing $0$, and $\mu$ a monotonic measure on $\{0, 1\}^E$. Then, for any $n \in \mathbb N^*:=\{1,2,\ldots\}$, we have
