{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:21:28.818645+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3d1dd24f397a7fcbcf92b3992eb6207fb06ec7157ae2872da66a1bf47eec5d7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corr intro:RS larkin of arXiv:2605.05631, 'Wandering Exponents and the Free Energy of the High-Dimensional Elastic Polymer'] Fix the choice of $t$ and $\beta$, and consider ((eqn:Larkin equation of the paper)) as an equation in $\mu$.
