{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:53:30.663079+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3d1f0fc3e1c724271967b4198683e4e5e21f82f635f4016112b702701fabace","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn $L^r$-optimal quantization error of arXiv:2506.01746, '\bf Optimal Bregman quantization: existence and uniqueness of optimal quantizers revisited'] The  $L^r$-optimal mean quantization error for $P$ at level $n\ge 1$ is defined by 
