        C_{OT,\lambda,\mu}' \cdot \sqrt{\gamma} \exp\left(-\frac{\lambda }{p\gamma}\right), & $p \in [1, D_{5,\lambda,\mu}/\gamma]$\\
        D_{4,\lambda,\mu}' \cdot \frac{p\sqrt{\gamma}}{\log(1+\gamma p/\lambda)} & $p \in [D_{5,\lambda,\mu}/\gamma, \infty)$
    \end{subnumcases}
    Where $\delta \in(0,1/2-\alpha)$ is any small constant, and all constants independent of $p,\gamma$, with closed forms in (equation eq: D_4, lambda, mu SSQ of the paper), (equation eq: constants for Wasserstein-$p$ JSQ of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:15.481226+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3f5583b2e2e1481c744fad8978dbf571737a5c67df68f13aebab2b1d7107401","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 14 of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] There is a universal constant $C>0$,
