{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.782398+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f406f080473a2313b734f6239503a5ae1132c9df1b8554398c2f321ab5926175","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Coro cor:Feller of arXiv:2411.19543, 'Feller property and convergence for semigroups of time-changed processes'] Let $\Omega$ be a bounded Lipschitz domain of $\mathbb{R}^d$ with boundary $F$ and $\mu$ the $(d-1)$-dimensional Hausdorff measure of $F$. Consider the second order elliptic operator $\mathscr{L}^V:= -\sum_{l,k=1}^d \partial_l(c_{kl}\partial_k) + V$, where $c_{kl}=c_{lk}:\Omega\to\mathbb{R}$ are real valued bounded smooth functions satisfying the uniform ellipticity condition
\begin{align*}
	C^{-1}|\xi|^2\leq\sum_{k,l=1}^dc_{k,l}(x)\xi_k\xi_l\leq C|\xi|^2,\quad \xi\in\mathbb{R}^d
\end{align*}
for some $C>0$
and $V:\Omega\to\mathbb{R}$ is a real valued bounded non-negative measurable function. Assume further that the operator induced by $\mathscr{L}^V$ in $L^2(\Omega):=L^2(\Omega,dx)$ with Dirichlet boundary condition, say $L_D^V$, is injective. Let  $S_t^V$ be the semigroup of the Dirichlet-to-Neumann operator on $L^2(F):=L^2(F,\mu)$ related to $\mathscr{L}^V$ (see [Ouhabaz] and references therein). Then $S_t^V$ maps $C(F)$ into itself and 
$S_t^V|_{C(F)}:C(F)\to C(F)$ has Feller property.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:26:26.775511+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4092bdf1fa3823e5dafeaf56c38774b7bff5f75e22b998ff7e5a52b0e30de0b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:FP-seed-linear of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] The seed functions $\psi_{t,x,a}$ and $\phi_{t,x,a}$
