{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.231068+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4aa664519776fa32340a2c970c77f9efe8176a51cc36fd0bca83e72df1fcae8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 24 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] For the \textbf{TASEP height function} $(\hTASEP(\lambda;y,t))_{y\in \Z,t\geq 0}$, assume that $(0,0) \in \lambda$ for a fixed down-right path $\lambda \in \Lambda$. For all $t\geq 0$, consider the down-right path
\begin{equation}
\lambda_t= (z^{t}_i)_{i \in \Z} := \{ w \in \Z^2 \, \colon \,  T_{\lambda,w} \leq t < T_{\lambda,w+(1,1)} \} 
\end{equation} such that $z^{t}_{0}=(x_t,x_t)$ for some $x_t \in \Z$. For $y \in \Z$ and $t > 0$, set $h_t(0)=x_t$ and recursively
\begin{equation}
h_t(i) - h_t(i-1) = \begin{cases} -1 & \text{ if } z^{t}_i-z^{t}_{i-1} = \eone , \\
 0 & \text{ if } z^{t}_i-z^{t}_{i-1} = -\etwo . 
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
 The \textbf{periodic TASEP height function} $\hpTASEP$ is defined as in \eqref{eq:CornerExtremalBasic} and \eqref{eq:CornerExtremalBasic2}, with respect to the periodic last passage times $\Tper$ from Definition~\ref{def:LastPassageTimes} and a down-right path $\lambda^{\per}_N \in \Lambda_{N,k}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:53:10.211653+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4ae21a8ecd3d0d9ac90a054571e45c01d05750ebd0cf0f50406fff1136c9afe","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem convex-opt of arXiv:2608.29018, 'Sharp Restricted Isometry Thresholds for\\ Global Minima of Rank-Restricted Matrix LASSO'] For $X\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}\times d_{2}}$, let $X=U\Sigma V^{T}$
denote its compact SVD. Suppose there exists $W$ such that 
