{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.679197+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4e276ecff944a6802dd0a0feacd8690e2b3ec18b435d20efb0c06497543e332","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 23 of arXiv:2609.02699, '\vspace{-0.5 cm}Gauge theory and symplectic structures'] There exists a constant $C>0$ such that if $(\phi=\phi^0+\phi^{0,2},A,\beta)$ solves the equations \eqref{Dirac 6d}, \eqref{Curvature 6d} on an almost K\"ahler $3$-fold $(M,g,J)$, then we have
