{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.815894+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f50ccea0bd557d0520c4e5e019bdcebb788e191a6741ede0493987b0fb2af998","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:seq_grow of arXiv:2607.16911, 'Multipartite random graphs with given degrees: local limit, revisiting the giant, distance'] Consider the sequences $(\underline{a}_i)_{i \geq 0}, (\Bar{a}_i)_{i \geq 0},$ as defined in (equation eq:inductive_def_seq_a of the paper) and $ (\underline{b}_i)_{i \geq 0}, (\Bar{b}_i)_{i \geq 0}$ as defined in (equation eq:inductive_def_seq_b of the paper). Then for all $i \geq 1$, there are universal constants $A,B>1$ such that
