{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.341081+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f53e0319f72d226f2a0fe2638a3d57f713e27947892af537a8d58efe79c55745","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:solution of arXiv:2412.01381, 'Ergodicity and mixing for locally monotone stochastic evolution equations'] An $H$-valued continuous $({\mathcal F}_t)_{t\in [0,T]}$-adapted process $(X_t)_{t\in [0,T]}$ is called a \emph{solution} to~(equation eq:model of the paper) if for its $\mathrm{d} t\otimes\mathbb{P}$-equivalence class $\widehat{X}$, we have
\begin{enumerate}
\item For some $\tilde{\alpha}>1$, $\widehat{X}\in L^{\tilde{\alpha}}([0,T];V)\cap L^2([0,T];H)$, $\mathbb{P}$-a.s.
\item For any $V$-valued $({\mathcal F}_t)_{t\in [0,T]}$-progressively measurable $\mathrm{d} t\otimes \mathbb{P}$-version $\overline{X}$ of $\widehat{X}$ it holds that
\begin{equation*}
X_t=x+\int_0^t A(\overline{X}_s)\,\mathrm{d} s+B \,W_t,\quad t\in [0,T],\quad\mathbb{P}\text{-a.s.}
\end{equation*}
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:51:11.952477+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5415fd2caad5db002ec2c28ee0e0f10df2f3da718111f18b8bb72f511f9e080","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 of arXiv:2608.07365, 'A pathwise Ito formula \\for weakly differentiable functions'] Let $\omega \in C^0([0,T], \Rr^d)\cap Q^\pi([0, T], \mathbb{R}^d)$ satisfying \eqref{2eq:oscassump}. For any $f\in C^1_b(\mathbb{R}^d, \Rr^d)$ the limit
\begin{align*}
 [ f(\omega), \omega]_{\pi}(t):=\lim_{n\to\infty}\sum_{k=0}^{m(n)-1} \left( f(\omega(t^n_{k+1}\wedge t)) - f(\omega(t^n_k\wedge t))\right)\cdot
  \left(\omega(t^n_{k+1}\wedge t)  - \omega(t^n_k\wedge t)\right)
\end{align*}
exists, and is equal to the Riemann–Stieltjes integral
\[
\int_0^t \langle \nabla f(\omega(u)),\, d[\omega]_{\pi}(u)\rangle.
\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:43:19.041394+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f541d2ecc908877f0e4d19f934becfc031e7acbeef13fe719bdfe88800e36a2a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm thm-V of arXiv:2609.02552, 'Resolvent Estimates for the Stokes Operator \\ in a Three-Dimensional Lipschitz Domain'] Let  $\Omega$ be a bounded Lipschitz  domain in $\mathbb{R}^3$.
Let $\lambda\in \Sigma_\theta$ and $3<q<3+\varepsilon$, where $\varepsilon=\varepsilon(\Omega)>0$ 
is sufficiently small. 
Let $(u, \phi ) \in W_0^{1, q} (\Omega; \mathbb{C}^d) \times L^q(\Omega; \mathbb{C}) $ be a weak solution of
\begin{equation}
\left\{
\aligned
-\Delta u +\nabla p +\lambda u & = F &\quad & \text{ in } \Omega,\\
\text{\rm div} (u) & =0 & \quad & \text{ in } \Omega,\\
u& = 0& \quad & \text{ on } \partial\Omega,
\endaligned
\right.
\end{equation}
where  $F\in L^\infty(\Omega; \mathbb{C}^3)$. Let $t=|\lambda|^{-1/2}$ and $N\ge 4$. Then
\begin{equation}
\aligned
  |\lambda| \| u \|_{L^\infty(\Omega)}
 & \le C  N^{20} \| F \|_{L^\infty(\Omega)}  
+ C N^{\frac{3}{q}-1}
 |\lambda| \| u \|_{L^\infty(\Omega)}\\
& + C N^{\frac{3}{q}-1}
|\lambda|^{\frac12}
\sup_{\substack{ t< r< r_0\\ B(x, 2r ) \subset \Omega}}
\inf_{\substack {\beta \in \mathbb{C} }}
\left(\fint_{B(x, r ) } | \phi  -\beta|^q \right)^{1/q}\\
&+ C N^{\frac{3}{q}-1}
|\lambda|^{\frac12}
\sup_{\substack{ x_0\in \partial \Omega \\ t< r< r_0 } }
\inf_{\substack {\beta \in \mathbb{C} }}
\left\{
\left(\fint_{B(x_0, r )\cap \Omega } | \phi  -\beta|^q \right)^{1/q}
+ \left(\fint_{B(x_0, r  )\cap \partial\Omega}
|\phi  -\beta|^p \right)^{1/p} \right\},
\endaligned
\end{equation}
where $\frac{2}{p}=\frac{3}{q}$ and $C$ depends only on $\theta$ and $\Omega$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.124886+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f54b082b81a6245507d19f3b3f80e113f7511190a0e6982a0c165b8121eeb672","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:mainth2d of arXiv:2510.00748, '\bf On irreducible central limit theorems'] Fix any $\beta \in (\frac{1}{2},1]$. Then
