    converges in distribution as $\delta \to 0$ to a random variable $\mathcal{Z}_{D}^{\xi,W,\lambda}$ with Wiener chaos expansion
    \begin{equation} 
        \mathcal{Z}_{D}^{\xi,W,\lambda} = 1+ \sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{C_{\sigma}^n}{n!}\int_{D^n} f_{D}^{(\xi,n)}(z_1,\dots,z_n) \prod_{j=1}^{n} \lambda(z_j)W(dz_j)
    \end{equation}
    where $W(\cdot)$ denotes white noise on $\mathbb{R}^2$ and where the functions $(f_{D}^{(\xi,n)})_n$ are as in Theorem (theorem_spin_correlations of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

