{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.335334+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5984ed62f55f07b07354332dc08ae6ceb4ccd6acd2e204f8b359f40edc6c61a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2608.30409, 'Gradient estimates and volume doubling for locally finite weighted graphs with $CD\psi(n,-'] Let $G=(V,E)$ be a locally finite weighted graph and let $\psi\in C^{1}(0,+\infty)$ be a concave function with $\psi^\prime \left(1\right)>0$ and $H_{\psi}<\infty$.  Assume that $u:V\times[T_{1},T_{2}]\rightarrow(0,+\infty)$ satisfies
