{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.284835+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5ad70c099a4d12ec70512e44af6fce787ad0c0d9f3c1b92f38d5ba6cb7482a3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop thm:smc-transition of arXiv:2604.20629, 'Rates of forgetting for the sequentially Markov coalescent'] Let $P_{\ell}(x,dy)$ denote the transition
kernel of the SMC process. Then 
\begin{equation}
P_{\ell}(x,dy)=e^{-\ell x} \delta_{x}(dy)+p_{\ell}(x,y) dy,
\end{equation}
where the density $p_{\ell}(x,y)$ is 
\begin{equation}
p_{\ell}(x,y)=\begin{cases}
