\end{cases}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.895613+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5b10f5acca25fee3a592ab130c768a7b190a8769edd980d738f8854ca2ef7bc","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn of arXiv:2411.11408, 'Multidimensional specific relative entropy between continuous martingales'] Let $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and $\mathbb{P},\mathbb{Q} \in \mathcal{M}_1(\mathcal{C})$ martingale measures such that $\mathbb{Q}|_{\mathcal{F}^n}\ll \mathbb{P}|_{\mathcal{F}^n}$. 
We denote the Radon-Nikodym density of $\mathbb{Q}|_{\mathcal{F}^n}$ with respect to $\mathbb{P}|_{\mathcal{F}^n}$ on $(\mathcal{C},\mathcal{F}^n)$ as $\frac{d\mathbb{Q}}{d\mathbb{P}}|_{\mathcal{F}^n}$ and define: 
\begin{equation*} \begin{split}
H(\mathbb{Q}|\mathbb{P})|_{\mathcal{F}^n}:=\begin{cases}
    \int _{\mathcal{C}} \log \frac{d\mathbb{Q}}{d\mathbb{P}}|_{\mathcal{F}^n}d\mathbb{Q} \, \text{ if } \, \mathbb{Q}|_{\mathcal{F}^n} \ll \mathbb{P}|_{\mathcal{F}^n} \\
    +\infty \, \text{ otherwise.}
\end{cases}
\end{split} \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:31.999035+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5b2b95e0f8195a21882518b5b6e4a0c381c5b080a72264c38327ac40a25fecb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 12 of arXiv:2512.02661, 'Worst-case mixing estimates for Brownian motion with semipermeable barriers'] There exist absolute constants $\delta_0,\gamma,c>0$ such that the following holds for every $\delta \leq \delta_0$.
