{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.828629+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5bb7762a19b87d55f589bf3f6c2570782798f0d41a78d349fcb8da7d2a9621b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:hoffman-exact of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] Let $z_1,\ldots,z_n\in\mathbb{R}^d$ be increments and let $X^{\rm PL}$ be the piecewise-linear path that traverses the increment $z_a$ on the $a$-th segment. Then
