{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:22:08.368069+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5c7701a7fc54e0bf57912332b56f04bcd607386eed6c87854ef52d5e7ca3fd7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm coupling of arXiv:2607.28817, 'Limiting spectral distribution for the adjacency matrix of the Watts--Strogatz random grap'] With the same notation as in Theorem~(thm:mainresult of the paper), define the distributions on $Z_n$ and $U_n$ as follows:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $Z_n$ is an $n\times n$ symmetric random matrix whose upper-triangular entries are independent, and for every $i \le j$,
    \[
        (Z_n)_{ij} =
        \begin{cases}
            \bernoulli(1 - p_n) & \mbox{if }\quad 0 < \min\big(|i-j|,\, n - |i-j|\big) \le \frac{K_n}{2}, \\
            0 & \mbox{otherwise.}
        \end{cases}
    \]

    \item $U_n$ is the adjacency matrix of an Erd\H{o}s--R\'enyi random graph of size $n$ with parameter $\frac{p_n K_n}{n}$, independent of $Z_n$. In other words, $U_n$ is an $n\times n$ symmetric random matrix independent of $Z_n$ and whose upper-triangular entries are independent and satisfy, for every $i \le j$,
    \[
        (U_n)_{ij} =
        \begin{cases}
            \bernoulli\left(\frac{p_nK_n}{n}\right) & \mbox{if }\quad i < j, \\
            0 & \mbox{if } i = j.
        \end{cases}
    \]
\end{enumerate}
Let $A_n$ denote the adjacency matrix of $WS_n(K_n, p_n)$. 
Then, under the same assumptions as in Theorem~(thm:mainresult of the paper), namely~(equation eq:assumption1 of the paper) and~(equation eq:assumption2 of the paper), there is a coupling of $A_n$ and $(Z_n, U_n)$ so that $Z_n$ and $U_n$ are independent and
\begin{equation} 
    \mu_{\frac{A_n}{\sqrt{p_nK_n}}} - \mu_{\frac{Z_n}{\sqrt{p_nK_n}} + \frac{U_n}{\sqrt{p_nK_n}}}\;\xrightarrow[n\to\infty]{}\; 0\qquad\mbox{ weakly in probability}. 
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.744463+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5d0f59aa61730e34dcf4ed3d72297651db3ca5bb6749dd3d283853813574553","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn of arXiv:2605.06429, '\large \bf $\mathsf{GL}_N(\mathbb{C})$ BROWNIAN MOTION AND STOCHASTIC PDE ON ENTIRE FUNCTI'] For $\mathfrak{s}>-1/2$ and $\nu>-1$ define the Hua-Pickrell $\mathbb{HP}_\mathfrak{s}$ and Bessel $\mathbb{B}_\nu$ stochastic zeta functions by:
