    \mathbb{B}_{\nu}(z)=\prod_{\mathrm{x}\in \mathcal{IB}_{\nu}}(1-z\mathrm{x}), \ \ \forall z \in \mathbb{C}.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:36:23.124713+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5d30f44cf3e5167523cbb2ead31b2d3bd0bc453c4eee19a9d5069db45c19800","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm GenLineInt of arXiv:2506.18207, 'Cartan's Path Development, the Logarithmic Signature and a Conjecture of Lyons-Sidorova'] Under the assumptions of Theorem (thm:LineInt of the paper),
