{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:20:07.901930+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f64ddbcbf44aa2167fc924fb033c783f8b604c88bb0dff489e544d85997dc642","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma quadratictermlocal of arXiv:2608.23765, '\texorpdfstring{Tight Majorizations and Convergence Rates\\ of Nuclear Norm Minimization I'] Assume that the linear measurement operator $\mathcal{A}: \mathbb{R}^{d_1 \times d_2} \rightarrow \mathbb{R}^m$ satisfies the NSP of order $r$ with constant $ \eta_r \le  3/5 $, and that for some $\mathbf{X}_\star$ of rank $r$, it holds that
 $ \mathcal{A}(\mathbf{X}) = \mathcal{A} (\mathbf{X}_\star) $ for some $ \mathbf{X} \in \mathbb{R}^{d_1 \times d_2}$. Assume that the weight operator $\W{\mathbf{X}}{\varepsilon}$ is a $q$-power mean weight operator (eq:power:mean:core:matrix of the paper) with $q \in [-1,0)$\footnote{This includes the harmonic-mean weight operator as special case with $q = -1$.}, that
\begin{equation}
	\nucnorm{\mathbf{X} - \mathbf{X}_\star} 
	\le 
	\frac{ \sigma_r \left( \mathbf{X}_\star \right) }{ \max \left( \eta_1 \sqrt{ d}, 2 \right)  },  
\end{equation}
where $0 < \eta_1 \leq \eta_r$ denotes again the order-one NSP constant of $\mathcal{A}$, and that
\begin{equation*}
\varepsilon \ge \vartheta \frac{\besterrNuc{\mathbf{X}}{r} }{d}
\end{equation*}
for some $\vartheta>0$.
Then for the constant $D_{\eta_r} = \frac{3+\eta_r}{1-\eta_r}$, it holds that 
\begin{equation*}
	\innerproduct{ \mathbf{X}_\star-  \mathbf{X} , \W{\mathbf{X}}{\varepsilon} (\mathbf{X}_\star-  \mathbf{X} ) }
	\le 
	\left(2 + 2^{-1/q}+\frac{D_{\eta_r}^2}{\vartheta}\right)  \nucnorm{\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{X}_\star}.
\end{equation*}
If $\vartheta = \frac{1-\eta_r}{(1+\eta_r)\left(\frac{3}{2}+\eta_r\right)}$, the bound reduces to
\begin{equation} 
	\innerproduct{ \mathbf{X}_\star-  \mathbf{X} , \W{\mathbf{X}}{\varepsilon} ( \mathbf{X}_\star-  \mathbf{X} ) }
	\le 
	\left(2 + 2^{-1/q}+E_{\eta_r}\right)  \nucnorm{\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{X}_\star}.
\end{equation}
with $E_{\eta_r} := \frac{(3+\eta_r)^2 (1+\eta_r)\left(\frac{3}{2}+\eta_r\right)}{(1-\eta_r)^3}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

