{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.490311+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f65585ee3c84bad0988b4cc2326e51f0124d0a88fd9155d4534a4146e360bf9f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 220 (Functions of the second kind, type II and III) of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] For each $g \in [H]$, let $\gamma(\alpha_g)$ (respectively $\gamma(\beta_g)$) be a small positively oriented circular loop around $\alpha_g$ (respectively $\beta_g$). If $f_g(z)$ is a meromorphic function in a complex neighborhood $\amsmathbb{M}_g$ of $[\alpha_g,\beta_g]$ with possible poles only at $\alpha_g,\beta_g$, then we define for any $h \in [H]$
