{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:11.640851+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f67ef41b67dc7d8e26e901a4f5e7d798afdf3268b25172d8de52305f87594e41","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2605.31374, 'Multi-point functions of a full-plane two-state\\ fuzzy $4$-Potts model'] For every $n\in 2\N$ and distinct points $(x_1,\cdots,x_n)\in(\R^2)^n$, we have
