{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.353340+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f691514c362bc279f0d50cb5e432f09940677b83492e41baa15cb01d8d36acb3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem.follmer of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] Fix $t_0 \in [0,1)$, $p \geq 2$, and $f \in \mathcal{A}_p^{\mathrm{F}}(t_0)$.
Define $v$ by (equation def.v of the paper). Then, the SDE
\begin{align*}
    dX^f(t) = \partial_x v(t,X^f(t))\,dt + dB(t), \quad t_0 \leq t \leq 1, \quad X^f(t_0) = 0,
\end{align*}
has a unique strong solution, which satisfies $X^f(1) \sim f \, d\gamma_{1- t_0}$. In particular,
\begin{align} 
     \|X^f(1)\|_{\infty} = [f]_{\infty}.
\end{align}
Moreover, the drift
\begin{align} 
    \alpha^f(t) \coloneqq \partial_x v(t,X^f(t)), \qquad t_0 \leq t \leq 1,
\end{align}
is a mean-zero martingale such that
\begin{align} 
    \|\alpha^f(t)\|_p \leq \frac{c_0}{2}, \qquad t_0 \leq t \leq 1.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

