{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.121673+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f6b4ce3c89760709a09be5c571a9bd16fb96bc4338894e4429766c1429eafe97","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 12 of arXiv:2608.27433, 'Scalar curvature on K\"ahler blow-ups and systolic inequalities'] For all sufficiently small $\eps$, the operator
\[
  \widetilde{\mathcal P}_\eps:
  C^{4,\alpha}_\delta(\widetilde X)\longrightarrow
  C^{0,\alpha}_{\delta-4}(\widetilde X)
\]
is an isomorphism in the following cases:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\roman*)}]
\item if $k>2$ and $4-2k<\delta<0$, then
\begin{equation}
  \norm{\phi}_{C^{4,\alpha}_\delta}
  \le C\norm{\widetilde{\mathcal P}_\eps\phi}_{C^{0,\alpha}_{\delta-4}};
