{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.629495+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f70dd960efba586de3a8982fd21e0e6897d4b22c059f4fc1f2c610da991198e9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem_drift_como_conv of arXiv:2411.03609, 'Asymptotically optimal Wasserstein couplings for the small-time stable domain of attractio'] \noindent\normalfont{(a)} Let $\alpha \in (1,2)$, and $p,\delta>0$ where $p\ne\alpha-1$ and $\delta\ne(\alpha-1)/\alpha$. Then, under Assumptions~(\nameref{asm:S}) \& (\nameref{asm:C}), we have, as $t \downarrow 0$,
