{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.615901+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7265c90ec58f57f73fb503800b0df623e9db9d12fcda2416b991d89384775d9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] Recall the definition of $a_n(t)$ from \eqref{E:1.24a}. There exist~$c,\tilde c >0$ such that
