{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:59:45.562443+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7330fe27a7e6de802e25a78c3402229ae3d3b298ae9f1a3bbff37fbb0af0975","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eq: R X X lambda Z of arXiv:2411.17109, 'On the maximal correlation of some stochastic processes'] Let $X$ and $Z$ be independent copies of $\alpha$-stable random variables with $0<\alpha\leq 2$. Then for all $\lambda\geq 0$, we have
