{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:36:23.138082+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7598cfc38a1f9f297f8ce6e837e04fbe10c048c2327e1a444e728527c6793db","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:averagecase of arXiv:2507.01236, 'Disintegration theorem for multifunctions, \\ with applications to empirical Wasserstein d'] Let $(\mathfrak{X},d,\mu)$ be a metric Polish probability space. Given $n\in\mathbb{N}$, $\epsilon > 0$ and $r>0$, we say that $(\mathfrak{X},d,\mu)$ is \emph{$(n,\epsilon,r)$-average-case approximable} if, whenever $X_1,\dots,X_n$ are i.i.d.\ with distribution $\mu$ on a probability space $(\Psi,\mathcal{F},\mathbb{P})$, there is an event of $\mathbb{P}$-probability at least $1-\epsilon$ on which one has
    \[
    \bigg|\int\!f(x)\,\mu(dx) - \frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^nf(X_i)\bigg|\leq r\cdot\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^n\|f\|_{\text{Lip},B(X_i,r)}
    \]
    for all Lipschitz functions $f:\mathfrak{X}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}$. Given $\epsilon,r:\mathbb{N}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}_{\geq0}$ which vanish as $n\rightarrow\infty$, we say that $(\mathfrak{X},d,\mu)$ is \emph{asymptotically average-case approximable with rate $(\epsilon,r)$} if, for all $n$ sufficiently large, $(\mathfrak{X},d,\mu)$ is $(n,\epsilon(n),r(n))$-average-case approximable.","status":"unverified"}

