{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.573172+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f77b9c850a227fdb318fc301473cef1c910a844d4b48c2877cfce4814ec916cb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 24 (Tree-graph inequality) of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $G=(V,E)$ be a subgraph of $\mathbb Z^d$ and $\beta\geq 0$. Then, for every $x,y,z\in V$,
