{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:37:14.981446+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7a6784cd565ea9c03586a0174d63dfacc53b82a86ef61d510c370f55b27054b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2607.11756, 'Full replica symmetry breaking in the Sherrington--Kirkpatrick model'] Fix \(R<\infty\).  There exist smooth functions \(c_2,c_3\) on
\([0,R]\) and a function \(\mathcal R_{\mathrm{end}}\) such that, with
\(\delta=1-B\),
\begin{equation}
 C(r,B)
 =2\delta+c_2(r)\delta^2+c_3(r)\delta^3+\mathcal R_{\mathrm{end}}(r,B)
\end{equation}
for \(0\le r\le R\) and \(B\) sufficiently close to \(1\).  Moreover,
