{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:31:49.910751+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7b5f8a2cd44984f3b65df6708e1fefca5d22e970fb092e90b72951da0456b2c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:conditional-TW of arXiv:2608.26745, 'Moderate Deviations for the Largest Eigenvalue of a Randomly Deformed Gaussian Unitary Ens'] There exist constants $c,C,c_*>0$ such that, whenever
$L\ge1$ and $L^3\le c_*\log N$,
\begin{equation}
 \sup_{\mathbf x\in\mathcal G_N}\sup_{{t\ge-L}}
 |\mathcal H_N(t;\mathbf x)-F_2(t)|
 \le CN^{-c}e^{CL^{3/2}}.
\end{equation}
Moreover, for every compact set $K\subset(0,\infty)$, the following two
estimates hold uniformly for $\mathbf x\in\mathcal G_N$ and $u\in K$:
\begin{align}
 \sup_{\mathbf x\in\mathcal G_N}\sup_{u\in K}
 \left|
 \log\mathbb P_{\mathbf x}(\chi_N>a_Nu)
 +\frac43(a_Nu)^{3/2}
 \right|
 =o(a_N^{3/2}),                                      \\
 \sup_{\mathbf x\in\mathcal G_N}\sup_{u\in K}
 \left|
 \log\mathbb P_{\mathbf x}(\chi_N\le-a_Nu)
 +\frac1{12}(a_Nu)^3
 \right|
 =o(a_N^3).                                          
\end{align}
In particular, evaluating a fixed version of the conditional probabilities at
$\mathbf x=\bm\xi$ gives the same deterministic bounds on $\mathcal G_N$.  By
(lem:good-event of the paper), the complement $\mathcal G_N^c$ is superexponentially
negligible at every speed used in (sec:phase-proof of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.364490+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7bbb05a0cd93f1b380ab19bf2ab261078c6a3b9897834150dbb71b78f5ae12a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:ftpbds of arXiv:2606.02472, 'Correlated uniform attachment trees'] Let $T_n\sim\mathrm{UA}(n)$ and fix constants  $0<s<\beta\leq 1$. Then for all $k=0,1,\ldots, n$, we have
