{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.889056+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f828198881cebaaf9ab2f98882e4793468e2c5b13176240406ef73feffd3c533","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 37 (Ergodicity of the Palm version) of arXiv:2504.02435, 'Poisson-Voronoi percolation in higher rank'] Let $G$ be a non-compact connected semisimple real Lie group and $(X,d_X)$ be its symmetric space. Let $\mathbf Y$ be a Poisson point process on $X$ with intensity $c \, {\rm vol}$ for some $c>0$ and with iid ${\rm Unif}[0,1]$-marks. Let $\mathbf Y_0=\mathbf Y \cup \{\mathbf o\}$, where $\mathbf o$ is equipped with an independent ${\rm Unif}[0,1]$-mark. Then the following hold:
\begin{itemize} 
\item[{\rm(1)}] Let $A$ be a $G$-invariant event and let $A_0$ be the restriction of $A$ to configurations containing the origin. Then $\mathbb P(\mathbf Y_0\in A_0)=\mathbb P(\mathbf Y\in A)\in \{0,1\}$.
\item[{\rm(2)}] Let $B_0$ be an event such that $B_0=B'$, where $B'$ is the restriction of the event $B:=GB_0$ to configurations that contain the origin.
Then $\mathbb P(\mathbf Y_0\in B_0)=\mathbb P(\mathbf Y\in B)$. In particular, $\mathbb P(\mathbf Y_0\in B_0)\in\{0,1\}$.
\end{itemize}
The same conclusions hold when $\mathbf Y$ is replaced with the unmarked Poisson point process $Y$ and $\mathbf Y_0$ is replaced with $Y_0=Y\cup\{o\}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:02:34.820150+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f82aa4df512a77a1264e9dc84faa5e768534cf83d10d0db06af556d5b963c15b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 (Thin boundary-layer volume) of arXiv:2607.19752, 'Weak Equilibrium Measures and Capacity--Hitting Identities\\ for the Hypoelliptic Third-Or'] Let $\Sigma\in\{\partial A,\partial B,\partial\calD\}$ and let
