{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:36:16.063077+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8734ab24bb42bf91ed6cf7ce0fd1f61b940aa43f2e8cf3f0af94b3b0a0136ca","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma BoltzB of arXiv:2606.28067, 'Ergodic approximation for the invariant distribution: An abstract framework for law-depend'] Suppose that (equation VL4 of the paper)--(equation VL5' of the paper) are in force. Moreover, suppose that Assumption~(ass:Boltz of the paper) holds and, for the even integer $p$ therein, set 
		$
		\kappa_{p}=2^{{p}-3}(p-1)(2Q_2+2^{p-1}Q_{p}).
		$	
		Let $X$ be $\mathcal{F}_s$-measurable with $\mathcal{L}(X)=\mu\in\mathcal{P}_p({\mathbb R}^d)$. Then for $t-s\leq 1$ and even integer $p$ one has
		\begin{equation}
			\begin{array}{rl}
				{\mathbb E}[ |\mathcal{X}_{s,t}(X,\mu)|^p]
				\leq &
				\displaystyle \Big(1-p\Big(\bar b_{p,\delta}-C(t-s)\Big)(t-s)\Big)\|\mu\|_p^p\\
				&+C(1+\|\mu\|_{p-2}^{p})(t-s),
			\end{array}
		\end{equation}

		where,  for $\delta>0$,  $ 
		\bar b_{p,\delta}:=	\bar{b}-\delta-\kappa_{p}$, 
		$C$ is a positive constant depending only on $p,b,\delta$ and $\|\mu\|_0:=1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.385775+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f87c4e4167078be5aab32a252fd4ba7b5262c7288d7aff16830a036942ff76fe","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem_new_c_star of arXiv:2411.02046, 'Speed of Convergence and Moderate Deviations of FPP on Random Geometric Graphs'] Under the assumptions of Theorem~(thm:speed.FPP of the paper), there exists~$C^* > 0$ such that almost surely, for every~$x \in \mathbb R^d$ with~$\|x\|$ large enough, we have
