where the pairing on the right hand side is the sum of the pairing on $\Ker(M_{k,k})$, and some symmetric pairing on $\Q_p^{n-k}$. The pairing on the left hand side is the pairing induced by $M_{n,n}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:28:08.661232+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8acdcb4a1bede531b134d6458d1a01713a0829623ed8b0463253eacd9a83f13","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 6 ($T^h$ and $h$-good) of arXiv:2607.29495, 'Fast Mixing for Low-Temperature Potts Models via Poisson Trees'] Let $T$ be a tree rooted at $r$, and $h,D>0$ be integers. Let $T^h$ be the subtree induced by the vertices of $T$ at depth $\leq h$. Moreover,
\begin{itemize}

\item All vertices at depth exactly~$h$ are $h$-good.
\item A vertex at depth less than $h$ is $h$-good if
it has at least~$D$  children that are $h$-good.
\end{itemize}
When   $T$ is fixed, we use
$ V^h_\mathrm{good}$ to denote the set of $h$-good vertices in~$V(T)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:48:24.316098+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8ad5521c3a4c051e5e128898510ec01d1ca80bf56f2c234d4b4200f23dc87f0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:rectangular Appell polynomials of arXiv:2605.31356, 'P\'olya--Schur problems and free probability'] Let $\{f_{n}\}\subset\mathcal{LPI}$ and satisfy Assumption (assump:main assumption of the paper). If $\beta\equiv\beta_n$ and $\frac{n}{n+\beta}\rightarrow \lambda\in (0,1]$, then \begin{equation}
