	\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.282666+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8af81b3a77c126757a172d93b0647ef0cc99cedfd1e3bcf4e1c75b41b775785","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2606.22656, 'Fluctuations of Point Vortex Ensembles\\ at Small Negative Inverse Temperature'] For every $\beta_*<8\pi$ there exists $C_{\beta_*}<\infty$ such that, for all $0\leq \beta\leq \beta_*$ and $2\leq n\leq N$,
