{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.513963+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8b993c702e0c9bc19028fda327c3c8c920f0d6dfdcb40bcf8af8feea844ddc4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop mb:mvsde of arXiv:2411.11759, 'Milstein-type schemes for McKean--Vlasov SDEs driven by Brownian motion and Poisson random'] If Assumptions \mbox{\normalfont  (asum:ic of the paper)} to  \mbox{\normalfont (asum:con of the paper)}   are satisfied, then there exists a unique solution of  the McKean--Vlasov SDE (equation eq:sde of the paper) as well as of its associated interacting particle system (equation eq:int of the paper). 
