{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.952916+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8d32dd4e61c0514c1344079a80a721d58015fbfa131bed38102d747e54c5f48","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 20 of arXiv:2604.05234, 'Quantitative propagation of chaos and universality for asymmetric Langevin spin glass dyna'] Let $\widehat X$ be a strong solution of \eqref{eq: fully regularized SDE}. Then $\widehat X\in \mathbb L^{1,2}$, and in particular for every $i=1,\dots,N$
