R\left(\sum_{i=1}^{m}\delta_{X_i},\sum_{j=\ell+1}^{n}\delta_{X_j}\right)=\frac{m-\ell}{\sqrt{m(n-\ell)}},
\end{equation}
where $\delta_{x}$ is the Dirac measure at $x$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.611890+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f90adac808e9ca6ee7503d79ea18d824aa8d2d2f8601025c7d468aa6c5f9b738","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor cor_bounded_st_times of arXiv:2606.23648, '\textsc{Optimal Stopping for a Diffusion with Unobserved Bernoulli Drift}'] Fix \(x\ge0\), and let \(y_x^*\) be as in Proposition (prop_stopping_for_large_y of the paper). In the fixed-\(x\) problem (equation 2d_value_func_def of the paper) with value $U_x(\cdot)$, it is enough to minimize over stopping times \(\tau\) satisfying
