{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.588999+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f91972e95fdae27967937f10873923a63366b1f2b3bed7568d169d7088e7cd64","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma-iteration-trick of arXiv:2608.30548, 'Finite speed of propagation and waiting time phenomena for stochastic porous media equatio'] Let $R>0$, $N,M\in \mathbb{N}$. Let $V,E, A, \left\{ U_i \right\}_{i=1}^N, \left\{F_j\right\}_{j=1}^M$ be non-negative, locally bounded functions defined on $[0,R)$ such that $A,F_j$ are non-increasing for all $j=1,\dots, M$. We assume that there exist $L_i,c_i, \tilde c, \ell_j\in [0,\infty)$, such that for any $s\ge 0$ and $\delta>0$ with $s+\delta \leq R$ we have  
    \begin{equation}

        \begin{split}
        V(s+\delta) + E(s+\delta)& \leq A(s) + \sum_{i=1}^N \left(\frac{2}{\delta}\right)^{L_i} U_i\left(s+\frac{\delta}{2}\right) \\
        & \leq A(s) + \varepsilon\sum_{i=1}^N c_i\left(\frac{4}{\delta}\right)^{L_i}U_i\left(s + \frac{\delta}{4} \right) + \varepsilon \, \tilde c \, E\left(s\right) + C_\varepsilon\sum_{j=1}^M \left( \frac{2}{\delta}\right)^{\ell_j} F_j(s),
        \end{split}
    \end{equation}for any $\varepsilon>0$ and a constant $C_\varepsilon<\infty$. Then, there exists a  constant $C^*\in (0,\infty)$ depending only on the preceding parameters, such that for any $s,\delta$:
    \begin{equation}

        V(s+\delta) \leq C^* \left(A(s) + \sum_{j=1}^M\delta^{-\ell_j} F_j(s)\right).
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.060039+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f91f47c371fd2f741538207a517ddc925f573fe1e4f690ace44fa8d805d480ca","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 (Banach-valued time lift) of arXiv:2606.16662, '2606.16662'] Let \(X(t,s)\), \(0\le s\le t\le T\), be a random field with values in a finite-dimensional Banach space \(B\).  Assume that for some \(A_N\), all \(p_0\ge2\), some \(\eta\in(0,1]\), and some \(\chi\ge0\),
\begin{align}
        \|\|X(t,s)\|_B\|_{L^{p_0}(\Omega)}&\le C_{p_0}A_N,\\
        \|\|X(t,s)-X(t',s')\|_B\|_{L^{p_0}(\Omega)}
        &\le C_{p_0}A_NN^{\chi\eta}
        (|t-t'|^\eta+|s-s'|^\eta),
\end{align}
whenever both pairs \((t,s)\) and \((t',s')\) lie in the Volterra simplex.  Then, for every fixed \(p\ge2\) and every \(\eps>0\), if \(\chi\eta<\eps/4\),
\begin{equation}
        \|\|X\|_{C_{t,s}B}\|_{L^p(\Omega)}
        \le C_{p,T,\eps}A_NN^\eps .
\end{equation}
The same statement holds for a separable Banach-valued modification.  In the application below \(B=\cL(\ell_q^2,\ell_n^2)\), a finite-dimensional matrix space; the continuous-time norm is obtained from rational time skeletons.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.462755+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f9241dd8921c5d7bf02a46288ce9f70cbfb8908b78e05f55bd647dcbd8c4e169","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 25 (Outgoing eikonal function and inverse foliation density) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] The \emph{outgoing eikonal function} $u$ is the solution of the following fully nonlinear hyperbolic initial value problem,
where $\gfour$ is the acoustical metric defined in \eqref{E:ACOUSTICALMETRIC}
and the PDE is known as the \emph{acoustic eikonal equation}:
\begin{align} 
\begin{cases}
(\gfour^{-1})^{\alpha \beta} \partial_{\alpha} u \partial_{\beta} u = 0, 
	\\
\p_t u > 0, 
	\\
u|_{\Sigma_0} = - x^1.
\end{cases}
\end{align}
We define the \emph{outgoing inverse foliation density} $\upmu$ by:
\begin{align} 
	\upmu 
	& 
	\eqdef 
	- 
	\frac{1}{(\gfour^{-1})^{\alpha \beta} \partial_{\alpha} t \partial_{\beta} u} > 0.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.574178+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f925ce43acf67f3ebc1d7c2c2f8c3151cd9602175ce5a382c0492ac84e34c08c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 46 of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:basic} and~\ref{ass:rand_ent}, suppose that $E_{+,0}$ is a regular right edge for $\Pi_0$ in the sense of Definition~\ref{def:reg_r_edge}. With high probability, $Y_0$ is $\eta_*$-regular around $\la_{1,0}$ in the sense of \cite[Definition~1]{ding2022edge} or \cite[Definition~1]{ding2022tracywidom}. More explicitly, there exist constants $c,C>0$ such that
        \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
                \item For $z=E+\ii\eta$ with \begin{align}
                        \la_{1,0}-c\leq E\leq\la_{1,0},\qquad \eta_*+\sqrt{\eta_*\abs{\la_{1,0}-E}}\leq\eta\leq10,  
                \end{align} 
                we have
                \begin{align}
                         \Im m_{0,N}(E+\ii\eta) & \sim\sqrt{\la_{1,0}-E+\eta},  
                \end{align}
                \item For $z=E+\ii\eta$ with \begin{align}
                        \la_{1,0}\leq E\leq\la_{1,0}+c,\qquad \eta_*\leq\eta\leq10, 
                \end{align}
                we have
                \begin{align}
                         \Im m_{0,N}(E+\ii\eta) & \sim\frac{\eta}{\sqrt{E-\la_{1,0}+\eta}}. 
                \end{align}
        \end{enumerate}
       Moreover, $\la_{1,0}\sim1$ and $\|W_0\|\leq C$ with high probability. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:08.850741+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f93070c4196c9fd8432accfe8810b3c801730ff87e06372b96c037002198e570","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2511.11189, 'Sharp asymptotics for the maximal distance from the boundary to the nucleus of a typical P'] When \(t \rightarrow \infty\),
