{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:49:05.413688+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f9ce7556b316d3259fd892dc2d7530ad988389aa8c24bf8bae72e626fbe77e5a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2601.07808, 'Supercritical long-range percolation on graphs of polynomial growth: the truncated one-arm'] \label[lemma]{lem:lattice_animal}
    Let $G$ be a transitive graph of polynomial growth with $d \geq 1$, and let $J : G \times G \to \mathbf{R}_+$ be transitive, and suppose that $J(x,y) = \Theta(d_G(x,y))^{-d \alpha}$ with $\alpha > 1$.

    The finite cluster of the origin $K$ has a unique block decomposition $\mathcal{B}(K)$, the block graph $\mathcal{H}(\mathcal{B}(K))$ is connected, and the block decomposition is $\mathcal{B}(K)$-isolated. 

    In particular,

    \begin{equation}
        \mathbf{P}_{\beta}
        \left(
            \#K <\infty 
        \right)
        \leq
        \sum_{\substack{
            b \in \mathbf{N},
            \mathbf{m} \in \mathbf{N}^{b}
            \\
            \mathbf{B} \in \mathcal{A}(b,\mathbf{m})
        }}
        \mathbf{P}_{\beta}
        \left(
            \mathcal{B}(K)
            =
            \mathbf{B},
            \mathcal{H}(\mathbf{B})
            \text{ is connected},
            \mathbf{B}
            \text{ is }
            \mathcal{B}(K)
            \text{-isolated}
        \right).
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:48:25.143147+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f9cef7f65ebbfaba43e66d35ef5cfd0a7d33be621da4950ef7e86057ae3b13cb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:constant-overshoot of arXiv:2607.04620, 'The Exact Ville Identity\\ \large From the Absorbing Case to the General Law\\ with an App'] Suppose there is a constant $\omega\ge0$ such that, on $\{T_b<\infty\}$, the conditional landing value obeys
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb{E}[M_{T_b}\mid \mathcal{F}_{T_b-1},T_b=n]\le b+\omega
  \quad\text{a.s., for every }n.

\end{equation}
Then $O_b\le\omega$ and $\mathbb{P}(T_b<\infty)\ge(1-D_b-R_b)/(b+\omega)$, with equality throughout when (equation eq:landing-bound of the paper) holds with equality. In particular, if the conditional overshoot is a level-independent constant $\omega$, then $O_b=\omega$ and $\mathbb{P}(T_b<\infty)=(1-D_b-R_b)/(b+\omega)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:35:10.793596+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f9d1f38beef83aff10519c3fa19aa53b55fdb4f4136d17e6e293a7807c907bc8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 27 of arXiv:2604.00635, 'Large deviations of the periodic Toda chain'] Let $V$ satisfy \ref{potentialh1} and \ref{potentialh2} and fix $\gamma > 0$.

Then there is a constant $C >0$ (which may depend on $\gamma$) such that, for $N$ sufficiently large, the upper bound holds

\begin{align}

\mc{I}(\bs{\la}^+_N ; \veps_N) \leq \mathrm{e}^{CN^{1- \frac{1}{4}}} \sqrt{\frac{ \mc{T}(\boldsymbol{\lambda}^+_N) \mc{T}(\boldsymbol{\lambda}^-_N)}{\Delta(\boldsymbol{\lambda}_N^+) \Delta(\boldsymbol{\lambda}_N^-)} } \cdot  \prod_{j=1}^N \max\{ \ln |\lambda_j^+ - \lambda_j^-|^{-1}   , \gamma N \} \;.

\end{align}

Above, given $\boldsymbol{x}_N\in \mathbb R^{N}$ we agree upon:

\begin{align}
