{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:04:07.031667+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa637e7df505138d4919cf2e47b2285b2a2f90226d51763c896d2400e8b54f2c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:first-variation-contact of arXiv:2607.29330, 'Large deviations for the maximum of\\ the generalized TAP free energy'] The map $\zeta\mapsto V_\zeta(q,\mu)$ is strictly convex.  If $\kappa$ is a finite signed measure on $[q,1]$ with $\kappa([q,1])=0$, then
		\begin{equation}
			D_\zeta V_\zeta(q,\mu)[\kappa]
			=\frac12\int_q^1\xi''(r)
			\left(\mathbb{E}[(M_r^\mu)^2]-r\right)
			\kappa([0,r])\,\mathrm{d} r .
		\end{equation}
		Define the obstacle
		\begin{equation}
			H_\zeta^\mu(s)
			:=\frac12\int_s^1\xi''(r)
			\left(\mathbb{E}[(M_r^\mu)^2]-r\right)\,\mathrm{d} r,
			\qquad s\in[q,1].
		\end{equation}
		The unique minimizer $\zeta_\mu$ of $V_\zeta(q,\mu)$ over $\mathcal P([q,1])$ is characterized by
		\begin{equation}
			\mathrm{supp}(\zeta_\mu)
			\subset
			\operatorname*{argmin}_{s\in[q,1]}H_{\zeta_\mu}^\mu(s).
		\end{equation}
		Moreover, $\zeta_\mu(\{1\})=0$. At every interior contact point
		$s\in\mathrm{supp}(\zeta_\mu)\cap[q,1)$, and at $s=q$ by the law matching when
		$\int a^2\mu(\mathrm{d} a)=q$,
		\begin{equation}
			\mathbb{E}[(M_s^\mu)^2]=s .
		\end{equation}
		For $q=0$ and $\mu=\delta_0$, this reduces to the usual first-variation and contact equations for the Parisi functional $P_\zeta$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:06.326619+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa68cc8f45ca869caf729fc74ea99ec89f11275029b7598941f7c452d4b31cdb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 16 of arXiv:2607.06242, 'Exponential mixing and Freidlin--Wentzell large deviation principle for Markov cocycles'] Assume Assumption \ref{a.050201}. For $m$-a.e. $\sigma\in\Sigma$,
