{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.194904+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa9724b23e79e0633f98ce8ae08f53fe1a878a085e481ffdc8cdb4b2bcd5fecc","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 16 of arXiv:2510.22783, 'Universality of Cutoff for Riffle Shuffling'] For all $t \in [K]$, we let
        \begin{equation}
            \ileft^{(t)}=\inf\Big\{l \geq 0:\frac{n^{(t)}_l}{N} \geq \chi\Big\},\quad 
             \iright^{(t)}=\sup\Big\{l \leq k-1:\frac{n^{(t)}_l}{N} \geq \chi\Big\}
        \end{equation}
        be the first and last piles with at least $\chi N$ cards in the $t$-th shuffle.
        Note that $\ileft^{(t)} < \iright^{(t)}$ if and only if $t$ is a $\chi$-good shuffle, and that if no pile sizes are small for shuffle $t$ then $\ileft^{(t)}=0$ and $\iright^{(t)}=k-1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.291561+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa98244e68bce035a08605b149341145b19e34ce1645ae4d483b8a5b3398bb2d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:rwcre_kernel of arXiv:2603.22652, 'A cohesive account on the ergodic behaviours and scaling limits of Random Walks in Cooling'] Given a resampling map $\tau$ and an i.i.d. environment sequence
$\bar{\omega}\sim\mu^{{\mathbb {N}}}$, the \emph{random walk in cooling random
environment} (RWCRE) is the Markov chain $X=(X_n)_{n\in{\mathbb {N}}_0}$ on ${\mathbb {Z}}$
with transition kernel
\begin{equation}
P^{\bar{\omega},\tau}(X_{n+1}=x+e\mid X_n=x)=
\begin{cases}
\omega_{\ell_n}(x), & e=+1,\\
1-\omega_{\ell_n}(x), & e=-1,
\end{cases}
\quad x\in{\mathbb {Z}},\ n\in{\mathbb {N}}_0,
\end{equation}
where $\ell_n$ is given by (equation eq:ell_def of the paper). We denote by
$P_x^{\bar{\omega},\tau}$ the quenched law and by
\begin{equation}
P_x^{\mu,\tau}(\,\cdot\,):=\int_{[(0,1)^{{\mathbb {Z}}}]^{{\mathbb {N}}}}
P_x^{\bar{\omega},\tau}(\,\cdot\,)\,\mu^{{\mathbb {N}}}(d\bar{\omega})
\end{equation}
the corresponding annealed law.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:22:59.740361+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_faac10a39c5b7886f8b5f6fb68e1d3251060ca4a8d17ddd76748a5980504a7e4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem trim_twist of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] Let $\xi$ and $T$ be as above.
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item (Trim) There exists a positive contact structure $\xi'$ which is $C^\infty$-close to $\xi$ and such that $\partial \xi \prec \partial \xi'$ along $T$.
        \item (Twist) Suppose $\xi$ is $\Phi$-horizontal for some smooth nonsingular flow $\Phi$ on $M$. For any smooth $\Phi$-horizontal foliation $\mathcal{G}$ on $\partial M$ satisfying $\mathcal{G} \prec \partial \xi$, there is a $\Phi$-horizontal positive contact structure $\xi'$ with $\partial \xi' = \mathcal{G}$.
    \end{enumerate}
    In both cases, we can arrange that $\xi'$ coincides with $\xi$ away from an arbitrarily small neighborhood of $T$.","status":"unverified"}

