{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.304505+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fabf8a5593a90b972953f6c1bdb570d2720dcb30a4511ba6579f819c52157025","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem \cite{FNRW} of arXiv:2411.14818, 'Scaling limits of solitons in the Box-Ball system'] Let $X_{k}(n)$ be the position of the leftmost component of a tagged $k$-soliton at time $n$ and ${\mu}$ be a probability measure on $\{0,1\}^{{\mathbb{Z}}}$ satisfying the following. 
                \begin{itemize}
                    \item ${\mu}(\Omega) = 1$. 
