{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.070034+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fac100e6b7efab4e85b5e081c3af0c04b1974e9cb8d08fe06ce33fda96f9ed72","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2606.01742, 'Large deviation principles for SPDEs with locally Lipschitz coefficients'] (\cite[Proposition 3.2]{BEM10}) Assume that $\sup_{0\le t\le T}\sup_{x\in\mathbb R}\mathbb E(|V(t,x)|^p)$ is finite for some $p$ large enough. Then,  we have
\begin{itemize}
