{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.332286+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fb78f19a0036bc3b7d23856a3bac06c3a5fe11bdc30bb18eda6b3d6ec67cbcc5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition thm:ap1:wellPosed of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] Fix $\kappa, d \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$ and $T \in (0, \infty)$. Suppose $\lambda \in \mathcal{Q}_{\kappa, d}$ and $(U, W)$ satisfy Assumption (as:results:lyapunov of the paper). Suppose that $(\mu, \gamma)$ is a linear growth solution to the $\kappa$-MLFE{} with potentials $(U, W)$ and initial condition $\lambda$. Then the following properties hold: 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item The time-marginals of $\mu$ have uniformly bounded second moments, that is
\begin{equation*}
    \sup_{t \in [0, T]} \int_{(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{1 + \kappa}} |\mathbf{x}|^2 \mu_t(d\mathbf{x}) < \infty;
\end{equation*}
        \item There exists a positive locally H\"older continuous function $\mu:[0, T] \times (\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{1 + \kappa} \rightarrow (0, \infty)$ such that $\mu_t(d\mathbf{x}) = \mu_t(\mathbf{x}) d\mathbf{x}$. Moreover, the H\"older coefficient and exponent of $\mu$ depends only on $(\kappa, d, T)$, the linear growth constant of $(\gamma, \nabla U, \nabla W)$, and the initial condition $\lambda$.
    \item  We have $\mu_t \in W^{1, 1}((\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{1 + \kappa})$ for almost every $t \in (0, T)$. Moreover the following estimate holds:
\begin{equation*}
    \int_0^T \int_{(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{1 + \kappa}} \frac{|\nabla_{\mathbf{x}} \mu_t(\mathbf{x})|^2}{\mu_t(\mathbf{x})} d\mathbf{x} dt < \infty.
\end{equation*}
\item For all $t \in [0, T]$, we have
\begin{equation*}
    \int \mu_t(\mathbf{x}) |\log \mu_t(\mathbf{x})| d\mathbf{x} < \infty.
\end{equation*}
\end{enumerate}
In particular, if $\lambda \in \mathcal{Q}_{\kappa, d}$ and $(\mu, \gamma)$ is a linear growth solution of the $\kappa$-MLFE{} on $[0, T]$ with initial condition $\lambda$, then $\mu_t \in \mathcal{Q}_{\kappa, d}$ for all $t \in [0, T]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.190447+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fb796a3a0a886b1b648e64f9a11d74f2025ff50cdcf2d2b90e2cc3d5f769c2ba","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 42 of arXiv:2510.20492, 'Heterochromatic two-arm probabilities for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For any $d\ge 3$ with $d\neq 6$, there exist $\Cl,\cl,\cl,\cl>0$ such that for any $n\ge \Cref{const_point_to_boundary1}$, $N\ge \Cref{const_point_to_boundary1}n$, $\psi\in \Psi(n,N)$ and $\diamond \in \{\mathrm{in},\mathrm{out}\}$, the following hold:
