 \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.258802+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fb81ae5870f82f3c0b74ec637dfdd7dc1f051f99b5895162d8460f13de61eabc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition lemma:dg of arXiv:2410.23509, 'Dynkin Games for L\'evy Processes'] Consider a pair $(\tilde{\sigma},\tilde{\tau})$ of stopping times  for the problem  in Definition (def:dg of the paper) and a real valued function $\widetilde{V}(x)$, defined by 
