{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:45:05.589005+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fb9a66006086d5f59214eee4839494dbf356e01d52470e641b6ebbb6bba5ab3a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2608.05842, 'Asymptotic Expansion of the Kallianpur–Striebel Formula under Perturbations of Linear Mode'] For any $0\leq t\leq T$ and $n \in \mathbb{N}$, it holds that 
  \begin{align}
    \begin{split}
      &E_{Q^\epsilon}[U_t^\epsilon Z_t^\epsilon|\mathcal{Y}_t^\epsilon]\\
    =&E_{Q^\epsilon}[U_{t}^{n-1,\epsilon} Z_t^0|\mathcal{Y}_t^\epsilon]+\sum_{i=1}^{n-1}E_{Q^\epsilon}\left[U_{t}^{n-i-1,\epsilon} Z_t^0J_t^{i,\epsilon}\middle|\mathcal{Y}_t^\epsilon\right]+O_{P}^T(\epsilon^n),
    \end{split}
  \end{align}
  where 
  \begin{align}
    &H_{t}^{i,\epsilon}=\sum_{j=1}^i H_t^{[j]}\epsilon^j,~~U_{t}^{i,\epsilon}=\sum_{j=0}^i U_t^{[j]}\epsilon^j\\
    \begin{split}
      &J_t^{i,\epsilon}=\int_0^t\int_0^{t_{i}}\cdots \int_{0}^{t_2} (H_{t_1}^{n-1,\epsilon})^\top (\sigma(t_1)\sigma(t_1)^\top)^{-1} (dY_{t_1}^\epsilon-c(t_1)X_{t_1}dt_1)\\
    &\times \cdots \times (H_{t_i}^{n-1,\epsilon})^\top (\sigma(t_i)\sigma(t_i)^\top)^{-1} (dY_{t_i}^\epsilon-c(t_i)X_{t_i}dt_i),
    \end{split}
  \end{align}
  for $i=0,1,2,\cdots$.","status":"unverified"}

