{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:29:21.899095+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fbdfe68fbb878aed63397c920f5463c37fb4354fabce095471c10f5b09480074","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 (Monotonicity of boundary conditions on finite bipartite graphs) of arXiv:2608.00449, 'First-order phase transitions in the hard-core model'] \label[lemma]{lem:boundarymono}
    Let $G=(A\cup B,E)$ be a finite bipartite graph, and for some fixed $\lambda>0$ write $\nu$ for $\mu_{G,\lambda}$ and $\prec$ for $\prec_G$. For a set $L$ contained in one bipartition class and an assignment $\tau\in\{0,1\}^L$, write $\nu^{L,\tau}$ for $\nu$ conditioned on the event $\sigma|_L=\tau$. Then
