{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:52.655202+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fca5d837521f1f4d5cfe52b86b32fd9c89a4ca4b9d1d3aa5ed832285b0083471","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 18 of arXiv:2609.03713, 'A Sharp Mass Threshold for Boundedness in a Critical Quasilinear Chemotaxis Model with Ind'] For each $\varepsilon>0$, there is a positive constant $c_\phi(\varepsilon)>0$, depending only on $m$ and $\varepsilon$, such that 
