{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.540017+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fcc14cb40acd97ccdc945409c1e26af9b535e7ef8416e8c095daefb61dfdd1e8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:1 of arXiv:2603.27906, 'Marked GUE-corners process in doubly periodic dimer models'] Let~$(u_{s,j}^t)_{1\leq s\leq t\leq 2\ell N}$ be the colored interlacing particle system described above.

Then there are (explicit) $\tau, \sigma>0$ (see later ~(equation eq:turning_point of the paper) and~(equation eq:sigma_square of the paper)) 

 such that the turning point has coordinates $(2\ell N, 2\tau N)$ and 

\begin{equation}
\left(  \frac{u_{s,j}^{t}-2 N\tau }{2\sigma\sqrt{N}}\right)_{1\leq s\leq t}\to \left(\xi_{s,j}^t\right)_{1\leq s\leq t},
