in the sense of weak convergence as~$N\to \infty$, and~$(\xi_{s,j}^t)_{1\leq s\leq t}$ is the marked GUE-corners process with an underlying marking function~$\theta$ given in (equation eq:intro:theta of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.122397+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fcc16f41902b54db99b0613f13fd13cca039c093cfde856839da962b896d5885","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma-one-pt-estimate-interface-discrete of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] Let $0 < \rho \ll 1$. There exist $\delta_0 > 0$ and an absolute constant $C>0$ such that for any $0 < \delta < \delta_0$, any $x \in \delta \mathbb{Z}^2$ and any $r > 0$,
