{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.313447+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fcc5345b073f7142a2a09073128ff6ad72f2028488b9f9da7f67bb73ba718156","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 35 of arXiv:2608.05931, 'Effective Lagrangian regularity and the uniqueness threshold for random H\"older velocity '] For each $N \in \N$, we let $U^N : [0,1] \times \T^d \to \R^d$ denote the truncated sum
    \[U^N(t,x) := \sum_{j=0}^N u^j(t,x).\]
    We then let $\Phi^N: [0,1]  \times \T^d \to \T^d$ denote the (uniquely defined) flow solution of the ODE
    \begin{equation}\begin{cases}
        \dot \Phi^{N}_t(y) = U^N(t,\Phi^{N}_t(y)),\\ \Phi^{N}_0(y) = y.
    \end{cases}
    \end{equation}
    For any $v : [0,1] \times \T^d \to \R^d$ with $v \in \mathcal{C}^0([0,1]\times \T^d)$, we let $\iop^{N} v : \T^d \times [0,1] \times \T^d \to \R^d$ be defined by
    \[\iop^{N} v(y,t,x) := \int_0^t v\big(s, \Phi^N_s(y) + x\big)\,ds.\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:35:19.870939+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fcc6e6534cc709d359e38a39af8da9f524b8757373a9e5b347b8d210d83dbac0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem cor:pointwise of arXiv:2608.24731, 'Optimal Alternating Regret for Online Learning and Games\thanks{Authors are alphabetically'] For every horizon $T \ge 1$, (alg:main of the paper) with the uniform probability measure $\mu \in \Delta_{\+X}$ guarantees
\begin{equation}
  \max_{\boldsymbol{u} \in \+X}\operatorname{Reg}_{\mathrm{Alt}}^T(\boldsymbol{u})
  \le
  8d\left(1+\log_{+}\frac{T}{2d}\right) + \frac{1}{4},
\end{equation}
where $\log_{+} z:=\max\{0,\log z\}$. Since $\max_{\boldsymbol{u} \in \+X}\operatorname{Reg}_{\mathrm{Alt}}^T(\boldsymbol{u}) \le 4T$ trivially, we have
\begin{align*}
    \max_{\boldsymbol{u} \in \+X}\operatorname{Reg}_{\mathrm{Alt}}^T(\boldsymbol{u}) = O\left( \min\left\{T, d\left (1+\log_{+} \frac{T}{2d}\right) \right\} \right) = O(d \log(1+T/d))
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

