	where $\zeta\in L^4(\Omega,\mathscr F_{\tau-t};\mathcal H)$ with $\mathscr{L}(\zeta) \in D(\tau - t)$, and $\mathcal{R}_3$ is a positive constant independent of $\tau$, $\epsilon$ and $D$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.254099+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fcdde6e329d30bd7b92e41d6447f583ef3ddb526043e417b9571295d400b7e59","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn 12 (Hausdorff distance, {\cite[Section 7.3.1) of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] {BBI01}}]
Let $(Z,d^Z)$ be a metric space and let $\calC_c(Z)$ be the set of all compact subsets in $Z$.
For $A,B\in\calC_c(Z)$, define the Hausdorff distance between the two $d_{\rm{H}}^Z(A,B)$
by setting
 \begin{equation*}
  d^Z_{\mathrm{H}}(A,B):=\inf\{\varepsilon>0:A\subseteq B^{\varepsilon},B\subseteq A^{\varepsilon}\},
 \end{equation*}
 and
 \begin{equation*}
  C^{\varepsilon}:=\{z\in Z:\exists c\in C,\;d^Z(z,c)\leq \varepsilon\},\quad C\subseteq Z.
 \end{equation*}
 Here, we use a convention $\inf\emptyset:=\infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:01:01.725526+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fce029fbd10d2dbedd7272126f80a20407401f7030fc24a73d80796733fa5691","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma expansion-curvature-0 of arXiv:2609.00108, 'The double sphere solution in the liquid drop model'] Let $\Sigma_0^{\varepsilon, +,1}$ be the surface parametrized as in (equation defSigma0ve12 of the paper), with $P$ and $Q$ defined as in (equation defPQ of the paper). Let $h = h(r)$ be a $C^{2, \alpha}$-small normal perturbation of $\Sigma_0^{\varepsilon, +,1}$ as in (equation def-np of the paper). Then: for all $r \in (1,2)$ we have
		$$
		\begin{aligned}
			| {\mathcal Q}_{\Sigma_0^{\varepsilon, +,1}} [h] (r)
			| &\lesssim  (|h| + (r-1) |h'|^2 ) \, (r-1) \, (|h''| + |h'|) \\
			&+ |h|^2 + (r-1) |h'|^2 + (r-1) |h| |h'|;
		\end{aligned}
		$$
		for any $r \in [2, \varepsilon^{-\frac12})$ we have
		$$
		\begin{aligned}
			| {\mathcal Q}_{\Sigma_0^{\varepsilon, +,1}} [h] (r)| &\lesssim  ( \frac{|h|}{1+ r^2} + |h'|^2 )  \, ( |h''| + \frac{|h'|}{1+r} )\\
			&+ \frac{|h|^2}{1+ r^6} + \frac{|h'|^2}{1+ r^2} + \frac{|h| \, |h'|}{1+ r^3} ;
		\end{aligned}
		$$
		and any $r \in (\varepsilon^{-\frac12}, \varepsilon^{-1})$
		$$
		\begin{aligned}
			| {\mathcal Q}_{\Sigma_0^{\varepsilon, +,1}} [h] (r)| &\lesssim  (\varepsilon |h| + (1-\varepsilon^2 r^2)^2 |h'|^2) \, ( (1-\varepsilon^2 r^2) |h''| + \varepsilon^\frac12 (1-\varepsilon^2 r^2) |h'|)\\
			&+ \varepsilon^3 |h|^2 + \varepsilon (1-\varepsilon^2 r^2)^2 + \varepsilon^\frac{3}{2} (1-\varepsilon^2 r^2 ) |h| |h'|. 
		\end{aligned}
		$$
		Here ${\mathcal Q}_{\Sigma_0^{\varepsilon, +,1}}$ is the quadratic term obtained in Proposition (generalH of the paper) for the surface $\Sigma_0^{\varepsilon, +,1}$.
		We also recall that $R=\frac{1}{\varepsilon}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:23:58.615126+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fce1ff400eac3eb28b6bf13cedf54b4b4b8ade2b75484c1cd29b4f5d8164e085","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 125 (Derivatives of logarithmic density) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] Let $\angularcoeffinmuweightedspatialcartesian_i^A$ be the $3\times 2$ matrix from  \eqref{E:ANGULARCOEFFINMUWEIGHTEDCARTESIAN}. Then the following identities hold:
