{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:16:46.131615+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fcf714b9e2ac78871cab8371fe626de5c43dad712997d5045d160a23e60dfc34","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:MPinverse of arXiv:2605.01444, 'From second moments to pairwise negative correlation: \\applications to minimal and unifor'] For any real $m\times n$ matrix $A$, the Moore--Penrose inverse  $A^+$ is the unique $n\times m$ matrix satisfying the four conditions :
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item[(1)] $AA^+A=A$;
		\item[(2)] $A^+AA^+=A^+$;
		\item[(3)] $(AA^+)^{\mathsf T}=AA^+ $;
		\item[(4)] $(A^+A)^{\mathsf T}=A^+A$.
	\end{enumerate}
When $A$ is square and invertible, $A^+=A^{-1}$. In the singular or rectangular case, $A^+$ generalizes the inverse.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:04:59.425560+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fcf88a0af0f651c26ebc4c3972f1902c055902ac166ba74391ca786609607b38","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm:3dPhaseTranstion of arXiv:2605.18744, 'Lattice random-field Widom--Rowlinson models'] There exist $c,C >0$ such that for all $\lambda\ge C\max\{1,\varepsilon\}$ and all $\Lambda\Subset \mathbb{Z}^d$
