{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.861410+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fd01ff6003a4900e4c82a9a7539c9458938555660f1e69ec7e027ac93d2f1e2c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2506.10817, 'On the Weak Error for Local Stochastic Volatility Models'] Let $h,T$ be such that $\frac Th\in \mathbb{N}$, $\sigma$ and $\xi$ satisfy Assumption \ref{Aspt_new} and $f$ be $3$-times weakly differentiable with derivatives of polynomial growth. Assume that $\left(\hE\bigl[\xi_{jh}|\,\hX_{jh}\bigr]\right)_{0\le j\le T/h-1}$ is uniformly bounded from above and below by positive constants not depending on $h$. Then for all $p>1$
