{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.388815+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fd201640ef873486eae8bdfeba52006c4328c058b90f4703a735062a80e7765f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:barbour of arXiv:2507.10531, 'Quantitative central limit theorems for exponential random graphs'] Let $\Lambda \subseteq \Omega$ and $f : \Omega \to \mathbb{R}$ such that the following two conditions hold for some
positive numbers $V$ and $\Delta$, as well as some time $T \in \mathbb{N}$.
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
    \item

    A bound on a proxy for the variance of $f$: for all $x \in \Lambda$,
    \begin{equation}
        \sum_{x' \in \Omega} P(x,x') \sum_{t=0}^{T-1} \mleft(
            \mathbb{E}[f(X_t^x)] - \mathbb{E}[f(X_t^{x'})] \mright)^2 \leq V.
    \end{equation}
    \item

    A bound on the future expected difference, measured by $f$, between chains started at two adjacent initial states:
    for all $x \in \Lambda$, and $x' \in \Omega$ with $P(x,x') > 0$, and for all $t \geq 0$,
    \begin{equation}
        \mleft| \mathbb{E}[f(X_t^x)] - \mathbb{E}[f(X_t^{x'})] \mright| \leq \Delta.
    \end{equation}
\end{enumerate}
Then, for any $x \in \Lambda$, we have
\begin{equation}

    \mathbb{P} \mleft[
        X_t^x \in \Lambda \text{ for } 0 \leq t < T,
        \text{ and }
        |f(X_T^x) - \mathbb{E}[f(X_T^x)]| \geq \lambda
    \mright] \leq 2 \Exp{- \frac{\lambda^2}{2 V + \frac{4}{3} \Delta \lambda}}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

