{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.306889+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fd3505260daade34ccb78d7fb07ce735ad23569d3db428050c47bde78bb2c5ca","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:shift_X of arXiv:2411.14818, 'Scaling limits of solitons in the Box-Ball system'] Assume that $\eta \in \Omega$.  For any $k, \ell \in {\mathbb{N}}$, $k > \ell$, $h \in {\mathbb{Z}}_{\ge 0}$ and $i \in {\mathbb{Z}}$, we have
                    \begin{align}
                        \xi_{\ell + h}\left(\eta, s_{k + h}\left(\eta, i\right)\right) 
                &= \xi_{\ell}\left(\Psi_{h}\left(\eta\right), s_{k}\left(\Psi_{h}\left(\eta\right), i\right) \right) \\
                &= s_{k - \ell}\left( \Psi_{\ell + h}\left(\eta\right), i \right) - s_{\infty}\left(\Psi_{\ell + h}\left(\eta\right), 0\right)  .
                    \end{align}
                In particular, if $s_{k + h}(\eta, i) = X^{(j)}_{k + h}(\eta,0)$ for some $j \in {\mathbb{Z}}$, then 
                    \begin{align}
                        s_{k - \ell}\left(\Psi_{\ell + h}\left(\eta\right), i \right) = X^{(j)}_{k-\ell}\left(\Psi_{\ell + h}\left(\eta\right),0\right) ,
                    \end{align}
                and thus
                    \begin{align}
                        \xi_{\ell + h}\left(\eta, X^{(j)}_{k + h}\left(\eta,0\right)\right) &= \xi_{\ell}\left(\Psi_{h}\left(\eta\right), X^{(j)}_{k}\left(\Psi_{h}\left(\eta\right),0\right) \right) \\
                        &= X^{(j)}_{k - \ell}\left( \Psi_{\ell+h}\left(\eta\right),0 \right) - s_{\infty}\left(\Psi_{\ell + h}\left(\eta\right), 0\right) \\
                        &= X^{(j)}_{k - \ell}\left( \Psi_{\ell+h}\left(\tilde{\eta}\right) ,0 \right) . 
                    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.760934+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fd366329b1f46ad1ac6570b1e8c1612e65261ee26cdca7e3e685d98e101bd2f2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop cor:Pottsconopt of arXiv:2609.02682, 'LDP for tensor forms'] Suppose we have
