{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.613369+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fd4adb4229c16675ff19e3091dd21ac5a05fd7ad121c9601ca05d84d4f1971b1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2506.09333, 'On the Dimension-Free Concentration of Simple Tensors via Matrix Deviation'] Let $Z_1,\ldots,Z_N$ be i.i.d. copies of a mean-zero subgaussian isotropic random vector $Z$, and let $T\subset \R^d$ be a bounded set. Then, for any integer $p\ge 2$, we have
