{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.615197+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fd6f1974b6b906a73e43ef24e45bdf7c4ba5ae5ab2b140d36df69acf45f64a3a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 19 of arXiv:2608.25785, 'Proper Actions on Homogeneous Spaces of the Upper Triangular Matrix Group via Coarse Geome'] Let $S$ be a set, $T$ a coarse space, and $f,g$ maps from $S$ to $T$.
    The maps $f$ and $g$ are \emph{close} (denoted by $f\sim g$) if the set 
    \[
