{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.223822+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fd818c8b7be6481af139cec8e6f37a8d0c939f8b5cf958e5c258649a05fd8bd8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pro: Wasserstein-$p$ bound without exchangeability final version of arXiv:2603.14163, '\LARGE \bf Tail Bounds for Queues with Abandonment: Constant, Moderate, Large Deviations, '] Let $X\in \mathbb{R}^d$ be a random vector, and $T: \mathbb{R}^d \to \mathbb{R}$ be a measurable function. Suppose $T(X)$ satisfies $\mathbb{E}[|T(X)|^p] < \infty$ for some $p > 1$. We assume Assumptions (assumption: Stein identity final version of the paper), (assumption: Kramers-Moyal expansion final version of the paper) and (assumption: integrability of Kramers-Moyal coefficients final version of the paper)
     hold for $X$ with operator $\mathcal{A}$ and mapping $T$. Then for any $t_0 > 0$, we have the following upper bound for Wasserstein-$p$ distance between $\mathcal{L}(T(X))$ and $\mathcal{L}(Z')$, 
    \begin{align}
        W_p(\mathcal{L}(T(X)), \mathcal{L}(Z')) &\leq g_0(t_0,p) + \sum_{k=1}^{\infty} g_k(t_0,p) \mathbb{E}[|a_{k}^{\mathcal{A}, T}(X) - a_{k}^{\mathcal{L}_{OU}, T}(X)|^p]^{1/p} \notag\\
        &= g_0(t_0,p) + g_1(t_0,p) \mathbb{E}[| a_{1}^{\mathcal{A}, T}(X) + T(X)|^p]^{1/p} \notag\\
        &+ g_2(t_0,p) \mathbb{E}[|a_{2}^{\mathcal{A}, T}(X) - 1|^p]^{1/p} + \sum_{k=3}^{\infty} g_k(t_0,p) \mathbb{E}[|a_{k}^{\mathcal{A}, T}(X)|^p]^{1/p}, 
    \end{align}
    where $Z'\sim N(0,1)$ and the coefficients $g_k(t_0,p)$ for $k\ge 0$
are continuous in $(t_0,p)$ and are given explicitly in (equation eq: W-p bound final of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

