{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.323534+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdb95781c8cd18b061f6fa1a7245b8f5c79866e4fe71f8138a1e2bfa7678f4e1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Cheeger theorem of arXiv:2606.01683, 'Singular-value gap of nonreversible Markov processes'] Consider a Markov jump process on a standard Borel space with generator (equation generator of jump process 2 of the paper), an invariant probability measure $\mu$,
    and jump rates bounded by $q(x,S) \leq q_{\mathrm{max}} < \infty$ for $\mu$-a.e. $x$. Let $\gamma$ be the associated 
