{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:37:51.458299+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdbdabc7b7d7a5c6f46b054f4125d7c94bee5563d208bcfcc8c776fcbdc931e0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 37 of arXiv:2604.03777, 'Equilibrium fluctuations for a multi-species particle system with long jumps'] Let $\gamma \in [1, \; 3/2)$ and fix $\lambda$ such that $0 < \lambda < 3-2 \gamma$. For every $n \in \mathbb{N}_+$, let $L_n:=n^{1 - \lambda}$. There exists some $f: \mathbb{N}_+ \mapsto \mathbb{R}$ satisfying $\lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} f(n)=0$, such that for any $0 \leq s \leq t \leq T$,
	\begin{align*}
