{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:14:37.619526+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdcfaac78d3c269d18ff3c4675b7797e78bf4486a4a09f685bf917db279f484f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 26 of arXiv:2608.19065, 'Boundedly exchangeable graphs'] There exists a unique Borel measure $\lambda_g$ on $M$ such that for every chart $(V, \varphi)$ of $M$, with $\varphi = (x^1, \dots, x^d)$, and every $B \in \Bcal(M)$ with $B \subseteq V$,
    \begin{equation} 
        \lambda_g(B) = \int_{\varphi(B)} \varphi_{\ast}\sqrt{\abs{G}} \; d\lambda_d,
    \end{equation}
    where $G \coloneqq \det[g_{jk}]$ is the determinant of the metric components $g_{jk} \coloneqq g\!\left(\frac{\partial}{\partial x^j}, \frac{\partial}{\partial x^k}\right)$ in the chart $(V, \varphi)$, and $\varphi_{\ast}\sqrt{\abs{G}} = \sqrt{\abs{G}} \circ \varphi^{-1}$ denotes the pushforward of $\sqrt{\abs{G}}$ on $V$ along $\varphi$. Moreover, $\lambda_g$ is diffuse, $\sigma$-finite, and satisfies $\lambda_g(B) < \infty$ for every $B \in \widehat{\Bcal}(M)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.365526+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdd3fe469b3a9e3d37a646650617b0d4de3b3bd3d9845ea1acc535cc78620e7b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop compatibility of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] Let $V,V'\in\mathfrak{C}$, $V\subset V'$, and $x,y\in\mathcal{X}\cap\overline{V}$ such that for every $u\in V'\setminus V$ there is a point $z\in\overline{V}$ that separates $u$ from $x,y$ in $\mathcal{X}\cap\overline{V'}$. Then
