{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.113916+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe362fdb3328570e55b014e44241076806fb7c5a2c6f2bd8a1e4cd1f9ea9c326","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem HKUB of arXiv:2608.16170, '\bf On hitting time distributions of Markov processes with sub-Gaussian heat kernel bounds'] Given a metric measure space $(M, d, \mu)$ such that there exist some $c>0, \alpha>0$ such that  $c^{-1}r^\alpha \le \mu(B(x,r))\le cr^\alpha$ for all $x\in M$ and $r>0$. Let $X$ be a stochastically complete diffusion on $M$ such that the heat kernel of $X$ is continuous and satisfies the on-diagonal estimate
$$
p(t,x,x)\le C t^{-\alpha/\beta}, \quad \text{for all }x\in M, \, t>0.
$$
Let $B(x, r)$ denote a metric ball of radius $r$ centered at $x \in M$. The following three conditions are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}[(a)]
\item The off-diagonal sub-Gaussian-type heat kernel estimate
\begin{equation}
p(t,x,y)\le \frac{C}{t^{\alpha/\beta}}\exp\left\{-C\left(\frac{d(x,y)}{t^{1/\beta}}\right)^{\beta /(\beta -1)}\right\},\quad \text{for all }t>0, \, x\in M;
\end{equation}
\item 
$$
{\mathbb{E}}^x\left[\tau_{B(x,r)}\right]\simeq r^\alpha, \quad \text{for all }x\in M,\, r>0;
$$
\item The tail estimate of the exit time:
\begin{equation}
{\mathbb{P}}^x\left[\tau_{B(x,r)}\le t\right] \le C\exp\left\{-C\left(\frac{r}{t^{1/\beta}}\right)^{\beta /(\beta -1)}\right\},\quad \text{for all }t>0, \,r>0
\end{equation}
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

