{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-09-07T12:18:10.806784+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fec4edb3c85e71998e6781d82224b127c4173eafe9c5aaa7cd95da3fbe405513","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2512.19517, 'Spiking and Resetting'] Let $e^\varepsilon_2$ be the stopping time defined by 
\begin{equation}

\begin{split}
e^\varepsilon_2 = \inf \{ t \ge e_1^\varepsilon \; ; \; X_t^\varepsilon =0 \} \ .
\end{split}
\end{equation}
We have that
\begin{equation}

\begin{split}
