{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.056789+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ff3ad71fb576b7ce5821f0f08b3c2a9d416a4d31f6412034260647ed146ca40a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Description of arXiv:2607.14062, 'Gilbert's disc model conditioned on the square lattice'] Let $k\geq1$ be such that $s_{n_k}= s_{n_k+2}= \hspace{.1cm}\rightarrow\hspace{.1cm}$ and $s_{n_k+1}= s_{n_k+3} = \hspace{.1cm}\uparrow\hspace{.1cm}$. Then, 
\begin{itemize}
    \item if $n_{k+1} - n_k = 2l$ with $l\geq1$, then between the points $u_{n_{k}+1}$ and $u_{n_{k+1}+1}$, the path alternates between the patterns  $(\hspace{.1cm}\rightarrow\hspace{.1cm},\hspace{.1cm}\uparrow\hspace{.1cm})$ and $(\hspace{.1cm}\rightarrow\hspace{.1cm},\hspace{.1cm}\downarrow\hspace{.1cm})$, i.e.,
    $$\forall m\in\{2,\ldots, 2l+1\}, \quad s_{n_k + m} =
    \begin{cases}
        \hspace{.1cm}\rightarrow\hspace{.1cm} & \text{if } m = 0 \mod 2,\\
        \hspace{.1cm}\downarrow\hspace{.1cm} & \text{if } m = 1 \mod 4,\\
        \hspace{.1cm}\uparrow\hspace{.1cm} & \text{if } m =3 \mod 4.
    \end{cases}
    $$
    \item if $n_{k+1} - n_k = 2l+1$ with $l\geq1$, then between the points $u_{n_{k}+1}$ and $u_{n_{k+1}+2}$, the paths alternates between the patterns $(\hspace{.1cm}\rightarrow\hspace{.1cm},\hspace{.1cm}\uparrow\hspace{.1cm})$ and $(\hspace{.1cm}\leftarrow\hspace{.1cm},\hspace{.1cm}\uparrow\hspace{.1cm})$, i.e., 
    $$\forall m\in\{2,\ldots,2l+2\}, \quad s_{n_k + m} = 
    \begin{cases}
        \hspace{.1cm}\uparrow\hspace{.1cm} & \text{if } m  = 1 \mod 2,\\
        \hspace{.1cm}\leftarrow\hspace{.1cm} & \text{if } m  = 0 \mod 4,\\
        \hspace{.1cm}\rightarrow\hspace{.1cm} & \text{if } m  = 2 \mod 4.
    \end{cases}
    $$
\end{itemize}
	In particular, for any $k \geq 1$,
	$$s_{n_{k+1}} = \left\{
	\begin{array}{ll}
		\hspace{.1cm}\rightarrow\hspace{.1cm} &\mbox{ if } n_{k+1} - n_k \mbox{ is even},\\
		\hspace{.1cm}\uparrow\hspace{.1cm} &\mbox{ if } n_{k+1} - n_k \mbox{ is odd}.  
	\end{array}
	\right.$$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:02.092461+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ff47fdb370058ef7165c6ff8a1daf7cd16a18d01ea24ba4b6dbb325563aa3faa","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 2 of arXiv:2604.25964, 'Strong convergence rate of Euler-Maruyama approximations in temporal-spatial H\"older-norm'] (A Lyapunov estimate) 
 Let $V\in C^{1,2}([0, T]\times \mathbb{R}, [0, \infty)), \alpha \in L([0, T], [0, \infty))$ with $\int_0^T \alpha (t) dt<\infty,$ let $\tau: \Omega\to [0, T]$ be a stopping time, let the coefficients $\mu, \sigma, \gamma$ be continuous functions and let $X: [0, T] \times \Omega \to \mathbb{R}$ be the c\`adl\`ag and adapted  solution process to the equation \eqref{eqn1} with sample paths satisfying
\begin{align}

        & \dfrac{\partial V}{\partial t} (t \land \tau, X_{t \land \tau}) + \dfrac{\partial V}{\partial x} (t \land \tau, X_{t \land \tau}) \mu (X_{t \land \tau})+ \dfrac{1}{2} \dfrac{\partial^2 V}{\partial x^2}(t \land \tau, X_{t \land \tau}) \sigma^2 (X_{t \land \tau}) \notag \\
        & \quad + \int_{\bR_0} \left[ V(t \land \tau, X_{t \land \tau} + \gamma (X_{t \land \tau})z ) - V(t \land \tau, X_{t \land \tau}) - \dfrac{\partial V}{\partial x}(t \land \tau, X_{t \land \tau}) \gamma (X_{t\land \tau}) z \right] \nu (dz) \notag \\
        & \leq \alpha (t \land \tau) V(t \land \tau, X_{t \land \tau}), \quad \mathbb{P} \text{-a.s. for all } t \in [0,T].
    \end{align}
    Then,
\begin{align*}
    \mathbb{E}\left[V(\tau, X_{\tau})\right] \leq \exp \left( \int_0^T \alpha(s) ds \right) \mathbb{E} [V(0, X_0)] \in [0,\infty].
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:23:58.626847+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ff4d4f371ce3729f6c75d76452699879574a506d24b8f31110e4a7fe80d5ea55","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 208 (The main a priori estimates for the acoustic geometry along the rough foliations) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] Under the data-assumptions of Sect.\,\ref{S:ASSUMPTIONSONTHEDATA},
