{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.471661+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ff5118f03a4bc6f714b32f45b8bc27a960da576903f7f07c5a938130824f5cc5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:dissipative of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] Let $P_t$ be a $C_0$-semigroup with generator $(\mathsf{L},\dom(\mathsf{L}))$. It holds that:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $x_t := P_t x_0$ for $x_0 \in \dom(\mathsf{L})$ is continuous differentiable on $[0, \infty)$ and satisfies $\dot{x}_t = \mathsf{L} x_t$ with initial condition $x_t|_{t = 0} = x_0$, and $x_t \in \dom(\mathsf{L})$ for all $t \ge 0$, that is, $$P_t (\dom (\mathsf{L})) \subset \dom(\mathsf{L})\,.$$  
    \item If $P_t$ is contractive,  we have  $ \sigma(\mathsf{L}) \subset \{\lambda \in \mathbb{C}\,;\ \mathfrak{Re} \lambda \le 0\}$ and $\norm{(\lambda - \mathsf{L})^{-1}}_{\mathcal{H}} \le (\mathfrak{Re} \lambda)^{-1}$ for $\lambda \in \mathbb{C}$ with $\mathfrak{Re} \lambda > 0$. Moreover, $\mathsf{L}$ is dissipative: 
    \begin{align*}
    \mathfrak{Re} \langle x, \mathsf{L} x \rangle_{\mathcal{H}} \le 0\,,\quad \forall x \in \dom(\mathsf{L})\,.
    \end{align*}
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

