{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.276408+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ff717e5d398a6b8a928646b465871b993c3e09bfeb41b3db9ce9351b2a5b58f0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem theorem3.14goods of arXiv:2412.06246, 'The smallest singular value for rectangular random matrices with Lévy entries'] [[brailovskaya2024universality]] There exists a universal constant $C>0$ such that for any $t>0$, 
