        \item $T$ is asymptotically contractive and has a tight trajectory in $\mathscr{P}(S)$.
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:29:21.917625+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ffbc1ec99a181fe6d030c2e3ce11e2a0b7a8c3525584431465d99a50455809f0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2608.01516, 'Nondegeneracy and regularity of polynomial pushforwards'] Let $\alpha\in(0,1]$ and let $\nu$ be a probability Borel measure on $\mathbb R^k$.
