{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.462832+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fff684df7cd58e69c972d511a598d4b86b38dbe04174a9f4a8acbebe161b9596","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 26 (Acoustical subsets of spacetime) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] We define the following ``acoustical subsets'' of spacetime:
